window.AKK_LONG_AOTIAN_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_LONG_AOTIAN_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["Crack——","Silver light blazed, thunder rumbled so loudly that it shook the eardrums. Lou Yue kept her eyes squeezed tightly shut, not opening them until the roaring in her head faded away.","Somehow, the dark night had turned into broad daylight, and through the hazy glow, a figure was walking straight toward her.","Lou Yue was just about to speak when her gaze locked onto a pair of icy, deep black eyes. To her horror, the man holding a spear was driving it right toward her chest.","\"Wait! Hold on a second!!\" Lou Yue's eyes went wide. She couldn't care less about upholding the dignified image of Miss Lou that she was known for, and raised her hand in a hurry to yell.","But before her hand could even move past half its path, a dull squelch drifted into her ears.","Lou Yue stared blankly down at her body, watching the spearhead sink completely into her right chest. Searing pain spread through every inch of her in an instant, her legs went weak, and she crumpled toward the ground.","\"Young Master!!\" A crowd of people swarmed over to catch her.","Lou Yue shakily pointed at the man holding the spear, whose eyes were now flashing with surprise: \"You...\"","As soon as she opened her mouth, blood gushed out. All around her, shouts of \"Young Master\" rose in a chaotic, wailing din. Lou Yue had no idea who they were calling for, she only stared fixedly at the murderer who still stood arrogantly before her, and used the last of her strength to speak each word clearly: \"You... are... done for...\"","Her head lolled to the side, and she lost consciousness entirely.","\"Young Master!!!\"","When Lou Yue woke up again, most of the pain in her chest had faded away. She lay still without moving, and the cold, sharp face of that man popped up in her mind.","Hmph, being good-looking doesn't help you at all.","In a society ruled by law, how dare he wield a spear in broad daylight and stab Miss Lou right through? He can look forward to rotting in a prison cell for the rest of his life!","Lou Yue bared her teeth in a grim smile and opened her eyes, only to meet four pairs of teary, stunningly beautiful eyes, one after another.","\"You've finally woken up, my lord... I've been so worried about you, Dou'er was crying her eyes out.\" The woman in the sheer pink dress grabbed Lou Yue's hand and pressed it to her own cheek.","The woman at her side pulled Lou Yue's hand away: \"Brother Yue, you've been unconscious for two whole days. Jiaojiao couldn't sleep a wink, I wanted to stay by your side the whole time, but Lord Xuan wouldn't let me, I...\"","Before she could finish, the woman in white crouched down and pushed the other two aside, wrapping Lou Yue's hand in both of hers, her voice so soft it seemed like it could drip water: \"My lord, is there any part of you that still hurts? Would you like Shuang'er to rub it for you?\"","The woman in yellow who had been standing to the side watching them all this time suddenly asked, \"My lord, is something the matter?\"","Lou Yue tugged at her hand twice but couldn't pull it free, so she gave up struggling. She licked her dry lips and asked, \"Is this Hengdian?\"","The woman in pink dabbed at the non-existent tears at the corner of her eyes: \"What's Hengdian? This is the Langlang Residence that you just bought, my lord.\"","Langlang Residence... what a tacky name... but why are they calling me \"my lord\"? If this isn't Hengdian, why is everyone wearing ancient-style clothing?","Lou Yue glanced around the antique furnishings of the room, and pushed herself up to sit.","The beautiful women rushed to help her up, propping her up and fetching back cushions for her, waiting on her like she was an empress dowager. Before Lou Yue could get fully settled, a patch of pale white skin came into her view.","Her collar had slipped open a little when she sat up, exposing most of her chest and abdomen.","Layers of gauze were wrapped around the wound on her right chest, making that side slightly higher than the left, but even so, it was still completely flat, no curves at all.","Lou Yue's eyes nearly popped out of her head. Where did her proud breasts go?!","\"My lord?\" A soft, questioning voice sounded beside her ear.","Lou Yue closed her eyes. Her left hand, still hidden under the quilt, trembled as she reached down toward her lower body. The moment her fingers brushed against the bulge in her trousers, she snapped her hand back like she'd been burned.","Damn it, that bastard who stabbed me isn't the one who's finished first—I am.","I've turned into a man! What kind of cruel prank is this?!","Lou Yue was so angry she almost laughed out loud. She might have an easygoing personality, but she never ever wanted to become a bulky, rough man with a hard body! This is totally impossible, I must be dreaming!","Right, it's just a dream!","Lou Yue frantically tried to hypnotize herself in her mind, and once she'd convinced herself of that, she flopped back down onto the mattress.","\"Ugh—\" A searing pain shot through her chest, the pain so sharp it forced her to face reality.","\"My lord! What's wrong? Did you pull your wound?\"","The beautiful women crowded around her in a panic, only to see a glisten of tears welling up in Lou Yue's eyes.","\"This is terrible! The pain is so bad it made the young master cry! Hurry up and call the doctor and Lord Xuan over!\" the pink-clad woman named Dou'er exclaimed in alarm.","\"...\" These are tears of anger, you know!","Lou Yue grabbed Dou'er's wrist, and forced a smile that looked like she was bearing her injury bravely: \"It's nothing, I'm not in pain. Really, it doesn't hurt at all.\"","Her mind was in total chaos, but the top priority was to figure out where exactly she was. She held her patience and chatted with the women to gather information.","After a long while... Lou Yue folded her hands in front of her, and gave the line of beautiful women a gentle smile: \"I want some quiet time alone. All of you, go out for a while.\"","The women obediently agreed and filed out. The door creaked shut behind them.","Now that she was alone in the room, Lou Yue waited until the sound of their footsteps had faded completely, then threw off the quilt, barefoot, and darted over to the full-length mirror in the corner of the room.","The mirror, made of some unknown material, reflected her figure with perfect clarity. Her face looked 50% similar to her original one, but the features were more delicate and striking—she had a high straight nose, thin, well-defined lips, a look that was both bright and heroic, a sharp, stunning beauty that could easily pass for either masculine or feminine.","Lou Yue's gaze drifted down the mirror, landing on the half-exposed chest of the person in the reflection.","It was perfectly smooth and flat, with not a single curve, only making the line of her neck look longer and more slender, carrying the unique lean, lanky air of a young man.","\"...\"","For a moment, she couldn't even tell if she should be glad that the new body was so good-looking, or upset that she'd swapped genders.","Lou Yue stepped away from the mirror, pacing back and forth irritably across the room, until she broke out in a sweat and the wound began to ache, forcing her to stop.","From all the information she'd just gathered, she had really transmigrated.","She'd crossed into that Long Aotian harem novel she'd spent the whole previous night mocking and complaining about.","She didn't end up as one of the women in the protagonist's harem, but damn it, she'd woken up as a man—and the male lead's rival in love, at that!","She no longer had to compete with all the women in the harem for the protagonist's favor, but now she had to go up against the Long Aotian male lead himself. The book was 1000 chapters long, and this rival survived 999 of them... his entire life's mission was to use every despicable trick possible to steal women away from Long Aotian.","The male lead had been dying to get rid of this rival for ages, but the original owner came from the Lou clan of Xuandu, a clan that controlled a quarter of all cultivation resources in the cultivation world. Before he had enough power, the male lead could only hold back his anger.","Finally, in the second-to-last chapter, the original owner fell right into the male lead's hands. His spiritual meridians were crippled, his tendons in his hands and feet were cut, and he was left in agony worse than death. In the end, the original owner begged the women in the male lead's harem through tears just to get a quick, clean end to his miserable life.","The more Lou Yue thought about it, the more hopeless she felt. Not only did she transmigrate into a man, she transmigrated into someone who was fated to die a horrible, tragic death at a young age—this was the worst luck ever!","She leaned back and collapsed into a carved wooden chair, sighing deeply. A beam of unruly sunlight streamed through the window lattice and landed right on her face, so bright that she couldn't even focus on wallowing in her misery.","Lou Yue snatched a teacup off the table and clapped it over her eyes. Perfect, now the whole world was nice and dark and quiet.","She didn't know how much time had passed before there was a knock on the door.","\"Knock knock.\"","\"Knock knock, knock knock.\"","Lou Yue didn't feel like answering, but the person outside was insistent and kept knocking, so she lazily raised her voice: \"Who is it?\"","\"Young Master, it's me, Little Qiu.\" The voice from outside the door was thick with fawning, and anyone could tell at a glance that this was the original body's most loyal sidekick.","Lou Yue tossed her teacup back onto the table. \"Come in.\"","Little Qiu, a short, scrawny fellow with a shifty, sharp face, stepped over the threshold and leaned in, grinning from ear to ear. \"Young Master, you're finally awake, I—\"","Seeing he was about to launch into a long, rambling speech full of fake concern, Lou Yue shot him a look of clear disgust. \"Cut to the chase.\"","Sensing Lou Yue was in a foul mood, Little Qiu thought for a second and asked in a considerate tone, \"Young Master, are you upset about Xiao Rangchen?\"","\"Who did you say?\" Lou Yue wondered if she'd heard wrong.","\"Xiao Rangchen! He hurt you, and right now he's locked up in the water dungeon, just waiting for you to wake up and decide what to do with him.\"","Lou Yue froze. Xiao Rangchen. The male lead of this harem novel, the original body's rival in love, the one and only Long Aotian.","That was right. The person who had stabbed her earlier wore a black gold thorn earring on his right ear cartilage, which was basically the signature mark of the novel's male lead. But she couldn't remember any plot point where the male lead shot the original body and then got locked up in a water dungeon.","\"Young Master?\"","Lou Yue snapped back to her senses and asked, \"How is he doing?\"","Little Qiu bared his teeth in a grin. \"Don't worry, Young Master. Xiao Rangchen is completely unharmed, no one has laid a finger on him! We've made sure he's in perfect shape for you to have your fun with!\"","Lou Yue choked a little. \"...Then tell me, exactly what kind of fun did you have in mind?\"","Thinking Lou Yue wanted him to come up with torture methods, Little Qiu immediately gushed on and on. \"You took a fancy to his little sister, even gave him a chance to fight you, and that ungrateful brat not only didn't show any gratitude, he took the chance to hurt you. Why don't you shoot him a few times first, then do his sister right in front of his eyes to drive him crazy!\"","Lou Yue: ... That's so vicious. He really lives up to being the despised villain's sidekick.","After he finished speaking, Little Qiu craned his neck, his eyes sparkling, waiting to be praised.","Lou Yue slowly raised her hand and pinched his shoulder blade, her tone loaded with meaning. \"Little Qiu, you really are such a good subordinate of mine...\"","Little Qiu chuckled. \"Thank you for the praise, Young Master!\"","Lou Yue's sharp glare went completely unnoticed, and she was too lazy to waste any more time chatting with this dim-witted, wicked sidekick. She pushed herself up with the armrest of the chair, her legs having fallen a little numb.","\"Young Master, are you heading to the water dungeon? Shall I help you change your clothes?\"","Lou Yue paused at those words.","In the novel, Lou Yue was a domineering, narrow-minded, dissolute and profligate aristocratic wastrel, while Long Aotian Xiao Rangchen was loyal and devoted, tough and decisive, cold and unflappable. The thought that the man who had shot her was still completely unhurt, keeping up his cold, unflappable act, made her too restless to stay sitting.","\"Yes, I'm definitely going!\" And she was going to go there full of swagger and confidence!","The water dungeon was located underground of Langlang Residence. It was obvious the cells had been newly dug, but they had every facility, not a single mess in sight. It was clear the person who had built the water dungeon was very experienced, though Lou Yue could not help but wonder where all that experience came from.","There were only two guards inside the water dungeon, both broad and muscular, each one as strong as two of Lou Yue put together. The moment they saw Lou Yue, they instantly perked up. \"Young Master!\"","Their voices boomed so loud Lou Yue almost winced and reached for her ears, but when she spoke, her own voice came out louder than usual. \"Where is he!\"","The first guard flipped the switch beside him, and with the clanking of interlocking gears, a cage was hoisted up from the water, revealing the soaked figure of Long Aotian inside."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["Long Aotian sat in the corner of the cage with his legs bent, wearing shackles made of a special material. His eyes were haughty and disdainful. Clearly, no matter where he was or how wretched his circumstances, nothing could keep him from radiating that proud, domineering aura of his.","Lou Yue snorted.","What a pretentious brat. Even if he was the male lead—Long Aotian himself—wasn’t he still a fallen tiger bullied by dogs... and by her?","On the way to the water prison, Lou Yue had already figured out what stage of the story they were in. If one were to name the weakest point in the male lead’s entire life, then aside from the brief mentions of his childhood, it would be now: his spirit veins had been damaged, causing his cultivation to plummet by two major realms, leaving him at only the late Foundation Establishment stage.","In other words, if she wanted to settle the score, this was a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.","Lou Yue raised her brows. “Drag him outside. I’m going to interrogate him properly.”","Little Qiu was an exceedingly smooth operator. By the time Lou Yue returned to the courtyard, he had already arranged for someone to bring over a grand chair, a footstool, and a tea table. Fresh fruit and candied snacks were piled high.","The beauties from the rear courtyard also came flocking at the news, surrounding Lou Yue with soft laughter and delicate voices.","Lou Yue sat down, crossed one leg over the other, and opened her mouth to accept a grape offered by one of the beauties. Her languid gaze swept toward Long Aotian, who was being shoved outside.","“Kneel!” the guards shouted as they kicked the backs of his knees twice. When he still refused to kneel, Lou Yue waved her hand and signaled them to stop.","The dim light in the prison had kept her from seeing him clearly. Now, under the sunlight, even Lou Yue—who had seen more than her fair share of handsome celebrities—couldn’t help clicking her tongue.","His disheveled black hair clung to the corners of his forehead. Droplets of water rolled down the high bridge of his nose, paused briefly at the sharp line of his jaw, and then fell into his collar. His thick, dark lashes were beaded with water, and when his eyes lowered, they seemed veiled in a thin mist. Yet the instant he looked up, a sharp edge pierced through the dampness, making his disheveled state inexplicably seductive.","No wonder Long Aotian could still attract so many women even while his cultivation was in decline...","Lou Yue glanced at the beauties beside her, who were staring blankly, and gave a not-too-loud cough. They immediately came to their senses and remembered who the rightful master of the place was.","Lou Yue understood the instinct to admire a handsome man. She herself enjoyed looking at beautiful men and women. But the womanizing scumbag in front of her was the exception.","“Where’s that spear?” Lou Yue glanced at Little Qiu.","Soon, two people carried over a spear that was pitch-black from end to end, its tip stained with dried blood. Lou Yue rose and walked toward it.","She was just about to pick it up when she remembered that the male lead’s spear recognized its master. In the hands of anyone else, it would weigh tens of thousands of pounds. The thought that she could simply lift it was nothing but wishful thinking.","“Find me another spear.”","The moment she spoke, a spear appeared out of thin air in Little Qiu’s hands. He held it out like he was presenting a treasure. “Young Master, Little Qiu prepared one long ago!”","Lou Yue took the spear from him and sauntered over to Long Aotian.","“Was this where you stabbed me that day?” The sharp spearhead pointed toward the left side of his chest, where his heart lay.","Xiao Rangchen’s deep, narrow eyes locked firmly onto her.","“Not saying anything? Then I’ll take that as a yes.” Lou Yue’s brows relaxed, her expression rich with sly charm.","“What do you want?” Xiao Rangchen’s thin lips parted slightly. His voice was hoarse, caught somewhere between that of a youth and a mature man.","“What do I want?” Lou Yue stepped closer, then unhappily retreated when she realized she was shorter than him. “Obviously, I want to repay you in kind. You should understand that very well.”","A sharp glint suddenly flashed through Xiao Rangchen’s eyes. Even the black-and-gold thorn on his right ear seemed to gleam with icy light.","Lou Yue ignored that glint completely. She shifted the spear in her hand toward Xiao Rangchen’s right chest—the same place where he had stabbed her.","She had never held a spear before, let alone killed even a fish. But he had attacked her first. If she didn’t return the favor, how could she swallow her anger?","Lou Yue steeled herself and thrust the spear forward. A muffled groan sounded from the man before her. Blood seeped from the spearhead, which had disappeared into his flesh. She froze for an instant, then tightened her grip around the shaft.","Her vaunted ability to adapt proved extremely useful at that moment. The spearhead had only penetrated about two centimeters; it was still far from piercing straight through him. But that was no longer a problem.","Lou Yue’s gaze shifted from the spearhead to Xiao Rangchen’s sharply defined face.","If she killed him right now, would it change her future? Or would she be sent back?","As long as she drove the spear through the heart on his left side, perhaps everything would return to normal.","The killing intent that rose in Lou Yue’s eyes was clearly reflected in Xiao Rangchen’s. A fierce glint flashed through his gaze, and his entire body tensed. The invisible confrontation was like a bowstring stretched to its limit.","Then, without warning—","Boom!","A thunderclap split the sky.","There were no dark clouds overhead. In broad daylight, lightning struck out of nowhere, hitting Lou Yue with pinpoint accuracy, as if Heaven itself had been enraged.","Lou Yue felt as though red-hot needles had pierced through her entire body. Electricity raced wildly through every limb and bone, leaving every inch of her flesh numb and burning.","The force of the lightning also traveled rapidly along the spear shaft and into Xiao Rangchen’s body. His muscles convulsed uncontrollably. The spirit-sealing stone shackles locked away his spiritual power, leaving him no choice but to withstand the lightning with his physical body alone. His blood and qi churned violently, and he vomited blood.","Everyone was stunned motionless by the sudden turn of events. Once they came to their senses, they hurriedly crowded around them.","“Young Master!”","Lou Yue’s trembling hand released the spear. It fell to the ground with a clatter. Bracing herself against her knees, she struggled to stand straight. “...I-I’m fine...”","At the instant she had been struck, she had sensed a force protecting her heart. Still, the lightning had left her trembling uncontrollably, and the pain made her bare her teeth in a grimace.","But why had the lightning struck her?","Could it be... because she had developed the intention of killing the Child of Heaven’s Fortune, Long Aotian?","Lou Yue was shaken to the core. Although her life had not been in danger, as a modern person, she was far too deeply affected by the psychological shock of being struck by lightning. Her plan to kill Long Aotian and change the future immediately retreated.","She calmly smoothed down her hair, which had been blown into a wild mess, and swept her gaze around. Seeing that everyone else was acting as though nothing had happened, she was just beginning to curl her lips in satisfaction when she suddenly met a pair of eyes filled with contempt.","“Impudent!” Following Lou Yue’s gaze, Little Qiu caught sight of the look in Xiao Rangchen’s eyes and shouted before she could say anything. “Xiao Rangchen, you’re nothing but a Foundation Establishment commoner. You’re not even fit to carry our Young Master’s shoes! If our Young Master weren’t merciful, do you think you’d still be alive?”","Xiao Rangchen gave a cold snort. His eyes, deep as a frigid abyss, swept over Lou Yue.","“Little Qiu.” Lou Yue sat back down in her chair. Resting a fingertip carelessly against her temple, she lifted her chin slightly toward the front and said blandly, “Go finish the job with that spear.”","Little Qiu obeyed at once. He picked up the bloodstained spear from the ground and walked forward. The guards understood immediately, clamping down hard on Xiao Rangchen’s arms from either side.","Without the slightest obstruction, Little Qiu thrust the spear through the wound Lou Yue had left behind.","A muffled groan escaped Xiao Rangchen’s throat, only to be swallowed back down.","Just as Xiao Rangchen was beginning to adjust to the pain, Little Qiu slowly twisted the spear. The shaft scraped against flesh, producing a harsh, grating sound that struck straight through the heart. Lou Yue’s brows furrowed slightly at the noise.","Only then did Little Qiu begin withdrawing the spear inch by slow inch. Blood gushed out at once, splattering onto the ground and spreading into a vivid red stain.","Xiao Rangchen bit down hard on his lip, refusing to utter another sound. His bloodshot eyes remained fixed on Lou Yue, wild ferocity mingling with unwillingness and humiliation as it surged toward her.","The two guards exchanged a glance, then suddenly lifted their feet and stomped hard on Xiao Rangchen's knees. He staggered, his legs buckling, and the guards seized the chance to press down on his shoulders, determined to force him to his knees. Every muscle in Xiao Rangchen's body tensed up, and no matter how hard they pushed, his knees remained suspended an inch above the ground, refusing to touch the floor.","Lou Yue propped her cheek on one hand, watching the whole scene unfold.","The more unyielding and proud Xiao Rangchen showed himself to be, the more the suppressed restlessness in Lou Yue's heart grew wild.","Back then, she had dived headfirst into this serialized novel and followed every update for so long, precisely because she was drawn in by this very tenacity of Xiao Rangchen. It was the first time she had ever been captivated by a fictional character on paper.","However, the more she had admired him at the start, the more disappointed she felt later on.","Watching him build a harem, flirting with every woman he met only to turn around and pursue someone new, Lou Yue felt a disgust so intense it was like swallowing a fly. She was a strong-willed, stubborn person who hated losing, and this was the first time she had \"fallen\" for a paper character, yet she was still clinging to that bit of unwillingness. She masochistically followed the novel all the way to its end, and the result was naturally that her disgust doubled, with even the initial admiration she once held turning into a total joke.","Thinking of this, that familiar wave of nausea rose in Lou Yue's stomach again. Old grudges tangled with new resentment, making the idea of humiliating him clearer and more urgent than ever.","\"That shot earlier was to repay what you owed me,\" Lou Yue said as she stood up, pacing unhurriedly over to Xiao Rangchen. She lowered her gaze, her condescending air laced with clear contempt. \"But then—\"","She drew out her tone, a faint smile playing on her lips as she stood with her hands behind her back, her voice carrying a hint of mischief. \"Interest still has to be collected.\"","Her gaze swept over his sharp, unruly brows and eyes, and she asked, \"What kind of punishment do you think won't take a life, but will be the most humiliating, the most unforgettable?\"","Voices immediately came from behind her, chattering all at once. Some suggested using poison, some brought up strange and exotic torture devices, and someone even shouted that they could strip him naked and hang him from the city gate. Those ideas were crude and unremarkable, none of them hitting the mark for Lou Yue, but they did successfully darken Xiao Rangchen's expression.","Lou Yue let them keep letting their imaginations run wild as she circled around Xiao Rangchen, sizing him up from head to toe—from his oozing, bleeding wounds to his tightly pressed lips, and finally to his eyes that burned with rage.","Xiao Rangchen was remarkably tolerant of pain. Ordinary torture would only play right into his hands, so the method she came up with didn't need to cripple him, but it had to be completely unexpected, enough to shatter his pride and leave him feeling thoroughly humiliated.","As she was thinking, a quiet murmur drifted over to her ears: \"I still haven't forgotten how my father spanked me in front of a whole crowd of people...\"","Lou Yue's eyes lit up all at once. She spun around sharply, pointing straight at the person who had spoken. \"Perfect!\" That person had only mumbled the thought offhand, never expecting to be praised by Lou Yue, and immediately looked rather sheepish.","Lou Yue walked back to her chair under Xiao Rangchen's deep, furrowed gaze, crossed her legs, and a slightly wicked smile tugged at the corner of her mouth.","\"Bring over a long bench, push him onto it, and tie his hands and feet down tight!\" Her voice rang out with unmistakable delight.","\"Lou Yue!\" Xiao Rangchen thundered, his chest heaving so hard it made the fresh blood seep out even more.","Lou Yue loved seeing him so furious and flustered. She lazily raised a hand, deliberately taunting him. \"Now, now, don't shout. Save your voice for later.\"","The ambiguous wording drew a burst of laughter from the crowd. Even someone as tolerant as Xiao Rangchen couldn't keep his face from darkening completely.","Before long, Xiao Rangchen was forced onto the long bench in the middle of his struggles. Lou Yue took the short whip from a guard's back, leaned down, and used the tip of the whip to lift his chin, forcing him to look up at her.","\"Xiao Rangchen, if you say out loud right now, 'Young Master Lou, I beg you to spare me', I'll consider waiving the interest. What do you say?\"","Xiao Rangchen looked at the person right in front of him, who was grinning with obvious eagerness. His Adam's apple bobbed, and he parted his lips to speak two words:","\"In your dreams.\"","Lou Yue nodded good-naturedly, then stood back up and waved away the others who were eager to watch the show for free. \"Everyone leave. No peeking. No matter what sounds you hear, don't come over.\"","\"Young Master, do you want Little Qiu to stay and help you out?\"","\"No,\" Lou Yue refused without even turning her head. She glanced at Xiao Rangchen's tensed back. \"Just stand guard and make sure no one peeks.\"","\"Rest assured, Young Master!\" Little Qiu replied, herding everyone else away.","The others didn't know what Lou Yue had in mind, and they just found it strange that she would chase them all away for what seemed like nothing more than a whipping.","Dou'er, the youngest of the group, couldn't hold back her curiosity and tugged at the sister beside her. \"Shuang'er, why won't the Young Master let anyone watch?\"","Shuang'er's eyes glinted with a knowing look, and she leaned over to whisper something in Dou'er's ear.","Dou'er was shocked. \"Ah! The Young Master is...\"","\"Shh!\" Shuang'er quickly covered her mouth, glanced around warily, then let go and whispered, \"It's not for sure. I only read about that kind of thing in a random anecdote book. But think about it—we've been by the Young Master's side for over a year, have you ever seen her spend the night with any girl?\"","Dou'er thought about it carefully, then frowned and nodded. \"You're right. The Young Master always makes up some excuse to send me away at night.\"","\"Same for me,\" Shuang'er said, pointing at the several other girls ahead. \"It's the same for all of them.\"","Dou'er thought of Xiao Rangchen's disheveled yet striking, tall and imposing appearance, and mumbled with a conflicted look on her face, \"But... I don't want to share the Young Master with him...\"","Lou Yue had no idea that her decision to chase everyone away had sparked such a ridiculous misunderstanding. It wasn't that she was being considerate to Xiao Rangchen—she simply didn't want anyone else to see her spank him. She didn't have any weird kink for that sort of thing, and technically she could have gotten someone else to do it for her, but that wouldn't be nearly as satisfying, or as humiliating for him, as doing it herself.","Even if it was a little awkward for her too, she'd still come out ahead. This was a good deal, no loss at all!","Lou Yue took a deep breath, then covered her eyes with a silk handkerchief she had swiped earlier from one of her maids. Oh, you think you're Long Aotian, huh? Today, she was going to make him taste the bitterness of humiliation, or her last name wouldn't be Lou!","Xiao Rangchen was tied to the long bench, a tearing pain spreading through his chest. He wasn't surprised at all that Lou Yue was going to \"collect interest\". The children of noble families all treated commoners like him as ants, and they could kill him on a whim without ever facing consequences. He had seen countless cruel methods from these aristocratic brats before. As long as he could stay alive, one day, he would pay back every bit of this torment a hundredfold, a thousandfold.","But then, a strange, unfamiliar sensation came from his waist.","The rough, corded whip had hooked onto the waistband of his pants.","The next moment, the whip pulled hard, dragging his waistband slowly downward...","Lou Yue: Surprise? Bet you didn't see this coming?"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["“Lou Yue!”","Xiao Rangchen suddenly began struggling.","Startled by his furious shout, Lou Yue’s movements faltered for a moment. She curled her lip in disdain. As if she wanted to take advantage of him. Even looking at a pig would be better than looking at him, okay?","She tightened the cloth over her eyes, tucking the corners in securely so it wouldn’t slip and soil her eyes midway. Then she moved behind Xiao Rangchen, out of his line of sight, and pulled his waistband down a little farther.","“Lou Yue!” Xiao Rangchen had never imagined that someone from a prestigious family, a young master no less, would disregard all sense of shame and pull down his trousers. He had never met anyone so unconventional and debauched.","Smack!","The whip landed with pinpoint accuracy.","Xiao Rangchen’s entire body went rigid, as if he had been nailed to the bench. Even his struggling ceased.","Smack—","Smack—","With his chin pressed against the surface of the bench, Xiao Rangchen’s disheveled bangs fell over his forehead, concealing most of his face. Only his tightly pursed lips were visible. They had already been pale from blood loss, but now his teeth clenched down so hard that not even the slightest trace of color remained.","The whip did not strike with much force, yet each blow was more unbearable than the last. Every time it came down, the muscles in Xiao Rangchen’s shoulders and neck would tense abruptly, while the fingers trapped beneath the bench clenched so hard they creaked.","When Xiao Rangchen was eight, he had once seen the little boy next door being disciplined by his father. The boy was a year older than him and usually spoiled and unruly. Relying on his larger size, he had often bullied Xiao Rangchen. That day, the boy had been stripped of his trousers and draped across his father’s knee. He had screamed at the top of his lungs, tears and snot smeared across his face, all his usual arrogance gone. His bare bottom gleamed especially brightly beneath the sun.","When the boy noticed him, he shouted, “Don’t look!”","His father gave him a heavy slap. The boy’s wail shot sharply upward as he kicked and thrashed, only to be pressed down more firmly by his father. The slaps continued to fall, one after another, against the reddened flesh.","At the time, Xiao Rangchen had felt only disdain—perhaps even a trace of childish schadenfreude.","But now, he and that miserable, sobbing boy from his memory had become one.","In his twenty years of life, Xiao Rangchen was experiencing for the first time the shame and indignation behind the boy’s cry of “Don’t look!” Yet he was no longer a child. The shame and indignation had transformed into even more violent anger and humiliation. Never had he hated anyone so much that he wanted to strangle them with his own hands!","Lou Yue had no idea that her humiliation had dredged up Xiao Rangchen’s childhood memories. After casually striking him a dozen or so times, she stopped. Roughly judging the position, she used the rope whip to perfunctorily pull his waistband back into place, then removed the cloth from her eyes.","Bound to the bench, Xiao Rangchen’s back was taut like a bow drawn to its limit, full of power with nowhere to release it.","Lou Yue figured he had probably suffered enough humiliation, so she walked around to stand before him. Xiao Rangchen raised his eyes to meet hers. His eyes were frighteningly bright, his pitch-black pupils seemingly tempered with ice, yet also burning with a dark fire. He remained silent, but the fury within him surged like a storm.","Lou Yue laughed. As expected of Long Aotian—he was truly furious.","When he refused to speak, Lou Yue added fuel to the fire, her tone smug and deliberately provocative. “Weren’t you shouting so boldly just now? Why are you so quiet now? Don’t tell me you’re feeling too ashamed to face anyone?”","Xiao Rangchen glared at her fiercely, his voice brimming with murderous hostility. “Lou Yue, one day, I’ll make you regret what you did today.”","Every word seemed to have been ground out from between his teeth. Anyone else confronted with such an expression—one that looked ready to tear them apart and drink their blood—might have retreated. But Lou Yue, rebellious by nature, was instead intrigued.","She blinked her alluring peach-shaped eyes, and even the tiny mole beneath her eyelid seemed to take on an air of arrogance. “Go ahead. Do you think I’m afraid of you?”","Xiao Rangchen’s face turned livid, and an intimidating chill burst from him.","Lou Yue straightened, the corners of her red lips curling upward. “But before that, you should think about how you’re going to escape from my hands.”","Xiao Rangchen was locked back in his cell.","To prevent any mishap—or his “dear mother” from striking her dead with a bolt of lightning—Lou Yue ordered the guards to apply medicine to the wound on Xiao Rangchen’s chest at regular intervals every day.","The medicine did have healing properties, but under her special instructions, applying it felt like pouring salt into the wound and was unbearably painful.","Lou Yue had watched once. Xiao Rangchen never even blinked throughout the entire process. He simply stared at her. Had it not been for his trembling fingers and the veins standing out on his body, which betrayed what he was truly feeling, Lou Yue might have thought they had used the wrong medicine.","Since she could not see Xiao Rangchen lose his composure, Lou Yue stopped going to offer herself up as a living target for his stare. While he was still at his weakest, she needed to seize her opportunity.","There was nothing she could do about being trapped in a man’s body. She could only rely on time to heal her wounded heart. But there was still hope of changing her doomed fate.","She could not kill Long Aotian. However, as long as she became strong enough that even Long Aotian could not kill her, the problem would resolve itself.","With the plot in her hands, stealing Long Aotian’s opportunities and cheat abilities would be easy. Perhaps she could even save the unfortunate sisters who had gone astray in the novel and spare them from being tormented by Long Aotian. But before those opportunities arrived, she had to improve her cultivation as quickly as possible and leave Long Aotian far behind.","The key to breaking out of this predicament was the mysterious “Lord Xuan.”","The book had never mentioned anyone with the surname Xuan. The original host had merely been an obnoxious supporting character, and the people who appeared at his side were usually referred to by titles or descriptions. Even when their names were mentioned, the entire novel ran for a thousand chapters, and she could not remember them at all. Still, given that the original host belonged to the Lou family, one of the four great clans, it made sense that he would have a powerful figure protecting him.","After getting up that morning, Lou Yue had Little Qiu tie her slightly curled hair high on her head. Then, between her favorite peacock green and moon white, she chose the moon-white outfit, which looked more obedient and suitable for currying favor with a senior.","“Where is Lord Xuan right now?” Lou Yue asked as she arranged her collar before the mirror. Only after confirming that everything about her was neat and proper did she speak.","Little Qiu answered without hesitation, “At this hour, Lord Xuan should be cultivating at the rockery on the southern side of the garden.”","Lou Yue raised an eyebrow. Lord Xuan certainly was diligent. His strength must be outstanding as well. With such an expert teaching her, a dramatic increase in her cultivation was surely just around the corner.","This concerned her life and death, so Lou Yue did not dare treat it carelessly. Before leaving the room, she asked Little Qiu once more, “In your opinion, what is my relationship with Lord Xuan like? If I were in danger, how would he react?”","Little Qiu froze for a moment before answering with absolute certainty, “If the young master were in danger, Lord Xuan would definitely protect you even at the cost of his own life. You and Lord Xuan are inseparable—you trust each other more than anyone else!”","Lou Yue was completely reassured.","She brought Little Qiu to the southern side of the garden. Beneath the morning light, the rockery stood tall and imposing. Dark-green vines wound through the seams of the blue-gray stones and climbed all the way to the steep peak. It was certainly full of life, but there was no sign of anyone.","Lou Yue looked around several times without finding him. She turned back and glanced at Little Qiu, questioning him with her eyes.","Little Qiu was just as puzzled, but then he suddenly slapped his forehead in realization. The young master must have quarreled with Lord Xuan again and needed him to smooth things over as usual!","Lou Yue saw Little Qiu nod discreetly and assumed he was going to look for someone. But instead, he came to her side, bowed respectfully toward the space beside her, and called out,","“Lord Xuan.”","Lou Yue: ?","She followed the line of sight upward to the highest point of the rockery. Calling it the highest point was a bit of a stretch—it was only about two meters high, and the very top was no larger than the mouth of a bowl. Yet perched on that tiny patch of space was an even tinier turtle. Its shell was ink-black, marked with crimson patterns.","When Lou Yue looked over, the turtle’s scarlet eyes met hers.","Wait—Lord Xuan wasn’t a senior cultivator. He wasn’t even human. He was a turtle?","A turtle smaller than her palm?!","Shock spread across Lou Yue’s face as a ridiculous scene flashed through her mind: her crawling around on the ground, demonstrating moves to a turtle and struggling desperately to communicate with it.","Lou Yue’s silence further convinced Little Qiu that the two of them had quarreled. As usual, he smiled and tried to smooth things over. “Young Master woke up asking about Lord Xuan. That’s why he came looking first thing this morning.”","As he spoke, he took a bag of dried fish from his storage ring and presented it with both hands. “Young Master personally instructed me to dry these a few days ago. They were only finished yesterday.”","The turtle addressed as “Lord Xuan” swept a chilly gaze over the bag of dried fish. The very next moment, the fish vanished from Little Qiu’s palm.","After handing over the dried fish, Little Qiu beamed as though he had accomplished something important and took his leave from Lou Yue. “Young Master, Little Qiu will be going down now.”","That left Lou Yue alone with a turtle, the two of them staring at each other.","Lou Yue had indeed wanted to have a private conversation with Lord Xuan, but she had no idea how to talk to a turtle... Especially since “Lord Xuan” was staring straight at her.","Lou Yue cleared her throat, looked up at the sky, then down at the ground. At last, she found an opening.","She pointed at the sun and traced a circle with her finger. Then she sat cross-legged on a flat rock nearby, closed her eyes, and struck a pose that suggested meditating and cultivating.","Her meaning was: The sun is shining beautifully today. It’s the perfect day for meditation and cultivation.","Lou Yue opened her eyes and looked toward Lord Xuan, both hopeful and nervous. She hoped he would understand and agree, allowing her to bring up the matter of improving her cultivation naturally. But she was also worried he might not understand her gestures at all.","Lord Xuan watched her earnest performance, then coldly turned his head away and closed his eyes.","Lou Yue: “...”","Was he dismissing her, or had he simply failed to understand her? He had accepted the bribe of dried fish, so surely he wouldn’t refuse to give her face?","Lou Yue rubbed her chin and muttered to herself, “He probably still didn’t understand what I was gesturing. But if he can’t even understand this, how am I supposed to discuss the important stuff with him later...?”","Suddenly, a strange sensation welled up inside her—a feeling of perfect mutual understanding, of hearts communicating without the need for words. And the other half of that connection was the “Lord Xuan” atop the rockery.","Little Qiu’s words echoed in her ears once more: “Young Master and Lord Xuan share life and honor, and disgrace and death. They’re the people each other trusts most.”","In a flash, Lou Yue blurted out, “You’re a contracted beast!”","Only a contracted beast and its master could share this kind of telepathic connection. And only a contracted beast bound by a blood contract would live and die alongside its master, never betraying them.","At the sound of her voice, “Lord Xuan” turned his head again. His eyes were still cold, but this time there was another emotion in them—something that seemed suspiciously like schadenfreude.","“You were struck by lightning,” it said, opening its mouth and speaking in a human voice.","“You can talk?!” Lou Yue was so astonished that she failed to notice the deeper meaning behind its words.","Her thoughts raced as she analyzed the situation.","When she had first transmigrated, her mind had been filled with thoughts of her inevitable death and the Long Aotian before her. She had never considered whether the original Lou Yue had a contracted beast. Now that she thought about it, the original did indeed have one. It had never been described in detail, but there had been several subtle mentions of it during her fights with Long Aotian.","It had already been five or six days since she transmigrated, counting the time she had spent recovering from her injuries. As a contracted beast connected to the original through their bond, Lord Xuan had not come looking for her or tried to settle accounts. That meant he had not sensed that the soul inside had been replaced.","She was safe!","Having reached that conclusion, Lou Yue relaxed at once.","A contracted beast? That would make things even easier...","Suppressing the smile tugging at the corners of her lips, she put on a pitiful expression and said, “Since you’re my contracted beast, I won’t hide it from you. A few days ago, I woke up after being injured and discovered that I’d lost my memory. I don’t remember your name or how to use spiritual energy. Other than remembering that my name is Lou Yue and that I have a father, I can’t remember anything...”","Seeing that Lord Xuan still wore the same expression of cold detachment and faint amusement, Lou Yue pressed on, her tone growing increasingly earnest. “Our honor and disgrace are tied together. Surely you don’t want to see other people bullying me, right?”","“If you stopped bullying other people, they’d be burning incense in gratitude,” the aloof Lord Xuan said blandly.","“...”","Seriously, why did everyone insist on thinking so badly of her? Her own mother had said the exact same thing. But she was the one who was being wronged here, wasn’t she? Were they saying she wasn’t even allowed to fight back??","Lou Yue lost her temper. Her already limited patience vanished in an instant. She crossed her arms, sat down on the rock, and shot him an irritated look. “I want to learn how to use spiritual energy. Are you going to teach me or not?”","Before she could finish speaking, a jade slip dropped from the sky and smacked her on the head. She hurriedly caught it in both hands.","“Focus your attention and sink into your mind.”","Lou Yue was just about to do as instructed when he added, “If you can’t understand it, read it more. Don’t ask questions. Even if you ask, I won’t know.”","“...”","Why did she have such an arrogant contracted beast?","Fortunately, she was exceptionally gifted. She was able to “see” the contents recorded on the jade slip.","The jade slip contained more than a single cultivation technique. It covered everything from profound spells to movement techniques and the use of magical artifacts. It was practically a comprehensive manual tailored specifically for her.","Lou Yue sighed in admiration. As expected of the wealthy and powerful Lou clan—even their children had personalized study plans.","As for why the jade slip was with the original’s contracted beast instead of the original herself, Lou Yue attributed it to the fact that the contracted beast was more reliable than its master and didn’t think much further. After all, in the novel, Lou Yue’s thoughts had been entirely occupied by women. If she hadn’t possessed countless magical artifacts to rely on, she might not even have been qualified to become Long Aotian’s rival in love.","The language in the jade slip was clear and easy to understand. Lou Yue became completely absorbed in it. Even after returning to her room at night, she couldn’t bear to put it down. She studied with more dedication than she had shown during her final year of high school.","It wasn’t until deep into the night that she finally fell asleep with the jade slip in her arms. But barely an hour after her head touched the pillow, urgent knocking shattered the silence.","“Young Master, this is bad!”","Little Qiu’s voice pierced through the door.","“Xiao Rangchen has escaped!”"]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["Lou Yue was wide awake in an instant. She hopped out of bed in a few quick strides and wrenched the door open.","\"Escaped? Where did he get to?\"","\"Somehow Xiao Rangchen pried open the spirit-restraining cage, knocked out Big One and Second One, and a servant only noticed when he went down to check just now.\" Little Qiu hung his head, his tone full of shame. \"But the spirit-restraining shackles on his hands and feet are still on, so he can't have gone far. The guards are already out searching. I'm so sorry, young master, it was my carelessness.\"","\"Has his injury healed?\" Lou Yue furrowed her brows. The medium-grade spiritual herb she had ordered to apply on Xiao Rangchen shouldn't have allowed him to recover this fast.","\"Not at all. The wound was still oozing blood when we changed his dressing yesterday, logically he can barely move around. If I'd known this would happen, I'd have kept him submerged in water!\" Little Qiu stamped his foot in regret. He knew Lou Yue had no intention of killing Xiao Rangchen, so he had moved the prisoner out of the water and onto dry ground these past days, afraid the dampness would worsen his injury and kill him. That move had accidentally given Xiao Rangchen the perfect chance to escape.","Barefoot, Lou Yue paced back and forth on the thick, plush carpet, her smooth soles sinking softly into the fibers.","She had thought too simply. Long Aotian was never someone who could be trapped easily.","She stopped short, her gaze suddenly clearing. \"Where is Xiao Aiai?\"","\"Still in the room in the backyard. We just sent more guards over there, to stop Xiao Rangchen from trying to rescue her.\"","Xiao Aiai, the sister Xiao Rangchen had no blood relation to, the one he had grown up relying on, and one of the five heroines in his harem in the original novel.","Unlike Xiao Rangchen, who was kept completely in the dark, Xiao Aiai had known from the very start that they were not real siblings. The moment Xiao Rangchen found out the truth, he had taken Xiao Aiai into his harem immediately, grandly claiming it was just to keep her by his side and protect her. What a hypocrite, scumbag, and total womanizer!","If the chance arose, she definitely had to pull Xiao Aiai out of that mess, at the very least let her see Xiao Rangchen's true colors as a man who doted on many women.","\"Xiao Rangchen would never leave Xiao Aiai behind,\" Lou Yue said firmly. Otherwise he would never have insisted on bringing her all the way here while fleeing for their lives, not to mention she was one of his future women.","Lou Yue spoke in a low, solemn tone. \"Stop searching for him. Move all the guards to the backyard. We'll wait for him to show up, like waiting for the rabbit to bump into the tree stump.\"","Little Qiu nodded quickly in agreement. \"Young master, you're so thoughtful. I'll go arrange that right now!\"","Watching Little Qiu's retreating, hurried figure, Lou Yue still had a strange feeling in her chest, like she was missing some crucial detail.","The night wind brushed over her thin clothes, carrying a chill.","\"Achoo!\" Lou Yue rubbed her nose, only realizing she had been standing barefoot in the draft in nothing but a thin robe for ages. Her previously tensed brows lifted in a sudden wave of nonchalance. Oh well, no matter how big the problem was, she needed a full night's sleep to have the energy to deal with it. She wasn't going to waste herself overthinking.","The moment the door clicked shut, a drop of bright red blood fell silently from the branches of the tree directly opposite the house, seeping into the damp soil without a sound.","\"Whooo?\"","\"No,\" Xiao Rangchen stared intently at the distant house, his voice icy and firm. \"Her contracted beast is there.\" He had caught a glimpse of that creature named Xuanba lying on the bed behind Lou Yue when she opened the door just now.","\"Whooo whooo!\" The little beast fretted, nuzzling against his neck. Xiao Rangchen's thin lips tugged faintly, his tone still deep and cold but carrying a subtle, soothing edge. \"I know you're strong, but there's no need for a head-on fight.\"","\"Whooo?\"","\"As long as we keep an eye on Lou Yue, Aiai will be safe,\" Xiao Rangchen leaned back against the rough tree trunk, steadying his breathing that had turned ragged from the sharp pain of his injury.","To escape safely, he had to get the spirit stone shackles off. Even if he rescued Aiai with them still on, they would never get far. He hadn't found the key to the shackles on any of the guards. It must be on Lou Yue herself.","Lou Yue...","Xiao Rangchen pressed his lips into a tight, straight line. After a long moment, his Adam's apple bobbed, and he tilted his head back to exhale a long, heavy breath.","***","Having stayed up late the night before and been woken up by the chaos of Xiao Rangchen's escape, Lou Yue didn't climb out of bed until the sun was high in the sky.","Actually, if it weren't for the certain turtle snoring loudly at the foot of the bed, she could have slept even later.","Lou Yue grabbed the silk quilt and draped it over the \"majestic\" Lord Xuan, then got out of bed to change her clothes. After yesterday's practice, she had already mastered quite a few tricks of using spiritual energy.","With a single thought, several sets of luxurious outfits flew out of her storage ring. Lou Yue's fingertips brushed over the soft fabric, and a bright, triumphant grin spread across her face. \"Tsk, I really am a natural at this.\"","In the end, Lou Yue picked out a robe with a striking peacock green and ginger yellow color block design. She left her long hair loose, only tucking matching hair accessories behind each ear. She looked bright, handsome, vibrant, and full of life.","Just as she reached for the door, a strange movement came from her storage ring.","Lou Yue raised her hand, and a light butterfly flew out of the ring. It danced in front of her, scattering a few lines of bold, flowing words in the air.","My dear son, your father has been very busy lately. You'll go to Xuan Du's birthday celebration in my place. As for the birthday gift, just pick some random wild flowers and weeds by the roadside. That old man never pays attention to gifts anyway. That's all for now. Your loving father sends his thoughts.","The golden words slowly faded, and the light butterfly flew back into Lou Yue's palm, turning back into an ordinary, lifeless object.","Lou Yue stepped back and sat down on the pear blossom wood chair, mulling over the message the messenger butterfly had brought her.","Xuan Du was located in Kanze Prefecture, the Lou family's home base. This birthday celebration was for the head of the Lou family, Lou Mo. It was a key plot point in the original novel, where the male lead Xiao Rangchen would obtain the old grandpa in his ring, and meet his beloved White Moonlight Goddess for the first time.","Thinking of that, Lou Yue's eyes lit up with bright excitement.","Her opportunity had arrived.","The old grandpa in his ring? She was going to get it before Xiao Rangchen could. The White Moonlight Goddess? She was going to save her too. Xiao Rangchen wasn't getting a single thing he was supposed to have.","Lou Yue couldn't sit still any longer. She wrenched the door open, then turned back to grab Lord Xuan right off the bed, and marched quickly toward the backyard.","Little Qiu rushed over upon hearing the commotion, but Lou Yue didn't slow down her steps. She spoke loudly and clearly. \"We're leaving for Xuan Du immediately. Go make the arrangements.\"","Little Qiu was taken aback. He had no idea why the originally scheduled departure in five days was suddenly moved up, but he responded promptly. \"Right away.\"","The backyard was lined with rows of houses, but one of them was surrounded by layers of guards, with every door and window tightly watched.","\"Stay outside, don't let anyone come in,\" Lou Yue ordered. She set Xuanba on the windowsill, then pushed the door open and stepped inside.","Right after she shut the door, a thick wooden stick, apparently broken off some furniture, was poked straight at her face.","\"Lecher!\"","\"Shameless!\"","\"Despicable!\"","Lou Yue: ......","She brushed the stick away from her face, but the next second, the stubborn stick was poked right back at her.","Lou Yue stopped moving. She silently counted to ten in her head, and Xiao Aiai's body went limp, collapsing. Lou Yue reached out and caught her steadily in her arms.","Xiao Aiai had a pretty face full of disgust, struggling weakly in her hold while yelling angrily. \"You filthy villain!\"","Lou Yue had indeed allowed Little Qiu to slip a mild drug to Xiao Aiai, the kind that temporarily blocked her spiritual energy and left her too weak to stand. Putting herself in Xiao Aiai's shoes, she thought it was pretty fair to be called filthy... As she reflected on that, she tossed the stick aside, carried Xiao Aiai over to the bed, and sat down on the edge of the bed.","Xiao Aiai dragged her limp body inward, and surprisingly pulled out an identical wooden stick from under her pillow. \"What-what do you think you're doing!\"","The sight of the beautiful girl looking both scared and furious made Lou Yue feel guilty all over again. She softened her voice, speaking gently to comfort her. \"I came here to talk to you about something very important. Don't worry, I would never do anything improper.\"","Xiao Aiai looked at her with obvious suspicion. Lou Yue simply moved all the way to the foot of the bed, putting a safe distance between them, her posture completely open and unguarded.","\"What is it? Speak quickly!\" Xiao Aiai gripped the stick tightly, staring at her with full vigilance.","Lou Yue had already organized her words on the way over, so she got straight to the point. \"Your brother has escaped.\"","Xiao Aiai froze for a second, then her entire face lit up with a genuine, bright smile. \"That's wonderful!\"","Lou Yue's tensed heart finally settled. What she had said just now was a test. Xiao Aiai had a spoiled, straightforward nature that never hid her true feelings, so if Xiao Rangchen had been here, she would never have acted so naturally.","\"I'm leaving for Xuandu today,\" Lou Yue said gently. \"I want you to come with me.\"","Xiao Aiai's smile froze, and she refused without a second thought. \"No way!\"","Lou Yue had expected this answer long ago. She spoke unhurriedly, \"I know you and your brother have been hunted down this whole time, never knowing when the next threat will come. Even right now, there could still be killers lying in wait for you in this city. If you think about it, I did save you two. Those people would never dare step foot into my territory.\"","Xiao Aiai frowned, growing impatient. \"What exactly are you trying to say?\"","\"You've only just reached the Qi Refining stage, and you've only stayed safe this entire journey because your brother has been protecting you. But his spiritual meridian is damaged, and he's been forcing his spiritual power to work nonstop, so he's already at his last breath. Now I'm giving you two choices.\"","Lou Yue bent one leg, tapped her knee lightly with her fingertip, and spoke in a calm tone. \"One, I let you go right now, you go find him, and you both live or die by fate. Two, you come with me to Xuandu, where the only Nianyan Flower in the world that can repair a damaged spiritual meridian grows.\"","The wooden stick in Xiao Aiai's hand slowly drooped. Lou Yue added one more push, her words striking straight at her heart. \"Do you want to be a burden to others for the rest of your life? Is that what you really want?\"","That push hit hard, obvious from the way Xiao Aiai stared at her, eyes already welling up with tears.","\"Why should I trust you?\"","Lou Yue held up two fingers to swear. \"Under the observation of the Heavenly Dao, I, Lou Yue, promise that from this moment on, I will respect all of Xiao Aiai's own wishes, and never force her to do anything against her will.\"","Just then, sunlight streamed through the window lattice, falling on her handsome side profile. She looked sincere and clear, without her usual flamboyance, full of candor. Xiao Aiai stared at her, her mind racing with all kinds of thoughts.","After a long while, she bit her lip and whispered, \"Fine. I'll go with you.\"","Lou Yue held out her palm, tilted her head and smiled, her eyes bright and striking. \"Then I hope all your wishes come true?\"","Xiao Aiai glanced at the outstretched hand, then rolled her eyes at Lou Yue, but finally bit her lip and lightly tapped the palm with her own hand.","Mission accomplished. Lou Yue pulled out a pill and handed it to her. \"The antidote.\"","Now that things had come to this, Xiao Aiai didn't hesitate any longer, and tipped her head back to swallow it.","Seeing her resolute look, Lou Yue blurted out suddenly, \"How about this—stop being Xiao Rangchen's sister, and be my little sister instead?\"","Xiao Aiai's almond eyes went wide as saucers in an instant.","Lou Yue herself was stunned for a second. Those words had slipped out without her thinking, but they actually... didn't sound half bad. She immediately smiled again. \"Think about it, huh? Give me a chance?\"","She wasn't sure if it was because her original reputation was far too bad, or if Xiao Aiai really was unwilling, but all she saw was Xiao Aiai turning her face away, getting off the bed, and deliberately changing the subject. \"The antidote's working now.\"","Lou Yue didn't want to push her, so she went along with the topic. \"Is there anything you need to pack? Get it ready, we're leaving right now.\"","\"So soon?\" Xiao Aiai looked shocked.","Lou Yue thought to herself, Of course not slow—do you think I want to wait here for Xiao Rangchen to show up?","Before she could explain, Xiao Aiai was already muttering to herself \"It's for the best anyway\", then walked a couple steps toward the door. Noticing Lou Yue wasn't moving, she turned back and urged, \"Hurry up, would you? Stop dawdling.\"","Lou Yue couldn't help but laugh. \"Coming.\"","Xiao Aiai's cheeks flushed a little, and she mumbled, \"What are you smiling so nicely for? Even if you do look good, you're still a... never mind, let's go!\"","Lou Yue recalled Xuanba who was on sentry duty, and as they walked past the table missing two legs, the corners of her eyes curved into a smile.","Xiao Aiai caught sight of Lou Yue's gaze, immediately turned her head away, then seemed to remember something and quickly threw away the wooden stick she was holding.","...","Little Qiu was extremely efficient. In less than half an hour, the cloud ship was fully ready for departure.","The four other girls in the backyard saw Lou Yue was leaving and taking Xiao Aiai with her, so they pestered her playfully. Not wanting to upset them, Lou Yue told them to play a finger-guessing game to decide the winner, and in the end she took the winning girl Dou'er onto the cloud ship with her.","The cloud ship was even more luxurious than Lou Yue had imagined. The bottom deck was for the guards and maids to live in, and there were four more floors above it. Xiao Aiai and Dou'er were arranged on the second floor by Little Qiu, while Lou Yue had the largest, most luxurious top deck all to herself.","After leading Xiao Aiai and the clingy Dou'er to their rooms, Lou Yue wandered slowly up to the fourth floor of the cloud ship.","Even though she hadn't managed to trap Xiao Rangchen, being able to take his sister away and save a person who would have ended up trapped by a scumbag in the future felt like she had done a really good deed.","She lay down on the soft bed, listening to the howling wind outside the window, gradually letting her mind relax, and closed her eyes to get some sleep—","A sharp fishy stench suddenly drifted into her nose.","Lou Yue's eyes snapped open, but it was already too late.","---","Happy New Year, my dears!!"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["The cold metal of the shackle chains clamped tight around Lou Yue's throat.","She tried to shift, but the man pressed his knee hard against the joint on the outer side of her thigh, his elbows weighing down heavily on both her arms, pinning her firmly to the bed.","\"Let my sister go!\"","Xiao Rangchen popped out of nowhere, reeking of fish, the ends of his hair still dripping with some unknown liquid.","Lou Yue wrinkled her nose. \"That stench is unbearable. Couldn't you have at least freshened up before coming to ambush me?\"","Xiao Rangchen's gaze was sharp and fierce, but the person he was holding hostage was Lou Yue. She showed not a hint of panic, her tone instead lazy and faintly mischievous. \"Oh, I get it now. You snuck up here hiding in a fish crate, didn't you?\"","Xiao Rangchen pressed his lips into a tight line, not saying a word, icy hostility rolling off him.","Lou Yue was about to tease him further when he cut her off sharply. \"Lou Yue!\" His voice was low and hoarse, thick with suppressed fury.","To subdue Lou Yue, who wielded spiritual power, Xiao Rangchen leaned his full weight over her, his half-dry long hair slipping down with the movement and smacking right against her face.","Lou Yue instantly felt the stench shoot straight to the top of her head, and gagged instinctively.","Xiao Rangchen: \"...\"","Lou Yue's brows knotted together. She wanted so badly to hold it in, but since neither of them could free a hand to move that clump of hair away, it kept brushing against her sensitive nose, irritating it nonstop.","Lou Yue could not hold back any longer, squirming despite the chains binding her. \"Wait— I'm gonna— ugh— throw up— ugh— loosen up first— ugh...\"","Seeing her face pale, the chains scraping red marks into his own neck, looking like she truly was struggling horribly, Xiao Rangchen frowned, and loosened his grip by half a fraction.","That was the split second she needed.","Lou Yue burst her waist upward with all her strength, kicking Xiao Rangchen right off the bed. At the same time, she cast a newly learned binding barrier, locking him in place so he could not move an inch.","\"You faked it.\" Xiao Rangchen's face was livid, every word ground out through gritted teeth.","It wasn't exactly a total lie— she just somehow ended up not actually throwing up in the end. But there was no need to explain that to Xiao Rangchen. She sat up slowly, brushing the messy strands of hair back from her neck, lifting her chin slightly with a smug, arrogant tone. \"That's right. I faked it.\"","Rage flared in Xiao Rangchen's eyes. He punched the barrier hard, but the spirit-restraining shackles on his wrists kept him from breaking through it at all.","\"Don't waste your energy.\" Lou Yue straightened her clothes, hopped off the bed, and circled around him to look him over.","Xiao Rangchen's clothes were far more rumpled than before. A piercing wound on his right chest gaped open, the flesh red tinged with gray, showing faint signs of rotting.","Lou Yue glanced away from the wound quickly. No wonder he's the classic overpowered hero, he really can take pain.","She walked back to stand right in front of Xiao Rangchen, fixing her gaze on him again. \"What did you use to break open the spirit-restraining cage? Something sharp enough to cut through the cage, but not the spirit-restraining chains on your hands and feet? It has some kind of usage limit, doesn't it?\"","Lou Yue's eyes darted to the storage ring on Xiao Rangchen's finger, then to the black-gold ear stud on the side of his ear. Since his spiritual power was sealed, he could not retrieve items from it, so whatever that thing was, it had to be hidden somewhere on his body.","She circled him two more times, but found nothing. She shrugged and gave up. \"Fine, I won't try to take it from you.\"","She sauntered back to the bed, propping herself up on her hands behind her, crossing her long legs to prop them up, looking down at the man on the ground from her elevated position. \"You could have just run off, but you had to sneak onto my cloud boat. Now look at the mess you've landed me in— I have to figure out what to do with you.\"","She thought about just tossing him right off the cloud boat, but they were so high up, he would definitely die if he fell. If the heavens came after her for that and struck her down with lightning, she would end up losing far more than she gained.","Then, a brilliant idea popped into Lou Yue's head.","\"Close your eyes. No peeking. If you do, I'm going to go sleep cuddled up to Xiao Aiai tonight!\"","Xiao Rangchen's Adam's apple bobbed sharply, his knuckles clenched so tight at his sides they blanched white. He took a deep breath and closed his eyes heavily.","Lou Yue immediately fished out a jade slip, swept her spiritual sense across it in a rush to find what she was looking for. After two failed attempts, she finally conjured a clear, pale-gold protective barrier. Glancing out of the corner of her eye to see Xiao Rangchen still standing perfectly still, she curled the corner of her mouth into a smile, lifted her fingertips, and the spherical barrier flew up and swelled abruptly, engulfing Xiao Rangchen inside.","\"Relax, this is a barrier to keep you safe,\" Lou Yue said, stepping over to Xiao Rangchen, who had jolted awake. She poked the golden ball with her fingertip, then thumped it hard twice, nodding in approval. \"Excellent elasticity. This is a really good ball.\"","\"What on earth do you think you're doing?\" Xiao Rangchen's back went rigid, his dark eyes fixed intently on her.","A playful, mischievous laugh tinkled from Lou Yue's lips. \"What am I doing? Why, getting rid of you, of course.\"","With a flick of her sleeve, the door swung open at once, and fresh breeze poured in. Lou Yue pushed the golden ball out the door, then looked out into the distance.","Hmm, the sky was a bright, clear blue, the wind gentle and the sun warm. It was a perfect day to dump someone.","\"Goodbye, Xiao Rangchen.\"","Lou Yue's smile was bright and unbridled. She channeled spiritual energy into her fingertips and sent the golden ball holding Xiao Rangchen flying straight off the top deck.","\"Lou Yue!\"","The low, deep magnetic voice wrapped in towering fury made Lou Yue arch her eyebrows high. She was just squinting to savor the moment, when suddenly —","\"Crack-boom!\"","Silver lightning came crashing down from the sky, striking Lou Yue square on.","Her vision swam, her body tilted, and she toppled straight over the guardrail of the cloud skyship.","The sensation of weightlessness jolted her fully awake. She reacted instantly, latching onto the ship's railing to steady herself, but then an icy-blue water-type spell coiled around her ankle, the other end of the tether leading straight down to the golden ball below.","The one who cast the spell was not Xiao Rangchen. It was a tiny cyan puppy with a horn on its head, gritting its teeth and scrabbling frantically at the golden ball with its short little limbs.","Lou Yue recognized it at once as Xiao Rangchen's contract beast, Qinglin. But in the book, Qinglin wasn't supposed to hatch until long after Xiao Rangchen left the Xuandu sect. How was it here so early?","Lou Yue had no time to dwell on that. She immediately tried to use her spiritual energy to break the binding, but this seemingly ordinary water could devour spiritual energy. She had been fine before channeling her power, but the moment she did, the spiritual energy in her dantian was siphoned away. Her fingers went limp in an instant, and her grip on the railing slipped completely.","Wind roared in her ears, and the terror of death wrapped around her, thick and suffocating.","\"Lord Xuan! Save me!\"","\"Lord Xuan!!\"","Panicked, Lou Yue screamed out a name by instinct: \"Xuanba!!!\"","The second the name \"Xuanba\" left her mouth —","A dark red-black tortoise lunged straight out from the cloud skyship, its body swelling dozens of times in size as it dove toward Lou Yue like a falling meteor. A wisp of spiritual energy wrapped around her first, blocking the howling gale completely.","Still shaken to her core, Lou Yue gathered what little spiritual energy she had left to conjure a golden protective barrier of her own.","Xuanba caught up to Lou Yue steadily, landing at the exact same moment as Xiao Rangchen, and the impact blew a crater over ten feet wide into the ground. It had just climbed out of the pit to catch Lou Yue —","Thud! Lou Yue's golden ball slammed right into its tortoise shell. The barrier didn't shatter at all; instead, it bounced high into the air. Right after that, Xiao Rangchen's golden ball also crashed into the shell with a thud. The two golden spheres, one right after the other, bounced and hopped rapidly toward the Misty Forest, vanishing from sight in the blink of an eye.","Xuanba: ?","Lou Yue: ??","...","Deep in the shadowy forest, the bouncing golden balls startled flocks of birds and beasts into flight.","At first, Xiao Rangchen had kept his composure, but after the ball kept bouncing wildly for what felt like ages, a cold frost began to creep over his sharp, chiseled face.","\"Release me,\" he said, his tone heavy with irritation.","Lou Yue's golden sphere dropped high up in front of her. She turned her back to Xiao Rangchen, planted her hands on her hips and shouted back, \"If you're so capable, break it yourself!\"","But out of Xiao Rangchen's sight, Lou Yue was frantically flipping through a jade slip, and the second she saw the note that \"the protective barrier will break on its own once its spiritual energy is exhausted\", her spirits immediately deflated.","Lou Yue slumped down inside the sphere, filled with the exasperation of having shot herself in the foot.","Still, her moods always came and went quickly. After a moment, she consoled herself that a contracted beast could sense its master's location, so instead of fretting pointlessly right now, she might as well wait patiently.","Lou Yue turned around and sat down leisurely, deciding to find some fun to pass the time.","She propped up her chin, raised her eyes to glance teasingly at the man behind her who was striking the sphere's wall to no avail, and said, \"Hey, still haven't cracked it? Where's that little cyan dog of yours? Why don't you let it help you out?\"","Xiao Rangchen lifted his gaze, gave her a deep, fleeting glance, and said nothing.","Lou Yue kept chattering away, \"Don't tell me it ran out of spiritual energy and dropped halfway down? Hm... That's some karmic payback for it dragging me down here in the first place.\"","Xiao Rangchen suddenly stopped his movements. His dark eyes fixed sharply on her, and after a long moment, he stated with absolute certainty, \"You can't break it either.\"","Lou Yue's smile froze on her face.","Xiao Rangchen then sat down too, recovering his strength while keeping a vigilant watch over their surroundings.","At some point, even the wailing sound of wind drifting through the tree branches in the forest vanished, leaving only the dull thud of the golden sphere bouncing on the ground. The dead silence was eerie enough to make one's skin crawl.","After the sphere bounced around for nearly another hour, its glow gradually dimmed.","When Lou Yue's golden sphere finally landed, it hit a slanted rock, veering off course and crashing straight into the other golden sphere that was descending right then.","\"Pop!\"","Both golden spheres shattered at the same time. Without the protection of the barrier, Lou Yue and Xiao Rangchen were caught off guard and collided hard into each other!","\"Ow—\" Lou Yue yelped in pain, her nose smacking squarely into Xiao Rangchen's hard jaw.","Xiao Rangchen instinctively reached out to push her away, and Lou Yue did the same. In the scuffle, Lou Yue's fingers got tangled in Xiao Rangchen's hair, and the ornament on her waist caught in the chains of her shackles. They lost their balance completely and plummeted straight down from the high altitude.","Lou Yue twisted around, trying to make him land under her to cushion the fall, while Xiao Rangchen bent his elbow to fend her off. As a result, the two of them crashed sideways onto the ground at the same time.","Two crisp cracking sounds rang out.","Lou Yue's right arm bone, and Xiao Rangchen's left leg bone, broke in unison, accompanied by Lou Yue's yelp of pain and Xiao Rangchen's low groan.","As if things weren't bad enough for them, a scarlet giant mouth suddenly lunged out of the thick fog. Both of them instinctively dodged to the side, but they picked the exact same direction, crashing into each other hard again. In the end, they could only tumble across the ground in a thoroughly embarrassing mess to barely avoid the fatal bite.","\"You did that on purpose to get back at me, didn't you!!\" Lou Yue rolled into a mud pit, her clothes all soiled. She sat up holding her broken arm, pointed at Xiao Rangchen and yelled furiously.","Xiao Rangchen glanced at her disheveled, mud-covered state. The coldness in his eyes softened a little, his mood lightening, and he only let out a faint, cold huff.","The snake demon that had been completely ignored flew into a rage. Two more heads poked out of the thick fog, making it a three-headed serpent. Its forked tongue flicked and hissed, and its thick, scaled tail swept over carrying a fierce gust of wind.","Lou Yue stared at the three feral, scale-covered snake heads, her throat tightening. All her earlier fire vanished in the blink of an eye, and her body shook like a sieve, completely out of her control.","In this life, and even in her past life, the thing she feared most was snakes... and the one right in front of her was the maxed-out pro version. She felt like her soul was about to leave her body any second.","In the gaps between her clumsy dodges, Lou Yue unconsciously inched her feet toward where Xiao Rangchen was standing.","The snake demon, which no longer had to split up to hunt them down, was absolutely delighted by this. Its attacks grew more and more fierce, and its sweeping tail forced the two of them to retreat again and again.","Seeing Lou Yue huddle back to his side after he had tried to get her to keep her distance, Xiao Rangchen finally lost his patience and snapped, \"Do you have any common sense at all?\"","Lou Yue clenched her fists, forcing herself to hold her ground as she yelled even louder than him, \"Brainless! So what!\"","Xiao Rangchen was left speechless, unable to come up with a retort for a moment.","In that split second of distraction, the snake's tail lashed out and struck Xiao Rangchen. His balance gave way, and he stumbled backward, crashing right into Lou Yue who had been trying to duck behind him. The two of them slammed hard into a tree, shaking the dry leaves off the branches to patter down all around them.","Crushed between the snake tail's massive force, Xiao Rangchen's body, and the hard tree trunk, Lou Yue's chest ached so sharply she felt like it was splitting apart. She yelped in pain, \"You're squashing my chest flat!\"","Having used her to soften the impact, Xiao Rangchen curled his lips into a cold, mocking smirk, his tone icy and unbearably teasing. \"There wasn't much there to squash in the first place.\"","The cruel jab hit her like a ton of bricks. Lou Yue was so furious that a sweet taste rose in her throat, and she spat out a mouthful of blood. Her voice trembling, she spat out a vicious threat, \"Xiao Rangchen! I curse you to never have a chest for your whole life!\"","Xiao Rangchen, who naturally had no chest to speak of, let out a dismissive \"heh\", his tone cold and flippant enough to make Lou Yue want to jump right out of her skin.","Far angrier than her, the giant python demon reared all three of its heads high, looming over them like a dark blanket blotting out the sky. Its jaws split open, and three streams of purple flame burst forth. One stream coiled around the perimeter to shrink the space the two could use to dodge, while the other two shot straight toward them.","Lou Yue's eyes were fixed entirely on those three enormous snake heads, and she couldn't stop her legs from trembling where she stood.","Seeing her zoning out at such a critical moment, Xiao Rangchen didn't have time to think twice. Biting back the searing pain of his broken leg, he lunged over and rolled to the side with her in his arms.","Xiao Rangchen lifted his head, just about to explain that he had only saved her for Xiao Aiai's sake, when he caught sight of the thick beads of sweat covering her forehead and neck. Her face was deathly pale, her whole body shaking so badly that none of her usual brash, fiery attitude was left.","Xiao Rangchen frowned, unable to figure out what trick she was pulling this time.","Lou Yue forced herself to fix her gaze on Xiao Rangchen, and then she noticed a tuft of purple flame burning on his left calf, creeping steadily upward. Realizing the fire was about to reach her too, all the strength in Lou Yue's body came rushing back at once.","She shoved Xiao Rangchen away hard, her voice cracking as she shouted urgently and sharply, \"Get out of here!\"","Xiao Rangchen saw the unmistakeable, genuine look of wanting nothing to do with him in Lou Yue's eyes. His dark eyes sharpened instantly, and he flipped himself over to retreat a good distance away.","----------------------","Xiao Rangchen: Tch, he never should have saved her in the first place."]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["The purple flames searing his broken leg were far from numb to Xiao Rangchen, but his hands and feet were locked with spirit-sealing stone shackles, leaving him no way to put out this peculiar fire.","He glanced at Lou Yue in the distance, his voice devoid of any warmth. \"Unlock these shackles, or we'll both end up as this snake's meal.\"","Whether it was the mention of being devoured, or the two words \"both of us\" that struck a chord, the next second a key came flying toward him.","Xiao Rangchen lifted his hand and caught it with pinpoint accuracy. The shackles clattered to the ground, and his previously blocked spiritual power coursed freely through his meridians once more. He swept his right leg out, kicking up a cloud of dust, and as his right hand curled open, the black spear that Lou Yue had seized from him materialized out of thin air in a swirl of spiritual light.","Xiao Rangchen hurled it with all his might. The spear tip cut through the dust, driving straight into the only unarmored spot on the python demon's body—its eye.","\"HISS—!\"","The demon's pained wail shook the entire forest. Its massive tail lashed out wildly, but Xiao Rangchen pushed off with his one good leg to leap onto the snake's body, using the strength of his arms to twist and dodge, narrowly avoiding several heavy blows. In the blink of an eye, he closed in on the vital point where the three snake heads connected.","The demon was certain Xiao Rangchen could not break through its scale armor, so it only focused on spitting purple flames frantically.","Yet Xiao Rangchen reached straight through the gaps in its scales with a hooked hand, and when he pulled his hand back, he was clutching a throbbing, scarlet snake heart.","All three snake heads froze at once, full of utter disbelief. It had long gained sentience, and had easily judged that Lou Yue, with her fine clothing, had a far higher cultivation level. That was why even after Xiao Rangchen jumped onto its body, it had never taken this Foundation Establishment stage cultivator seriously. It could never have imagined he would be able to pierce the toughest part of its scale armor.","It died still confused.","But Lou Yue had seen clearly that when Xiao Rangchen reached into the snake's scales, his hand had been covered in a faint, water-like glow—it was that thing that had broken through the armor.","In the novel, there was a power called \"Spirit Bond Manifestation\" that originated from contracted spirit beasts. It could be used to armor one's body, and was known alongside the \"Dharma Aspect, Heaven and Earth\" technique as the two most powerful moves for cultivators. But \"Spirit Bond Manifestation\" required a level of mutual life-and-death trust and seamless tacit understanding between a master and their contracted beast that made its activation conditions a hundred times more stringent than those for \"Dharma Aspect, Heaven and Earth\", which could be mastered once one reached the Nascent Soul Great Perfection stage. In the novel, the male lead did not even cultivate \"Spirit Bond Manifestation\" until he reached the Great Vehicle stage. There was no way Xiao Rangchen could have it right now.","But if it really was \"Spirit Bond Manifestation\", then that would explain why Xiao Rangchen had been able to break out of the spirit-sealing cage earlier—and why he had not broken the shackles yet, because his \"Spirit Bond Manifestation\" was still immature at this stage?","Lou Yue pushed the chaotic thoughts down hard, telling herself it was probably just some kind of treasure, that she was overthinking things.","While she was lost in thought, Xiao Rangchen had already cut out the demon's inner core and stored it away. He gripped his spear and turned to walk toward her. Lou Yue's gaze fell on his dragging calf— the purple flames had gone out, leaving the flesh there charred black, a sight that made her wince with pity.","She frowned and instinctively looked away.","Xiao Rangchen abruptly stopped four meters away from Lou Yue, not coming any closer. His dark eyes fixed on that delicate, handsome face.","The trembling, sweating, panicked look Lou Yue had shown earlier was completely gone. All that remained was the haughty arrogance in her bones, and the clear rejection directed at him— as if all that earlier display had been nothing but an illusion.","A cold laugh escaped Xiao Rangchen's throat. Sure enough, it was all an act. The tricks of a pampered young master from a noble clan were nothing but tiresome.","\"What do I have to do to make you release my sister?\" Xiao Rangchen asked, his voice icy.","Lou Yue turned to look at him. \"What? You can't even keep yourself safe right now, and you still want to drag your sister into danger along with you?\"","Before Xiao Rangchen could reply, Lou Yue added another line. \"Your sister came with me of her own free will.\"","\"I don't believe that.\" Xiao Rangchen's cold eyes were full of disbelief.","Lou Yue let out a scoff, her gorgeous features twisting into clear disdain. \"Why is that impossible? Does she have to revolve entirely around you, putting your needs above everything else?\"","The annoyance she had felt back when she'd forced herself to read that harem novel came surging back all at once. In her mind, Xiao Rangchen instantly became utterly detestable. She raised her brows and huffed sharply. \"No one in this world owes anyone else the sacrifice of their own self. You have no right to stop her from being her own person.\"","\"And being with you counts as being her own person?\" Xiao Rangchen sneered back.","\"It's certainly better than staying with you,\" Lou Yue shot back.","The surrounding forest fell dead silent. The residual warmth of the purple flames drifted past the two of them.","Lou Yue turned her head to the side. What was the point of her wasting breath on this selfish, womanizing scumbag? Even with his harem full of beauties he never knew how to cherish, what difference would a few words from her make?","Lou Yue glanced at Xiao Rangchen out of the corner of her eye, her undisguised contempt plain to see. This scumbag deserved to be lonely for the rest of his life.","Xiao Rangchen caught the disdain in Lou Yue's sidelong glance, and a surge of anger flared up in him in an instant.","Cultivator clans all treated common folk like ants, and he had always been too cold and detached to care about that kind of behavior. But when Lou Yue looked at him like that, the contempt felt amplified a hundred times over, heavy enough to suffocate him. It made him want nothing more than to crush that proud look of hers to pieces...","The snake demon was dead, but the residual purple flames were still burning in the forest.","Lou Yue stared at the dancing flames and thought that Xiao Rangchen had sort of saved her just now. Even if he'd done it for Xiao Aiai's sake, she always believed in repaying debts, especially when the person she owed was the overpowered male lead of the novel.","Once they got back on the cloud skyship, she would let Xiao Aiai explain everything to him herself. That would count as paying back the favor.","\"Don't think I won't give you a chance—\" Lou Yue started, turning her head, but her words got stuck in her throat.","Xiao Rangchen had closed the distance between them in a split second, his sharp, icy aura sweeping straight toward her face. Lou Yue's heart jolted, and she instinctively stepped back.","CLICK!","The crisp clink of metal locking together rang out. The very same spirit-sealing stone shackles that Xiao Rangchen had worn earlier snapped tight around her ankle. The hand she had just lifted was wrenched behind her back with brute force, the grip so tight it felt like her bone was about to shatter.","Lou Yue's eyes went wide, her mind filled with nothing but a string of huge question marks. All her earlier thoughts about repaying the favor vanished in an instant, and fury burned through her.","To hell with that favor! Xiao Rangchen, I will never let you get away with this!","Xiao Rangchen tied Lou Yue's left hand securely behind her waist, leaving her broken right arm hanging limply at her side. Once he was done, he glanced impassively at the fury in her eyes, then turned to sit down on a nearby rock, pressing his palm to his broken leg.","A harsh, teeth-grating sound of grinding bones echoed out. Before Lou Yue could make sense of what he had done, he was already standing steadily, walking with a smooth, easy stride as if his leg had never been broken at all.","He reached out and tugged on the extra length of the rope binding her hands behind her back, not caring if she stumbled or stayed upright as he started heading toward the direction of the setting sun.","Lou Yue was yanked backward, and her foot caught on something, making her lose her balance and stagger. The back of her head slammed hard against another hard, solid head.","\"OW—!\"","Lou Yue yelped, tears nearly bursting out of her eyes from the pain.","Xiao Rangchen ground his teeth together so hard they ached, forcing himself not to turn around, and kept walking forward.","Lou Yue had just gotten steady on her feet when the pull on her waist came again. She hurried to follow along.","\"Xiao Rangchen! The tables will turn one day, don't you get too cocky!\" Lou Yue glared at the back of his head and fumed.","That head abruptly paused. Lou Yue barely managed to stop herself before she ran into him.","\"You just reminded me.\" Xiao Rangchen turned around slowly, a cold, menacing air rolling off him. \"I told you that day that I would make you regret this.\"","\"What do you think you're doing? Don't forget, your sister is still on my cloud skyship!\" Lou Yue used Xiao Aiai as leverage.","Xiao Rangchen said not a single word. He just kept advancing on her with icy pressure, the oppressive feeling crashing over her.","Lou Yue was completely at his mercy right now, so she decided that a smart woman did not pick a fight when she was at a disadvantage. She stepped back two paces, but Xiao Rangchen kept pressing closer. She bit her lip and stepped back again— and the next second, her heel caught on a raised tree root. The shackle on her ankle left her no way to steady herself, and she landed hard on her butt on the ground, her face crumpling up in pain.","A faint, triumphant smirk tugged at the corner of Xiao Rangchen's lips, softening his cold, sharp features with a hint of boyishness.","Lou Yue was just about to fly into a rage when she realized she could not get up— Xiao Rangchen had sealed her movements with his spiritual power.","\"Xiao Rangchen!\" she yelled, glaring up at him, the fury in her eyes almost bursting into flames.","Xiao Rangchen remained completely unmoved. He stepped forward, grabbed her by the back collar, and started dragging her along like a piece of trash, letting her bottom scrape against the rough ground.","\"Xiao Rangchen, you're out of your mind?!\"","\"Let go of me!\"","He kept walking at a steady pace, his tone flat and cold. \"Keep yelling, and I'll treat you exactly the way you treated me before.\"","Lou Yue instantly fell silent, repeating the age-old saying \"a wise woman does not pick a fight when the odds are against her\" to herself over and over.","But being able to tolerate it rationally did not mean her body could stand the discomfort.","The Lou clan was a lineage of spell and incantation practitioners, born with extraordinary spiritual perception but notoriously frail physiques, a trait the original body had inherited fully. Barely a quarter of an hour had passed before Lou Yue could not take it anymore. She was half-convinced her bottom had turned into a bright red braised pork belly, and a spicy one at that.","\"Fine! I'll let you see Xiao Aiai, will that satisfy you?!\" she gritted her teeth and caved in.","Xiao Rangchen finally stopped in his tracks and turned his head to look at her. \"I'm taking her away with me.\"","\"Whether she wants to go with you is her own choice. You cannot force her.\"","The protective edge in her tone made Xiao Rangchen's brows knit together.","Lou Yue was determined to get his promise, staring him down unyieldingly. \"Xiao Rangchen, you can't force her.\"","\"She's my sister, and you're nothing more than an outsider.\" His implication was clear: this was none of her business.","Lou Yue called his bluff coldly. \"You just don't dare to gamble. You're scared Xiao Aiai will choose not to go with you.\"","It was a blunt goading tactic, but Xiao Rangchen had to admit it worked on him.","\"If I win, you will not stand in our way,\" he stated.","Lou Yue lifted her gaze, a determined, unyielding glint shining in her eyes. \"If I win, you are never to seek her out again unless she decides to meet you on her own accord.\"","Their gazes clashed mid-air, one brimming with unruly confidence, the other sharp and unyielding. Even the wind around them seemed to still for a moment.","After a long while, Xiao Rangchen released the back of Lou Yue's collar and undid the spell he had cast on her legs. Lou Yue immediately jumped to her feet and put a safe distance between herself and him.","The two traveled in silence for what felt like ages, before Xiao Rangchen noticed the footsteps behind him growing more and more sluggish. He turned around to look at her, his gaze laced with impatience. \"Are you seriously insisting on wasting our time here, in a place teeming with hidden dangers?\"","\"Then why don't you call out your contracted beast? Aren't you worried something might have happened to it?\" Lou Yue shot back sarcastically.","Xiao Rangchen let out a cold snort. \"Young Master Lou spends all his days indulging in pleasure and debauchery. You really should spend some time using that brain of yours to learn basic sense. If word got out that you can't even tell directions apart, you'd be disgracing your entire clan.\"","Lou Yue truly had no sense of direction—back in her modern life, she had never done any wilderness survival training. But hearing those words come out of Xiao Rangchen's mouth, the second time he had called her brainless, she was genuinely furious.","\"Xiao Rangchen, one day, I'll make you kneel down and beg me,\" she swore to herself. Beg me to spare you, beg me to stop snatching away all your lucky chances and stealing all your romantic interests.","Lou Yue held her head high with haughty pride, even with her clothes dirty and her limbs previously bound.","Xiao Rangchen had no idea where she got such unbridled confidence. Seeing the disdain in her eyes that treated him like a random weed to be trampled underfoot, he stepped closer. His tall figure cast a long shadow that completely enveloped her. \"Not in this lifetime, not in the next, not ever. That day will never come.\"","\"Then we'll just see about that,\" Lou Yue tilted her head up and curled her lips into a sharp smile, her eyes full of unyielding grit. \"Let's see who will be the first to lower their head and admit defeat.\"","The slanting sunset filtered through the treetops, falling on Lou Yue's dust-streaked face, making her stubborn, fiery eyes glow brilliantly.","Xiao Rangchen said nothing more and turned to walk ahead.","Spurred on by their petty rivalry, Lou Yue did not drag her feet for the rest of the journey. Even with the searing pain on her bottom and her legs aching and trembling so badly they felt like giving out, she bit her lip and did not make a single sound of complaint. Xiao Rangchen also did not stop, nor did he look back, even though the rope tied between them was feeling heavier and heavier.","All of a sudden, rustling noises came from not far away. Lou Yue sensed something, and focused her gaze in that direction.","Moments later, the grass parted, and a small red-black tortoise crawled out. Its long, scale-covered tail was coiled around a little cyan-colored puppy that was even bigger than itself.","Lou Yue's face lit up with joy for a split second, before she looked on in disgust. \"Took you long enough. If you'd been any later, I probably would've collapsed from wobbly legs and kneeled right in front of Xiao Rangchen.\"","\"Whimper whimper...\" Qinglin looked at Xiao Rangchen with a pitiful, helpless expression.","Xiao Rangchen glanced at Xuanba, then turned his gaze back to Lou Yue. \"Let it go, and take me to see my sister.\"","\"Untie the rope first,\" Lou Yue insisted.","Xiao Rangchen shot her a quick glance, then raised his hand to undo the rope tied around her waist. At the same time, the key Lou Yue had tossed to him earlier appeared in his palm. \"Release it.\"","The moment Qinglin was set free, the key was passed back into Lou Yue's hand.","Spiritual energy surged through her legs, and the soreness vanished instantly. But the burning pain on her bottom was still there—Lou Yue was sure the skin had been scraped raw, otherwise the friction of her clothes against the wound would not hurt so much when she walked. But she did not show a single sign of discomfort on her face. Even in front of her own contracted beast, she did not want anyone to find out the embarrassing fact that she had been dragged across the ground.","\"Where's the cloud skiff? I'm tired,\" Lou Yue tapped the tortoise shell under her feet, looking down at it as she spoke.","Xuanba did not move. It spoke slowly and lazily. \"The cloud skiff is waiting at the next hill. We have to go through this forest and climb another mountain to get there.\"","Lou Yue froze, raising her voice in shock. \"Why didn't the cloud skiff wait for me here?\"","\"Hovering in the air consumes too many spirit stones,\" Xuanba replied calmly.","\"Do I look like I'm short on that tiny number of spirit stones?!\"","Xuanba said plainly, \"But I am.\"","Lou Yue was left completely speechless.","For the sake of saving spirit stones, Xuanba expanded its body so Lou Yue could sit on its back. Lou Yue hesitated for a second before steeling herself and sitting down. She immediately raised her sleeve to cover her face, hiding the grimace of pain that had twisted her features.","The forest stretched on endlessly, home to many high-level demonic beasts. To avoid drawing unwanted attention, none of them used their spiritual power, suppressing their auras as they moved forward at a snail's pace. By the time they caught sight of the cloud skiff, the sun had already risen the next morning.","Lou Yue slid down from the tortoise shell listlessly, tossed a quick \"wait here\" over her shoulder, and marched onto the cloud skiff without looking back.","Xiao Rangchen narrowed his eyes slightly, his gaze lingering on the slightly awkward way Lou Yue was walking, before he slowly looked away.","Lou Yue thought to herself, Hmph, you dead scumbag, just you wait.","Xiao Rangchen thought to himself, Prejudice in a person's heart is like a towering mountain that no one can easily move."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["\"Brother!\"","Xiao Aiai hurried down the steps in no time.","The hard, cold lines on Xiao Rangchen's face softened a little, and he stepped forward to meet her.","\"What's wrong with your leg?\" Xiao Aiai said, already bending over to check the blackened, burnt wound, only to be pulled back by Xiao Rangchen.","\"It's nothing.\" His tone was calm and unconcerned.","\"Don't try to fool me!\" Xiao Aiai's pretty brows knit into a tight frown, huffing angrily. \"No matter how bad your injury is, you always downplay it as a casual 'nothing'.\"","Xiao Rangchen patted her gently to soothe her. \"It really is nothing. Don't you trust me?\"","Xiao Aiai dodged his hand, her eyes stubborn. \"It's already in such a state, and you still say it's nothing. I could clearly help, but you always treat me like a little kid!\"","Xiao Rangchen paused for a moment. \"As long as your big brother is here, Aiai, all you need to do is be happy. I promised Mother I would protect you forever.\"","Xiao Aiai looked straight into his eyes, her expression earnest. \"Brother, I've already decided to go to Xuandu with her.\"","Xiao Rangchen's hand, which had been hanging mid-air, dropped to his side. \"Aiai, her words can't be trusted.\"","\"She didn't even persuade me. I came to this decision on my own.\" Xiao Aiai bit her lower lip.","\"No, I won't allow it.\" Xiao Rangchen's face darkened, his tone turning sharp. \"Lou Yue is frivolous and unrestrained, no good person at all. If you follow her, you'll only get hurt.\" He stared at Xiao Aiai, pressing her in a low, stern voice. \"Is it because you have a crush on her?\"","Xiao Aiai's almond eyes went wide. Unbidden, the memory of that day when sunlight streamed through the window and fell on Lou Yue's profile flashed through her mind. Her cheeks burned instantly, and she quickly turned her face away to deny it. \"No! Brother, what nonsense are you talking about!\"","Xiao Rangchen had watched Xiao Aiai grow up, so that flustered, shy look could not be hidden from him. Remembering how Lou Yue had tricked and teased him the day before, his lips pressed into a tight straight line, and his voice carried clear irritation. \"You are not allowed to go with her!\"","\"Why not?\" Xiao Aiai was so angry and upset that her eyes turned red.","\"Don't be fooled by her appearance. Even if she's a little interested in you right now, with her flighty, romantic nature, how long do you think that will last?\" Every word he said was laced with overpowering firmness. \"Aiai, stay far away from her.\"","But his warnings did no good at all. Xiao Aiai stood her ground firmly. \"No matter what you say, I'm going to Xuandu with her.\"","\"We can go there by ourselves.\"","\"It's not the same!\" Following him would only be a burden to her, and the only way to get the rare Buyan Flower that grew in Xuandu was to go with Lou Yue. \"Brother, stop talking. I won't go with you!\"","Xiao Rangchen only thought she had been bewitched by Lou Yue. His anger toward Lou Yue flared up even more, and he reached out to grab Xiao Aiai's wrist, determined to take her away by force.","Just then, a group of people stepped down from the cloud boat.","Little Qiu walked at the front. His eyes landed on their clasped wrists, and he wore a smiling, obsequious expression. \"Have you two finished your talk? My master is here to ask for Miss Xiao's decision.\"","\"Aiai.\" Xiao Rangchen's voice was icy and commanding.","Xiao Aiai gritted her teeth, looked up at Little Qiu, and said, \"My decision hasn't changed.\"","Little Qiu smiled and stepped to the side, holding his hand out in a gesture of invitation.","\"Brother, I'll come back for you.\" Xiao Aiai gave Xiao Rangchen one last look, steeled her heart, and turned to step quickly onto the cloud boat.","Xiao Rangchen's expression instantly turned stormy. He lifted his foot to chase after her, but two guards blocked his path.","\"Young Master Xiao,\" Little Qiu's voice rang out from behind the guards. \"My master told me to remind you not to forget the agreement.\"","As if sensing something, Xiao Rangchen suddenly looked up toward the top deck of the cloud boat.","The morning sun was just rising, spilling thousands of golden rays that gilded the magnificent cloud boat with a shimmering edge. The carved doors of the top cabin were wide open, and Lou Yue, dressed in a new red robe, was leaning lazily on the white jade railing.","Her uninjured right hand propped casually under her chin, the corner of her lips tugged up in a half-smirk, half-amused arc. The sidelong gaze in her eyes carried an innate air of noble arrogance, glowing like a burning fire under the golden sunlight, bright and scorching.","The formation patterns carved into the hull lit up one after another, and as streams of light coursed across its surface, the cloud boat slowly lifted off the ground, kicking up a strong gust of wind.","The wind blew straight against Xiao Rangchen's face, tangling the stray locks of hair over his forehead.","He stood rooted to the spot, his gaze trailing the cloud boat as it pulled further and further away, until it vanished completely into the thick layers of clouds.","\"Woof?\"","Xiao Rangchen bent down to pick up Qinglin, brushing the fallen leaves off its back. \"It's nothing.\"","\"Woof woof woof!\"","\"I'm not giving up,\" a flash of unyielding stubbornness flickered in Xiao Rangchen's eyes. \"If the mountain will not come to me, I will go to the mountain.\" Even if he had to walk every step of the way, he would still reach Xuandu.","Qinglin nuzzled his palm, then suddenly froze and tilted its head to stare at the sky. Xiao Rangchen looked up too—","Beneath the sprawling morning glow, the cloud boat burst out from the depths of the clouds wrapped in warm golden light, dragging a trail of crimson-gold radiance as it descended right in front of him.","Xiao Rangchen's gaze swept past the empty white jade railing at the top deck and landed on the group of people who had just stepped off the boat.","Little Qiu wore a wide, ingratiating grin on his face. \"Young Master Xiao, my young master couldn't bear to see Miss Xiao sad, so he specially invites you to ride the cloud boat with us to Xuandu.\"","Xiao Rangchen froze for a moment. He could not figure out what devious scheme Lou Yue was cooking up this time, but getting to travel to Xuandu together was the best possible outcome for him. The moment his foot touched the boat deck, the cloud boat swayed gently before shooting straight up into the air, darting into the clouds in the blink of an eye, so fast it seemed to leave no room for anyone to change their mind.","Meanwhile, in the luxurious top cabin of the cloud boat.","Lou Yue sat on the edge of the bed draped in snow fox fur, her eyes blazing like a wildfire. \"What a Heaven’s Chosen One, indeed!\"","She had felt a killing urge toward Xiao Rangchen, and the heavens had struck her with a lightning bolt.","She had tossed him off the cloud boat, and another bolt had struck her.","Just a moment ago, when she had abandoned him to leave with Xiao Aiai, the heavens had hit her with three lightning bolts in a row! If her control over spiritual power had not grown so much more skillful by now, she would have been charred to a crisp the very first time.","\"Five lightning bolts, huh,\" she gritted her teeth. \"I'm keeping count.\" Not to mention that other account of getting her butt dragged earlier. Even if Xiao Rangchen was just getting back at her for whipping him back then, she was never going to swallow that anger.","Lou Yue punched down hard, her voice ringing with sharp resolve. \"Xiao Rangchen, this is just the start of settling the scores between us!\"","\"Why are you punching me when you want to vent your anger on the guy downstairs?\" Xuanba poked its head out from under her fist, its tone dripping with exasperation.","Lou Yue grabbed it at once and held it right up to her face. \"Why shouldn't I punch you? What were you doing when I was getting struck by lightning?\"","\"You were enjoying the show!\" Lou Yue laughed angrily. \"Were you just waiting for me to kick the bucket so you could get a new master?\"","Xuanba flicked its long tail, sounding completely unconcerned. \"You're not going to die. Besides, you'd better get used to this as soon as possible.\"","\"You're cursing me to get struck by lightning every day from now on?!\" Lou Yue could not believe her ears.","Xuanba simply tucked its head back into its turtle shell, refusing to engage with this nonsensical conversation.","Lou Yue stared at the bright red mark that looked just like the number 8 on its turtle shell, remembering the name she had blurted out when she fell off the boat earlier. A wicked smirk spread across her face. \"Heh, I've unilaterally decided your new name is Xuanba! The 'ba' part is the same character as in 'turtle'.\"","Xuanba, the bastard, did not respond at all, acting like it was just going to laze around and not even care if its master lived or died. Lou Yue huffed in frustration, thinking that the original owner of this body really had led a pathetic life.","A contractual beast that was not even loyal to her, obsequious attendants, a father who never bothered to look after anything...","She flopped down heavily, then rolled over onto her stomach on the soft mattress, poking at the patterns on Xuanba's shell as she pondered. There was no way around bringing Xiao Rangchen to Xuandu now, but she was not about to just swallow all this resentment and let it go.","The original story only gave a brief account of Xiao Rangchen's journey to Xuandu, but he was destined to make a name for himself on the day of the Enlightenment under the Longevity Birthday Ancient Tree. Not only would he obtain the Buyan Flower that could restore broken spiritual veins, but later, he would also enter the \"Queyun Sheng\" and gain his golden finger — a senior expert living in his consciousness. The original host of this body was the one who suffered a crushing defeat to Xiao Rangchen at the ancient tree enlightenment, only to later discover that the white moonlight he had long admired had taken a special liking to Xiao Rangchen. It was that exact moment that twisted his resentment into a lifelong, all-consuming grudge.","But no one knew if it was the effect of Lou Yue crossing over into this world, or some other unknown factor, she had met Xiao Rangchen far earlier than the plot dictated. As if it was a punishment, or perhaps a necessary measure to keep the storyline on track, the Heavenly Dao forced her to bring Xiao Rangchen along to Xuandu.","In fact, judging from the five thunderbolts that had struck down earlier, it was true as Xuanba had said — those strikes were never meant to kill her. Maybe she could try once more to...","Lou Yue's fingers, which had been picking at the tortoise shell, suddenly paused, and she quickly cast that thought aside. There was no telling if the Heavenly Dao would unleash even harsher punishments next time, and more importantly...","All at once, Xiao Rangchen's cold, stern face popped into her mind.","Lou Yue ground her teeth, mentally crushing that imaginary face to pieces. More importantly, she, Lou Yue, could never be no match for Xiao Rangchen! How could she admit defeat before the game had even properly started?","\"I am definitely going to beat Xiao Rangchen!\" Lou Yue declared with full, bold resolve. She unceremoniously dumped Xuanba aside, jumped to her feet, and immediately began to cultivate.","A breeze drifted in from the depths of the sea of clouds, carrying a faint, crisp dampness that made the pennants hanging on both sides of the cloud boat snap sharply in the wind. Little Qiu led Xiao Rangchen past the flapping pennants and down to the cloud boat's lower cabin.","The lower cabin was divided into dozens of small rooms meant for the guards and maids. Each room housed eight people, fitted with two-tier wooden bunk beds, only partitioned off by rough linen curtains for a modicum of privacy.","Little Qiu stopped in front of one of the rooms that was not yet full. \"I apologize for the humble arrangements, Young Master Xiao. Your meals will be sent to you here on time.\" There was a meaningful glint in Little Qiu's smile. \"There are so many people on this cloud boat that rumors spread easily. I would advise you not to wander around without good reason, and especially not to meet people you have no business seeing. My young master has made it clear that once we arrive in Xuandu, you are free to leave whenever you wish, no need to report to anyone.\"","He deliberately observed Xiao Rangchen's expression as he spoke, and only after seeing that the man's cold face did not show the slightest ripple of emotion did he bow slightly and turn to leave.","Xiao Rangchen's eyes darkened. Lou Yue's intentions were still unclear, but those words had made it obvious that she was forbidding him from meeting Xiao Aiai. The very thought of Lou Yue stirred up an inexplicable restlessness in his chest, making him feel unwell all over.","He suppressed that discomfort, swept his gaze across the cabin, casually picked an upper bunk, and flipped himself up onto it. He had slept out in the wilderness before, and laid on frozen cold ground, so these conditions were already more than good enough. If Lou Yue had hoped to make things difficult for him with this, her plan was completely futile.","Qinglin let out a soft, whimpering cry. Xiao Rangchen whispered to soothe it to go back, and Qinglin, its little head drooping, transformed into a streak of cyan light and darted into his chest to hide away.","Using the linen curtain as cover, Xiao Rangchen loosened his belt and took off his outer robes.","The dim light outlined his firm, tall shoulders and back, the lines sharp and hard, brimming with raw power. Dozens of old and new scars crisscrossed across his back, and there was a piercing through wound on his right chest, the flesh around it turned outward, dark and gray.","Xiao Rangchen bit down on a strip of coarse cloth, and with deft, practiced movements, used his dagger to cut away the rotting dead flesh, his other hand quickly sprinkling hemostatic medicinal powder over the wound. After resting for a short moment, he lifted his arm to reach behind his back to treat the other end of the piercing wound. Since his view was blocked, his movements slowed a little, and the coarse cloth in his teeth was crumpled out of shape.","After he finished treating the wounds on his upper body, he followed the exact same process to deal with the purple flame burns on his legs. By the time all his injuries were properly bandaged, he released the cloth from his jaws, leaned against the cabin board, and panted softly. Beads of sweat dripped down his sharp jawline and onto his abdomen.","A strange, faint tickle came from his stomach. Xiao Rangchen slowly lowered his head, narrowed his eyes, and picked out a slightly curled dark strand of hair from the crevice of his abdominal muscles.","In an instant, he knew exactly who it belonged to.","He flicked it away forcefully, then rubbed his fingertips against the fabric of his clothes.","After a moment, he twisted it again. After quite a while, he clicked his tongue in exasperation.","----------------------","Xiao Rangchen: This hair is just as annoying as its owner."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["Xiao Rangchen took quite a while to calm himself. He was just about to sit down and cultivate when a timid young voice came from outside the bed curtains.","“Are you asleep?”","Xiao Rangchen pulled open the curtains. Standing beside the bed was a slender youth of about sixteen or seventeen.","When he saw Xiao Rangchen looking at him, the boy gave a shy smile. “I—I’m the one who sleeps in the bunk below yours. My name is Chai Zhuang.”","“Xiao Rangchen.” Seeing that he was still standing there, Xiao Rangchen asked indifferently, “Is there something you need?”","“N-no, nothing... Oh, no, actually, there is something...” Chai Zhuang’s eyes darted toward Xiao Rangchen’s side, as if searching for something. When he met Xiao Rangchen’s gaze, he awkwardly tugged at the blue guard uniform he was wearing. “Just now, I saw you holding a little blue-green beast. Is that your contracted beast?”","Xiao Rangchen gave a quiet “Mm.”","Summoning his courage, Chai Zhuang looked up at him and asked in a small voice, “C-can I ask where you got it?”","Xiao Rangchen frowned slightly.","Chai Zhuang hurriedly defended himself. “Brother Xiao, don’t misunderstand! I didn’t mean anything by it—”","“He didn’t mean anything by it? He’s just coveting your contracted beast, hahaha!” The burly man across from them, who was removing his wrist guards, snorted mockingly. Another man followed with a burst of laughter.","Chai Zhuang’s face flushed crimson. He said anxiously, “That’s not it, Brother Xiao! I’m not coveting it. I really just wanted to ask!”","“Chai Zhuang, the young master merely said you were ‘not bad,’ and you actually took it seriously? Go take a piss and look at yourself—how much do you think you’re worth? And you want a contracted beast? Even if you had one, would it ever be your turn to get it?!”","The other man teased, “I say, Xiong Wu, are you jealous that Chai Zhuang received the young master’s praise?”","“Jealous of that pretty boy? Hell no!” Xiong Wu spat.","He looked at Chai Zhuang with contempt and sneered. “Praise? Do you really think the young master still remembers something he said offhand a year ago? Even if you stood right in front of him, he wouldn’t recognize you!”","Xiao Rangchen’s expression suddenly stiffened for an instant.","“N-no, that’s not...” Chai Zhuang’s lips trembled. He was unable to say anything more for a long while. At last, he lowered his head and murmured, “I have to change shifts,” before hurrying away as if fleeing.","“Hmph. What a coward.” Xiong Wu cursed at his back.","Xiao Rangchen’s indifferent gaze settled on Xiong Wu.","“Brother, Steward Qiu seemed pretty polite to you just now. Are you a newly assigned guard?” the other man asked.","Xiong Wu glanced at Xiao Rangchen, tossed his wrist guards aside, and sneered. “Him? A few days ago, he was still locked up in the water dungeon. He only escaped and then got captured again.”","“Then how did he end up here?”","Xiong Wu tugged at the eyepatch covering his face. His remaining eye crawled over Xiao Rangchen with a greasy, disgusting look.","“That’s something you’ll have to ask him. Back then, the young master dismissed everyone and did something shameful with him in the garden—”","Xiao Rangchen appeared before Xiong Wu like a ghost. The tip of his dagger was nearly pressed against Xiong Wu’s single eye.","“Hey, brother, let’s talk this out!” The other man hurriedly tried to intervene. “Guards who fight among themselves are severely punished. Put that down first!”","Xiao Rangchen ignored him. “Continue.”","His cold tone sent a chill through Xiong Wu. Xiao Rangchen’s fingers were clamped around both his wrists, right over his vital points, their bones hard as iron. They were both Foundation Establishment cultivators, yet Xiong Wu was completely powerless to resist. He felt as though his wrist bones were about to be crushed.","His heart trembling, Xiong Wu realized that this man’s true strength was far beyond what he appeared to possess.","A poisonous look flashed through his eyes, but he also knew that clashing head-on with Xiao Rangchen would do him no good.","“I’m sorry!” The flesh on Xiong Wu’s face twisted. “My mouth got ahead of me!”","“All right, Xiong Wu has apologized. Brother, be the bigger man and let him off this time.”","The other man tried to play peacemaker and reach for Xiao Rangchen. Xiao Rangchen withdrew his hand before the man could touch him. Once released, Xiong Wu instinctively retreated two steps.","Xiao Rangchen stared down at him. “If there’s a next time, I’ll make sure you can never open your mouth again.”","Xiong Wu lowered his head, hiding the sinister look in his eyes.","Xiao Rangchen left and walked to the end of the passageway. Through the window, he gazed at the clouds roiling behind the airship and slowly exhaled.","Sure enough, the kind of master one had determined the kind of guards one attracted...","Up in the top cabin, Lou Yue suddenly sneezed.","She rubbed her nose, then sneezed twice more. With a solemn expression, she said, “Someone’s cursing me.”","After thinking for a moment, she declared, “It must be Xiao Rangchen. He’s the only one who harbors such deep resentment toward me!”","Xuanba had originally had no intention of responding to Lou Yue’s muttering. But hearing the certainty in her voice, he slowly poked his head out.","“You’re underestimating yourself.”","Lou Yue: “?”","Xuanba said, “The people who resent you could circle this entire airship several times.”","Lou Yue’s face twisted as though she had swallowed something bitter. “...You’re making me feel like I’m in grave danger.”","Xuanba showed no remorse. Instead, he added fuel to the fire. “Once we reach Xuandu, you’ll be in even greater danger.”","“Why?”","“Because you’re too arrogant on a daily basis.”","Lou Yue: “...”","Because of Xuanba’s provocation, Lou Yue threw herself into cultivation for three full days. Aside from memorizing the Lou family’s illustrated manuals that Little Qiu had obtained for her and getting the sleep she absolutely needed, she devoted every remaining moment to cultivation. She worked harder than she had during her college entrance exams.","As a result, she missed the visit from Xiao Aiai, who had gone to see Xiao Rangchen.","“They talked for a long time?” Lou Yue asked Little Qiu, who had come to report the matter.","“They chatted on the deck for about fifteen minutes. The young master had given orders beforehand that Miss Xiao was to be treated as a guest, so no one was allowed to approach them. I don’t know what they discussed.”","“What about Xiao Rangchen?”","“After seeing Miss Xiao, he returned to the lower cabin. He spent most of his time meditating on his bed. At night, he would go to the rear deck to practice with his spear and only return at dawn.”","Lou Yue had initially intended to rest for a day. Upon hearing this, she ground her teeth. “He didn’t sleep?”","Little Qiu paused, then answered, “It seems not.”","“Is he even human?”","After dismissing Little Qiu, Lou Yue paced back and forth across the room. She took several deep breaths before sitting back down on the bed.","So he wanted to compete, did he? Who was she to be afraid?","This bout of cultivation lasted from morning until the following day before finally coming to an end.","Feeling the spiritual energy within her body remain stubbornly fixed at the middle stage of the Golden Core realm, Lou Yue experienced, for the first time, the frustration of having great ambitions but no way to fulfill them.","In the novel, Lou Yue’s talent had ranked at the very bottom of the Lou family. The Lou clan had maintained its position as one of the four great families through a perception-based talent passed down from generation to generation, with the talent being especially pronounced among the direct descendants.","Lou Yue, however, was an anomaly. She was as direct a descendant as one could possibly be, yet her perceptive abilities were no better than those of an ordinary cultivator. As for her Golden Core cultivation, it was merely an impressive facade piled together with rare treasures of heaven and earth.","No, this wouldn’t do. She needed to get outside and take a breath of fresh air. If she kept shutting herself away to cultivate, she was going to develop depression!","The moment Lou Yue came downstairs, Dou’er, who had been waiting for several days, caught her.","“You finally came out, Young Master!” Dressed in an especially flamboyant manner, Dou’er threw herself into Lou Yue’s arms and complained that she had forgotten all about her.","Dou’er sobbed theatrically. “Little Qiu said you were cultivating and wouldn’t let me go upstairs, but Dou’er missed you, Young Master, so I had no choice but to wait here every day...”","Lou Yue raised a hand and gently patted her. “I’m free today. I can keep you company for a while.”","Dou’er had defeated her sisters with great difficulty just to get onto the airship. How could she possibly waste this opportunity?","“Young Master, Dou’er learned a new dance. I want to perform it for you. Shall we go to the deck?”","Lou Yue readily agreed.","Before long, a soft couch had been set up on the deck. Several maids stood around Dou’er, each holding a musical instrument.","Lou Yue was initially surprised that the maids were proficient in music as well. Then she thought about it and realized that, given her status as a member of an aristocratic clan, even the servants must have been selected through layer upon layer of screening. It was hardly strange for them to be talented in many different areas.","On the spacious deck, songs and dances flourished. Lou Yue reclined on her side, her slightly curled black hair spilling across the snow-white fur cushion. One hand supported her forehead while the other rested on her raised knee, her posture languid and uninhibited.","When the song and dance ended, Dou’er, glistening with sweat, threw herself into Lou Yue’s arms and asked sweetly, “Young Master, did I dance beautifully?”","Lou Yue hurried to praise her, giving her all the emotional reassurance she wanted. “Beautiful. You’re gorgeous no matter what you do, Dou’er.”","Dou’er pouted coquettishly and slid her lotus arms around Lou Yue’s neck. She puckered her lips and leaned in for a kiss, but Lou Yue tilted her head slightly, allowing the kiss to land on her chin instead. With a light push, she sent Dou’er back and teased, “Don’t be so eager.”","“Mm~ Young Master, how am I acting like a monkey~?” Dou’er whined coquettishly, twisting her body.","A handsome man and a beautiful woman, whispering sweet nothings to each other.","In the distance, Xiao Rangchen turned his face away, refusing to look at such blatant daytime indecency.","He was standing far away, yet he still couldn’t stop Lou Yue’s nearly murmured words from burrowing into his ears. Her voice was not as deep and resonant as that of an ordinary man. When she softened it to coax someone, it was like the tinkling drops of water formed by melting snow in early spring, striking blue-gray stone again and again—impossible to drive away, and deeply distracting.","“Brother Xiao, did I say something wrong?” Chai Zhuang asked awkwardly.","It was no secret that Xiao Rangchen came to the deck every night to practice his spearwork. The previous night, Chai Zhuang had mustered up the courage to approach him with a question about spear techniques. He had expected to be mocked, but Xiao Rangchen had not only answered patiently; after learning that Chai Zhuang also cultivated the spear path, he had even offered to teach him some of his insights in the coming days.","This was their lesson for the day. Unfortunately, they had barely exchanged a few words when singing and dancing began on the forward deck.","Chai Zhuang had long since grown used to it, but Xiao Rangchen, standing before him, had his brows tightly furrowed, as though enduring tremendous discomfort.","“No. Continue,” Xiao Rangchen said in a low voice.","Chai Zhuang became even more cautious, stumbling over his words as he spoke. Xiao Rangchen pointed out one flaw and began explaining his own understanding of it, but halfway through, he suddenly stopped, as if his mind had wandered. Only after a while did he continue.","“Brother Xiao, do you dislike the music? If it’s bothering you, should we talk later? It probably won’t stop anytime soon up front.”","Xiao Rangchen had been about to deny it, but then Lou Yue’s soft laughter drifted into his ears again. The words at the tip of his tongue changed.","“Mm.”","Just as he was leaving, Xiao Rangchen suddenly asked, “They said before that Lou Yue once praised you as ‘not bad’?”","Chai Zhuang hurriedly waved his hands. “I didn’t go around telling people! That time, Xiong Wu and I were on duty together. He just happened to overhear it.”","Xiao Rangchen raised a hand to stop him. “There’s no need to be nervous.”","“You needn’t care how others see you. The road of cultivation is long and arduous. The person who determines your future has never been anyone else, but you yourself.”","Chai Zhuang had never expected Xiao Rangchen to say something like that to him. His shoulders trembled slightly, and a glimmer of tears flashed in his eyes as he stared at Xiao Rangchen’s sharp, resolute features. He nodded firmly.","“Brother Xiao, I’ll remember that!”","...","The glow on the horizon was gradually swallowed by dusk, and the clamor of the day was slowly quieted. Lamps shone across the cloudship, bathing the cold silver radiance in a warm hue.","Lou Yue had soaked in the private bath in her quarters. Although bathing in her underclothes was uncomfortable, she was even less willing to see her flat chest and the other parts of her body that she couldn’t bear to face. Fortunately, balancing work with relaxation had temporarily allowed her to forget the frustration of her slow cultivation.","However, when she happened to glance at the figure practicing with a spear on the deck after returning to the upper cabin, all the “relaxation” she had enjoyed that day went to waste.","Xiao Rangchen wore nothing more than a coarse hemp robe, yet it could not conceal his broad shoulders, narrow waist, and upright figure. As his long spear swept through the air, the wind shrieked around it, each movement sharp, forceful, and decisive.","Lou Yue felt irritated just looking at him. When he leaped into the air, she took the opportunity to throw a strand of spiritual power at his feet, attempting to bind them.","Xiao Rangchen reacted with astonishing speed. He twisted in midair and dodged the spiritual restraint.","Lou Yue clicked her tongue and turned to walk up the wooden stairs leading to the third level.","Thunk!","The long spear that had been in Xiao Rangchen’s hands moments earlier suddenly shot forward, carrying the force of a thousand jun, and slammed into the wooden step directly in front of her."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["Behind Lou Yue came Xiao Rangchen’s icy voice.","“You tricked my sister into going to Xuandu with you using the Buyan Flower. Lou Yue, what exactly are you trying to do?”","Lou Yue turned around leisurely.","From the moment Xiao Rangchen had been brought aboard the cloudship, Lou Yue had never intended to hide it from Xiao Aiai. She had expected Xiao Rangchen to come see her. After all, a friendship spanning more than a decade was not something she could sever so easily. Since Xiao Rangchen knew about the Buyan Flower, his learning the truth was only natural.","In fact, this was the outcome she had tacitly allowed.","On some subconscious level, she did not want to stop Xiao Rangchen from restoring his spiritual meridians. She wanted to defeat him fair and square. But that was something she could never tell Xiao Rangchen.","She bent slightly at the waist, looking down at the person half a meter below her. Her tone was carefree and unruly. “Why don’t you guess?”","Seeing the half-amused, half-mocking curve of Lou Yue’s lips, Xiao Rangchen wanted nothing more than to press that teasing smile flat. He pursed his lips and said sternly, “I won’t let you succeed.”","Lou Yue’s damp hair hung loose, its slightly curled strands clinging to her cheeks and accentuating her delicate features. Her smile deepened, her voice laced with scorn. “Don’t speak too soon. Be careful you don’t end up eating your words.”","“That applies to you as well.” Xiao Rangchen’s throat bobbed as his gaze swept inch by inch over her confident, flamboyant face. “Lou Yue, things won’t always go according to your wishes.”","At that, the smile faded from Lou Yue’s lips.","Xiao Rangchen’s words seemed to mock all her efforts as futile. She would never change the outcome—just as she could never change her own cultivation talent.","Spiritual energy abruptly gathered in her palm. Xiao Rangchen immediately retreated, but Lou Yue swiftly closed the distance, deliberately hurling the unstable ball of energy in her hand straight at his face.","Xiao Rangchen did not dare underestimate her. He raised both arms to block it, but Lou Yue suddenly bent her other knee and kicked fiercely at his chest. The angle was vicious and entirely lacking in rules.","Xiao Rangchen’s pupils contracted. His left arm took the brunt of the wildly surging spiritual energy, while his right hand clamped around Lou Yue’s kicking ankle like an iron pincer.","The two froze in place. Xiao Rangchen’s left arm had gone numb, while half of Lou Yue’s leg was held suspended in midair.","“Underhanded,” Xiao Rangchen said, tightening his grip.","Lou Yue’s smile returned, her brows and eyes dazzling. “It’s called ‘all’s fair in war.’”","Before she finished speaking, Lou Yue suddenly leaned forward. Her stunning face abruptly filled Xiao Rangchen’s vision, and the faint, warm fragrance of sweet flowers slipped into his breath.","Xiao Rangchen’s mind faltered for an instant. Lou Yue seized the opportunity to pull her foot free, then successfully kicked him in the knee with her other leg.","Having gained the advantage, Lou Yue stopped there. She went “thump, thump” up the wooden steps and called over her shoulder, “Since you have so much time to stand around making threats, why don’t you think about how you’re going to enter Xuandu on your own ability?”","Lou Yue ignored him from then on. But when she passed the long spear embedded in the wooden steps, she stopped and turned her head.","“This is premium sandalwood. Either pay for it or repair the hole yourself. Don’t even think about shirking responsibility.”","After dropping those words, she turned around with effortless swagger and went straight back to her room.","Xuanba had yet to return from absorbing the moonlight outside. Lou Yue sat in a chair for a while, then rolled into the soft brocade quilt. But just as she comfortably closed her eyes, the image of Xiao Rangchen practicing with his spear appeared in her mind.","Irritated, Lou Yue kicked her legs, then turned over and crawled back up to meditate.","After some time, she opened her eyes and gazed wistfully at the full moon outside the window.","There was a disturbance at the window ledge. Xuanba huffed and puffed as it climbed inside. Lou Yue turned her attention to its clumsy yet composed movements. Accustomed to being watched, Xuanba’s lofty pace was completely unaffected.","“Xuanba...”","At the sound of Lou Yue’s mournful voice, Xuanba briefly paused.","“Why is it that no matter what I do, the speed at which my dantian absorbs spiritual energy is as slow as you crawling?”","Xuanba abandoned its brief pause.","Perhaps because she had suffered one blow after another, and because the stillness of the late night had allowed her emotions to overwhelm her reason, Lou Yue was especially vulnerable tonight. She got out of bed and picked up Xuanba, somewhat on the verge of a breakdown.","“Xiao Rangchen’s dantian power goes whoosh, whoosh, whoosh—faster than the cloudship can fly. Am I really never going to surpass him...?”","Xuanba asked calmly, “How do you know he goes ‘whoosh, whoosh, whoosh’?”","“Is that the important part?” Lou Yue shook Xuanba hard. “The important part is that he’s ‘whoosh, whoosh, whoosh,’ while I’m ‘heave-ho—heave-ho’!”","Xuanba calmly retorted, “When have I ever been ‘heave-ho—heave-ho’?”","Lou Yue felt as though she had been talking to a brick wall. She slapped Xuanba against the wall, pinning it there, and spoke forcefully.","“I’m giving you a chance to show what you can do!”","Xuanba turned its head away. “Don’t want to.”","Lou Yue straightened its tiny head and gazed at it with deep feeling. “I believe in you.”","Xuanba did not appreciate it in the slightest. “Oh. I don’t believe in myself.”","Lou Yue glared at Xuanba. She did not know why she was so certain that Xuanba could help her. She simply felt that it could, and therefore acted accordingly.","Xuanba knew all too well how stubborn Lou Yue could be once she dug in her heels. If it said nothing, she might keep it pinned against the wall for an entire day. It stretched out its little legs and consoled her.","“Why insist on comparing yourself to him? His spiritual meridians are naturally powerful. For anyone else, having damaged spiritual meridians for two years would have turned them into a cripple. Yet not only have his spiritual meridians survived, he can still draw upon spiritual energy. You simply cannot compare yourself to him in that regard.”","This was the first time Lou Yue had heard Xuanba say so much at once. Unfortunately, every word struck directly at her sore spots.","She refused to accept it. “So what? Just because he has exceptional talent, am I supposed to deserve having his brilliance blind me?”","She had no intention of giving up. Even if all her efforts ultimately ended in failure, she would at least bite off a piece of her enemy—hard.","Xuanba was silent for a long while before saying, “What if the price is attracting the covetous attention of everyone, even having the people you trust at your side betray you?”","Its voice was calm, yet carried a strange depth of meaning.","Instead, Lou Yue laughed with arrogant abandon. “Then I’ll make sure no one dares covet me, not even in their dreams! As for betrayal—when the old leaves, the new can take its place.”","Xuanba was slightly stunned. Unexpectedly, it felt that those words suited her perfectly. She was arrogant and overbearing, yet possessed a kind of magnetism that made it impossible to look away.","Lou Yue scratched its belly and urged it on. “Well? Can you do it, Lord Xuan?”","Xuanba wriggled free of her hand and landed on the floor. Slowly, it replied, “Got it.”","“What does ‘got it’ mean?” Lou Yue bent down and followed after it as it shuffled along in tiny steps, her eyes full of anticipation. “You have a way, don’t you?”","Xuanba said, “Wait.”","“How long do I have to wait?”","Xuanba stopped and turned to look at her. “Are you going to wait or not?”","Lou Yue nodded eagerly. “I’ll wait, I’ll wait! Naturally, I must listen to whatever Lord Xuan says!”","Xuanba climbed to the head of the bed, closed its eyes, and entered meditation. Brimming with enthusiasm, Lou Yue bounced back onto the bed and decided to meditate a little more, making one last-minute effort.","In the silent room, Xuanba opened its scarlet eyes.","Make it so no one dared to covet her...?","**","Xuandu was located in the center of Zezhou and was divided into Xuantiandu and Xuandicheng. Xuantiandu floated high in the sky and was where the direct descendants and core members of the Lou clan lived and cultivated. Xuandicheng was rooted on the ground and served as a dwelling place for branch families, commoners, and others.","The entire Xuandu was shrouded in an enormous barrier. Aside from its defensive function, the barrier also prohibited all cloudships, magical vessels, and escape arts from flying through the heavens. To reach Xuantiandu, one had to pass through the teleportation array in Xuandicheng.","The cloudship carrying Lou Yue landed outside Xuandu several days later, in the late morning.","Since parting from Xiao Rangchen that night, Lou Yue had not seen him again. She had spent all her time cultivating. It was not until she descended the wooden steps from the upper cabin after arriving that she suddenly remembered something and turned back to look.","The gap torn open by the long spear that night had already been mended, its edges smoothed and fused together with spiritual power. But because a different type of wood was used for the repair, it looked just like a lopsided, ugly flower blooming across the grain in the sunlight.","Lou Yue pictured Xiao Rangchen crouching on the wooden steps with a cold, stern look on his face, patching the damage bit by bit with deliberate patience, and could not help snickering out loud.","\"Young Master?\" Little Qiu wondered what had suddenly put Lou Yue in such high spirits, to the point that the joy in his eyes was almost spilling over.","\"It's nothing, nothing at all.\" Lou Yue lifted his feet and kept walking down the steps.","Seeing how good a mood Lou Yue was in, Little Qiu could not help smiling too. \"By the way, Young Master, Xiao Rangchen left on his own the moment the cloud ship stopped.\"","\"He's already gone?\" Lou Yue paused for a brief moment, then quickly relaxed. If he had not chosen to leave on his own, she would have chased him off anyway. As for how he planned to get into Xuandu, she did not worry about it, nor did she care. \"Never mind him. Where is Xiao Aiai?\"","\"Miss Xiao and all the others are waiting out on the deck.\"","Lou Yue nodded in acknowledgment.","There were still three days left before the birthday celebration of the Lou family head Lou Moshu, and all kinds of cloud ships had already landed outside the Xuandu barrier. The temporary campsite was bustling with noise and crowds.","At the entrance to Xuandi City, the lines were clearly divided. The two lines on either side stretched out so far that their ends were nowhere to be seen, and everyone in them had to take off their outer garments to undergo a thorough inspection. The wide middle passage only had a group of people in pale lake-blue robes, and the number of cultivating monks assigned to check their identities had gone from two to eight. Lou Yue did not think much of it, and led her people straight to the end of the lake-blue line to queue up.","She had barely stood still when a rough, furious shout burst out from the left line. \"Why don't they have to take their clothes off? This isn't fair!\"","\"Yeah, that's right, it's not fair at all!\" Many people in the two side lines chimed in, and the crowd, already agitated by the slow-moving queues, immediately erupted into a commotion.","\"Quiet down, all of you!\" A shrill voice rang out, laced with undisguised contempt. \"Fairness? Letting commoners like you into Xuandu is already the greatest fairness you could ask for. Keep running your mouths, and not a single one of you commoners will be allowed in.\"","The crowd was packed so tight that Lou Yue could not see what was happening up ahead. Xiao Aiai, standing right next to her, let out a huff of annoyance at those words.","Dou'er, who saw Xiao Aiai as her rival, immediately wrapped her arms around Lou Yue's arm, craned her neck and said in a sugary voice, \"Miss Xiao, you'd better be a little more restrained. Be careful of your words and deeds, don't bring shame on our Young Master.\" After she finished speaking, she quickly tucked her head back in.","\"What's wrong with my behavior? Am I not even allowed to huff?!\" Xiao Aiai was also irritated by Dou'er, who stuck to Lou Yue's side all day long.","Seeing that the two of them were about to start bickering again, Lou Yue waved her hand helplessly. \"Be good, both of you. I can't hear what they're saying up front.\"","The two made eye contact, huffed at the same time, and turned their faces away from each other.","\"How can this be right? Do you think you can do whatever you want around here?!\" The two side lines broke out into even more fierce protests.","\"I can't do whatever I want, but I can easily shut the lot of you lowly commoners up.\"","Lou Yue's brows furrowed slightly. Just then, a young man stepped out from the lake-blue line ahead of her. He waved his hand, and several flying swords zipped through the two side lines one after another, slashing all the people who had been shouting in protest.","\"Lowly commoners should know their place.\" The flying swords merged into one and slid back into their sheath. The young man's tone was utterly disdainful. \"Instead of wasting your breath yelling about fairness, you should have told your mothers not to give birth to you in your next life. There are lowly commoners everywhere, the world won't miss even one of you.\"","Low, muffled snickers rippled through the lake-blue line.","\"Bang!\" The burly man who had spoken earlier slammed the tip of the axe on his shoulder against the ground, sending dust flying. The sword wound on his arm was bleeding nonstop, staining half his sleeve red, but he did not even seem to notice it. \"You're abusing your power! Damn it, I'll fight with everything I've got to get a fair answer today!\"","\"Ask for a fair answer? You're just delusional.\" The young man scoffed. \"I'm abusing my power against you, so what can you do about it? If you want to blame someone, blame the fact that I have more power than you!\"","\"Well said!\"","Xiao Aiai spun around to look at Lou Yue in complete disbelief that she would actually side with that young man.","Under the gaze of the whole crowd, Lou Yue walked over unhurriedly, with dozens of her followers trailing right behind her, moving from the back of the crowd to the side of the lake-blue line.","Cang Youshan looked at the newcomer. He saw a young man dressed in a moon-white brocade robe, with dark gold patterns trimming the hem and cuffs. The gold threads glinted with fine streaks of light in the sunlight as he walked, wrapped in a faint aura of spiritual power. It was obvious at a glance that the robe was a treasure from the Yuanhuan Pavilion. The hair ornament behind his ear and the dangling thin beaded chain were no ordinary items either.","His clothes were exquisitely luxurious, and his looks were even more outstanding. His eyebrows were like ink-drawn moons, his eyes like stars, and the corners of his eyes curved with a smile that somehow carried a hint of captivating affection.","Cang Youshan stared blankly for a moment. Then the thought that the person who had just agreed with him was such an outstanding young man made a surge of pride rise in his chest.","His father was seriously ill, and he had been sent here on his father's orders to attend the birthday celebration. He had long intended to make connections with more noble and powerful families to pave the way for taking over the family in the future. This young man, with his extraordinary bearing, was clearly someone worth currying favor with.","Cang Youshan set aside his arrogant demeanor, cupped his hands and said in a gentle tone, \"I am Cang Youshan, from the Cangya Clan of Northern Ming. May I ask how I should address you, brother?\"","Lou Yue stopped right beside him, tilted her head and blinked, asking in a curious tone, \"You're from the Cangya Clan of Northern Ming, so why don't you have the surname Cangya?\"","Cang Youshan's expression froze.","Little Qiu stepped forward at just the right moment, his voice neither too loud nor too soft, enough for everyone present to hear clearly. \"Young Master, only the direct line of the Cangya Clan inherits the surname Cangya. All collateral branches and offshoots take the surname Cang.\"","\"Oh——\" Lou Yue drew out the word, her tone teasing. \"So you're from a collateral branch. No wonder...\"","Cang Youshan lowered his hands, his face darkening. \"Sir——\"","Lou Yue cut him off. \"But that sentence you said just now, I completely agree with it.\"","Cang Youshan could not figure out what she was thinking, and was just trying to work out how to respond, when he saw the young man lead her whole group of people to squeeze to the very front of their queue.","Even though Cang Youshan had been trying to maintain his composure, his face turned dark at this. \"Sir, don't you understand the rule of first come, first served?\"","The cultivating monk in charge of checking identities at the city gate also spoke up. \"Which family do you come from, sir? Please go to the back of the line and wait for your turn to be verified.\"","Lou Yue ignored them. She only fished a smooth, glossy jade plaque out of her storage ring and tossed it to the man in charge of the checks.","The front and back of the jade plaque were carved with intricate star patterns, and in the center was embedded a gilded ancient character —— Lou.","The monk in charge was stunned at first, and mistakenly thought Lou Yue was from a side branch of his own family. But when he flipped the jade plaque over out of habit, his whole body froze in utter shock, his eyes wide as saucers. With a plop, he fell to his knees, holding the jade plaque high above his head with both hands, his voice trembling so badly he could barely get the words out. \"M-My Lord... This lowly one has failed to recognize your eminence!\"","He was the squad leader in charge of identity verification. The moment he knelt down, all the other checking monks knelt towards Lou Yue in a rustling line. The sight was astonishing.","The once noisy city gate instantly went dead silent.","Every single person's gaze was fixed right on the young man in the middle of the crowd, who wore a faint, unruffled smile."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["\"What on earth is going on!\"","The sharp, young voice that had spoken earlier rang out, and Lou Yue then noticed a portly man standing at the back.","The man squinted his tiny, slit-like eyes to size her up, then flipped over the jade tablet he was holding up to reveal its back.","Where the star pattern was supposed to be, two bold, sweeping characters had appeared out of nowhere: Chengfeng.","The carving was so imposing that just looking at it made one's eyes sting.","He suddenly broke into a grin. \"Well, if it isn't our Young Master Yue! It's been years, and Young Master Yue's airs are even grander than they used to be.\"","Lou Yue confirmed that the man was not in the Lou family character album Little Qiu had given her, so she asked, \"Who are you?\"","The chubby man's smile froze on his face for a moment, then he forced it back, his voice shrill as he said, \"Young Master Yue, you have a lot on your mind and a bad memory. I'm Lou Haina, I work under the First Young Master.\"","In the Lou family, the only one addressed as First Young Master is Lou Weixiao, the eldest grandson of Lou Mo. He is known as the genius most likely to inherit the position of clan head, and a ruthless character who sees the male lead Xiao Rangchen as his sworn enemy.","Normally, the enemy of my enemy is my friend, and the subordinate of a friend is my own subordinate. But unfortunately, Lou Haina's words just now didn't sit right with her, so there was no way she could take him on as her subordinate.","Lou Yue lifted her eyelids to glance down at him haughtily, her tone lazy. \"Oh, no impression. But your name really fits your build.\"","Lou Haina had hated nothing more in his life than having people tease his figure by making jokes about his name. But Lou Yue's father Lou Chengfeng, even though he was exiled to guard the mountain, still held the jade tablet personally carved by the clan head, which had never been taken back. Lou Haina didn't dare to turn on her for real, so he could only swallow his resentment and hand the jade tablet back. \"Young Master Yue still loves to crack jokes... Shall I lead you to the resting spot?\"","Lou Yue put the jade tablet away without answering, instead glancing around casually as she said, \"Say, Haina, you're not doing your job well for the First Young Master, are you? You only assigned two people to the busy lanes on both sides, while the middle is so idle that people are just sitting around eating for nothing. Those who know might understand you were trying to arrange proper receptions for the noble families, but those who don't would think you can't even handle the trivial task of city entry checks. Makes it sound like everyone under the First Young Master is a good-for-nothing.\"","Lou Haina ground his back teeth. He had been sent to the city gate to reflect on his mistakes precisely because he had botched a task earlier, so he couldn't afford to get into any more trouble now.","He couldn't lash out at Lou Yue, so he could only take his anger out on others. He lifted his foot and kicked a kneeling man away, yelling in a shrill voice, \"Are you all blind? Can't you see the queue is so long? You, you, and all of you, get over there right now, speed things up, stop dawdling!\"","None of those people dared to utter a word of complaint. They didn't even bother to brush the shoe prints off their clothes before hurrying over to work on both sides.","Lou Yue curled her fingers slightly, but a satisfied smile spread across her face. \"Let's go then. Where's the resting spot?\"","Lou Haina couldn't wait to get this difficult guest off his hands, so he turned around and led the way. He had only taken two steps when the young master stopped again.","\"Oh, I almost forgot something.\"","Lou Haina forced a strained smile. \"Forgot what?\"","Lou Yue pointed at the lake-blue clad group whose check was almost finished. \"Just now, I was standing right behind them, and I kept sensing this eerie, wicked aura of a Ghost Wraith. The clan head's birthday celebration is coming up soon. If something unclean sneaks into the city, that would be a huge problem.\"","\"Ghost Wraith?!\" Lou Haina stiffened. The matter of Ghost Wraiths was too serious to trifle with. No matter if Lou Yue was telling the truth or not, he couldn't afford to be the slightest bit negligent right now. If something went wrong during the birthday celebration, even ten of his lives wouldn't be enough to pay for it. He immediately raised his voice sharply. \"Do a thorough recheck! Bring the probing needles over!\"","Cang Youshan at the front of the queue was so furious that his face was twisted. He pointed at Lou Yue and shouted, \"What Ghost Wraith! You're spouting nonsense and slandering us!\"","Lou Yue shrugged innocently.","\"You're going too far! Let go of me! How dare your Lou clan treat our Cangya people like this? Aren't you afraid—ah—!\" Before Cang Youshan could finish his sentence, Lou Haina's men had pinned him down and stripped off his outer clothes. The icy probing needle was jabbed straight into his back, and a shrill scream echoed across the city gate.","Lou Yue looked at Cang Youshan's pain-twisted face and sighed with feigned regret. \"Didn't you just say 'I'm the one using my power to bully you, what can you do about it? If you want to blame someone, blame the fact that I have more power than you'? I really thought what you said made perfect sense. Sigh, I thought we were kindred spirits, but it seems we're not.\"","Cang Youshan's face alternated between green and white, no one could tell if it was from rage or pain. But Lou Yue was feeling perfectly cheerful. She had made the whole Ghost Wraith thing up. She just wanted to make that guy suffer a little.","The probing needle looked terrifying, but it wouldn't do any real permanent harm. The only thing was the sharp, intense pain the moment it pierced the skin, leaving the person weak for just a day afterward. But for someone like Cang Youshan, the humiliation of being stripped and jabbed with a probing needle in full public view would be enough for him to remember for a lifetime.","Lou Yue had achieved her goal. She was just about to ask a random person to lead her away when the black probing needle was pulled out, half of it stained bright red.","Lou Yue: \"...\"","This was a totally unexpected turn of events.","Cang Youshan was also stunned. He stared fixedly at the red-stained half of the needle, his face as pale as paper. \"Impossible... This can't be true! You all conspired against me! I want to see the Young Lord of Cangya!\"","Lou Haina wouldn't give him any chance to explain. He raised his hand and chopped at the back of Cang Youshan's neck. Cang Youshan's eyes rolled back, and he slumped to the ground.","\"Take him away and keep him under strict guard!\" he ordered, then turned to look at Lou Yue. There was a hint of inquisitiveness in his slit-like eyes. Only highly cultivated great powers could sense the aura of a Ghost Wraith. How could Lou Yue have such an ability? Was it just a coincidence, or had she come across some extraordinary adventure? No matter which it was, he had to remind the First Young Master to keep an eye on the returned Lou Yue.","While his mind was racing with thoughts, he still wore a smile on his face. \"Young Master Yue, I'm really swamped with work right now. Let me assign someone else to take you there, okay?\"","Lou Yue nodded, her gaze sweeping over the Cangya disciples pinned to the side. \"What about them?\"","Lou Haina followed her line of sight, thinking to himself that she really had too many trivial demands. But he still answered politely, \"If none of them have been possessed, their lives won't be in danger. But they still have to be kept under guard, and they'll be released once the whole matter is investigated clearly.\"","Lou Yue didn't ask any more questions. She turned and followed the guiding guard away. The huge crowd of people at the city gate gradually dispersed.","People by the gate started whispering and discussing. A soft, childish voice mixed in with the chatter. \"Mom, that big sister is so cool! I want to be just like her when I grow up!\"","The little girl's mother was so scared that she quickly covered her mouth. After making sure no one was paying attention to them, she whispered in a shaky, reproaching tone, \"That's a young master of the Lou family, not a big sister. Qin'er, how many times have I told you? Don't ever talk about the noble clans out in public. We can't afford to offend them. Do you want to get taken away, and never see mom again?\"","The little girl named Qin'er blinked her big round eyes and mumbled, \"You all keep saying that all the noble clan people are... but there are good ones too, right?\"","Her mother looked at her innocent, wide-eyed face and sighed. \"Stand still properly. It took us half a year to get here. When the spirit rain falls later, you have to absorb as much of it as you can.\"","Qin'er broke into a sweet smile. \"I know, mom!\"","**","The city of Xuanba was bustling. Rows of shops lined both sides of the streets, filled with a dazzling array of magic tools and rare treasures. Lou Yue looked around at the surroundings, full of curiosity.","\"I... I'm thanking you on their behalf,\" Xiao Aiai suddenly said, her voice soft as a mosquito's hum, sounding a little flustered.","Lou Yue turned around and looked at her, realizing the girl was talking to her. \"Out of nowhere? What are you thanking me for?\"","Xiao Aiai glanced at Lou Yue, who looked completely oblivious and even rather nonchalant, and pouted. \"Forget I even mentioned it.\"","Lou Yue was still grinning. She lifted a hand and pointed at the shops nearby. \"The birthday banquet is still a few days away. Don't mope cooped up in your room all day. If you see anything you like, just tell the shopkeeper to send the bill over to Little Qiu to pay. A young lady like you shouldn't dress so plainly, you know?\"","Xiao Aiai looked down at her own pink dress, wondering where on earth she could be considered plain. But when she lifted her head again and caught sight of the glittering, dazzling ornament tucked behind Lou Yue's ear, she rolled her eyes silently. Fine, compared to Lou Yue, she really did come off as underdressed.","The so-called lodging area was a specially designated district built to host visiting guests, with countless courtyards arranged in a neat, scattered layout. Most of the courtyards had a faint soft glow hovering above them.","Lou Yue and her party were led to the front of a courtyard marked with the two characters \"Mianyun\". The moment they stepped across the threshold, the sign lit up, and a faint glow began to emanate from above the entire courtyard too.","From the outside, this looked like nothing more than an ordinary small courtyard, but once inside, it turned out to hold a whole other world. It was big enough to house not just a few dozen people, but hundreds at a stretch.","Lou Yue told Little Qiu to arrange accommodations for everyone, then took Xuanba and headed into the uppermost room.","The second the door closed behind her, Lou Yue leaned in eagerly. \"You said you'd tell me how to speed up my cultivation once we reached Xuandu. We're here now, so spill! What's the plan?\"","The grand birthday banquet was only three days away, and the day after that would be the Ancient Tree Enlightenment trial. From what she'd learned of her own aptitude during this period, she stood zero chance of beating Xiao Rangchen fairly. She needed a cheat code.","\"Have your people search the city of Xuandi for a place that holds the combined power of the five elements: metal, wood, water, fire, and earth,\" Xuanba's voice was as icy as ever.","Lou Yue's eyes lit up. \"Once we find that place, my cultivation will shoot up like a rocket?!\"","\"Once you find the place, clear out a hundred meters in all directions. No one is allowed to step inside that area.\"","\"Got it, got it! And then? What happens next?\" Lou Yue stared at him, full of anticipation.","\"Then you've already found the place?\" Xuanba glanced at her faintly.","Lou Yue hissed in frustration, turned around, plopped Xuanba down on the table, and stormed out to find Little Qiu. \"Just you wait,\" she tossed over her shoulder as she left.","It was hard to tell if Little Qiu was just exceptionally efficient or if Xuandi City was so rich in spiritual energies that such places were common, but the five-element gathering spot Xuanba had asked for was found in less than half a day.","It was a clear, circular lake, right in the middle of which grew a towering ancient tree so thick that ten people stretching their arms out still couldn't wrap their hands around its trunk. Its branches were thick and sturdy, heavy with lush foliage. On the lower mid-level branches twined vines bright as burning fire, while the outermost boughs were covered in pale white blossoms that looked like drifted snow.","\"Young Master, Lord Xuan, what do you both think of this spot?\" Little Qiu noticed Lou Yue staring at the tree, and sighed in admiration. \"The Karmic Fire Vine is aligned with the fire element, and the Zhangluan Tree with the wood element. Normally they would repel each other, but Xuandi City is so brimming with spiritual energy, and nourished by the city's grand barrier formation, that the two ended up growing together in harmony instead.\"","Lou Yue reached out to touch the tree trunk, and felt a distinct, unique ripple of energy. \"It's a spirit-gathering spot?\"","Little Qiu smiled and nodded. \"Exactly, Young Master. I checked thoroughly. This tree is the center of a natural small-scale spirit-gathering formation. Anywhere else, a place like this would be fought over by everyone, but here in Xuandi City, it's nothing out of the ordinary.\"","Xuanba confirmed the positions of the five elements at the site, and nodded. \"This will do. Post guards at every direction, and make sure no one comes within a hundred meters for twelve full hours.\"","Little Qiu agreed immediately and rushed off to arrange the manpower. If both Lord Xuan and his young master were taking this so seriously, he knew without a doubt this was a matter of the utmost importance, and he couldn't afford to be the slightest bit careless.","The moment Little Qiu left, Xuanba expanded his form to its full size. Vast, surging spiritual energy spread out to cover a hundred miles in all directions, even sealing off the sky above. Then his massive body slithered across the surface of the lake and around the great tree, as golden, ancient runes kept appearing and condensing beneath his feet.","After what felt like ages, Lou Yue finally realized he was drawing a gigantic, mind-bogglingly intricate pattern, layered over and over with formations so complex she couldn't make heads or tails of them. It was just endlessly, impossibly complicated.","Lou Yue got so bored watching that she started dozing off. By the time Xuanba called her over, she'd already eaten two Chunhua fruits and curled up against the tree for a quick nap.","Lou Yue rubbed her bleary eyes, glanced around at the seemingly unchanged surroundings. \"It's done?\"","Xuanba had shrunk back down to his palm-sized form, his head hanging limply like he was completely worn out. He let out a faint hum. \"Go lie down in the middle of the lake. And keep sleeping.\"","Lou Yue stepped into the water, fully expecting her feet to get wet, but she found she could walk on its surface as easily as on dry land. She raised an eyebrow, amused, and made her way to the center of the lake. \"I really don't have to do anything else?\"","\"This is way too easy,\" she said happily as she laid down. But she suddenly shot back up into a sitting position. \"Wait a second, this feels exactly like lying down on an operating table! Is there some kind of risk to this method?!\"","Xuanba stared at her, his tone low and grim. \"Don't you think it's a little late to be asking that?\"","Lou Yue jolted in alarm. \"There really are risks?! Am I going to kick the bucket? Is there a chance I'll never wake up again?!\"","She couldn't stay still any longer, and immediately tried to scramble off her \"operating table\".","Xuanba was already completely drained of spiritual energy, too tired to even move a muscle, but seeing Lou Yue refusing to cooperate made him snap. He suddenly leaped up and gave her a sharp kick right to the head, knocking her right back down flat.","\"You are not going to die, and you are not going to fail to wake up! Now stay there and lie still!\" Xuanba snapped, thoroughly annoyed.","Lou Yue rubbed the sore spot on her head, muttering in a wronged, pouty tone. \"But—\"","\"There are no risks! Unless some random person pops out of thin air!\"","Lou Yue pressed on cautiously. \"What would happen if someone really did pop out of nowhere?\"","\"The grand formation would treat that person as a part of you. After it's done, there'd only be a little bit of residual connection between the two of you, that's all.\"","\"What kind of connection?\"","\"Are you going to lie down or not?! If you're not, we're going home right now!\" Xuanba was completely out of patience from her pestering.","Seeing that her \"lead surgeon\" was on the verge of losing his temper, Lou Yue quickly tried to calm him down. \"Alright, alright, don't get mad. C'mon, take a deep breath, stay calm and steady.\"","Xuanba was speechless.","Lou Yue actually thought she was overthinking it anyway. There were guards posted outside, and Xuanba's barrier sealed the inside of the area too.","Short of a person materializing out of thin air, how could anyone possibly get in?","----------------------","All that build-up was for the satisfying payback.","The next chapter is the one you've all been looking forward to."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Lou Yue settled down comfortably and closed her eyes.","Xuanba landed beside Lou Yue, looking at the person who had finally calmed down, and for the first time, a flicker of hesitation crossed its mind.","\"If you regret it now, there is still time. Once you take this step, there will be no turning back, and your entire future will be completely changed.\"","Lou Yue opened her eyes to look at it and said with a soft laugh, \"You were just lecturing me, but who is being long-winded now?\"","She stretched out her hand, her slender fingers spreading out under the vast blue sky: \"Xuanba, I believe fate is in my own hands. My heart is telling me to move forward and never look back.\"","Xuanba fell silent. After a moment, it spoke in a cold tone, \"Stop being so emotional. Close your eyes and stop moving.\"","Lou Yue curled her lips into a smile, \"Yes, Lord Xuan!\"","Xuanba took a deep breath and opened its mouth, letting a half inner elixir float out slowly. The elixir was missing half, yet it still glowed brilliantly with dazzling seven-colored light.","Almost at the same instant, streams of seven-colored radiance surged out from Lou Yue's body, echoing the half elixir from afar.","She could not see what Xuanba was doing. She only felt her forehead suddenly grow hot, and all the blood in her body seemed to boil. Contrary to that sensation, her consciousness grew drowsy and blurred.","The moment before she completely lost consciousness, dense sun-shaped golden patterns slowly emerged on the surface of her skin, spreading out from the sun mark right in the center of her forehead to every part of her body, even wrapping around her strands of hair.","Xuanba rose into the air, its front paws pressed together, and shouted in a deep voice, \"Open, Illusionary Form!\"","In the blink of an eye, the golden patterns on Lou Yue's body lit up sharply, detached from her body like cicada wings, and floated gently in the air above.","After the golden patterns left her, Lou Yue's figure changed quietly. The outline of her facial features did not alter much, but her lip color became all the more bright and rosy. The faint Adam's apple that had been there vanished, smoothing into a graceful line of the neck that extended down to her collarbone.","Her originally flat front of clothing was now propped up into a full, soft curve that rose and fell gently with her breath. The slightly open collar revealed a hint of delicate, fair skin. The whole person had completely transformed from a noble, handsome young man into a strikingly bright and beautiful young girl.","Xuanba was not surprised by this at all. It took out a drop of its own heart blood and injected it into the stripped golden patterns. The next moment, the golden patterns trembled violently, and half a seven-colored inner elixir slowly precipitated out from the sun mark at its core.","The moment this half elixir appeared, the two halves of the elixir were drawn to each other, eager to merge into one. Xuanba stopped the elixirs from fusing. It looked calmly at that half of the elixir which had been separated from its owner for eighteen years, then lowered its eyes.","\"Crack!\"","Drawn by the other half of the elixir, the newly separated half shattered inch by inch. The vast spiritual power contained within the elixir surged towards the golden patterns like a tidal wave.","For Lou Yue, this step she took left her with no way to turn back, and for Xuanba, it was the same.","The Illusionary Form Secret Art was an ancient forbidden spell. It could mask one's appearance and turn a person into a completely different look, such that even a cultivator with supreme cultivation could not see through the disguise. If the person under the spell did not know of its existence, even they themselves would not notice the change.","But in exchange, the person under the spell would have their perception and absorption of the spiritual energy from the outside world extremely reduced.","To regain that perception, retrieve the inner elixir and undo the Illusionary Form Secret Art, that was all it took. But once the spell was undone, the secret of Lou Yue's real female identity would be exposed, and at that time, she would draw the covetous gaze of everyone around her.","This was an unsolvable dilemma. The only thing Xuanba could do was to do its utmost to delay that day after the spell was undone, even at the cost of losing half of its inner elixir forever, making it almost impossible for its cultivation to advance further.","Xuanba glanced at Lou Yue's peaceful sleeping face, and thought of another face that looked so similar to hers. It sighed silently. Perhaps encountering this mother and daughter in its life was the tribulation fated for it.","Under the infusion of the vast spiritual power, the golden patterns gave off a dazzling, blinding light. As the half inner elixir was completely reduced to ashes, the golden patterns suddenly went into turmoil, as if trying to break free from the restraints and fly away through the air.","The formation array around lit up instantly. Several golden threads darted out like agile spirit serpents, coiling tightly around the fleeing golden patterns. Several more threads stretched out, pulling Lou Yue's body up into the air. Five-colored spiritual light from the water depths, the water surface, the earth, the karmic fire vine, and the Cinnabar Phoenix Tree converged, all rushing towards the golden patterns, forcing them back into Lou Yue's body.","The golden patterns could resist no longer. They slowly returned to their place and sank back into Lou Yue's body.","All that was left now was to wait quietly for the golden patterns to fully merge with Lou Yue. Xuanba lay down, turning a blind eye to the rumbling thunder from the outside world, and guarded Lou Yue silently.","At this very moment, above the capital of Xuandu, silver heavenly lightning curled down like a green dragon stretching its claws, striking fiercely. It hit the barrier that enveloped the entire Xuandu capital and was blocked, scattering into dancing electric sparks all over the sky.","People in both the Xuantian Capital and the Xuandi City all looked up at the sky, guessing that someone in the city must have broken through their cultivation and failed to rush to the designated tribulation ground in time.","At the highest point of Xuantian Capital, under the towering tower corridor that pierced the clouds, stood an old man in a black robe. His white hair fell loosely, yet there was no trace of decrepitude about him.","\"Patriarch.\"","An old servant with white hair and beard walked out from the corner, his voice loud and clear, \"Young Master Yue has arrived at Xuandi City with the Third Master's jade token. Do we need to send someone to bring him up?\"","\"No need.\" Lou Mo did not turn his head. He tossed a dark square object over, \"Lou Zhongyan, put this thing in an inconspicuous corner of the Queyun Residence.\"","Lou Zhongyan caught it steadily, and a knowing smile flashed in his eyes, \"After all, the Patriarch has decided to give it to Young Master Yue.\"","\"Who said I'm giving it to her!\" Lou Mo snapped, his voice loud enough to drown out the thunder outside.","Lou Zhongyan had served him for seventy years, so how could he not know his master's habit of saying one thing but meaning another? He also understood the hardships and trade-offs that came with managing such a large aristocratic clan.","\"It was my slip of the tongue, Patriarch.\" He bowed to beg for forgiveness, a smile still on his lips, \"I will head to Queyun Residence right now.\"","The lightning outside the barrier was still striking, making people feel irritated. Lou Mo's white eyebrows shot up, he gave a cold snort, and waved his sleeve. A powerful burst of spiritual power shot straight to the sky. With a loud boom, all the lightning that had gathered above the barrier was swept away.","The world fell back into silence.","None of the changes happening outside affected Xuanba in the slightest, much less Lou Yue, who was in the middle of the merging process.","The sun set and rose again. Xuanba fought to stay awake despite its overdrawn spiritual power and the backlash from its damaged inner elixir, refusing to fall into a state of hibernation. It was not until Lou Yue shifted back to her young man's form, and the merging process only had the final steps left, that it could hold on no longer. In an instant, icy frost wrapped its entire body.","Shortly after Xuanba was sealed in ice, a fluctuation of spiritual power suddenly arose within the barrier.","\"Splash --\" The sound of water breaking the surface broke the silence.","The moment Xiao Rangchen emerged, the previously dormant golden threads in the formation array woke up abruptly, and with a swish, coiled around his limbs and waist.","Xiao Rangchen's expression sank. He had used the power of the Green Spirit to escape from outside the city to this spirit-gathering ground, but he never expected there would be a formation array here. The seemingly thin golden threads contained spiritual power far beyond what he could resist at his current cultivation level.","Xiao Rangchen quickly scanned his surroundings for a way out, and his peripheral vision caught sight of Lou Yue in the air. Before he could react, the golden threads tightened sharply, pulling him upwards with an overbearing force that left no room for resistance.","In his field of vision, the face that was always unruly and free drew close all of a sudden.","The next second, a soft touch landed on his lips.","Xiao Rangchen froze all over, his dark eyes filled with utter shock, and even his breath came to a halt.","He tried to pull back hard, but the golden threads wrapped around him seemed to have a mind of their own. Not only did they not allow him to retreat, they tightened even more, as if trying to press his entire body into Lou Yue's.","\"Lou Yue!\" Xiao Rangchen growled in a low voice, trying to wake her up.","As their lips moved, that softness slipped into his mouth.","Xiao Rangchen froze up again. He did not dare make the slightest movement, but even as he stayed perfectly still, that strange, warm sensation made its presence unignorable. He could even taste the faint, lingering sweetness of spring berry fruit left on those lips.","Xiao Rangchen's Adam's apple bobbed. He shut his eyes tightly all at once, and wrenched his head sharply to the side.","Their gliding lips brushed past each other's cheeks, landing on nothing but empty air.","Xiao Rangchen let out an inexplicable quiet breath of relief, his taut back trembling faintly. Before he could even fully steady his frayed nerves, a scorching warm breath washed over his right ear.","Lou Yue's lips parted slightly, hovering right beside his ear, almost touching but not quite.","Xiao Rangchen had never been this close to anyone in his entire life, much less a man...","Time dragged on unbearably, as if a full year had passed in that span, yet at the same time it felt no longer than a fleeting second.","The golden threads binding him suddenly loosened their hold, and the glow of the surrounding formation faded away little by little. Xiao Rangchen broke free the very instant he could, and dropped back down to the ground.","Once he was steady on his feet, he lifted a hand and scrubbed hard across his lips. The back of his hand brushed the corner of his mouth, his movement paused for a beat, then he unconsciously swiped at his burning hot right ear.","He did not so much as glance at Lou Yue, just clenched his fists tight and started walking straight for the exit.","\"Xiao Rangchen?\"","A slightly dazed voice called out from behind him, and Xiao Rangchen's steps halted.","Lou Yue stared at the familiar figure of his back below him, and his foggy, muddled wits slowly cleared.","\"What are you doing here!\"","\"How did you get in?\"","\"When did you arrive?!\"","Lou Yue fired off three panicked questions in a row. He had never expected a person to pop out of thin air right there, and that person turned out to be Long Aotian, the very last person he could stand.","The last of the golden threads dissolved completely. Lou Yue pushed off the ground with the tip of his toe to land softly, then swept Xuanba wrapped in a layer of icy cold into his arms. His clear crisp voice was sharp with full vigilance and suspicion. \"What did you do to Xuanba?\"","Xiao Rangchen's eyes narrowed at the corners as he slowly turned around to look at Xuanba in Lou Yue's arms. His tone held not a shred of warmth. \"Can't you tell it's fallen into a tortoise sleep from overexerting its spiritual energy? I'm a useless cripple with a damaged spiritual vein. What could I possibly do to it? You're vastly overestimating me.\"","As someone who had wandered into this world from somewhere else, Lou Yue really did not know as much about the hidden underlying rules of this realm as Xiao Rangchen did. Hearing that Xuanba's state was just tortoise sleep, he relaxed a little. Even though he disliked Xiao Rangchen, he knew full well that Xiao Rangchen was a man who owned up to his actions.","But still... why was he so riled up? With his usual cold, detached temperament, he would normally just toss out a single line of \"I didn't do it\" and walk away. Now he not only offered an explanation, he even called himself a useless cripple... that was so completely out of character.","While Lou Yue was puzzling over this in his head, Xiao Rangchen's gaze slowly settled on him too.","By some strange coincidence, the peacock-green brocade robe Lou Yue was wearing was the exact same shade as the one he had worn the very first time Xiao Rangchen met him three years ago.","His hair was never tied up in a topknot like all the other men, only loosely pinned behind his ear with an ornate hairpin. It framed his peach blossom eyes that always looked like they were half-smiling, making him stand out so sharply in any crowd that no one who had seen him could ever forget him.","But he was like the blazing sun hanging high in the sky, shining unapologetically straight into everyone's line of sight, yet no one could ever leave a single mark on that sun.","Xiao Rangchen thought that in Lou Yue's eyes, he was probably nothing more than a lowly commoner that Lou Yue wanted nothing to do with. Even if they were not enemies, there was no way they could ever be friends.","\"When did you get here? Did anything out of the ordinary happen?\"","Xiao Rangchen's voice was deep and succinct. \"Just got here. Nothing happened.\"","\"Good then...\"","\"Now, can I leave?\" Before Lou Yue could even answer, Xiao Rangchen turned on his heel and strode away with long, firm steps.","Lou Yue stood rooted to the spot, staring at that tall, straight back, feeling that something was very strange.","His gaze drifted over the thorn stud on Xiao Rangchen's right ear, and the abnormal flush high on the tip of that ear, and that odd, uneasy feeling grew even stronger.","It stayed that way until the break of dawn the next day..."]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Dawn spilled through the lattice window and fell across Lou Yue’s bed.","Xiao Rangchen slowly awoke amid a sweltering restlessness. He had unexpectedly grown drowsy while meditating the night before and, for once, slept soundly through the entire night. Even now, his consciousness still felt hazy and sluggish.","What met his eyes was an unfamiliar ceiling. Before he could think it through, a faint, sweet floral warmth curled into his nose, accompanied by a heavy pressure against his body. He lowered his eyes—and a familiar profile crashed into view.","Lou Yue was sprawled over him without the slightest hint of decorum. One arm lay across his chest, the sleeve having slipped to the crook of his elbow and exposing skin so white it was almost dazzling. One leg rested against the root of his thigh, his slender bare ankle and faintly pink toes hanging beside the black fabric of Xiao Rangchen’s clothes like a handful of snow fallen into an inkstone.","Xiao Rangchen’s breathing abruptly stalled. He raised a hand and shoved Lou Yue away with considerable force.","“Mm...” Lou Yue mumbled. His thick, dark lashes fluttered as his eyes opened, and from the corner of his vision, the tall figure’s broad back and taut waist gradually came into focus.","Lou Yue rolled over and sat up. His voice shot up an octave. “Xiao Rangchen?!”","Xiao Rangchen was straightening his loosened belt. At the sound of his name, his hand paused for a moment before he continued as though nothing had happened.","Lou Yue jumped off the bed and circled around to face him. Seeing that it really was Xiao Rangchen, his eyes widened. “You actually dared sneak into my room? Have you no shame?!”","Anyone would be unhappy to wake up and be cursed at first thing in the morning, especially when the person doing the cursing was Lou Yue. Xiao Rangchen lifted his eyes toward him, but the sharpness in his gaze froze the moment it landed on Lou Yue.","Lou Yue’s chest rose and fell. His slightly curled hair spilled over his shoulders, with a few strands hanging over his chest. The collar of his plain white silk robe gaped wide, revealing smooth, lustrous skin. A sleepy softness still lingered between his brows and eyes. At a glance, it was difficult to tell whether he was male or female.","In Lou Yue’s eyes, Xiao Rangchen’s momentary stiffness became confirmation of the truth. He gritted his teeth. “What did you do behind my back? Are you trying to assassinate me?”","Xiao Rangchen came back to himself. “I came to assassinate you dressed like this? Are you sick? I’m not.”","Lou Yue folded his arms over his chest, his tone hostile. “Then explain why you’re in my room.”","Xiao Rangchen pressed his lips together. Explain? He wanted someone to explain this to him.","“What’s the matter? Can’t explain yourself?” Lou Yue sneered.","A wave of irritation rose in Xiao Rangchen’s chest. “I woke up here.”","Lou Yue lifted his chin. “If you heard that excuse from someone else, would you believe it?”","He wouldn’t. But he couldn’t find a reason for what had happened either. Xiao Rangchen suppressed his vexation and said coolly, “Whether you believe me is your business.”","He walked around Lou Yue toward the door, but Lou Yue slipped in front of him and blocked his path.","The two of them were less than half an arm’s length apart. That faint, sweet fragrance curled toward Xiao Rangchen once more. His Adam’s apple bobbed as he countered, “Or perhaps you did something to me, and that’s why I ended up here?”","“So I dragged you into my room?” Lou Yue laughed in exasperation. “Why don’t you just say I put a spell on you, so you can’t bear to stay away from me?”","The moment the words fell, they both froze. Remembering what had happened the day before, they spoke at the same time.","“When exactly did you arrive yesterday?”","“What were you doing setting up that formation yesterday?”","Lou Yue frowned. Xiao Rangchen concealed the flicker of emotion that had crossed his eyes.","Each harboring his own suspicions, neither was willing to answer the other. For a moment, the room held nothing but their shallow breathing, its silence strangely eerie.","Lou Yue recalled Xuanba’s mention of being “entangled.” If Xiao Rangchen had lied and arrived earlier than he claimed, could the grand formation have identified him as Lou Yue himself, causing him to appear by her side? Lou Yue glanced toward Xuanba, who was still in a state of breath-concealment on the table. It seemed only Xuanba could give her an answer.","But on the bright side, even if they had become entangled, perhaps this would be the only time. One had to stay optimistic.","Deciding to look on the bright side, Lou Yue magnanimously stepped aside. “Forget it. I’ll let you off today. But if there’s a next time, don’t expect to get away with it so easily.”","Xiao Rangchen sneered. He had no idea which of them was trying to get away with something easily. Still, he had no desire to say more and strode toward the door.","“Wait.” Lou Yue suddenly called out. There was an unnatural note in his voice. “You... sneak out through the window.”","Xiao Rangchen fell silent.","Lou Yue felt a little awkward under his gaze, but he still stubbornly held his chin high. “Do you want people to see you leaving my room first thing in the morning?” Though they were both men and no one would draw any strange conclusions if they were discovered, Lou Yue still felt that it was better to avoid unnecessary trouble.","Xiao Rangchen had no wish to be seen either, but leaving through the window would truly make him look as if he had done something shameful.","“No one will see me,” he said, then opened the door and walked out.","Lou Yue poked his head through the doorway, but Xiao Rangchen’s figure had already vanished. He curled his lip. Fine. Long Aotian really was Long Aotian. Even with his spiritual meridians crippled, he could still act so arrogantly.","Lou Yue closed the door again, carried Xuanba to the bed, and observed him for a long while, but could not see any sign that he was about to end his breath-concealment state.","He sighed and muttered to himself, “See? You wouldn’t let me ask at the time, and now everything’s become a complete mystery. Still, at least nothing else happened.”","“Besides, your method yesterday really worked. The speed at which I absorb spiritual power is so much faster now. I feel like I can break through to the late Core Formation stage with just a little more cultivation today. Ha ha, maybe by the time you wake up, I’ll already have reached the Nascent Soul stage!”","The icy chill in his hands was piercing. Before long, Lou Yue’s hands had frozen purple, but he continued to hold Xuanba and murmured, “So you have to wake up soon, Xuanba. Otherwise, you won’t get to see how powerful I’ve become...”","The morning mist had only just dispersed, and the courtyard remained quiet.","Xiao Rangchen evaded the guards on night duty. He had originally planned to take the opportunity to find Xiao Aiai and leave with her, but after considering it, that would truly make him look like the “sneak” Lou Yue had called him. In the end, he left alone.","The moment he stepped outside the courtyard, he ran into someone he least wanted to see.","Fortunately, he had not brought Xiao Aiai with him, he thought.","“Well, speak of the devil. This is truly finding what I’ve searched for without the slightest effort.” Cang Wu’s voice was full of contempt.","Before Cangya Xun, who stood beside him, could say anything, Cang Wu had already drawn his sword and thrust it at Xiao Rangchen.","Xiao Rangchen spread his right hand, summoning his spear from thin air, and knocked the sword aside. With a clang, sparks flew through the morning light. The two figures moved as swiftly as ghosts, exchanging more than a dozen blows in the blink of an eye.","“What’s going on?”","The speaker was Lou Weixiao. He had come to find Cangya Xun over the imprisoned Cang Youshan and was escorting him toward the prison when he suddenly saw one of his men attacking the person who had emerged from the nearby courtyard.","Cangya Xun’s fingertip brushed leisurely over the dragon pattern on his sword sheath. His expression was inscrutable. “He is merely a traitor who abandoned my Cangya clan. What? Young Master Lou, do you intend to interfere?”","His voice was icy and carried an unmistakable arrogance.","Lou Weixiao’s hand tightened imperceptibly. Unlike the Lou clan, which had never settled on its next clan head, the Northern Dark Cangya clan had long since designated Cangya Xun as its heir. So long as Cangya Xun did not die, he was guaranteed to become the next head of the Cangya clan. His power and status were far beyond what Lou Weixiao, the current Young Master Lou, possessed.","“Since this is a matter concerning the Cangya clan, I naturally will not interfere.”","Lou Weixiao forced a smile, though it did not reach his eyes. At that moment, Lou Haina suddenly stepped forward and whispered several words into his ear.","Lou Weixiao’s gaze shifted toward the courtyard bearing the sign “Sleeping Clouds.” His brows drew together. “Lou Yue?”","“Yes,” Lou Haina replied. He had already told Lou Weixiao yesterday about how Lou Yue had seen through the guiwang at the city gate, adding plenty of embellishment as he recounted Lou Yue’s disrespect toward the Young Master.","Only then did Lou Weixiao take a closer look at the situation before him.","Xiao Rangchen was already at a disadvantage, a sword from Cang Wu piercing his abdomen.","The silver-glinting blade in Cang Wu's hand pointed straight at Xiao Rangchen's heart. Xiao Rangchen darted to the side, and the tip of the sword brushed past his left chest before sinking deep into his shoulder.","\"Puchi—\" the blade slid clear through his shoulder.","Xiao Rangchen pushed off the ground with the tip of his foot, letting his body lurch backward. Fresh blood gushed the moment the sword was wrenched free, but he seemed not to feel the pain at all. As he spun, both his right hand and the spear he held wrapped in a rippling water-colored halo, and he thrust the weapon toward Lou Weixiao with a force that split the air.","The second he laid eyes on Cangya Xun, Xiao Rangchen knew there was almost no chance he would walk away from this alive. Cangya Xun had broken through to the Mahayana stage two years prior. If his spiritual meridian had not been damaged, the outcome might have been anyone's guess, but now he could barely maintain a foothold at the Foundation Establishment stage—fighting Cangya Xun was nothing less than hurling an egg against a rock.","Since death was inevitable, the least he could do was wound Cangya Xun. How else could he rest in peace?","This strike from Xiao Rangchen was driven by total resolve to die. The spear trembled as it tore through the air, letting out a low, wailing whistle, and a faint dragon shadow coiled around its tip, its momentum utterly terrifying.","Cangya Xun looked at the familiar spear technique, a flicker of dark malice crossing his eyes.","Back on the summit of Cangya Peak, his father had once said, \"If this boy takes up the sword, I fear his comprehension of the sword path will not be inferior to Xun's.\" Even then, Xiao Rangchen's spiritual power had been an entire great realm below his own, and he was nothing but a commoner of humble birth. What right did he have to stand equal to him? Cangya Xun had never once fought Xiao Rangchen, even after the latter skipped all the usual procedures to go from an outer sect disciple to an inner sect one, then climbed the ranks of cultivation at an almost dizzying speed.","He had always kept a full great realm of cultivation above Xiao Rangchen. But only he himself knew that the gap was growing harder and harder to maintain.","When Cang Wu attacked Xiao Rangchen during the trial, he had turned a blind eye. The damage to Xiao Rangchen's spiritual meridian had been an \"unfortunate accident\". If anyone was to blame, it was Xiao Rangchen's own stubborn pride, for forcing himself to refine a demon core two full stages above his own level. If he had just bowed his head and submitted, Cang Wu would not have pushed him so far, and his parents would never have lost their lives afterward.","At the end of the day, Xiao Rangchen was nothing but a commoner. Where did he get such unyielding pride? And what gave him the right to compare himself to Cangya Xun?","Disgust welled up in Cangya Xun's eyes. He did not even bother to draw his sword, raising his palm to meet the oncoming spear tip directly. No matter how fierce the spear's momentum was, Xiao Rangchen was only a Foundation Establishment cultivator now, and he had long since left the other man far, far behind.","That was exactly the moment Xiao Rangchen had been waiting for.","His left hand flicked outward sharply, sending three silver needles shooting straight for the vital points on Cangya Xun's face.","\"Futile last struggle,\" Cangya Xun scoffed, brushing the needles aside effortlessly. But he had not expected that Xiao Rangchen's move was only meant to buy a split second of time.","A wash of blood-red light spread from Xiao Rangchen's body to the black spear that had been blocked. The instant the bloody glow wrapped around the spear tip, a dragon's roar that shook the surrounding wilderness exploded through the air. The next second, the spear tore straight through Cangya Xun's palm, its sharp edge grazing the side of his face and leaving a stinging, bleeding gash.","Cangya Xun's expression darkened. He let out a cold huff, and the sword at his waist flew out of its sheath on its own, slashing straight for Xiao Rangchen's neck.","Those few earlier moves had already exhausted every last bit of Xiao Rangchen's strength and every trick he had up his sleeve. To land that one wound on Cangya Xun, he had left himself completely open, with no way to defend himself now.","That was the very best he could do...","Xiao Rangchen closed his eyes, a bleak, sorrowful smile tugging faintly at the corner of his lips as he waited for death to claim him—","\"Clang!\"","A clear, ringing crash of metal against jade burst right beside his ears.","The next moment, something coiled around his waist and abdomen, yanking him sharply backward out of harm's way."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["Cangya Xun raised his sword to give chase, but the jade token that had just knocked his blade aside suddenly erupted with a tidal surge of spiritual power.","With a thunderous boom, he was hurled backward several yards and slammed heavily into the courtyard wall, blood seeping from the corner of his mouth.","“Young Lord!” Cang Wu’s expression changed drastically as he rushed toward Cangya Xun.","Everyone present—including the bystanders who had come merely to watch the spectacle—stared in shock at the jade token lying in the dust. Then, as one, they turned to look at Lou Yue standing at the courtyard gate.","Lou Yue stared blankly at the scene, as though she had not been the one to hurl the jade token in a moment of desperation. The spiritual force she had used to pull Xiao Rangchen backward also dissipated midair, allowing him to fall from the air.","“...” Could time rewind?","The moment she received her subordinate’s report and came out, she had seen a sword coming down on Xiao Rangchen’s neck. Her hand had moved faster than her brain, flinging out the jade token from the book—the one that had shielded the original owner’s body from three fatal attacks.","Damn it. Just like that, her chance to change her life was gone...","“Who are you, to dare interfere in the affairs of our Cangya?” Cang Wu demanded sharply as he supported Cangya Xun.","Lou Yue was still caught up in her regret and had not heard a word he said. To everyone else, however, her silence looked like sheer disdain.","A gloomy, vicious look spread across Cang Wu’s face. Just as he was about to rush forward, Cangya Xun caught his arm.","Wiping the blood from his lips and brushing the dust from his clothes, Cangya Xun moved with unhurried elegance, yet carried an intimidating pressure. “Which branch of the Lou clan do you belong to?”","Lou Yue met his cold, savage gaze. Cangya, and addressed as Young Lord—there was no need to think further. This man had to be Cangya Xun, the culprit in the book responsible for the male lead losing both his parents.","According to the plot, the two of them were never supposed to encounter each other in Xuandu. Yet now they had not only met, but Xiao Rangchen’s spiritual channels had yet to recover.","Protect him or not? That was the question.","Protecting him meant becoming enemies with the Cangya of Beiming from this day forward.","Not protecting him meant Xiao Rangchen would most likely not survive today.","Lou Yue’s gaze drifted uncontrollably to the other side.","Xiao Rangchen was leaning half his body against a tree beside the courtyard gate, his face pale. Blood poured from the wounds in his shoulder and abdomen, soaking broad dark patches into his black robes. Before long, a pool of blood had gathered beneath him.","Lou Yue scoffed inwardly. Weren’t you acting all high and mighty when you left? Look at you now. That’s what you get for being so smug.","As if sensing her gaze, Xiao Rangchen turned to look at her as well. The hatred in his eyes still burned fiercely. Their gazes met in midair for a brief instant before Xiao Rangchen looked away first, as though he did not care what Lou Yue chose to do next.","Lou Yue sneered and turned back.","She lifted a hand and drew the jade token from the ground with spiritual power. After blowing the dust from its surface, she answered casually, “Oh, my father is just a man who guards a mine for the Lou family in some backwater village. I suppose I barely count as a branch of a branch family.”","“Young Master Yue is being far too modest. Young Lord of Cangya, this is the only son of our Third Master—Lou Yue,” Lou Haina “helpfully” introduced Lou Yue.","Lou Yue shot Lou Haina a cool, cutting glance.","“Brother Yue, it has been many years. I never recognized you.” Lou Weixiao waved the jade-bone fan in his hand, a smile playing on his lips. His tone was so intimate that they might truly have been close brothers. “Young Lord of Cangya, please forgive him. Brother Yue must have been deceived by some villain and does not yet know that this man is a traitor to your Cangya.”","Lou Yue suddenly laughed, his tone languid, though every word was distinct. “Who says I don’t know? It’s just the same old trick—crying thief first, then wiping out the evidence.”","Xiao Rangchen abruptly turned to look at Lou Yue. Surprise and confusion flickered uncertainly in his eyes.","Cangya Xun’s expression darkened, and an overwhelming, icy hostility radiated from him.","Unmoved, Lou Yue said, “I don’t care what grudges you had before. But he owes me something now, and until he pays it back, I’m not letting him go.”","Seeing the two sides locked in confrontation, Lou Weixiao realized this was an opportunity to test just how much weight Lou Yue carried in the family head’s eyes. He immediately signaled for Lou Haina to report the matter.","Yet in less than half the time it took to drink a cup of tea, Lou Haina returned—bringing someone wholly unexpected with him.","“Grandpa Yan, why are you here?” Lou Weixiao froze.","Lou Yue looked toward the elderly man called “Grandpa Yan” and recognized him as Lou Zhongyan from the portraits: Lou Mo’s most trusted confidant. Lou Yue had no interest in forging ties with the Lou family. He merely glanced at the man before preparing to look away, but their gazes happened to meet. The old man’s eyes were filled with the kindly warmth and affection an elder might show a younger generation.","Lou Yue: ?","“I was handling a small errand for the family head. I ran into Haina and came along.”","After speaking, Lou Zhongyan walked toward Cangya Xun and smiled slowly. “Young Lord of Cangya, weren’t you meant to interrogate Cang Youshan today? Why are you still here? If you delay any longer, I’m afraid you won’t make it in time.”","He did not release even a trace of spiritual power and looked like nothing more than an elderly man in good health. Yet as his words fell, everyone felt an invisible pressure settle over them.","Cangya Xun fell silent. At his side, Cang Wu could no longer hold back. Pointing at Xiao Rangchen, he shouted, “He is a traitor to our Cangya! Are you openly sheltering him?!”","Lou Zhongyan merely lifted his gaze to the sky, speaking unhurriedly as though making casual conversation. “If you do not leave now, you truly will not make it in time.”","Cang Wu: “You—”","Cangya Xun stopped Cang Wu with a hand. His cold, proud eyes fixed steadily on the old man. After a long moment, he concealed the malice in his gaze and said with finality, “Leave.”","“Young Lord?!” Cang Wu cried in disbelief.","Cangya Xun ignored him. After casting one final glance at Xiao Rangchen, he turned and left first. Cang Wu had no choice but to hurriedly follow.","Lou Weixiao looked toward Lou Yue, his expression complex and unreadable. Then, with the respectful manner of a junior bidding farewell to an elder, he took his leave of Lou Zhongyan and departed with Lou Haina.","A confrontation on the verge of erupting into violence ended in an entirely unexpected fashion.","Lou Yue could not help marveling at the strength of a dragon protagonist’s luck. Thinking of it that way, he regretted his earlier impulsiveness; he had needlessly made himself an enemy.","Lou Yue was just considering going over to mock Xiao Rangchen and recover a little psychological balance when someone suddenly stopped in front of him.","“Young Master Yue, don’t go throwing your jade token around next time,” Lou Zhongyan said with a smile, his voice as gentle as that of a kindly old neighbor. “If it breaks, there won’t be another one.”","Lou Yue brushed the bits of dried grass clinging to the tassel of the jade token without the slightest embarrassment. With a slight movement of her fingers, she stored the token engraved with the characters “Riding the Wind” in her storage ring, then gave a cool “Oh.”","Lou Zhongyan continued smiling as he asked, “Young Master Yue, will you be taking part in the Ancient Tree Dao Insight the day after tomorrow?”","“I will.”","Compared with Lou Weixiao’s respectful attitude, Lou Yue’s response could only be described as cold. Lou Zhongyan, however, did not seem to mind. “Good. If you have the chance, Young Master Yue, you should pay the family head a visit and keep him company for a while.”","Lou Yue gave a perfunctory “Mm.”","Lou Zhongyan did not linger. He turned around and, after a few steps, disappeared from everyone’s sight.","With no more excitement to watch, the crowd had already dispersed. The only ones left at the entrance of Sleeping Cloud Courtyard were the few people following behind Lou Yue, along with Xiao Rangchen, who was leaning against a tree and could barely remain standing.","His once-straight back was now hunched, trembling faintly. His eyes, usually as sharp as an eagle’s, were clouded with exhaustion. For once, Lou Yue could make out a hint of frailty in him.","Before she could say anything, Xiao Rangchen spoke in a firm voice. “I owe you my life. I’ll repay you, but this has nothing to do with Aiai.”","Lou Yue had been facing him, but upon hearing those words, she turned her toes in another direction. Too lazy to say even a single word, she went straight back into the courtyard.","Inside Sleeping Cloud Courtyard, Lou Yue went up the stairs two or three steps at a time. Little Qiu hurried after her. “Young Master, aren’t we bringing Xiao Rangchen inside?”","Lou Yue did not slow down. “Bring him in for what? He’s not worthy of entering!”","That scumbag was on the verge of death and still thinking about taking his harem beauty away. He wasn’t worth it! She had wasted the life-saving opportunity on her jade token for nothing—what a terrible loss.","Little Qiu asked softly, “Young Master, are you angry that Xiao Rangchen is still thinking about taking Miss Xiao away?”","Lou Yue stopped and turned her head toward him, her voice suddenly rising several pitches. “Who said I’m angry? Is that bastard even worth it?”","Little Qiu fell silent for a moment. He had already called him a bastard—how could that not be anger?","Though he thought that to himself, he quickly agreed aloud. “It was Little Qiu’s mistake. It’s just... Xiao Rangchen is so severely injured. If he leaves, might the people from the Cangya clan secretly make a move against him? If something happens, I’m afraid Miss Xiao will be heartbroken and blame you, Young Master.”","Lou Yue said nothing, but her pace up the stairs gradually slowed. Just as Little Qiu thought she was about to order someone to follow him, Lou Yue’s voice came through, gritted with fury.","“Saving him once doesn’t mean I’m going to save him twice. Dream on!”","With that, Lou Yue stomped up the stairs and slammed the door shut with a heavy bang.","Little Qiu stared at the tightly closed door and sighed inwardly.","That had really made her angry...","Inside the room, Lou Yue held Xuanba in her arms and complained about Xiao Rangchen’s ingratitude. Only after venting her frustration did she gradually calm down. She closed her eyes, focused her mind, and began cultivating.","It was not until the moon had risen high overhead and all things had fallen silent that she lay down to get her beauty sleep.","Lou Yue did not sleep peacefully that night. She kept feeling cold drafts drilling into her bones from every direction.","She wanted to pull up the covers, but somehow she could not find them. The bed had also become hard as stone, while her head felt unusually heavy, leaving her unable to wake up. At last, she finally managed to touch something warm. Clutching it tightly in her arms, she was at last able to sleep more soundly.","The following morning, Lou Yue had only just managed to fall into a deep sleep when she was awakened by something pressing against her stomach.","Whenever she moved, it moved with her, prodding her abdomen again and again and disturbing her so thoroughly that she could not find peace.","Lou Yue had no choice but to summon a little more energy and reach out to remove whatever was pressing against her.","A hoarse, muffled male groan suddenly sounded above her head.","Lou Yue's hand froze. Her mind cleared at once. Xiao Rangchen, who was lying beside her, also woke up, though pain was what had jolted him back to his senses.","He seized Lou Yue by the wrist. His voice was husky with the distinctive rasp of early morning, and there was a hint of restraint in it. “Let go!”","Only then did Lou Yue belatedly realize that she was curled up in Xiao Rangchen's arms. She stiffened and immediately tried to push him away, but her left hand was pinned beneath him while her right was caught in his grip. In her panic, her brain failed to keep up, and her fingers instinctively tightened.","Xiao Rangchen sucked in a breath, unable to suppress the muffled sound that escaped from his throat.","Lou Yue lowered her head to look at what she was holding. The next second, she let go with her right hand. Even with Xiao Rangchen's hand clamped around her wrist, she instantly unleashed a surge of powerful spiritual energy and sent him flying with a forceful shove.","“What the hell is wrong with you?!”","Xiao Rangchen twisted in midair, but his movements were noticeably sluggish. When he landed, he even staggered twice before managing to steady himself.","Lou Yue sat up and discovered that they were in the branches of a camphor tree. But that was not the point right now. The point was that Xiao Rangchen had actually gotten hard against her!!","She was a man right now! How much of a scumbag was Xiao Rangchen? Did he swing both ways??!!","“If you can't control what you've got down there, I'll cut it off for you!” Lou Yue was on the verge of breaking down. This was the first time she had ever encountered a scumbag who had gotten handsy with her, and the first time she had ever touched... Even the one on her own body had never done this to her...","The more she thought about it, the more distraught she became. Lou Yue jumped straight out of the tree and rushed to the lakeside to wash her hands, looking as though she intended to scrub off an entire layer of skin from her right hand.","The veins on Xiao Rangchen's forehead throbbed violently.","No man would let another man take advantage of him first thing in the morning unless he was sick in the head. As a man himself, Lou Yue could not possibly fail to understand that. Xiao Rangchen could only attribute her reaction to deliberate provocation.","“You're so capable, so why don't you try controlling it yourself?” he said through clenched teeth, his pale face looking ashen.","Xiao Rangchen had meant for Lou Yue to try controlling her own problem. However, possessing a woman's heart, Lou Yue instinctively misunderstood him and assumed he was asking her to control his.","Lou Yue's eyes flew wide. She could not believe Xiao Rangchen was making such a filthy joke.","She casually grabbed a stone beside her and hurled it at Xiao Rangchen. The stone struck him squarely in the chest.","Xiao Rangchen collapsed on the spot.","----------------------","Xiao Rangchen: Take responsibility.","Lou Yue: Are you faking this for sympathy??"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["Xiao Rangchen collapsed at the foot of the tree, his eyes squeezed tightly shut.","Lou Yue shuffled slowly over. \"Hey, don't you dare try to scam me.\" The rock she'd thrown was no bigger than a bird's egg, there was no way it could have knocked him out cold.","Xiao Rangchen still didn't open his eyes, as dark red blood seeped through the gray-blue outer robe over his shoulder and abdomen, spreading silently across the fabric.","Lou Yue's brows tightened, and she squatted down very reluctantly.","Xiao Rangchen's face was as pale as a sheet, his lips tinged purple. His long, thick eyelashes trembled faintly, and his shoulders shook along with them, as if he was holding back some searing pain.","Lou Yue poked his forearm. \"Hey, Xiao Rangchen, stop playing dead.\"","She shook his arm again, but there was still no response.","\"Your fainting has nothing to do with me hitting you, don't try to frame me!\" Even as she said that, though, catching sight of the pool of blood under Xiao Rangchen growing wider and wider, she pulled out a hemostatic pill.","The tip of Lou Yue's finger holding the pill paused just before it reached his lips, then she let out a disgusted \"tut\" sound, pressed her fingers hard, and stuffed the pill into his mouth roughly and quickly, giving his chin a perfunctory little nudge to make him swallow.","As soon as she saw the prominent bob of his Adam's apple move down, she pulled her hand away, ran to the water's edge, and washed her hands thoroughly.","She dawdled for the time it takes to burn half an incense stick, waiting until she figured enough time had passed before she ambled back.","The bleeding had stopped, and the pool of blood under him was drying up, but the exposed skin on Xiao Rangchen's body had turned from cold white to a dull, ashen gray that spoke of approaching death.","Lou Yue hesitated for a moment, then reached out to feel the pulse on the outside of his wrist.","She couldn't diagnose pulses, but she knew a normal person's pulse didn't beat once every five or six breaths. The thought suddenly popped into her head: Xiao Rangchen isn't going to die, is he?","\"Hey! Xiao Rangchen, wake up! Xiao Rangchen!\" Lou Yue shook him hard, raising her voice, but the person she was calling didn't react at all, not even his breath seemed to be there anymore.","Lou Yue was just debating whether she should flee the scene immediately when the hand she was holding on his wrist with just let go—only for a sudden, strong force to clamp down hard on her.","Lou Yue struggled several times but couldn't pull free. The unconscious Xiao Rangchen was like a drowning man clutching the last piece of driftwood, holding her hand tightly in his palm.","Lou Yue's mouth twitched. Great, she'd successfully been scammed.","She gritted her teeth, but in the end she still couldn't just leave him here. If he really died, who knew if the Heavenly Dao would strike her down for it.","Lou Yue first sent a message to Little Qiu, telling him to find a reliable physician and wait at Cloud Sleep Courtyard, then send people to the place where they were maintaining the formation earlier.","After sending the notice, she realized she was still wearing her inner garment, so she slipped on an outer robe, then frowned and hauled Xiao Rangchen onto her back.","Even though she'd braced herself for it, the moment Xiao Rangchen's full weight came down on her, Lou Yue was crushed right into the ground, and bit down on a mouthful of mud.","\"Fuck me!\"","She spat out the blades of grass in her mouth, and grumbled and cursed as she channeled spiritual power to her limbs to heft the man up onto her back again. If she wasn't worried that he wouldn't make it in time, she wouldn't have gone to all this trouble—she could have just waited slowly for people to come carry him.","\"I must have had the worst luck in eight lifetimes, getting transmigrated into this stupid book!\"","\"What did Xiao Rangchen even eat to grow up?! Rocks? He's so heavy!\"","Lou Yue's one hand was still being clutched, and she tried to yank it free with spiritual power, but the unconscious Xiao Rangchen just squeezed even tighter by instinct.","Lou Yue gave up trying to get her hand back. But even with spiritual power, it was very difficult to steady a man half a head taller than herself with only one hand. After just a few steps, the man on her back started sliding down. Lou Yue had to bend her waist even lower to keep him from slipping off too fast.","\"My poor back...\"","She panted for breath, the sweat on her back mixing with Xiao Rangchen's blood, sticking to her skin in a sticky, uncomfortable mess. \"Xiao Rangchen, you owe me more than you could ever pay back...\"","\"You... really are... so heavy...\"","Lou Yue moved forward with difficulty, pouring spiritual power into her feet so that each step she took carried her ten times further than her usual strides.","\"You know how to grab my hand, but you don't know how to stay steady on my back?!\"","\"Slide again, and I'm not carrying you anymore. I'll just leave you here to fend for yourself!\"","Damn, he's slipping more!","When Little Qiu came hurrying over with a group of people, Lou Yue was leaning against a tree, bent over, straining to haul the slipping man on her back back up. Her messy strands of hair were stuck to her face with sweat, and no one could tell if the wetness on her face was her own or the man's on her back.","\"Young Master!\" Little Qiu rushed over immediately.","Lou Yue froze when she heard him, and the next second she roughly shook the man off her back. Who would have thought that when he fell, he would drag her down with him, and the two of them ended up toppling over onto the ground together.","Little Qiu was startled, and quickly helped her up. \"Young Master! Are you alright?\"","Lou Yue coughed lightly. \"I'm fine.\"","Little Qiu caught sight of the large dark red stain on the back of Lou Yue's brocade robe, and his face paled in shock. \"Young Master!\"","Lou Yue glanced back, and explained, \"It's his.\" Then she looked up and asked, \"Where's the physician?\"","\"He's already waiting at Cloud Sleep Courtyard.\" Little Qiu directed the others to lift Xiao Rangchen onto their backs.","Just as they were about to set off, everyone's eyes landed on Lou Yue's hand with a strange, awkward look.","Lou Yue followed their gazes and looked down, realizing they were staring at their two tightly clasped hands. Her cheeks burned instantly, and she snapped, red-faced and indignant, \"What are you all looking at! Hurry up and go.\"","The crowd averted their eyes at once. Lou Yue walked beside Xiao Rangchen, keeping a moderate distance. She tugged at her hand again, but still couldn't pull it free, and in her heart she cursed Xiao Rangchen a thousand more times—what a troublemaker, ruining her good reputation!","Lou Yue had already traveled most of the way, so it wasn't long before the group returned to Cloud Sleep Courtyard.","\"You say he's poisoned?\"","In the room next to Lou Yue's at Cloud Sleep Courtyard, Xiao Rangchen was carefully laid on the bed. The physician who had been waiting felt his pulse, examined his wounds, and after a long while, stated his conclusion.","\"This poison does little harm to people with fully intact spiritual meridians, but to someone whose spiritual meridians are damaged like him, it's a deadly poison. At its current rate of eating away at him, he'll be dead in less than two days.\"","The room fell quiet. Lou Yue asked sharply, \"What is this poison, and how did he get it?\"","\"The poison was on the sword wound. Its name is Banehusk, and it loves to feed on spiritual meridians. As soon as it enters the body, it latches on. If your spiritual meridians are unharmed, you can dispel it on your own. But if you're in his condition, Banehusk will devour straight through the damaged parts of the meridians. If it was discovered early there would still be a chance, but now... there's no way to save him.\"","A sword wound... it must have been those people from Cangya the day before.","\"What if I get the antidote from the people who injured him?\" Lou Yue pressed.","The old physician put his silver needles back into their case as he spoke. \"There is no antidote for Banehusk. For most people it's barely toxic, and people without spiritual meridians won't even be affected by it at all. To put it plainly, this poison was made specifically to target him.\"","He put his things into his medicine box and stood up. \"It's a poison tailored to his condition. He can't be saved.\" He turned to leave.","Lou Yue spoke up behind him. \"You just can't save him because your medical skills are not good enough.\"","The old man turned around. \"Young Master, no need to goad me. If I say he can't be saved, there is no other person under heaven who can.\"","Lou Yue didn't know where Little Qiu had found this physician. She couldn't tell if his medical skills were any good, but his arrogance was definitely top-tier. And his getup was so ordinary he would blend right into any crowd, looking exactly like the kind of quack you see everywhere in TV dramas.","\"But,\" the old man suddenly said, a glint of mischief in his eyes that didn't match his age, \"what's your relationship with that young man over there, anyway? You two are both men.\"","Seeing the man's gaze fixed on their still-clasped hands, Lou Yue's face darkened, and she said irritably, \"If you can't cure him then leave, stop gossiping!\"","\"Tsk tsk, what a bad temper. He's willing to be a cut-sleeve for someone like you, tsk tsk...\"","Lou Yue was already frazzled, and her temper flared up the second she heard that. \"...What nonsense are you spouting? What's this 'men who love men' garbage? Stop rambling on and on! If you can't even save someone, just scram right now!\"","\"Who said this old man has no way to save him? I said I can't cure him easily, that doesn't mean I have no solution at all.\" The old man glared right back at her.","Wasn't that the exact same thing?","\"His spiritual meridian is damaged, that's why the toxin seeped right into his meridians.\" Feng Que took a seat on the stool with surprisingly brisk steps, poured himself a cup of tea, and said slowly, \"If you can track down the Never-Fading Flower to rebuild his spiritual meridian, that silly Huntu poison will dissolve completely no problem.\"","Lou Yue tried to step over, but her hand was held fast, so she could only stay by the bedside and ask, \"His current state... can he even withstand using the Never-Fading Flower?\"","The Never-Fading Flower was indeed the only known thing that could repair a damaged spiritual meridian, but the process of rebuilding one was as agonizing as having your tendons ripped out and your bones flayed. In the book, Xiao Rangchen had bled from all seven orifices, suffering nonstop for a full day and night before he pulled through. Right now he was already hanging on by a thread, so using the Never-Fading Flower carelessly would very likely turn into the last straw that killed him.","\"Anyone else on their deathbed using this would have less than one in ten chance of surviving, but for him\" the old man glanced at the person on the bed, then held up five fingers, \"this old man is fifty percent confident.\"","\"Only fifty percent?\" Lou Yue frowned in dissatisfaction. They were going to use such a precious thing as the Never-Fading Flower, and still only got half a shot?","The old man paused, rolled his eyes at her, \"Go find anyone else, and you won't even get a ten percent success rate, you believe that or not?\"","Lou Yue furrowed her brows and said nothing more.","Feng Que finished his cup of tea, patted the dust off his robes and stood to leave. \"Alright, take all the time you want to think about it. But once this night passes, even if you bring the Never-Fading Flower back, it'll be too late.\"","\"Wait.\" Lou Yue called after him. \"How am I supposed to trust you? And what makes you think I can get the Never-Fading Flower before nightfall?\"","The old man turned around, a confident glint in his eyes. \"You don't have to trust me. The choice is all yours. As for whether you can get the Never-Fading Flower\" he stroked his beard, a knowing smirk spreading across his face, \"this old man is just making a little bet. If you can track it down, then I can bring up the little request I have next, right?\"","\"...\" So he was testing her capabilities this whole time. Lou Yue was so annoyed, her tone turning sharp. \"What request? Tell me now.\"","\"Relax, all I want is a specific spiritual herb. If you can get your hands on the Never-Fading Flower, that herb will be a piece of cake for you to grab too.\" He waved his hand casually, walking out without even looking back. \"Come find this old man again once you have the Never-Fading Flower.\"","Watching the figure vanish through the doorway, Lou Yue finally relaxed her furrowed brows.","He had a request, which at least proved he would put his full effort into saving the patient.","Before Lou Yue could call for him, Little Qiu already stepped into the room. Lou Yue asked him where he found that old man.","\"His name is Feng Que,\" Little Qiu explained, \"he's the most famous physician in Xuandi City. He charges whatever consultation fee he feels like, he's a total oddball, but everyone says his medical skills are top-tier. He even treats commoners for free sometimes.\"","Lou Yue's mind stirred a little, and she asked, \"How much did you pay him as the consultation fee?\"","Little Qiu looked a little sheepish. \"Five hundred spirit stones... I knew you were in a huge hurry, young master, and I was scared no other doctor would be half as skilled as him, so I paid it.\"","Five hundred spirit stones was enough for an ordinary civilian family to live comfortably for a whole lifetime. It was exorbitantly expensive, but for the rich second generation that the original body was, it was nothing out of the ordinary.","\"Young master, do you want me to run a background check on him?\" Little Qiu asked.","Lou Yue thought for a moment, then shook her head. \"No need.\"","\"Understood.\" Little Qiu nodded. For a moment, no one said anything, and Little Qiu's gaze drifted down unconsciously, landing on the two hands clasped tightly together.","The man's hand had sharp knuckles, clean, defined lines, the wrist bone stretching the skin tight, blue veins faintly bulging on the back of his hand, carrying a wild, unyielding will to survive that refused to be broken free.","And the hand he was clutching tightly in his palm had slender knuckles, the wrist glowing with the soft, fine luster of polished jade.","The man's unconscious tight grip left a faint pink mark on that pale jade-like wrist, casting a faint, ambiguous, tender vibe between the two that was hard to put into words.","Young master...","Could it be that the rumors were really true? That he really liked men?"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["“Go wait outside.”","Little Qiu came back to himself and hurried out, closing the door behind him.","Lou Yue calmly watched the door. The moment it clicked shut, she turned and tried to pry Xiao Rangchen’s fingers away. She forced at them for a long while, but his hand did not budge. Instead, her own wrist was squeezed red.","She glared irritably at the unconscious man on the bed. “Fine. You’re the one refusing to let go. Don’t blame anyone else for leaving you to die once you reach the Yellow Springs!”","Lou Yue sat down directly on the edge of the bed. Long Aotian didn’t want to live, and that had nothing to do with her. Surely the heavenly thunder wouldn’t strike her for no reason, right? Hmph.","The thought had barely crossed her mind when the hand gripping hers suddenly loosened.","“...”","Lou Yue whipped her head around and glared daggers at the man on the bed. “Xiao Rangchen, did you do that on purpose?” He had to be awake!","Lost in a hazy stupor, Xiao Rangchen’s long lashes drooped listlessly. The sharpness that usually defined his brows and eyes had faded, leaving behind nothing but exhaustion. He looked, in fact, rather pitifully fragile.","Lou Yue shot to her feet and began pacing around the room, her steps hurried.","She was Long Aotian’s rival in love. Why did the Heavenly Dao always force her to face the question of whether or not to save her enemy? Was it testing her moral character? This was ridiculous...","The future Long Aotian would kill her. Of course she couldn’t save him. There was no need to think about it—","Yet when her gaze accidentally swept over the edge of the bed, Lou Yue froze.","The hand that had been gripping hers now hung limply at his side, utterly devoid of color. It reminded her of a withered skeleton on a snowfield, drained of all vitality and steeped in deathly silence.","Lou Yue stamped her foot hard and warned herself in a low voice, “Lou Yue, don’t be a bleeding-heart saint!”","As long as she stood by and did nothing, the future would be completely rewritten. As long as she did nothing...","The air in the room was oppressively heavy, making it difficult to breathe.","Lou Yue turned and headed for the door, but just as her foot crossed the threshold, she inexplicably stopped.","Seeing Lou Yue with her brows lowered and a troubled look on her face, Little Qiu wisely said nothing.","After a long while, Lou Yue slowly closed her eyes and muttered resignedly, “I must have been cursed for eight lifetimes.”","Then she suddenly opened her eyes and instructed him, “I’m going out for a while. Whether I’m back or not by the end of the late afternoon, go and bring Feng Que here.”","Little Qiu was just about to ask whether she needed someone to accompany her when Lou Yue had already hurried back into the room, changed clothes, and swept out like the wind.","Little Qiu thought for a moment, then personally stood guard outside Xiao Rangchen’s door.","Dusk descended, and the lanterns came alight.","At the end of the late afternoon, a dust-covered figure hurried back.","A thin sheen of sweat glistened at Lou Yue’s temples. In her arms, she carried a three-foot-long white jade box, its surface wreathed in faint spiritual energy.","“Where’s Feng Que?” Lou Yue asked between breaths.","“He’s inside,” Little Qiu hurriedly replied.","“You stand guard here. Don’t let anyone come near.”","Lou Yue tossed out the order, pushed open the door, and closed it behind her.","In less than half a day, the man on the bed had somehow grown even more pallid. He looked no different from a corpse.","Lou Yue’s heart clenched. She hurried forward and grabbed one of his hands to feel for his pulse. She had rushed back, and her heart was pounding wildly in her chest. For a long moment, her fingertips could not detect the slightest beat.","“Stop checking. He’s not dead yet.”","Feng Que looked at the woman who had entered without sparing him a glance and teased her.","At last, Lou Yue felt a faint pulse. The heart that had been hanging in her throat dropped back into place, and she immediately flung Xiao Rangchen’s wrist away in disgust.","Tsk. At least he knew better than to die. If he had, she would have suffered a huge loss.","Lou Yue placed the white jade box on the table in front of Feng Que. “Now it’s your turn to show what you can do.”","Feng Que opened the box. Inside lay a Buyan flower wreathed in spiritual energy. Its petals were a translucent purple, and it was of the highest grade.","He raised his eyes to Lou Yue, his meaning clear. “This old man really didn’t misjudge you.”","Lou Yue dragged over a chair and sat down. She poured herself a cup of tea and drained it in one gulp before lifting her eyes. “Spare me the nonsense. If you can’t save him, I’ll hold you responsible.”","Feng Que pinched one of the petals between his fingers. “With a Buyan flower of this quality, this old man now has a seventy percent chance.”","Lou Yue rolled her eyes. “I only accept success.”","“Then it depends on him, and on whether Heaven is willing to give him a way to live,” Feng Que replied irresponsibly.","He took out his tools and began processing the Buyan flower. Without even looking up, he ordered, “Go have someone bring in a large bathing tub and fill it halfway with clean water.”","Lou Yue couldn’t be bothered to move. She called out, “Little Qiu!” toward the door and tossed the errand to him.","Before long, a huge bathing tub was carried inside.","Feng Que chased Little Qiu out and had Lou Yue set up a barrier. Only then did he begin pouring the medicinal pills he had ground into powder into the water. The once-clear water immediately began bubbling, and a faint medicinal fragrance spread through the room.","Lou Yue stood beside him, watching. Just as Feng Que was busy with his work, he suddenly jerked his chin toward her.","“What are you standing there for? Go bring him over.”","Lou Yue remained rooted to the spot. After a long moment, she forced out three words. “...Absolutely not.”","Feng Que: “?”","He turned to look at her, then gestured toward the half-processed Buyan flower in his hand. His expression was exaggerated. “If you’re not going, what are you doing here? If you’re not going to help, find someone else. Don’t waste time!”","Lou Yue: “...”","She didn’t want to help, and she especially didn’t want to carry anyone. But she did want to stay.","Clearly, Feng Que didn’t care in the slightest about her wishes. He remained completely absorbed in fussing over the Buyan flower.","Lou Yue clenched her jaw, then walked to the bed. She raised both hands for a long time, unable to find anywhere to put them, and finally abandoned the idea of carrying him.","Instead, she bent down and helped Xiao Rangchen sit up, draping his uninjured arm over her shoulder. Then, dragging and hauling him with all her might, she finally managed to move him beside the bathing tub.","Feng Que happened to turn around. He glanced at them, then frowned. “Why is he still wearing clothes?”","Lou Yue, who had just breathed a sigh of relief, stiffened. “He has to take them off too?”","Feng Que looked at her as if she were an idiot. “Who takes a medicinal bath fully clothed? If you don’t mind the clothes getting in the way, this old man minds wasting the medicinal ingredients!”","Lou Yue: “...”","Feng Que even urged her on. “Stop dawdling. The medicine will lose its potency. You’ll be the one crying then.”","Lou Yue gritted her teeth and crouched down, settling Xiao Rangchen on the rim of the tub. Then she reached for his belt.","But an unconscious person couldn’t cooperate. Xiao Rangchen’s body kept listing first to the left and then to the right. By the time sweat had beaded on her forehead, she still hadn’t managed to remove even his outer robe.","Afraid Feng Que would start nagging again if she delayed any longer, Lou Yue steeled herself. Since he was unconscious and wouldn’t know anything, she might as well get it over with.","She stood in front of Xiao Rangchen and rested his chin in the hollow of her shoulder, letting him lean against her. Only then did she finally manage to strip off his outer robe and inner garment.","Under the effects of the high-grade pills, the sword wounds on his shoulder and abdomen had nearly healed on the surface.","Lou Yue’s gaze swept over his old and new scars before finally settling on his trousers. She found herself at a loss.","The last time she had stripped off his trousers, she had been blindfolded. Besides, she had done it then to humiliate him. This time was different.","Lou Yue supported his waist. Her hand rose, then fell. She repeated the motion several times. Just as Feng Que was about to turn around, spiritual energy suddenly flashed in her hand.","With a sharp ripping sound, Xiao Rangchen’s trousers turned into scraps and scattered across the floor, leaving him wearing only a pair of close-fitting black shorts.","Feng Que looked over at the sound.","Lou Yue hurriedly turned her head away, the tips of her ears flushing uncontrollably.","“...Put him in.”","Feng Que’s voice carried a strangely meaningful tone. Lou Yue had no desire to investigate what it meant. She only felt as though she had narrowly escaped disaster.","But just as she was about to put him into the tub, she realized that her ordeal was only about to escalate.","With no clothes between them, the skin beneath her palms was cool and smooth, the powerful muscle beneath it firm and clearly defined. It was a completely different sensation from her own.","Lou Yue frowned. She had no interest in taking advantage of Xiao Rangchen. Even if he was handsome and had an incredible physique, that did nothing to change the fact that he was a womanizing scumbag. Besides, she was a man right now.","She simply imagined the sensation beneath her hands as three-layer pork belly on a butcher’s chopping board.","Well, it really did feel rather similar. The corners of Lou Yue’s lips curled up. Once she was free of the psychological burden, her work became much more efficient.","“All done.” Lou Yue stood beside the tub and clapped her hands.","Feng Que came over, pried open Xiao Rangchen’s jaw, and fed him a pill. “In ten breaths, use your spiritual power to heat the water.”","Lou Yue did as instructed.","“That’s enough. Keep the water at this temperature and let him absorb the medicine’s effects for now. Get ready.”","Lou Yue did not ask what they were preparing for. She simply braced one hand against the rim of the tub and pressed the other against its side, continuously channeling her spiritual power into it.","Whether it was because of the warm water or because the medicine had begun to take effect, Xiao Rangchen’s complexion gradually regained some color. He no longer looked as lifeless as before.","After roughly the time it took to burn a stick of incense, Feng Que came over carrying a bowl of medicine. Judging by the careful way he held it, as though he could not bear to spill even a single drop, it was probably the processed Buyan Flower.","He carefully fed every drop of the medicinal liquid into Xiao Rangchen’s mouth before straightening up. “You can stop now. From this moment on, there is only one thing you need to do.”","Feng Que’s tone was grave. “Hold him down firmly. Under no circumstances can you let him climb out of the tub, or all our efforts will be wasted! Remember, no matter what happens, you must not use your spiritual power.”","Under Feng Que’s solemn gaze, Lou Yue gave a slight nod. She bent over and pressed both hands against Xiao Rangchen’s shoulders.","Feng Que said nothing more. He moved behind Xiao Rangchen, drew a dagger across the back of his neck, and cut a small opening beneath it. Then he opened an intricately carved metal sphere.","Lou Yue stared at the translucent insect crawling out of the sphere. “What is that?”","“A gu worm. I’ve nurtured it with my own heart’s blood for fifteen years, and it is linked to my mind and spirit.” Feng Que gazed at the worm as it slowly crawled onto his finger, his voice turning gentle and affectionate. “Good little treasure, I’m counting on you...”","He brought the translucent worm to the wound at the back of Xiao Rangchen’s neck. The instant it caught the scent of blood, it burrowed straight inside. Feng Que immediately closed his eyes and sat cross-legged behind Xiao Rangchen.","Lou Yue looked away and pressed down hard with her palms.","Before long, Xiao Rangchen began to move. At first, it was only a faint tremor, but soon his hands and feet began to struggle as well.","Splash!","Xiao Rangchen’s arms suddenly shot upward, both hands gripping the edge of the tub as he desperately tried to pull himself out. Lou Yue increased the pressure and forced him firmly back down.","The muscles throughout his body bulged one by one. The veins on his arms stood out like twisted cords, and his fingernails dug into the wood with a creaking sound. Mixed with his heavy breathing, the noise lingered beside Lou Yue’s ears.","His struggles grew more violent. His legs began kicking, while his hands tried to pull away the ones she had pressed against his shoulders. Bent over him from the front, Lou Yue found it increasingly difficult to hold him down.","At this rate, she would not only fail to restrain him—the tub itself was going to be torn apart...","Lou Yue clicked her tongue. Forgetting whether she was wasting the medicinal water, she slid both hands down along Xiao Rangchen’s arms, locked them against his sides, and pressed inward with all her strength. Then she lifted one leg and stepped into the tub, using her knee to pin down his thrashing legs.","With one of his points of support gone, Xiao Rangchen’s struggle weakened considerably, but he still refused to give up.","To keep him restrained, Lou Yue inevitably ended up very close to him. His rapid breathing sprayed across the side of her face, carrying a faint, crisp scent of frost and snow.","Lou Yue glared at him, but the unconscious man had no idea what restraint meant. Again and again, his breath brushed across her cheek, irritating her more and more.","Time seemed to stretch endlessly. Every second passed with excruciating slowness.","His trembling gradually subsided. Just when she thought it was over, Xiao Rangchen’s entire body suddenly tensed, and he heaved upward with tremendous force. Lou Yue was caught off guard, and her knee slipped off his legs.","Seeing that he was about to sit up, Lou Yue steeled herself and threw caution to the wind. She sat directly on his thighs, lowered her body, and wrapped both arms tightly around his neck, using her own weight to keep him down.","Xiao Rangchen struggled violently in his unconscious state. Pulled along by his movements, Lou Yue swayed back and forth in the water, splashes of medicinal liquid flying everywhere. Some of it got into her eyes, burning painfully.","Lou Yue closed her eyes and devoted all her strength to resisting Xiao Rangchen’s struggles, clinging tightly to him.","Just then, his violent struggling came to an abrupt stop.","Lou Yue did not know what had happened, but afraid that the same thing might happen again, she still did not dare loosen her hold. She continued to cling tightly to him until a pair of slightly cool hands covered her arms—","Hehe."]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["Xiao Rangchen woke up to the gnawing pain in his meridians. The agony receded like a tide the moment he opened his eyes, leaving only a faint tingle behind.","What felt far clearer was the other person clinging tightly to his body, along with that familiar, soft warm scent of sweet flowers.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his head, his wrist curved to push the person off, but just as his hand brushed the other's arm, the person in his embrace suddenly lifted their head —","Lou Yue's red lips were slightly parted, her damp bangs curled and fell against her fair, smooth forehead, with a few strands stuck to the curve of her ear.","Her damp eyelashes were like dewy butterfly wings, trembling gently, and her peach blossom-shaped eyes were veiled in a hazy layer of watery confusion, showing a softness she had no idea she was exuding.","It was an expression he had never seen on her before.","The daze in Xiao Rangchen's eyes lasted only a split second before it was swallowed by a surging, dark undercurrent.","His sight was fixed entirely on those slightly parted red lips so close to him, and those eyes, misty and unguarded as they looked right back at him.","His heart felt as if it had been brushed by a soft, warm feather, and then as if something had bumped into it — not hard, but enough to make his blood boil, and a heat spread to every corner of his limbs and bones.","Xiao Rangchen's Adam's apple bobbed. His fingers curled unconsciously, and the hand that had been about to push her away, as if bewitched, drew her half an inch closer into his arms instead.","Lou Yue jolted awake as if scalded, scrambling up in such a hurry that the medicinal bath water sloshed loudly out of the tub, splashing onto the floor and spreading dark stains across the stone.","She was soaked through, water droplets dripping down her sodden clothes, but she did not spare it a single thought. Stepping through the puddles on the ground, she darted out of the room in two quick strides.","The sound of her hurried footsteps faded, followed by a loud bang as the door to the next room slammed shut hard.","Little Qiu, who had been standing guard outside, peered curiously through the door crack, looking utterly confused before he quietly closed the door again.","The room fell silent.","Xiao Rangchen's gaze was fixed on the closed door, and after a long while, he slowly lowered his eyes.","The rippling water in the bath tub gradually stilled, and in its reflection, the man's features were cold and stern, yet beneath his eyes churned a searing intensity he had never known himself capable of.","It was the look of plunder, of unassailable possession, of a long-hibernating beast that had finally laid eyes on its prey.","Xiao Rangchen frowned, his thin lips pressed into a hard, unyielding line.","A moment later, he lifted a hand and disturbed the reflection in the water...","\"Cough, cough!\"","Feng Que cleared his throat, a hint of helplessness in his voice. \"You two, did you completely forget there was another person in this room?\"","He had just been seeing off the gu worms that had crawled out of the wound — after all, he had raised them for fifteen years, so naturally he had grown a little attached. Who would have thought that in the time it took him to dispose of their remains, one of them would suddenly run off, and the other would act like he did not exist at all.","Xiao Rangchen snapped back to his senses and looked over at him.","\"Well, how do you feel? Pretty great, right?\" Feng Que asked enthusiastically. Logically, with such a high-grade Bu Yan Flower paired with his gu worms, both the residual poison in Lou Yue's body and the blockages in Xiao Rangchen's meridians should have been completely cleared away.","Not only that, the Bu Yan Flower would repair his damaged spiritual meridians, and the gu worms would widen them. After this experience, his spiritual meridians would be far stronger than they had ever been, and the remaining power of the Bu Yan Flower would continue to nourish them for a long time to come.","To his surprise, the man in the tub had not even bothered to sense the changes in his own body. Instead, he asked absent-mindedly, \"What?\"","\"...Your spiritual meridians! I'm asking how it feels to have your spiritual meridians healed!\" Feng Que exclaimed loudly.","Only then did Xiao Rangchen circulate his spiritual energy, and he realized that the previously obstructed feeling had vanished entirely. His spiritual meridians, which had throbbed with pain day after day, now felt light and unburdened.","The look of astonishment on Xiao Rangchen's face did not escape Feng Que, who turned away contentedly, waiting for the thanks he was owed. But after waiting for quite some time, the words he expected never came.","Feng Que turned around in confusion, only to find that the man had already sat cross-legged and entered a state of meditative cultivation, completely oblivious to him.","...","For the first time in his life, Feng Que had the bitter experience of being cold-shouldered after saving someone. Neither his patient nor this \"family member\" of his had uttered a single word of gratitude, and both of them had treated him like he was air. The aggrievement he felt outweighed every bit of praise he had ever received in his life.","He glared at Xiao Rangchen fiercely, then huffily packed up his things and stormed out of the room, forgetting to even maintain his usual casual gait.","In the room just on the other side of the wall.","Lou Yue had been leaning against the door since she shut it, not moving an inch, letting the cold water drip from the ends of her hair and seep through her clothes, pooling into a puddle at her feet.","It was not until she heard the sound of Feng Que and Little Qiu talking outside that she jolted back to her senses, lifting a hand to touch the back of her neck.","The moment her fingertips brushed her skin, she snapped her hand back sharply.","Frustration flooded her in an instant.","Why did she run? And why did she run so fast, like she was fleeing in total defeat?","But the moment she thought of the wild, possessive look in Xiao Rangchen's eyes just now, the hairs on the back of her neck prickled again — that was her instinctive alarm at a threat.","Yet tangled up in that feeling was a strange, inexplicable flutter in her chest.","Lou Yue bit her lip, then kicked the door hard several times, muttering a curse at her own uselessness under her breath.","Knock knock.","The door was rapped on.","Knock knock knock —","\"Speak!\" Lou Yue snapped, her tone sharp with irritation.","\"The old man has finished curing him. Now it's your turn to keep your end of the bargain,\" Feng Que said, sounding perfectly justified.","\"Go ask the person you treated for payment! I'm not running a charity!\" She had already gone out of her way to get the Bu Yan Flower for him, and now he expected her to pay Xiao Rangchen's medical bills? As if. Xiao Rangchen was her rival, for heaven's sake.","\"You're going back on your word?!\"","\"I never said I agreed to anything in the first place.\"","Feng Que, standing outside the door, was so angry his beard bristled. \"This old man can heal that boy just as easily as I can harm him!\"","\"Go ahead then. I won't stop you in the slightest.\" Lou Yue shot back, not backing down an inch.","Feng Que was pointing at the door, about to step up his threats, when a low, deep male voice sounded from beside him.","\"Sir.\" Xiao Rangchen had stepped out of his room at some point. Plain black robes outlined his tall, straight figure as he looked at Feng Que, his voice slow and steady. \"Whatever it is you desire, Xiao shall do his utmost to grant it.\"","At the sound of his voice, Lou Yue's eyelashes fluttered involuntarily.","Feng Que dropped his hand, sauntering over to pat Xiao Rangchen approvingly. \"Hey, you're the one with real loyalty here, far better than your partner over there!\"","Clang! The door was wrenched open violently.","\"Partner?! You old coot, if you spout that nonsense one more time, I'll —\" Lou Yue's angry yell died in her throat the second she lifted her eyes and met his deep, dark gaze.","Lou Yue was still wearing her soaked clothes, the thin fabric clinging to her skin. A bead of water was tracing a slow path down her fair collarbone, slipping beneath the edge of her robe. Xiao Rangchen's gaze lingered there for only a brief moment before he turned away. \"Sir, why don't you tell us first what it is you seek.\"","Feng Que had been about to tease Lou Yue a little more, but Xiao Rangchen's broad frame blocked his view, so he held back and stopped paying her any mind.","\"Fine, I'll tell you all about it. Come on, let's go inside and talk.\"","Feng Que walked back into Xiao Rangchen's room, with Xiao Rangchen following right behind him.","Lou Yue watched as the two outsiders waltzed right into the house without even a by-your-leave, and the whole situation felt utterly absurd.","Little Qiu, who had been watching the scene unfold, hurried over and draped a cloak over Lou Yue's shoulders. \"Young Master, don't catch a cold.\"","Lou Yue took a deep breath, forcing her frayed nerves to settle, as Little Qiu continued, \"You were occupied earlier, so I didn't get a chance to report. The Xuantian Capital just released news that the Ancient Tree Enlightenment event scheduled for the day after tomorrow has been moved up to tomorrow afternoon.\"","Lou Yue hummed in acknowledgement. She guessed that since she had used the Bu Yan Flower directly to heal Xiao Rangchen's spiritual meridians, the plot had shifted slightly to maintain its own coherence.","\"Also, news just came in from the Liufeng clan of Langhua that the Saintess has entered the city, and she's currently staying at the Tingyu Courtyard.\"","\"Liufeng Xin is here?\" Lou Yue's eyes lit up.","The Liufeng clan of Langhua was the most proficient in the Dao of Alchemy among the four great clans. Liufeng Xin was their Saintess, and a top-tier expert in the Dao of Alchemy as well.","She had another identity too.","She was Long Aotian Xiao Rangchen's white moonlight, the woman he loved the most among all his consorts in his harem.","Lou Yue hurried back to her room, picked out a brocade robe in ginger yellow peacock green that flattered her complexion perfectly, then called Little Qiu over to tie a neat high ponytail for her, adorned with an exquisite jade hairpin.","Lou Yue checked her reflection in the mirror over and over, making sure her handsomeness outshone Xiao Rangchen's by a large margin, before stepping out quickly.","Little Qiu followed after her, unable to hold back his question: \"Young Master, are you going to see the Saintess right now?\"","\"Of course, hurry up.\" Lou Yue replied casually.","The master and servant were chatting as they passed by Xiao Rangchen's wide-open door, neither of them spared a second glance inside.","Inside the room, Xiao Rangchen's words came to an abrupt halt.","Lou Yue's side profile, with the corners of her lips lifted in a smile, flashed past his field of vision.","Feng Que clicked his tongue, his tone full of teasing: \"Now I believe the two of you aren't a thing. Dressing up so fancily this late at night to go meet a woman for a tryst is exactly the kind of behavior these young masters from aristocratic families would get up to.\"","\"Sir, do not jest any further.\" Xiao Rangchen picked up the teacup on the table, tilted his head back and drained it. His fingertip slowly brushed over the rim of the cup as he said in a low voice, \"Both of us are men, and we were barely acquainted to begin with. There must be some other consideration behind her saving me earlier.\"","\"Ugh, being men isn't a problem.\" Feng Que waved his hand, lowering his voice, \"You have no idea, there are no small number of people who secretly came to me for medicine made for relations between two men.\"","Xiao Rangchen's hand holding the teacup tightened slightly. He did not take the remark, only calmly steered the conversation back on track: \"About the spirit insect you mentioned earlier, aside from the Queyun Chamber in Xuanitian Capital, is there really nowhere else we can find it?\"","\"Nowhere. I've already looked into every possible lead.\"","\"The four great clans have a strictly hierarchical system. As the stronghold of the Lou clan, Xuanitian Capital is not a place that ordinary commoners, or even young masters from other aristocratic clans, can enter whenever they want. Let alone the Queyun Chamber, which houses all their secret texts and precious artifacts.\"","\"No, you have a chance.\" Feng Que leaned closer to Xiao Rangchen, speaking with absolute certainty, \"During House Lou's clan head's birthday celebration, the cultivation world will hold a junior cultivation tournament. These aristocratic clans, in order to show off their so-called 'magnanimity', will nominally allow commoners to take part. As long as you make it into the top three in the end, you will be able to enter the Queyun Chamber fair and square.\"","Feng Que paused here, lifting a finger to point at the room next door: \"She's a member of the Lou clan, and holds a fairly high status, isn't she?\"","Xiao Rangchen looked at Feng Que. His gaze was not sharp, but it was far from gentle.","\"Tsk tsk, barely acquainted?\" Feng Que glanced at him and put his hand down. \"Relax, I have no interest in her identity. Even if you can participate in the tournament, you still need to get to the teleportation formation properly first. Get her to give you a title like personal bodyguard, and with her status shielding you, no one will raise any suspicion if you win the competition.\"","Xiao Rangchen fell silent.","Feng Que let out a deliberately exaggerated sigh: \"Young man, I've gone so far as to sacrifice the Gu worm I raised with my own heart's blood for fifteen years just to save you. And besides, going to Xuanitian Capital this time will bring you immense benefits too.","Do you know that the Ancient Enlightenment Tree is a supreme treasure that has been nurtured in the Lou clan's ancestral grounds for thousands of years? Every single leaf and bud on it holds the purest spiritual energy between heaven and earth, which is tremendously beneficial to one's soul and spirit. What's even rarer is that it carries the lingering aura of the Lou clan's mighty elders when they achieved enlightenment. With a bit of luck, it can help you grasp your own great Dao. So many young people from other clans are coming this time precisely for that tree.","Your spiritual veins are damaged and your cultivation has plummeted, but when the Gu worm traveled through your body earlier, I noticed that your spiritual veins are far more powerful than any I have seen in my entire life. While the spiritual energy from the Wisteria Flower hasn't dissipated completely, you can draw fully on the ancient tree's spiritual energy during your enlightenment, and you won't have to worry about any risks at all.","Kid, this is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity. Are you really willing to let it slip through your fingers?\" Feng Que's low, aged yet not feeble voice echoed through the room.","He did not wait for Xiao Rangchen to give a definite answer, nor did he say another word, before he left the Mianyun Courtyard directly.","Damaged spiritual veins are just like a riverbed that has lost its flowing water, with surging spiritual energy dried up and exhausted. If any cultivator dares to draw in qi and channel it through such veins, it would be no different than tearing at a piece of frayed silk — the pain would pierce through one's bones and blood, and it would destroy the last sliver of hope for recovery.","A riverbed without flowing water will keep shrinking. That is why the best time to use the Wisteria Flower after sustaining spiritual vein damage is within a month. The longer one waits, the harder it becomes to recover.","Xiao Rangchen's damaged section of spiritual veins had been injured for at least two years, but his spiritual veins had not shown the slightest sign of shrinking.","There was only one possible explanation for that —","He had been drawing qi into his veins every single day, enduring the excruciating pain of spiritual energy scraping past the stiffened meridians, constantly stimulating his spiritual veins to keep them active.","The entire process was such that even the slightest misstep, too much or too little, would cause his spiritual veins to shatter. But he had persisted for two whole years, forcing a thin trickle of flow back into a riverbed that was supposed to have long since withered away.","That level of perseverance bordered on paranoia.","That careful, daring, and precise mind was something ordinary people could never hope to match.","How could someone like that give up the chance to drag himself out of the mire so easily? He would do everything he could to grab hold of every possible opportunity to break free from the chains of fate.","That was exactly why Feng Que dared to take that gamble. From start to finish, he had been staking all his hopes of getting the spirit insect on Xiao Rangchen.","Lou Yue had no idea she was being schemed against by Feng Que. Her mind was completely wrapped up in thinking about how to win Liufeng Xin's favor when she met her, and she had even carefully picked out a perfect excuse to use.","Unfortunately, when she arrived at the Tingyu Courtyard full of excitement, she was met with a firm shut door. Even bringing up the Lou clan's name did not help her get in.","Logically speaking, the Liufeng clan should have given the Lou clan some face...","On her way back, Lou Yue kept wondering if the plot restrictions in this world were the reason she could not meet Liufeng Xin. After all, in the book, it was the male lead Long Aotian who met Liufeng Xin first, not her.","The male lead Xiao Rangchen was the core of this world. Maybe only he himself could unlock the appearance of this important character.","Lou Yue's mood sank to rock bottom. If that was really the case, it would be far harder for her to seize the first mover advantage.","\"Young Master.\" Little Qiu called out to her.","Lou Yue listlessly lifted her eyes, and froze in her tracks the moment she caught sight of the figure ahead.","Xiao Rangchen was standing quietly in the shadow by the courtyard gate, his black robe merging into the night. His eyes were glowing bright in the darkness, fixed unblinkingly on her.","----------------------","Writing this got my own heart pounding (covers face and runs away)","I wonder, dear readers, are you satisfied with this chapter?"]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["Lou Yue was even more displeased now.","Because of that Buyan flower, she had been forced not only to attend the Lou family banquet, but also to stay in Xuantian Capital for an entire month.","She had paid such a steep price, and now she merely wanted to turn around Liufeng Xin’s first impression of her in the book—that of a spoiled, dissipated young master—and gain an advantage so she could lend Liufeng Xin a hand. Even that wasn’t allowed.","How unfair. So what if he was Long Aotian?","Lou Yue snorted and withdrew her gaze from the man standing in the shadows, treating him as though he didn’t exist. Just as she was about to step into the barrier surrounding Mianyun Courtyard, the man emerged from the darkness and called out to her.","“A quarter of an hour. It won’t take much of your time.”","His voice was calm and steady, as though everything was under his control.","Lou Yue stopped and turned her head slightly, her tone cold with displeasure. “You say a quarter of an hour, and I’m supposed to agree?”","She stepped into the barrier, leaving the searing gaze behind her outside.","“When does the birthday celebration begin tomorrow?”","Little Qiu answered, “At a quarter to eight. It will take some time to get there from Mianyun Courtyard, so Young Master, you’ll have to rise at five.”","Lou Yue nodded carelessly. “Go get some rest. Wake me tomorrow morning.”","With that, she went inside and closed the door.","After night fell over Mianyun Courtyard, light sigils would ignite on their own in every room.","A warm yellow glow spread gently through the room, illuminating the dried water marks on the floor with perfect clarity.","Lou Yue stood there for a moment before slowly walking to the bed and picking up Xuanba, who was still in a tortoise-breathing state.","“Xiao Rangchen’s spiritual meridians have recovered. With his aptitude, it’ll take him at most a month to catch up from the Foundation Establishment stage to my current Golden Core stage.” Lou Yue absentmindedly scratched at the surface of the ice. “Sigh... Did that rotten heavenly law place some kind of restriction on me? Why do I keep saving him?”","Her fingers paused. “It must have! I hate scumbags the most. A womanizer like him—I have no reason to save him over and over again. It must be the heavenly law influencing me.”","Having found a perfectly good excuse, Lou Yue inexplicably felt relieved, though she had no idea what exactly she was relieved about.","Her face once again wore its careless smile. She flicked the ice with one finger. “Xuanba, if you don’t wake up soon, I’m going to stuff you into my storage ring.”","Living creatures were uncomfortable inside a storage ring, but there was no way she could leave Xuanba at Mianyun Courtyard. Besides, in its tortoise-breathing state, it probably couldn’t tell whether it was comfortable or not.","Lou Yue stared at Xuanba, hoping it would show some reaction. Unfortunately, it remained utterly still. She set it down, planning to put it in her storage ring when she left in the morning and let it enjoy one more comfortable night.","A knock suddenly sounded at the door.","Lou Yue assumed it was Little Qiu returning, so she called out for the person to come in.","But the moment she saw who was standing outside, she wished she could swallow that single word back whole.","“Xiao Rangchen, are you stalking me now?”","Xiao Rangchen did not enter. He simply stood outside the door.","“A quarter of an hour,” he repeated, looking as though he would refuse to leave unless Lou Yue agreed.","Lou Yue’s face darkened. After a long moment, she rubbed her forehead and waved dismissively. “If you have something to say, say it quickly. Then leave.”","Xiao Rangchen stepped inside and stopped two meters away from her. With a wave of his hand, he set up a soundproof barrier.","Seeing how freely he could now wield his spiritual power, Lou Yue secretly clenched her teeth.","“I need to go to Xuantian Capital,” he said bluntly.","Lou Yue raised an eyebrow. “What does that have to do with me?”","“What are your terms?”","Lou Yue raised her voice. “I said, what does that have to do with me?”","“I can help you with three things, as long as they don’t violate my principles.” His voice remained calm.","Lou Yue laughed in exasperation. “Do you not understand human speech?”","“Three things.”","“...”","Grinding her teeth, Lou Yue said, “Xiao Rangchen, are you overly confident?”","She rose and took several steps toward him, looking him straight in the eye. “What makes you think I’ll agree?” She folded her arms, the corners of her eyes lifting. “Don’t forget—you still owe me two lives.”","“What will it take for you to agree?” Xiao Rangchen’s gaze settled on the bright yet haughty eyes before him.","Lou Yue raised two fingers and poked them toward his face. “Two lives. Did you not hear me?”","Xiao Rangchen glanced at those fingers, more lustrous and delicate than any woman’s, and gave a faint hum.","“...‘Hm’? That’s it? Just one little ‘hm’?” Lou Yue was furious. She poked him again.","Xiao Rangchen caught her wrist. Even through the fabric of her sleeve, it was so slender that it seemed as though it would snap with the slightest pressure. The sensation reminded him of the previous morning...","Xiao Rangchen abruptly came back to himself and calmly pressed her hand down.","“I’ll repay you in the future.” His deep voice carried a faint huskiness at the end.","Lou Yue yanked her hand back in displeasure. “In the future? You might as well just say you’re never going to repay me!”","Xiao Rangchen lowered his empty hand and looked at her steadily. “I keep my word. Unlike you.”","Lou Yue lifted her chin, radiating arrogance. “What’s that supposed to mean? Are you insulting me? This young master has an excellent memory. I may forget something, but I certainly won’t forget anything you’ve done!”","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze slowly passed over her face. After a moment, he gave a derisive laugh. “Is that so? I hadn’t noticed.”","“...Are you finished? If you are, get out. I must have been out of my mind to let you in!”","Xiao Rangchen, however, refused to give up. “What will it take for you to let me accompany you to Xuantian Capital?”","“Heh. You’ll have better luck dreaming.”","Lou Yue turned her face away, too lazy to look at him anymore.","The warm yellow glow of the light sigils flowed between them. In the silence, even their breathing seemed magnified without limit. Every rise and fall felt like it was plucking at something unseen.","After a moment of silence, Xiao Rangchen spoke. “That day, I did arrive earlier.”","What day? Arrive earlier than whom?","It took Lou Yue a moment to realize that he meant the day Xuanba had performed “surgery” on her. Her eyes widened, and she abruptly turned to him.","“You actually lied to me? What exactly did you do?”","Lou Yue regretted ever thinking that, at the very least, he was a man who dared to take responsibility for his actions. She wished she could go back and knock some sense into her past self.","Xiao Rangchen fell silent again. Just as Lou Yue was about to grab him by the collar and demand an explanation, he finally spoke.","“Do you dare to make a bet? Bet on whether tomorrow morning will be the same as before.” His deep black eyes locked onto hers, his tone confident and certain. “If it is, I’ll take you to Xuantian Capital.”","“Why should I bet with you?” Lou Yue said unhappily.","Xiao Rangchen arched a dark brow. “You don’t dare?”","Lou Yue knew perfectly well that he was provoking her, but she still couldn’t resist when she saw the mocking look on his face.","“What don’t I dare? Fine, I’ll bet. If you lose, you’ll serve as this young master’s slave for a month.”","“Agreed.”","Lou Yue crossed her arms, the motion sending a breeze through the loose strands of hair at her temples. “The wager is settled. Now it’s your turn to talk. What exactly happened that day?”","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze lingered briefly on the stray strands brushing past her flushed lips before he slowly replied, “The moment I appeared, I was bound by your formation.”","“And then?”","Xiao Rangchen lifted his eyes again. “Nothing else.”","“Are you playing me?!”","Lou Yue’s expression hardened at once.","There had been a great deal of thunder but hardly any rain. Either he was still hiding something, or there had truly been nothing more to it. Either way, the result was the same: he was making a fool of her.","Xiao Rangchen’s voice deepened. “What else did you expect to happen?”","“...”","Lou Yue was momentarily rendered speechless, then immediately shot back, “I didn’t expect anything! I’d be delighted if you stayed far away from me and never showed your face in front of me again!”","“If that’s the case, why did you save me?”","Xiao Rangchen stared at her intently. Then, all at once, he lifted his foot and took a step forward, narrowing the distance between them. His cool, clean scent swept over Lou Yue, carrying a sense of oppression while hiding a hint of bewitching allure.","“Why?”","Lou Yue restrained the urge to retreat and met his gaze without yielding an inch.","“Xiao Rangchen, I saved you. Not only are you ungrateful, you even came here to interrogate me.”","She let out a derisive laugh, her tone filled with disdain. “What do you want me to say? That I’ve fallen for you?”","She leaned toward him of her own accord, her red lips almost brushing his.","“Putting aside the fact that this young master doesn’t like men—even if I did, you would never be the one.”","Xiao Rangchen’s dark eyes abruptly deepened. The turbulent emotions within them were forcibly suppressed, leaving behind nothing but a heavy pool of ink.","Lou Yue turned and walked to the table, pouring herself a cup of water. “That’s enough. You’ve said what you came to say, so leave.”","Silence lingered behind her for a while. Then came the sound of departing footsteps. Once the noise of him going downstairs had faded, Lou Yue closed the door.","After a long moment, a low chuckle sounded inside the room.","On her way back from Tingyu Courtyard, she had already been thinking about how to get Xiao Rangchen to Xuantian Capital. She was worried that, if the male lead refused to go, the cheat ability wouldn’t activate. Then, even if she entered Que Yunsheng, she still wouldn’t be able to obtain the old grandpa who was supposed to accompany her.","Just as she was fretting over how to make it happen, Xiao Rangchen had delivered himself right to her door.","The outcome of tomorrow morning’s wager would make no difference. Regardless of who won, she would help Xiao Rangchen reach Xuantian Capital. The only difference was whether she did it openly or in secret.","Of course, winning would be best. Even if it didn’t affect the outcome, she still didn’t want to lose to him.","Thinking of how she had left him speechless with her final retort, the corners of Lou Yue’s lips rose uncontrollably once more.","That felt good.","Even the gloom of not seeing Liufeng Xin that evening had been completely washed away by the satisfaction.","Lou Yue returned to the bed. There were still five shichen before dawn, so she simply decided to meditate and cultivate until morning. Perhaps the mechanism triggered by “waking up in bed with Xiao Rangchen” required her to be asleep.","Lou Yue sat down cross-legged, adjusted her posture, and closed her eyes. Her lowered gaze happened to sweep past her chest, and she caught sight of its rise and fall.","Her eyes flew open. She looked down—","It was still as flat as a plain, flatter than flat.","Had she imagined it?","Lou Yue touched her chest. It was slender and flat, no different from usual.","She pursed her lips. Fine, it could only have been a trick of the eyes. How could she possibly have developed breasts out of nowhere? This body was unquestionably a man’s...","Lou Yue encouraged herself. She might not be able to become a woman, but she could still build a career. Pinning Long Aotian to the ground and rubbing his face in the dirt would be the best consolation for her wounded heart.","She was determined to defeat him in enlightenment beneath the ancient tree!","Lou Yue swept away her dejection, straightened her back, and entered meditation once more. Her breathing gradually settled, blending with the night beyond the window.","Little by little, the dawn light stripped the darkness from the sky.","The faint morning glow quietly crept into the room, spreading a hazy radiance beside the bed.","Just as Xiao Rangchen broke free from the murk of sleep, the sensation of warm, fragrant softness nestled against him left him dazed for a moment.","Lou Yue’s uniquely familiar scent wrapped tightly around him. Her delicate skin brushed lightly against the tip of his nose with every breath.","Her arm rested beside his neck, her fingers threading into his hair in an unmistakably embracing posture. His own hand, meanwhile, was clasped around her waist, his palm pressed against its supple curve.","He didn’t need to look. The intimate, suggestive scene had already imprinted itself in his mind.","Reason clamored that he should push Lou Yue away, that he should immediately escape this overly intimate embrace.","Yet his hand felt unbearably heavy.","His body seemed to possess a will of its own, sinking into the moment and refusing to pull away...","————————","Long Aotian, you’ve changed."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["“Xiao Rangchen...”","Lou Yue suddenly called out.","Xiao Rangchen’s heart sank, but the rejection he had expected never came. Instead, he heard a soft, slurred murmur:","“Hehe... I told you you couldn’t beat me... loser...”","Xiao Rangchen was speechless for a moment. He deliberately waited a while before slowly moving Lou Yue’s arms away from him, lifting his face from the warmth of her collarbone.","Morning light fell across her cheek, softening her delicate, exquisite features. The proud, disdainful lashes from the night before now hung low, dark as crow feathers over her eyelids.","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze drifted downward of its own accord, settling on those crimson, yielding lips.","His breathing slowed, and the air around him seemed to grow viscous.","—She was a man.","—So what?","—This went against propriety.","—Did he truly care about worldly morals and etiquette?","Chaotic thoughts surged like a tide...","Suddenly, a series of knocks broke the silence.","Xiao Rangchen came to his senses with a start, as though someone had poured a basin of cold water over his head.","Lou Yue’s brows drew together slightly, and she looked as though she was about to wake. He immediately withdrew from her embrace. His movements were unhurried, yet gentle.","“Young Master, it’s time to get up.”","By the time Lou Yue opened her eyes, Xiao Rangchen was already standing far away by the table.","Waking up under Long Aotian’s watchful gaze was hardly pleasant, especially since it meant she had lost the bet.","Lou Yue puffed out her cheeks.","“Young Master?” Little Qiu called again.","“I know. You can go for now.” She answered through the door.","Only after the footsteps had faded did Lou Yue cast a sidelong glance at the man by the table and say bluntly, “Stop staring. I keep my word.”","“I’m changing clothes. Go wait next door.”","Xiao Rangchen said nothing. He merely turned his back to her, making it clear that he did not trust her.","“...”","Forget it. She was only changing her outer clothes anyway.","Lou Yue turned around, too lazy to argue any further.","The rustling of fabric was magnified endlessly in the quiet room.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his gaze to the patterns in the bricks at his feet.","As Lou Yue undressed, her hair caught on something, and the hairpin slipped free, dropping into the back of her clothes. She reached in twice but failed to retrieve it, then clicked her tongue in irritation.","At the sound, Xiao Rangchen raised his eyes slightly. His gaze swept inadvertently toward the corner—and he froze.","A full-length mirror, nearly as tall as a person, stood in the corner, clearly reflecting Lou Yue’s back.","Her black, curling hair had been swept to the front. Her undergarment had slipped halfway off, hanging loosely from one shoulder.","Her slender, fair back curved faintly, while her delicate shoulder blades jutted out ever so slightly, like a butterfly about to take flight. It stirred an irresistible desire in him to imprison those wings.","The air seemed to boil in an instant. Before Xiao Rangchen could think, he hurriedly looked away.","“Clink.”","The jade hairpin struck the floor. After pulling her clothes back on, Lou Yue bent down to retrieve it and redid her hair.","She turned and walked a couple of steps toward the full-length mirror in the corner. After giving her appearance a cursory glance, she put away Xuanba, opened the door, and left without sparing Xiao Rangchen a glance.","It was not until she reached the first floor that Xiao Rangchen finally emerged from her room.","“Young Master~”","Everyone in the courtyard knew that Lou Yue was heading to Xuantian Capital today, so Xiao Aiai and Dou’er were no exception.","The moment Dou’er saw her, she rushed over and hugged her arm, whining sweetly, “Young Master, does this mean I won’t get to see you for several days again~?”","Lou Yue smiled. “Wouldn’t you be freer with me gone?”","“Oh, Young Master, how could you say that?” Dou’er’s cheeks flushed slightly. Knowing that Lou Yue was aware of all the things she had secretly bought these past two days, she hurriedly shook her arm coquettishly. “I even picked out clothes and hairpins for you! If you don’t believe me, ask Little Qiu!”","Little Qiu was staring at Xiao Rangchen as he came down the stairs, his mind full of questions. He did not hear Dou’er at all.","Xiao Aiai was in the same state.","“Brother?”","Lou Yue glanced at Xiao Rangchen’s cold expression, then turned to Xiao Aiai and said warmly, “His spiritual meridians have recovered, and he’s going to Xuantian Capital too. He’s perfectly fine, so stop worrying about him.”","Xiao Aiai’s face lit up, and she hurried over. “Brother, your spiritual meridians have recovered?!”","She had originally waited here to ask Lou Yue about the Bu Yan flower. She never expected to receive such wonderful news instead.","“Mm.”","Xiao Rangchen stopped and withdrew his dark gaze from Lou Yue and Dou’er, who were standing close together. He instructed Xiao Aiai indifferently, “Don’t run off anywhere. Wait until I return.”","“When have I ever run off? I’m not her.”","Xiao Aiai huffed, though she could not hide the joy on her face. She was genuinely happy for her brother. No one knew better than she did what he had endured since his spiritual meridians were damaged. At last, the heavens had recognized his resilience and effort.","At the thought, tears misted her eyes.","“Aiai?”","Xiao Aiai quickly wiped away the tears and looked up at Xiao Rangchen with a radiant smile. “It’s nothing. I-I’m just happy. Finally... finally...”","Xiao Rangchen fell silent. After a moment, he lifted his hand, intending to pat his sister’s head and comfort her.","At that moment, Lou Yue’s voice came from beside him, tinged with a hint of sourness.","“Aiai, your brother’s spiritual meridians recovered because of the Bu Yan flower I gave him. Aren’t you going to thank me?”","Xiao Rangchen looked over and saw Lou Yue arching her brows, mischief gleaming in her eyes as she stared intently at Xiao Aiai.","“Thank you.” Xiao Aiai was solemn. “I used to think you were nothing but a spoiled young heir, but now I know you’re a good person.”","Having been unexpectedly handed a very earnest “good person” card, Lou Yue instead felt a little embarrassed. She brushed back the hair by her ear and looked away as she replied casually, “Mm. It’s good that you know.”","Xiao Aiai seemed to discover something amusing. She leaned closer and teased with a sweet smile, “Could it be that you’re shy?”","Lou Yue immediately choked and began coughing. A faint blush spread across her smooth, lustrous face.","Xiao Rangchen stood to one side. His gaze paused for a moment on Lou Yue’s bashful, evasive expression before passing over Xiao Aiai and landing on the person clinging to Lou Yue.","The woman’s fingers, their nails painted with red lacquer, were gently stroking up and down Lou Yue’s slender back.","It was nothing more than an ordinary gesture to help her catch her breath, yet it looked especially irritating to him.","Expressionless, Xiao Rangchen turned his head away.","“All right, that’s enough... cough. In a little while, spiritual rain will descend from Xuantian Capital. Go outside and absorb it before you go play. Little Qiu, take people with you and make sure they’re protected.”","After giving his instructions, Lou Yue saw that it was nearly time. She nodded and walked outside.","Xiao Aiai had just opened her mouth to tell Xiao Rangchen to be careful, but her brother had already walked past her without so much as a sideways glance.","Xiao Aiai closed her mouth and stared at the two tall figures walking one after the other. Suddenly, the question that had been interrupted earlier sprang to mind:","Why had her brother come out of Lou Yue’s room that morning? When had he gone in?","“Could it really be...?” Little Qiu let out a sigh beside her. His tone held both confusion and a trace of grief, as though someone had dug up the cabbage in his own garden, though he still could not bring himself to believe it.","“What are you two doing? Why are you standing there like fence posts?” Dou’er asked, utterly bewildered. “Young Master isn’t never coming back. You two are acting like you’re seeing him off to his funeral.”","Little Qiu: “...”","Xiao Aiai shot her an exasperated look. “...Just shut up.”","“Xiao Aiai!”","Seeing that the two of them were about to start arguing again, Little Qiu hurriedly tried to mediate. But neither of them was willing to listen. One spoke after the other, and soon their bickering grew lively and loud.","Not a trace of the commotion in Sleeping Cloud Courtyard reached Lou Yue’s ears.","The streets of Xuandi City were packed with people, all waiting for the spirit rain that was about to fall. Spirit rain descended only on the birthdays of the patriarchs of the four great families. It contained spiritual energy that could cleanse a cultivator’s meridians and aid their advancement, while even ordinary people could benefit from its life-prolonging effects.","In this world, cultivation resources were monopolized by the great clans. Spirit rain was one of the few blessings available to everyone, which was why there were so many commoners gathered in Xuandi City.","Lou Yue and Xiao Rangchen walked through the surging crowd toward the teleportation array, maintaining a distance that was neither too close nor too far.","Unlike the areas elsewhere, the teleportation array was heavily guarded but surprisingly spacious.","Lou Yue handed over her jade token and gestured toward Xiao Rangchen, who was following her. “Two people.”","The guard took one look at her and respectfully returned the token. He had recognized Lou Yue long ago. In all of Xuandi City, the only person who possessed such a special jade token and was as strikingly beautiful as she was could only be her.","Lou Yue had just stepped onto the stone stairs when her gaze fixed on a figure standing before the array. She could not tear her eyes away.","It was a woman dressed in a silver-white robe. A veil of white gauze covered her eyes, revealing only her smooth forehead and beautifully shaped chin. She resembled a flawless divine statue hidden atop a snow-capped mountain, radiating a cold beauty so pure and lofty that she seemed untouchable.","Lou Yue’s heart jolted.","That outfit, that bearing... Could it be...?","The woman seemed to sense her gaze and slowly turned her face. Through the thin veil, Lou Yue could not make out her eyes. She only felt a gaze as faint as a mountain breeze, brushing lightly across her before withdrawing, as if the woman cared about nothing at all.","It was Liufeng Xin. Lou Yue was even more certain now.","Xiao Rangchen noticed Lou Yue’s dazed expression and followed her line of sight. Almost at the same moment, Lou Yue glanced toward him and saw that he was indeed staring at Liufeng Xin. She gave an inward scoff.","Xiao Rangchen swept the woman with a cold glance before looking away, but Lou Yue had already continued forward.","When they drew closer, Lou Yue heard the person accompanying Liufeng Xin speaking in a lowered voice. The words came rapidly and urgently, but just as they reached the array, the person cautiously fell silent.","The two of them seemed to be waiting for someone and had no intention of entering the teleportation array yet. Not wanting to give Xiao Rangchen a chance to meet his white moonlight, Lou Yue immediately led him into the array.","Just as the teleportation array activated, Lou Yue heard Liufeng Xin’s voice, cool as snowmelt, say in a flat and detached tone, “If you keep making empty promises, I’ll have to go set up a street stall.”","Lou Yue’s peach-blossom eyes flew wide, but the blue light of the teleportation array had already swallowed her vision.","She hadn’t misheard, had she?","“Making empty promises” was modern internet slang, wasn’t it?! No matter how she interpreted it, Liufeng Xin’s words did not sound as though she meant literally drawing a pancake with a brush!","Could it be...?!","No, she had to confirm it! She absolutely had to!","The light of the teleportation array faded, and the two arrived in the Xuantian Capital.","Lou Yue walked toward the covered bridge in a state of excitement mixed with distraction. Seeing her like this, Xiao Rangchen pressed his lips tightly together.","Suddenly, Lou Yue stopped and pointed toward the clock tower in the distance. “I have something to take care of. Go wait for me over there.”","A cold edge tinted Xiao Rangchen’s brows and eyes. He asked no questions and left without a word.","Lou Yue waited in place for less than half a quarter of an hour before the teleportation array lit up again. Liufeng Xin appeared with two others.","Liufeng Xin showed no reaction whatsoever at seeing Lou Yue again. The person who had been speaking earlier, however, looked at her warily.","The three of them walked straight past her. Staring at Liufeng Xin, Lou Yue spoke softly.","“Odd changes, even stays the same.”","The cold, sacred figure came to a halt.","Lou Yue’s heart rose into her throat. She was both nervous and hopeful.","The next moment, Liufeng Xin slowly turned her head and looked at her. Her cool voice held a trace of uncertainty.","“...Signs depend on the quadrant?”","Lou Yue: !!","But just as Lou Yue was about to say something else, Liufeng Xin turned away again, as if worried that someone else might understand them. She tossed back one final sentence:","“Nine tonight, here.”","Then she left with the others.","Lou Yue watched their departing figures and broke into a foolish grin.","She had actually encountered another modern person here—and it was none other than Liufeng Xin, her white moonlight.","After grinning stupidly for quite a while, Lou Yue finally headed toward the clock tower.","As she drew near, she looked up and saw Xiao Rangchen leaning against the wall beneath the tower, his arms folded across his chest. His deep gaze suggested that he had no idea how long he had been watching her.","What was with that look in his eyes?","Oh, she knew.","The Dragon Proud Heaven was jealous."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["Gilded rosy glow draped over Xuandu, the floating city.","The auspicious hour struck, and three peals of bells resounded across the skies.","From the highest spire of Xuandu, a magical passage coalesced. Its cyan-blue radiance cascaded down like a winding river of stars, looping three full times around the entire city.","Along the luminous path, ninety-nine auspicious beasts trod slowly forward bearing rare treasures. Every item glowed and shimmered, a rare treasure-level magic artifact hard to come by even in the cultivation world, drawing gasps of admiration from the spectators.","The Hundred Treasures Parade, staged as the opening of the birthday celebration, was the Lou Clan, one of the four great families, showcasing their status to the entire cultivation realm.","Lou Yue had no interest in any of this. She had long since picked a random seat at the very back of the banquet, while Xiao Rangchen stood not far away, arms folded, feigning sleep.","When the last auspicious beast reached the spire accompanied by curling celestial music, the whole world fell abruptly silent.","A white-haired elder whose hair fell to his waist stepped out through the air. His gaze was sharp as a torch, and his imposing aura filled the surroundings. This was none other than the head of the Lou Clan, Lou Mo.","\"By the spirit vein of my Lou Clan that has endured a thousand years as the catalyst, let the spirit rain fall, and nourish all of Xuandu!\"","Billions of streams of light shot up behind Lou Mo, converging into the shadow of a colossal whale that blotted out the sky and blocked out the sun.","The great whale flicked its tail and let out a long, resonant cry. Wherever it circled, golden light fell in a rustle, like a rain of golden stardust that spilled over every inch of land in the floating Xuandu City and the grounded Xuandi City below.","Lou Yue's features softened as she watched the golden glimmers of falling stardust fill the sky.","She stretched out her hand. A drop of the spirit rain touched her palm and dissolved into pure spiritual energy that seeped into her dantian, warm and comforting.","As a cultivator at the peak of the Golden Core stage, the spirit rain was more of a visual treat than anything of practical use to her. But for ordinary people, for Xiao Aiai, Dou'er, and Little Qiu, it was of immense benefit.","A smile tugged unconsciously at Lou Yue's lips. She rested her cheek in her hand, watching the specks of light on her palm intently.","Sensing something, she glanced to the side.","Everyone else there was looking up at the whale phantom and the spirit rain, only Xiao Rangchen still had his arms crossed and his eyes closed. His long, lean legs were propped casually apart, making him look icy, aloof, and strikingly handsome.","Tch, showing off for no reason.","Lou Yue decided not to look and spoil her mood, turning back to the spirit rain.","Xiao Rangchen slowly lifted his eyes. His gaze cut through the crowd, deep and heavy, settling steadily on the figure in the distance.","Amidst the sea of golden rain, there was only her. All the brilliance in the world paled in comparison to her.","...","The colossal whale phantom circled the sky for a full half an hour before it gradually dissipated. By then, Xuandu had turned into a fairyland, with plants and trees growing wildly, sprouting new green leaves and blooming flowers, brimming with vibrant life.","Lou Mo landed, standing with his hands behind his back before the dais.","On the high platform sat the heads of the three other great clans: the Cangya Clan from the Northern Sea, the Yue Clan from Qingzhou, and the Liufeng Clan from Langhua. The three of them raised their wine cups, and the younger generation of all the clans in the seats below followed suit, offering distant birthday wishes.","After all, this man was the original host's grandfather, so Lou Yue casually lifted her wine cup in acknowledgement.","Next came the session where representatives from each clan presented birthday gifts and performed musical and dance acts. Lou Yue had prepared a gift too, just as her father Lou Chengfeng had suggested: she plucked a small wild flower, making sure not to show up empty-handed. She had no intention of personally presenting it, and figured Old Master Lou would not hold it against a junior like her.","As Lou Yue watched the scene of people toasting and fawning over each other at the feast, she was already thinking of slipping off to a quiet spot to nap before the Ancient Tree Enlightenment session in the afternoon. Just then, a person at the table next to hers leaned over to greet her.","\"May I know your name, brother? I am Yue Qi, of the Yue Clan from Qingzhou.\"","Before Lou Yue could even open her mouth, a man who had come up beside Yue Qi scoffed, \"Yue Qi, why are you sitting with her?\"","\"Cang Wu, do you know her?\"","Cang Wu twirled the wine cup in his hand, his tone full of disdain. \"Just an abandoned child of the Lou Clan. Not worth my attention.\"","Yue Qi looked confused. \"An abandoned child?\"","Lou Yue had no patience for the two annoying people rambling on and spoiling her mood. She tossed down her wine cup and got up to leave, but Cang Wu deliberately blocked her path.","\"Running away? Afraid of losing face?\" Cang Wu said, stopping her with a hand, his words sharp and mean.","\"Not running. I'm afraid you'll be the one losing face,\" Lou Yue shot back. Too lazy to waste words on a pest, she tried to step around him and leave.","Cang Wu reached out to grab Lou Yue, but a hand clamped around his wrist and wrenched him backward. The force was so strong that even he winced in pain.","\"Xiao Rangchen? You're still alive?\" Cang Wu sneered the moment he saw who it was, but the smile faded instantly, replaced by shock. \"Your spiritual vein has healed?!\"","Xiao Rangchen flung Cang Wu's hand off, his tone cutting and icy. \"Cang Wu, starting from this moment on, you'd better cherish every single day you have left.\"","\"Xiao Rangchen, even if your spiritual vein is healed, so what? You're still just a lowly Foundation Establishment cultivator, while I have already stepped into the Nascent Soul stage!\"","\"It only took you five years to go from Golden Core to Nascent Soul,\" Xiao Rangchen retorted mockingly.","Lou Yue was just about to laugh when she suddenly remembered that the original host had been stuck at the Golden Core stage for six years now. She trailed off, speechless.","That line landed on Cang Wu like a slap too. Among the young aristocratic cultivators, that level of progress could only be called mediocre. He flew into a rage, yelling, \"You spout nonsense! You're a lowly commoner who snuck up to Xuandu, how dare you even dream of participating in the Enlightenment? You don't deserve it!\"","The people nearby had already noticed their argument, and now all eyes turned to Xiao Rangchen.","\"He's a commoner...?\"","\"How did he even get up here?\"","\"Must have snuck in through some crooked, underhanded means, right?\"","\"Can a commoner even look that good?\"","\"A toad from the mud, trying to climb the immortal platform?\"","...","Lou Yue's expression turned cold. None of these people had lowered their voices, they were all gossiping about him blatantly right to his face.","What's wrong with being a commoner? They're people too! With their noses stuck so high up in the air, no wonder Long Aotian would eventually turn all these great aristocratic clans upside down.","Calling him a toad? They probably had never even seen what a real toad looked like.","Lou Yue was seething with irritation. Xiao Rangchen just hung his head, not saying a word, not even bothering to refute them.","She could not hold back any longer. She pushed Xiao Rangchen aside, lifted her chin, and called out to Cang Wu loudly, \"He's my guest. What, you got a problem with me too?\"","\"You're so desperate to stop him from joining the Enlightenment, I think you're just scared that he'll succeed in the enlightenment and leave you in the dust, making you lose all face.\"","Lou Yue feigned a look of sudden realization and nodded. \"Right, you could make up excuses for losing to someone else, but if you lost to that 'lowly commoner' you just mentioned? You'd have no face left at all, you'd probably kill yourself out of shame.\"","Cang Wu was so choked by Lou Yue's words that he could not find a retort, his face turning red and then pale. For a moment, he could not utter a single response.","Lou Yue stepped forward, looked up at him, her eyebrows raised, a sharp, unyielding aura radiating straight toward him. \"Let's make a bet. We'll see who achieves great success in the enlightenment, you or Xiao Rangchen. The loser kneels down and barks like a dog three times.\"","\"You're pitting a Foundation Establishment cultivator against my Nascent Soul stage self?\" Cang Wu sneered. \"You're definitely going to lose.\"","Lou Yue smiled back brightly. \"I'll be waiting for your dog barks.\"","Cang Wu's eyes were red with fury. He opened and closed his jaw, grinding his teeth almost to dust, caught between agreeing and refusing.","Lou Yue grinned cheerfully, then grabbed Xiao Rangchen by the arm and pulled him away, leaving Cang Wu standing there under the teasing glances of the surrounding crowd.","\"Hey, Cang Wu,\" Yue Qi walked over, a gentle smile on his face. \"I've been meaning to talk to you about something. Come on, let's go over to that quieter spot.\"","The onlookers scattered. Yue Qi led Cang Wu to a side area, where Cang Wu shook his hand off roughly, his face dark. \"Cut the fake act, we both know what this is.\"","Yue Qi's smile faded instantly. He straightened the creases on his cuffs slowly and deliberately. \"I don't care what grudge you have against those two, but don't kill that girl from the Lou Clan.\"","Cang Wu glanced at him sideways. The thought of this man's peculiar, vile preferences made his stomach turn, but he did not show it on his face. \"Lou Yue looks so frail and delicate, she wouldn't even last two days with you.\"","\"Her name is Lou Yue... what a lovely name,\" Yue Qi said, licking his lips.","Cang Wu could no longer stand Yue Qi's leering, familiar expression. \"I don't care a thing about Lou Yue's life, but that man beside her — I want him dead!\"","\"Here in Xuan Capital City, do you really dare to kill someone openly?\"","Cang Wu spat hard on the ground. He still rued the fact that he failed to kill Xiao Rangchen back in Xuandi City. He had no idea what kind of fortuitous opportunity the man had run into, but Xiao Rangchen had not only been cured of his Greedy Worm affliction, his spiritual meridians had fully healed too.","\"There's no rush to kill him. We can make him taste a bit of suffering first,\" Yue Qi's voice dropped low, carrying a sinister, icy edge.","Cang Wu did not believe Yue Qi would go out of his way to help him for no reason.","The Yue clan of Qingzhou was the preeminent artifact-making family among the four great clans, responsible for forging nine out of ten of the world's divine weapons. Yue Qi was the oddity of the clan, who specialized in crafting insidious, cruel hidden weapons. Still, if he chose to lend a hand, their chances of success would indeed rise considerably.","Xiao Rangchen was a wild, unruly wolf cub. The more desperate the situation he was pushed into, the more reckless and unbridled he acted. Back in the day, to break out of an encirclement, he had not hesitated to forcefully absorb a demon core by leaping two whole realms of cultivation. Cang Wu still remembered that desperate, burn-his-boats ferocity vividly. If he had not used other people as human shields back then, he would have lost his own life that day.","Cang Wu asked tentatively, \"You're willing to help me?\"","\"It's a partnership,\" Yue Qi stroked his chin, a wicked, sinister smile spreading across his face.","Cang Wu knew full well that Yue Qi was selfish, cunning, and never let a slight go unavenged. He refused to believe the man would wade into this muddy water purely on a fleeting whim.","All of a sudden, he recalled the rumors he had heard on the road to Xuan Capital. Yue Qi had an elder brother, and the two had a very close relationship. Word had it that his elder brother had fallen in love with a direct-lineage daughter of the Lou clan, only to be tied up by the Lou clan and sent back to the Yue clan, leaving the Yue family utterly humiliated.","The four great clans had deeply intertwined relationships, and political marriages were a common practice. The problem was that the woman in question was a direct-lineage daughter of the Lou clan.","Everyone within the four great clans knew that the direct-lineage members of the Lou clan inherited a powerful perception talent. The women of the lineage, aside from possessing extraordinary perception and affinity for spiritual energy, were also extremely rare, perfect cauldrons for cultivation partners.","The stronger one's external perception power, the more potent the cauldron power they held.","For that exact reason, direct-lineage female infants were very rarely born into the Lou clan. For a hundred years, Lou Mo, who had the strongest perception power, had only fathered three sons, and all of his sons had sons as well. It was not until the fourth generation that two girls were finally born.","And the woman Yue Qi's elder brother loved was one of them.","The Lou clan never allowed their direct-lineage daughters to marry outside the clan, and they would never tolerate outsiders coveting them. Every time a direct-lineage daughter of the Lou clan was born, the clan leader would personally plant a soul seed to protect her. Once she turned sixteen, she would be married to a person designated by the clan, whose cultivation she would help elevate by drawing on her cauldron power, so that the clan could produce top-tier powerhouses.","That meant Yue Qi's elder brother was never meant to be with her. Word had it the Lou clan had already scheduled the woman's wedding to take place right after the clan's longevity banquet.","Cang Wu saw the full picture now. \"You want to get back at them for your elder brother.\"","\"Lou Yue isn't even a woman who bears that cauldron power. What's the harm in having a little fun with her?\" Yue Qi tugged at the corner of his mouth. \"Besides, she does strike my fancy. This move kills two birds with one stone.\"","Cang Wu cast away all his lingering doubts. \"What kind of 'suffering' did you have in mind?\"","\"According to the usual protocol, the Lou clan will arrange for all the visiting guests to stay in the same residential compound.\"","Cang Wu caught on instantly. After a moment of silent thought, he lowered his voice and said, \"There's someone who might be able to help us.\"","...","Lou Yue had grown up bold and unruly, and she did not take Cang Wu seriously at all.","Compared to Cang Wu, it was Xiao Rangchen who really got under her skin.","She dragged Xiao Rangchen to a corner, then roughly shook his arm off. \"You're so arrogant to me on a normal day, but why don't I ever see you act that wildly toward outsiders?\"","Xiao Rangchen looked up at her. If those people were outsiders, then what was she?","The unpleasantness from earlier that morning seemed to fade away a little.","Seeing that he still had that unflappable, completely indifferent look on his face, Lou Yue's face darkened even more. \"Ugh, I was a meddling cat picking on a mouse, sticking my nose into something that wasn't my business.\"","She turned to leave after throwing out those words, but Xiao Rangchen reached through her clothes and grabbed her wrist.","\"Who gave you permission to paw at me?\" Lou Yue glared at him, brows furrowed.","Xiao Rangchen released her. His voice was low and magnetic as he spoke. \"I was thinking about some old memories back then. By the time I snapped out of it to speak, you had already stepped in ahead of me.\"","Lou Yue crossed her arms over her chest, lifting the corner of her eye. \"Oh, so now it's my fault?\"","A faint, almost imperceptible smile flickered in Xiao Rangchen's eyes, like tiny ripples spreading across a cold, deep pool.","He spoke slowly, every word clear and unwavering. \"I won't let you lose.\"","That was how it should be.","Lou Yue huffed and turned her face away.","Xiao Rangchen gazed at Lou Yue, his eyes deep and unreadable.","The slanting sunlight fell into her eyes, lending them a clear, translucent luster like glazed glass. Her cheeks were flushed a soft, faint crimson from her anger.","A breeze drifted through the corner, carrying the faint, sweet scent of osmanthus blossoms.","The sounds of the ongoing banquet, with guests toasting and chatting noisily, felt as if they were separated off in a world of their own."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["It was not until the Ancient Enlightenment Ceremony began that Lou Yue suddenly realized something was wrong.","She had only planned to bring Xiao Rangchen here to trigger the plot, never expecting him to take part in the ancient tree enlightenment?","In the original story, Long Aotian had already pulled off a stunning enlightenment and stole the show with his damaged spiritual vein. Now that Xiao Rangchen had a fully restored spiritual vein, what on earth was he going to do??","Impulse really is the devil...","Up on the high platform, Lou Mo had already raised his hand, pressing his palm against the void.","The surrounding spiritual energy rippled softly, and a giant gate several yards wide gradually materialized out of thin air. Its door was carved with ancient chi dragons, and dark gold light flowed along the powerful, simple character \"Lou\" right at its center.","As Lou Mo curled his finger, the giant gate rumbled open downward. Dazzling yet gentle warm light gushed out, forming a cascading waterfall of light that fell down, slowly revealing the outline of an ancient tree through the floating light dust.","The tree's trunk was more than ten zhang thick, entirely pale gold, with powerful branches stretching out in all directions. Its boat-shaped leaves were edged with a deeper ring of golden glow.","The wind brushed the treetops, but there was no rustling sound of ordinary wood, only a deep, melodious hum that stretched on for ages.","Just standing beneath it, Lou Yue could feel her sea of consciousness growing clear, and the spiritual energy all around her started circulating on its own.","Lou Mo glanced at the crowd below before turning to take his seat. Lou Zhongyan at the edge of the high platform stepped forward and spoke, \"Everyone, this is our Lou Clan's ancient banyan tree. It has taken root in our ancestral land ever since the clan was founded, standing for thousands of years and absorbing the dao insights of generations of our strongest cultivators.\"","\"Today, our clan leader has opened the ancestral gate to manifest this ancient banyan, so that all of you may climb the tree and gain enlightenment. But the dao mysteries stored within this ancient banyan are vast, far more than ordinary cultivators can casually bear. After you climb the tree, you must remember three rules.\"","\"First, do not touch the clear dew. That dew condenses the dao of the primordial era, and anyone with an unstable dao foundation whose recklessly touches it will have their spiritual energy collapse. Second, each branch of the ancient banyan holds a different dao. Find the one that resonates with you and sit there, do not fight over positions or climb too high. Third, if you feel your sea of consciousness churning, that is the sign you have reached your upper limit of capacity. Immediately calm your mind and come down from the tree, do not force it, or you will surely suffer backlash.\"","Lou Zhongyan extended his hand to gesture toward the ancient tree, and a winding spiritual ladder rose from the ground all the way up. \"All the guests here are accomplished cultivators of the cultivation world. Today, our Lou Clan makes no distinction of status. Anyone who wishes to gain insight may climb the tree.\"","Someone in the crowd spoke up, \"Even commoners?\"","\"We make no distinction of status. If a commoner is here, that is their own good fortune,\" Lou Zhongyan nodded with a smile. \"Everyone, you may begin now.\"","That person still had more to say, but seeing so many others already stepping onto the spiritual ladder, they did not bother to argue further.","Cang Wu stared at Xiao Rangchen in the distance and swore under his breath, \"Lucky bastard.\"","Yue Qi patted his shoulder, \"Relax. He's only at the Foundation Establishment stage, what insight could he possibly get? You're not going to lose this bet.\"","Cang Wu took a deep breath, suppressing the unease in his heart. Right, so what if his spiritual vein is healed? He's still just a Foundation Establishment cultivator. Their understanding of dao is two entire great realms above his.","Most of the people who had come for the birthday celebration were here for the ancient tree enlightenment. Before long, nearly all of them had climbed up. Lou Weixiao, Cangya Xun, Liufeng Xin and several others had already found their own branches to sit cross-legged on.","Lou Yue followed suit onto the spiritual ladder, found a suitable spot and sat down. She glanced over to see Xiao Rangchen still seeming to search for a place, then turned her eyes away.","The process of enlightenment was magical. It was like a dusty mirror being slowly wiped clean of all its grime by mountain winds. The disturbances of the mortal world and the restlessness in one's heart gradually faded away. All that was left between heaven and earth was the soft hum from the branches, one's breath and heartbeat falling in sync with the tree, until one's soul felt almost merged with every gust of wind and every single leaf...","When her consciousness finally returned to clarity, she had no idea how much time had passed.","Thick, mellow spiritual energy swirled and condensed in her dantian, suddenly breaking through the bottleneck.","She had advanced. She skipped the entire Nascent Soul Initial Stage from her Golden Core Great Perfection base, and had directly broken through to the Nascent Soul Middle Stage.","Lou Yue reined in the spiritual energy around her, slowly opening her eyes, only to meet the sharp gaze Lou Mo had cast down from the high platform. He only looked at her for a split second before shifting his sight away.","Quite a few people who had finished their enlightenment were already standing beneath the ancient tree. Lou Yue got to her feet and scanned the area.","Apart from herself, there were only two people left on the massive tree.","Xiao Rangchen, and Cangya Xun.","The moment her feet touched the ground, Cangya Xun also finished his enlightenment. When he realized the only person left up there was Xiao Rangchen, his face turned dark in an instant.","\"Isn't he that commoner? Why is he still on the tree?\"","\"Could it be that he didn't gain any insight at all, so he can't even feel the point where he's reached his limit? Hahaha.\"","\"Even the Young Lord of Cangya has come down. Could it be that he's stronger than the Young Lord of Cangya?\"","\"No way, he's just putting on a show. Commoners really are tacky and unrefined.\"","\"Why does the Lou Clan let him get away with that?\"","\"Hahaha, is he so busy pretending that he can't even bring himself to climb down now? Should we go up and drag him down?\"","...","The man was sitting cross-legged on top of a golden leaf, a few strands of dark hair hanging loosely, brushed gently by the wind.","On his sharp, handsome face, his long eyelashes cast a dark shadow over his eyes, and the black thorn earring on his right ear glinted coldly, matching his slightly pursed thin lips, adding a touch of cool, distant allure.","Humans are such strange creatures.","The more someone seems to shut others out, the more they make one's heart itch.","It makes you want to peek, to see what's hidden under that cold, hard exterior.","Lou Yue suddenly froze. What on earth was she thinking?","What was hidden under there? Nothing but a scumbag, of course.","No matter how he pretends, he can't change the fact that he's the type who likes to keep multiple people around.","Just then, whispers from two girls beside her drifted into her ears.","\"Ugh, even though he's a commoner, his looks are genuinely outstanding. And that waist, from my experience, his waist strength must be incredible. Aren't you going to regret it later?\"","\"Here you go again... My father would never let me marry a commoner...\"","\"You sound so full of regret.\"","\"...Aren't you the one who's regretting it? If only he wasn't a commoner...\"","See? On top of being a scumbag, he just naturally draws people to him.","Lou Yue lost all interest. She walked over to sit down by the side, sinking her mind into feeling the changes in her body after the breakthrough.","About half an hour later, a clear dragon roar rang out from the top of the ancient tree.","The tiny bits of golden light swirling around Xiao Rangchen turned into thousands of golden rainbows that shot straight into the sky. The ancient tree trembled, spiritual winds surged wildly, instantly triggering a resonance with the heaven and earth. Masses of spiritual energy from all over the sky rushed toward him like crazy.","\"He broke through two entire great realms!!\" someone in the crowd gasped out loud in shock.","Lou Yue focused her gaze on him, sensing that Xiao Rangchen was now at the Nascent Soul stage.","From Foundation Establishment to Golden Core to Nascent Soul, he had actually skipped two entire major levels. Thankfully, he hadn't surpassed her, stopping at the Nascent Soul Initial Stage.","But a breakthrough that skipped two great realms had never been seen before. Even the several clan leaders up on the high platform had turned their eyes toward him.","The moment Xiao Rangchen climbed down, he was immediately surrounded. Even as a commoner, with such monstrous natural talent, every great clan would be eager to recruit him.","Lou Yue moved quickly, blocking the path of someone who was trying to sneak away.","\"Where do you think you're going? Afraid of losing face?\"","Cang Wu's face darkened completely when Lou Yue threw his earlier words right back at him.","\"The four great clans stand united. Lou Yue, you'd better not pick a fight with the Cangya Clan over some irrelevant nobody.\"","Lou Yue scoffed contemptuously, \"You lost the bet, don't drag the entire Cangya Clan into this.\"","Just as Cangya Wu's face was turning livid, thinking he was about to be humiliated in front of everyone, Cangya Xun's voice came from up ahead, \"Cang Wu.\"","Cang Wu's face lit up with relief, as if he had been granted amnesty. He arrogantly huffed at Lou Yue, then quickly followed behind Cangya Xun and left.","Lou Yue lifted her foot to follow after them, but her arm was suddenly pulled from behind.","\"Don't go.\" Xiao Rangchen had somehow shaken off the surrounding crowd. \"Cangya Xun is deep and cunning. Don't confront him head on.\"","Lou Yue watched Cangya Xun and Cang Wu walking off, her peach blossom eyes narrowing. She was just about to snap at him when a familiar figure caught her sight.","\"He won't be happy for long.\"","Xiao Rangchen spoke in a slow, even tone, but Lou Yue acted as if she hadn't heard him at all. She stared straight ahead into the distance, and the resentment in her eyes faded, replaced by obvious delight.","Xiao Rangchen followed her line of sight, and saw the woman who was the reason she had been willing to wait on the covered bridge.","When Lou Yue pulled her gaze back, she noticed that Xiao Rangchen was also looking at Liufeng Xin. This was the second time he had stared at Liufeng Xin that day.","The white moonlight was indeed something special.","It wasn't exactly disappointment. More like a sudden realization that the time had come.","It was like a bird with a wounded wing that had accidentally fallen into her home. She had cared for it for a few days, and now that its injury had healed, it was flying off to the place it belonged.","So many things had spiraled out of her control lately that she had almost forgotten her own identity. She and Xiao Rangchen were rivals, and in this world, she was nothing more than a side character who existed to play the part of his romantic rival.","Earlier, he had been stuck at his lowest point, which had let her get the upper hand. But now, his spiritual meridian had healed, and the entire cultivation realm would soon witness his rise, with no one left able to stand in his way.","She had to give it her all to avoid falling too far behind him, to gain the power to change the doomed ending.","Lou Yue pulled her arm out of his grasp, stepped back to put some distance between them, and said in a cool, steady voice, \"I brought you up to Xuan Tiandu. Now that your cultivation level is nearly the same as mine, there's no need for you to stay by my side any longer.\"","\"We were never meant to walk the same path. From now on, you take your wide open road, and I'll cross my single-plank bridge. The life you owe me, plus the three favors you promised me, I'll come find you when the time comes to collect.\"","Xiao Rangchen lifted his eyes. There was no expression on his face, but the look in his eyes darkened.","\"Tomorrow you...\" Lou Yue had been about to tell him not to take part in the competition the next day, but then she thought better of it. There was no reason Xiao Rangchen would listen to her. Tomorrow, she was the one who should be on edge. If she lost, she would never get into the sect of Que Yunsheng, never get that special advantage she needed, and things would only get harder for her from there.","\"Don't hold back against me tomorrow.\" She wanted to see for herself how big the gap between them really was.","Lou Yue glanced in the direction Liufeng Xin had left. \"I have things to take care of. I'm leaving now.\"","\"Oh right,\" she stopped in her tracks. \"Your sister. I think it's better for Xiao Aiai to stay here in Xuan Tiandu. I'll arrange everything properly, make sure she has a safe place to stay.\"","Seeing Xiao Rangchen stay silent, Lou Yue assumed he was unwilling. \"You're going off to seek revenge. You might not fear the danger, but what will those people do to her? Staying by your side will only put her in harm's way. I suggest you give up on that idea.\"","\"Stop talking.\"","Lou Yue frowned. \"It's better for both of you if you let this go. She has a bright future ahead of her. Before she even—\"","\"I said stop talking!\" Xiao Rangchen cut her off sharply, his tone taut with a hint of suppressed rage.","Lou Yue froze. She had never expected Xiao Rangchen to care so deeply about Xiao Aiai. But that made sense. In the book, when he found out he and Xiao Aiai were not blood-related, he had immediately taken her into his harem. If their bond had only been that of siblings, that shift would never have happened so naturally.","After all, she was just an outsider. All she could do was give Xiao Aiai a choice and make sure there was a safety net for her. What would happen to the girl in the end, she had no way of knowing.","Just like she had no idea if she would end up dying at Xiao Rangchen's hands someday.","Lou Yue brushed a stray strand of wind-tousled hair away from her face. Forget it. She had said all that needed to be said. Other people's lives should be decided by themselves.","She no longer looked at the man with the dark, heavy expression in front of her, turned around resolutely, and left.","Xiao Rangchen swallowed the bitter taste in his throat, slowly closed his eyes, and stood there, listening to the sound of her footsteps fade away little by little."]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["Before it was even ten o’clock at night, Lou Yue had made her way to the covered bridge by the teleportation array.","Liufeng Xin was nowhere to be seen. At the spot where they had agreed to meet, a firefly was hovering. It circled Lou Yue twice, then flew out over the bridge. Lou Yue followed after it.","The Langhua Liufeng Clan occupied the fertile Langhua Valley in the west. Spring lasted there all year round, with spiritual herbs and flowers growing everywhere. In addition to alchemy, they were also highly skilled at controlling spirit insects and Gu beasts.","This firefly was Liufeng Xin’s eyes. Not only could she command it, she could also see everything it saw.","Sure enough, the firefly led Lou Yue to a secluded forest in one corner of Xuantian City before flying onto Liufeng Xin’s shoulder, where she sat on a tree branch.","Lou Yue leaped up into the tree and sat down beside her without the slightest hesitation. Resting both hands against the rough bark, she sighed, “I never thought there’d be more than one modern person in this world.”","Liufeng Xin said nothing. With a white veil covering her eyes, she stood beneath the bright full moon, cold and aloof as a Goddess.","“You’re making this so exhausting.” Lou Yue tilted her head back to look at her.","Liufeng Xin remained silent, but at least she sat down beside Lou Yue.","Lou Yue swung her legs and tilted her head. “How long ago did you transmigrate?”","“Two years.”","“Hmm, longer than me. It’s only been a month or so for me.”","No one spoke. The silence was absolute.","Liufeng Xin really was ice-cold. Lou Yue couldn’t tell whether she had always been like this before transmigrating, or if she had changed after arriving here.","“So how did you transmigrate?” Lou Yue asked.","Liufeng Xin was silent at first. After a while, she answered in her cool, detached voice, “There was a typhoon. I wanted to get home early, but I was blown here instead.”","“...That’s a pretty lame joke.”","Liufeng Xin turned her face toward her. “It wasn’t a joke.”","“I was swept into the sky. When I landed, I had become Liufeng Xin,” she said calmly.","Lou Yue burst out laughing at her utterly matter-of-fact delivery. “Then you were pretty lucky. At least you didn’t land dead on arrival.”","“Mm.”","“Did you know you’d transmigrated into a book?”","“Mm.”","“Then what did you think when you met your Prince Charming today?”","Liufeng Xin’s lips curved faintly. “He’s handsome, but I don’t ship him with Liufeng Xin.”","“Ship? What does that mean?”","Liufeng Xin seemed to consider how best to explain. After a moment, she said, “I have no interest in him and Liufeng Xin as a couple.”","“Then who are you interested in?” Lou Yue asked, following the opening.","Through the thin veil, Liufeng Xin stared fixedly at her. Her voice remained utterly calm. “I’m a heretic.”","Lou Yue looked at her, waiting for the rest.","“I ship him with you.”","Lou Yue was confused at first. Then she understood what Liufeng Xin meant and couldn’t help laughing helplessly. “Girl, this body is male.”","“Mm...?” Liufeng Xin caught the implication in Lou Yue’s words and asked, “You were a woman before you transmigrated?”","Lou Yue nodded. “Obviously. I’m not nearly as lucky as you.”","Liufeng Xin showed the first smile of the night, though it was no more than the slightest lift at the corners of her lips.","Lou Yue said frankly, “Sigh. Even now, I still can’t accept that I’ve become a man.”","Liufeng Xin said nothing, but Lou Yue no longer felt the conversation sinking into awkward silence. She continued, “Do you know, I even bathe with my clothes on?”","Liufeng Xin pressed her lips together, looking faintly uncomfortable. Lou Yue was just about to ask why when the aloof Goddess in front of her suddenly raised a hand and pulled off the veil covering her eyes.","Those eyes were as beautiful and pure as the book had described, breathtakingly holy. Yet in an instant, that holiness transformed into a look brimming with mischievous amusement.","“I couldn’t hold it in anymore,” the Goddess said.","“...?”","Lou Yue felt as though her brain had become a little sluggish.","With her otherworldly face, Liufeng Xin leaned closer. “Girl, how unlucky can you be? You actually transmigrated into a man.”","When she saw Lou Yue staring blankly, a smug smile spread across her face. “I love seeing that expression—the one that says, ‘Who is she? Where’s my saintess?’”","Lou Yue stared at her for a long moment before finally finding her voice. She pointed at the veil in Liufeng Xin’s hand. “Is there some kind of seal on that?”","Liufeng Xin froze for a moment, then laughed so hard she nearly fell sideways. Wiping the tears from the corners of her eyes, she said, “You’re hilarious! I was pretending to be like that.”","“It was killing me. Everyone around me is there to keep an eye on me. The moment I do anything that doesn’t fit the saintess persona, they nag me endlessly.”","Lou Yue had already figured that out. The talkative one between them had become Liufeng Xin.","But she seemed to prefer Liufeng Xin like this—lively, radiant, and full of laughter.","“Even if we’re both transmigrators, aren’t you afraid I might have ulterior motives? I could expose your true nature, you know.” Lou Yue smiled.","Liufeng Xin tilted her head. “You won’t.”","She turned her head away. Her voice was still cool, but it no longer carried that forbidding distance. “Besides, I’ve had enough of living like this. I didn’t come out tonight intending to go back.”","In the book, Liufeng Xin had only been able to break away from the Langhua Liufeng Clan after Long Aotian had forcibly subdued them with his overwhelming strength. The saintess held extraordinary significance for the Liufeng clan. If Liufeng Xin wanted to leave by relying on her own strength, it would be incredibly difficult.","“What can I do to help you?” Lou Yue asked directly.","A flicker of surprise crossed Liufeng Xin’s eyes. Then she smiled. “With you saying that—”","She suddenly stopped. Her pupils shimmered with a kaleidoscope of colors, then returned to normal in an instant. She leaned toward Lou Yue and lowered her voice to a whisper.","“Shh. Don’t move. Long Aotian is here, about thirty or forty meters behind us.”","Lou Yue froze. Why had Xiao Rangchen come?","“He concealed his aura. If it weren’t for the firefly, I wouldn’t have noticed him either.”","Lou Yue’s lips moved as she whispered, “Did he come looking for you?”","Liufeng Xin rolled her saintly, cool eyes. “When we ran into each other this morning, the way he looked at me...” She paused, searching for the right words. “It was as if I’d stolen his home.”","Lou Yue couldn’t help letting out a muffled laugh.","Liufeng Xin looked helpless. “I’m serious. It was that kind of look—the sort that says he wants to stab me a few times and wishes I would disappear immediately. That’s no way to look at a lost love. He looked at me like I was his mortal enemy.”","As she spoke, the colors in her pupils shimmered again. Lou Yue knew she was using the firefly’s eyes to observe him.","“I have a theory,” Liufeng Xin said.","“What is it?”","“He followed you here. If he were looking for me, he wouldn’t have waited until now to come. Besides, I don’t think someone who looks at me with such murderous intent would follow me unless he intended to assassinate me.”","Lou Yue considered this. “Hmm. I did offend him this afternoon. He might have come to assassinate me.”","“Should we test him?”","“How?”","Liufeng Xin hooked an arm around Lou Yue’s neck and leaned her whole body against her. Lou Yue immediately understood and lowered her head cooperatively.","Liufeng Xin continued watching through the firefly’s eyes as she quietly directed Lou Yue. “Quick, put your arms around me. Pretend we’re making out.”","Lou Yue laughed inwardly but slipped an arm around her waist, applying just enough pressure to make it look from behind as though she were holding Liufeng Xin tightly against her.","Liufeng Xin adjusted the angle of her face so that Lou Yue completely blocked it from view. Her voice was teasing. “He’s here. That murderous look has finally arrived, right on schedule.”","“Tsk, tsk. This is getting serious. Judging by the way he’s coming, he’ll be charging over any second now.”","“...Wait. Why do I feel like he’s looking at us the way a husband catches his wife cheating?”","Lou Yue struggled not to laugh. The experience was far too novel for her. It was a shame she couldn’t see Xiao Rangchen’s expression herself and could only watch through Liufeng Xin’s live commentary.","“I’m going to fan the flames a little more.”","Then Lou Yue suddenly heard an ambiguous sound escape Liufeng Xin’s lips.","“Mm... ah...”","Lou Yue: “...”","Liufeng Xin’s acting was nothing short of masterful. Her voice was hazy and heated, with just the slightest tremor, every note perfectly measured. If Lou Yue hadn’t known she was acting, hearing only those sounds would have made anyone think they’d stumbled upon an indecent scene.","Lou Yue laughed and mouthed, “That’s enough. Don’t overdo it.”","“Mm...”","Before long, Liufeng Xin said, sounding somewhat disappointed, “Tsk, he’s gone.”","Her pupils returned to normal as she rose from Lou Yue’s arms, still wearing an unfulfilled look of regret.","“I thought he was going to charge over. Who knew he’d actually leave?”","“If he didn’t leave, was he supposed to keep watching you and me make out?” Lou Yue was genuinely impressed by her. Who would have thought that beneath the outwardly aloof and untouchable Liufeng clan’s saintess lurked such a shameless drama queen?","Liufeng Xin fell silent for a moment, seemingly recalling something. After a while, a mischievous smile appeared on her face.","“I have a bold guess.” She turned to Lou Yue. “Do you want to hear it?”","“No.”","The moment Lou Yue saw that expression, she knew it couldn’t be anything good. She leaped down from the tree, making her refusal perfectly clear.","Liufeng Xin jumped down after her and tugged at her sleeve. “Oh, come on, listen. I’m kind of excited.”","“No. It’s late. We should go back. Aren’t you afraid the people watching over you will be searching everywhere for you?”","At once, Liufeng Xin deflated.","Lou Yue took the veil from her hand and draped it over her eyes. “I’ll come find you tomorrow. You said you don’t want to be the saintess anymore, right? I have a way to help.”","“What way?” Liufeng Xin immediately perked up.","“You’ll find out tomorrow.”","“Still being mysterious.” Liufeng Xin curved her lips. “But I like it.”","The two walked side by side toward the exit. When they passed a tree, Liufeng Xin grabbed Lou Yue’s arm.","“Long Aotian was standing behind this tree just now.”","As she spoke, she imitated Xiao Rangchen’s stance and raised a hand to brace it against the trunk. But the instant her palm touched the bark—","Boom!","The enormous tree, which would have taken two people to encircle with their arms, exploded right in front of them and turned to ash.","Lou Yue: “...”","Liufeng Xin stared blankly at the empty pit where the tree had been. Then she murmured, “I think... I may have shipped a real couple...”","**","Baichuan Hall was the temporary residence the Lou clan had prepared for its guests. Built against the mountains and beside the water, it consisted of five pavilions arranged one after another.","Each floor held two rooms, and it was only after leaving her room that morning that Lou Yue discovered Yue Qi was staying next door.","She disliked the way Yue Qi looked at her. His gaze was sticky and cold, and whenever he drew near, a strange scent would drift over and burrow into her mind, like some kind of cheap perfume that made her feel sick.","Lou Yue hurried downstairs to get away from him. After she left, several black, glassy bead-like objects rolled out from Yue Qi’s sleeve. The moment they touched the wall, they silently sank into it without leaving a trace.","Yue Qi gazed in the direction she had disappeared, his eyes narrowing slightly. Open madness and viciousness flashed within them.","Lou Yue had no idea what Yue Qi had done. She encountered Liufeng Xin just as the latter was leaving the second pavilion.","When no one was paying attention, Liufeng Xin crooked a finger at her, clearly urging her to keep the promise they had made the night before. Lou Yue looked at her with curved brows and shook her head.","Liufeng Xin turned away with an icy, haughty air. Lou Yue chuckled, but before the smile had faded from her face, she ran straight into another cold gaze.","Xiao Rangchen glanced at her, expressionless, then turned and headed down another path.","To be honest, when she woke that morning and didn’t find Xiao Rangchen in her room as she had before, Lou Yue had felt relieved. After all, they had only just declared that they were going their separate ways yesterday. Hugging each other first thing the next morning would have been far too embarrassing.","This was better. Strangers crossing paths, pretending not to see each other—that was what their relationship ought to look like.","Lou Yue stepped onto her own path.","Today’s matches were open only to cultivators below the Mahayana stage. The top three winners would be allowed to enter the Lou clan’s treasure vault, Que Yunsheng, and choose one magical artifact. Their rankings would determine which floor they could enter.","The item that served as her cheat was on the second floor, so Lou Yue set her sights on finishing in the top two.","The matches were decided by drawing lots. After fighting only two rounds, she received a series of byes. Xiao Rangchen, meanwhile, had beaten nearly everyone else so thoroughly that they gave up on the remaining matches altogether.","At first, the spectators had been indignant, feeling that the arrangement was unfair. But by the end, they could only watch in silence as one battered and disheveled contestant after another came down from the platform, while Lou Yue somehow made it into the top three.","She and Xiao Rangchen were in the first match of the finals. Whether he was tired or deliberately trying to repay the favor he owed her, Xiao Rangchen no longer attacked with the decisiveness and ferocity he had shown earlier. Most of his moves were defensive.","“Are you looking down on me? I told you not to hold back.”","Xiao Rangchen dodged the ice spikes she conjured, then thrust his black spear straight at her. Lou Yue hurled spell after spell, but he broke through every one of them.","She knew she couldn’t let a body-refining cultivator like Xiao Rangchen get close. Yet Xiao Rangchen kept defending, and if the fight dragged on, she would be the one to lose once her spiritual energy ran dry.","She planned to unleash her strongest offensive spell at the instant Xiao Rangchen came within striking distance and settle the match in one decisive blow.","She wasn’t particularly confident in the move. After watching his earlier matches, she knew it would be extremely difficult for her to win.","What she hadn’t expected was that, after closing in, Xiao Rangchen would actually lose focus and allow her spell to strike him head-on, sending him tumbling off the platform.","Lou Yue: ??","The next match began. Lou Yue watched from below as the man onstage beat the Cangya cultivator so badly that he was practically questioning his entire life. Then, belatedly, she touched her own lips.","There was a narrow split in the middle of her lower lip. She had caused it the previous night in bed while talking to Xuanba, when she had failed to catch a falling piece of ice.","Had Xiao Rangchen lost focus just now because he was looking at that cut?"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["The final match ended with Lou Yue in first place, Xiao Rangchen in second, and a certain Cangya disciple in third.","When that Cangya disciple—who was at the peak of the Nascent Soul stage—was beaten so thoroughly by Xiao Rangchen, who was only in the early Nascent Soul stage, that he could not fight back at all, Cangya clan lord Cangya Lan’s expression on the high platform turned cold. With a snort, he waved his sleeve and vanished.","“He was originally a disciple of the Cangya Summit, but was later expelled. No wonder Old Lan can’t bear to show his face.” The red-haired, red-browed old man stroked his beard with a chuckle.","The woman beside him arched her willow brows. “That old bastard Cangya Lan must’ve had lard clogging his brain. Serves him right!”","The woman was Liufeng clan lord Liufeng Herong. When they were young, she and Cangya Lan had once been a couple. Yet in the end, Cangya Lan married the daughter of another sword immortal, and the two of them became sworn enemies. Even now, despite their advanced years, she still took every opportunity to berate him.","The red-browed old man cast a glance at Lou Mo, who remained calm and composed. Lou Mo acted as though he had seen nothing.","That old bastard only knows how to sit on the sidelines and watch the fire burn, the red-browed old man cursed inwardly.","The more Liufeng Herong thought about it, the angrier she became. With a bang, she set her cup down on the stone table. “That boy isn’t anything special either. My Liufeng clan was willing to take him in as a live-in son-in-law, yet a mere commoner actually dared refuse us!”","“He hasn’t even reached the Mahayana stage. Isn’t it a little too hasty to win him over?” The red-browed old man took a sip of wine and spoke unhurriedly.","“Hmph. With Cangya as your backer, of course you’re in no rush.”","The red-browed old man’s expression turned cold as well. “Aren’t your Liufeng and Lou clans in cahoots? It’s a joyous occasion today, so show some restraint at your age.”","“Yue Qianzhong, what are you pretending—”","Lou Mo interrupted, “Enough. I summoned you here to discuss the exploration of the Savage Wasteland, not to trade insults. Since the matter is settled, my Lou clan will not be keeping you.”","With that, Lou Mo’s figure vanished from the high platform.","Liufeng Herong and Yue Qianzhong exchanged a glance, each snorted coldly, and then disappeared one after the other.","The quarrels on the high platform were clouds in the heavens, impossibly distant to those below. To Lou Yue, who had been led to Queyun Tower, they were completely irrelevant.","Queyun Tower stood in the heart of Xuantian City. The entire building was hidden amid rosy clouds and drifting mist, while the radiance of eighteen sealing arrays slowly revolved around it.","Lou Zhongyan raised a hand and pressed it against the door. One after another, the eighteen arrays unlocked, revealing the passage beyond.","He led the three of them inside.","“Everyone, you have only one hour. Each person may take out only one magical treasure.”","With that, he tossed out a jade water clock to keep time. He then walked over to a reclining chair in the hall, sat down, closed his eyes, and began to rest.","Lou Yue paid no attention to Xiao Rangchen’s frequent glances in her direction. She seized every moment and leapt onto the cloud corridor on the second floor.","The interior of Queyun Tower was far vaster than she had expected. Although she knew that the old grandpa in his ring was residing inside a damaged bamboo slip, she still had to search for him—and she also needed to leave enough time to deal with whatever trials awaited her.","Lou Yue swiftly passed all kinds of floating magical artifacts and spirit treasures. After searching for roughly fifteen minutes, she had covered only a quarter of the second floor, while Xiao Rangchen had already left the first floor and stepped onto the level where she was.","She grew anxious, wishing she could conjure a clone. As her eyes swept rapidly across the area, they suddenly fixed on a spot two meters behind Xiao Rangchen.","A damaged bamboo slip was quietly suspended there amid the clouds.","She had found it!","Lou Yue took off running. She no longer cared about maintaining her dignity. At this speed, she was certain she could snatch it before Xiao Rangchen. She could already feel the bamboo slip beckoning to her!","But just as she rounded the corner, a strange sensation shot through her. She instinctively glanced at the magical artifact beside her, and that single glance caused her to trip over nothing and fall flat on her face.","The moment she steadied herself, a pitch-black cube the size of a fist dropped from above and struck her squarely on the forehead.","It hurt a little. She had probably broken the skin. Lou Yue raised a hand, intending to put the cube that had landed in her arms back where it belonged, but the thing suddenly emitted a faint black radiance. At that very moment, a drop of blood slid from her forehead and fell into the cube.","Lou Yue’s pupils contracted.","No. Please, no!","The cube completely ignored her desperate prayer. After absorbing the bead of blood, it returned to its original pitch-black color. At the same time, a thread of unfamiliar consciousness appeared in her mind.","...Damn it.","The blasted thing had recognized her as its master.","Struck senseless by this sudden misfortune, Lou Yue could only watch helplessly as Xiao Rangchen picked up the bamboo slip in the distance.","“......”","She wanted to go home. This world was far too hostile toward her...","It had given her hope, only to dash it. She felt as though she had been starving for a long time, and a plate of roast chicken had suddenly appeared before her. Just as she was about to sink her teeth into it, the roast chicken had abruptly transformed into a toy squeaky chicken. She could practically hear its shrill cry mocking her.","This was too much!","Lou Yue stamped her foot furiously, her eyes reddening with rage.","Xiao Rangchen failed to notice the scene in the distance. He had just found the spirit insect Feng Que wanted, but when he turned around with it in hand, his gaze was drawn to the shabby bamboo slip in the corner. Without realizing it, he picked it up, and his divine sense was pulled into the bamboo slip in an instant.","“Boy, you’re quite lucky.”","A middle-aged man’s voice rang out in the void-like space.","“Sorry.” After saying this, Xiao Rangchen tried to withdraw his divine sense, only to find it restrained by some unseen force.","“Boy, do you know who I am?”","Xiao Rangchen’s voice remained indifferent. “I had no intention of disturbing you, Senior. Please release my divine sense and allow it to leave.”","“...Do you have any idea how powerful I am? Let me tell you—”","“Please let me leave, Senior.”","“......”","In the next instant, a scholar in Confucian robes, holding a paper fan, appeared beside Xiao Rangchen out of thin air. He raised the fan handle and repeatedly rapped it against Xiao Rangchen. “Get out, get out! I said let him leave!”","Xiao Rangchen’s divine sense was completely immobilized by the man’s restraints, leaving him no choice but to endure the blows.","“You can leave if you want,” the man said after venting his anger, once again resuming his refined demeanor. He slowly opened his paper fan. “You need only pass through my Seven Emotions Trials, and I’ll let you go.”","Xiao Rangchen frowned. He had no desire to waste time here.","“Don’t worry. These Seven Emotions Trials won’t be difficult for you. If you want to leave as soon as possible, just give them everything you’ve got and pass through them.”","Yu Youchun pushed forcefully, sending Xiao Rangchen straight into the first trial: Hatred.","The Seven Emotions Trials consisted of Joy, Anger, Sorrow, Fear, Love, Hatred, and Desire. Based on Yu Youchun’s probing of Xiao Rangchen’s divine sense, Hatred was the obstacle he would find most difficult to overcome, while Desire would be the easiest.","If he could pass Hatred with ease, the remaining six trials would pose no challenge at all.","Yu Youchun had waited a thousand years before finally finding someone who met all his requirements. He absolutely refused to let him go.","Just as he had expected, Xiao Rangchen possessed extraordinary talent and a will as unyielding as solid rock. In less than half an hour, he had cut through six trials in succession. Delighted, Yu Youchun immediately raised a hand and sent him into the final trial—Desire.","The Desire Trial used the entrant’s memories as its foundation to weave a dreamscape of desires so realistic that truth and illusion were impossible to distinguish.","Everything within the dream was exactly what the heart yearned for, within easy reach. Unlike the other six trials, this one required only that the entrant see through the illusion and voluntarily withdraw.","Time flowed slowly within the dreamscape. Yu Youchun estimated that Xiao Rangchen would emerge in at most a few breaths.","But he had never imagined that the Desire Trial—which he believed would be the easiest for Xiao Rangchen—would consume even more time than the other six trials combined.","Within the “Desire Gate,” Xiao Rangchen slowly opened his eyes.","Before him was the familiar Sleeping Cloud Courtyard—the room that belonged to Lou Yue.","“Xiao Rangchen...”","Lou Yue’s voice came from behind him. It was not her usual bold, carefree tone, but the soft, sweet murmur she used in her dreams.","His instincts told him not to turn around. Yet another quiet call reached his ears, this one carrying a hint of helplessness.","Before he could react, his body had already turned.","Lou Yue stood two paces away with her back to him. Her clothes were half undone, her moon-white undergarment hanging loosely from her right shoulder, barely holding on.","“Xiao Rangchen... My hairpin fell inside my clothes.”","Her voice held Lou Yue’s characteristic lilt, softened by a touch of sweetness that made it sound almost coquettish.","“Help me get it.”","Xiao Rangchen remained where he was, his gaze helplessly drawn to the slightly raised butterfly-shaped shoulder blade on her left side.","“Xiao Rangchen...”","The shoulder blade trembled lightly with each of her breaths, as though trying to break free from its cage.","“Xiao Rangchen...”","It trembled even more intensely now, radiating a fragile, shattered vulnerability that could ensnare the heart.","“Xiao Rangchen... Help me get it...”","Xiao Rangchen’s Adam’s apple bobbed. It took all his willpower to tear his eyes away from that shoulder blade.","The jade hairpin she wanted was half tucked into the hem of her clothing, resting right against the hollow of her lower back. Its lustrous white surface, stained with emerald green, was dazzling.","Xiao Rangchen closed his eyes for a moment, suppressing the dark tide churning beneath them, then took a step forward and reached for it.","“Ah.” A hurried, delicate gasp escaped her. “It’s cold...”","Though she called it cold, her trembling body instinctively leaned toward him, and the back of his fingers brushed against her smooth, lustrous skin.","“Xiao Rangchen, you’re so slow...” she grumbled unhappily, drawing out the last syllable.","Xiao Rangchen pulled out the hairpin. Yet, as if possessed, he held it by the middle, letting its tip rest against one side of her back before slowly tracing upward—gliding over her spine, then over the butterfly poised to take flight.","“Xiao Rangchen... Xiao Rangchen...”","Her trembling voice called his name again and again.","And amid those repeated calls, Xiao Rangchen sank completely into the moment.","Everything around him blurred into indistinct shadows. The only thing left was the woman before him.","His lips replaced the hairpin, kissing the butterfly that, from the very first moment he had seen it, had been impossible to banish from his mind.","He lingered over it, leaving behind marks that belonged to him, turning that pearly white butterfly into a luxuriant, flushed red.","The woman in front of him seemed unable to hold herself upright any longer. Her body swayed, and he hooked one arm around her waist while his other hand clasped her left wrist, preventing the butterfly from escaping his territory and allowing it to beat its wings only within his embrace.","Lou Yue’s soft, trembling voice continued to pour into his ears.","Urgent, ragged breaths mingled with the frantic pounding of his heart against his ribs.","Xiao Rangchen knew this was an illusion.","He knew the Lou Yue before him was not real.","Yet he still could not restrain himself.","The moment he kissed her, realization dawned.","So this was how he felt about Lou Yue.","Everything that had happened before finally had an answer.","He wanted to kill that woman because he had been jealous—jealous of the intimacy she shared with Lou Yue, jealous that she could make Lou Yue smile.","Jealous of everything he could never possess, yet she had obtained with ease.","It turned out that, without realizing it, he had already fallen in love with Lou Yue.","It turned out...","He had been longing for her all along.","----------------------","My darlings, did you like it?"]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["After Xiao Rangchen returned to the void space inside the bamboo slip, he was stared at the entire time.","“I never would have guessed that you were actually so lustful.”","Yu Youchun gazed at his cold, sharp features, still unable to understand it. Xiao Rangchen clearly looked so passionless and aloof—how had he nearly failed the trial of desire?","Xiao Rangchen acted as though he had not heard him. He merely reminded him, “Senior has passed all seven trials. Please fulfill your promise.”","“Young man, are you truly not going to regret this? If you acknowledge me as your master, forget about becoming the strongest cultivator among the four great clans. Even if you wish to break through to a realm above the Deity Transformation stage, I’m confident I can help you achieve it.”","Xiao Rangchen fell silent.","Yu Youchun thought he had wavered, but then heard him say, “I cannot take Senior out of here. I promised someone that I would retrieve the spirit insect to repay his kindness.”","Yu Youchun naturally knew that he was holding the spirit insect, but how could the value of such an insect compare with his own?","“It’s merely a rare spirit insect. But if you miss the chance to have me as your master, what you’ll be losing is the opportunity to stand at the very peak of the world.”","“If he hadn’t saved me, I would not be where I am today.” Every word Xiao Rangchen spoke was firm. “Please let me leave, Senior.”","Yu Youchun waved his sleeve with great flair. “Fine. I won’t force you to do anything against your will. Go.”","Xiao Rangchen’s consciousness returned to his body, and he immediately placed the bamboo slip back where it had been.","Inside the bamboo slip, Yu Youchun stood with his hands behind his back, “watching” the outside world. His carefree expression turned crafty.","“Like hell I won’t!”","“I waited a thousand years for you to appear. To hell with this ‘I won’t force you’ nonsense. If I can’t get what I want through honest means, I’ll achieve it by any means necessary. Once you passed through the Seven Emotions Trial, our agreement was already complete. Hahahaha—”","His hearty laughter echoed through the void, and his figure gradually faded away amid the sound.","As Xiao Rangchen turned and left, the bamboo slip suddenly cracked apart, as though the force sustaining it had been completely drained away.","“Have you all chosen?” Lou Zhongyan glanced over the treasures in the three disciples’ hands. When his gaze reached Xiao Rangchen, it paused. “Are you certain you want that spirit insect?”","“Yes.”","Lou Yue had already been staring blankly at the spirit insect in his hand.","Why hadn’t he taken the bamboo slip?","The strongest cheat in the story’s plot, Yu Youchun, was inside that bamboo slip. Could it be that Xiao Rangchen had failed the Seven Emotions Trial?","Impossible. In the novel, he had passed it at lightning speed, and Yu Youchun had been delighted.","Could that spirit insect be an even more incredible magical treasure?","Lou Yue stared intently at the spirit insect in Xiao Rangchen’s hand, wishing she could instantly analyze all the countless abilities it possessed.","Her gaze was far too intense to escape notice.","However, Xiao Rangchen’s eyes lingered only briefly on the small wound on her forehead before shifting away.","Lou Zhongyan knew how Lou Yue had obtained her treasure, and he understood that she was feeling somewhat dejected. He spoke up, “It suits you very well. You can study its uses.”","The Cangya Sect disciple beside them hurriedly leaned forward. “What about mine?”","“Acceptable.” After giving his indifferent assessment, Lou Zhongyan rose to his feet. “The time is up. Let’s go.”","Once they emerged from Queyun Pavilion, Lou Yue left directly.","Only then did Xiao Rangchen’s gaze sink heavily toward that departing figure. He watched until she had completely disappeared, then slowly lowered his eyes.","The reason an illusion was an illusion was that it was separated from reality by a distance that could never be crossed.","He gave a cold, indifferent tug at the corner of his lips before turning and walking in the opposite direction.","**","The stone forest on the western outskirts of Xuantian City.","“The things you gave me are completely useless!” an agitated voice suddenly rang out.","Yue Qi sat on a low rock, frowning. “Are you certain you threw all the realm-locking beads into the wall?”","“Of course.” Cang Wu snorted coldly. He opened his palm, revealing more than a dozen fragments resembling black glass. “I threw them in while he was away. He did enter the room, just as expected, but he still participated in the competition as usual this morning. I just went to check, and all the realm-locking beads inside the wall had been shattered into scraps!”","Yue Qi picked up one of the fragments and held it close for a careful examination. After a long while, he lowered his hand, his expression grave.","“Two years ago, he was at the Nascent Soul stage. His spiritual meridians were damaged, causing his cultivation to fall to the Foundation Establishment stage. It was only a few days ago that his meridians recovered, and he returned to the Nascent Soul stage after comprehending the Dao through the ancient tree?”","“That’s right.”","Yue Qi exhaled heavily, his voice turning cold and grim. “I advise you to stay as far away from him as possible from now on.”","Cang Wu frowned. “What do you mean?”","“Anyone capable of destroying the realm-locking beads like that could kill you as easily as turning over a hand.”","“Impossible!” Cang Wu shouted. “During the competition this morning, I clearly only lost on the final move.”","“He deliberately held back.”","Cang Wu still refused to believe it. Yue Qi could not be bothered to explain further. “In any case, our cooperation ends here.”","He turned to leave, but Cang Wu called out from behind him, “Yue Qi! Aren’t you afraid I’ll tell Lou Yue that she’s already been poisoned by your drug?”","Yue Qi stopped. His eyes filled with sinister malice, but he did not turn around. He merely tossed out three words:","“Go ahead and try.”","Cang Wu was furious. He punched a stone pillar, blasting it apart and sending shattered rock flying in all directions.","Yue Qi ignored Cang Wu’s fit of rage. He only wanted to get as far away from him as possible, lest Xiao Rangchen discover that the realm-locking beads had come from him.","Cang Wu did not understand, but Yue Qi was the one who had refined them. He knew their power better than anyone. No one below the Great Ascension stage could possibly destroy them. Even cultivators at the Great Ascension stage might not be able to break them if they were not skilled in offensive techniques.","Xiao Rangchen’s cultivation was definitely not as simple as the early Nascent Soul stage he displayed on the surface.","However, just as Yue Qi was about to leave the stone forest, the person he least wanted to see at that moment appeared ahead of him.","Yue Qi’s face changed drastically.","Xiao Rangchen approached step by step.","Yue Qi hurriedly backed away, only to be stopped by an invisible barrier. He had nowhere left to retreat.","“You drugged Lou Yue.”","His tone was utterly certain.","Yue Qi was terrified. Xiao Rangchen had heard his conversation with Cang Wu. How much had he heard? Did he know that the realm-locking beads had come from him?","“Ten breaths. Hand over the antidote.”","A pressure far beyond the Nascent Soul stage descended in an instant. Yue Qi’s knees slammed heavily into the ground, and cold sweat immediately soaked through his robes. He specialized in artifact refinement, and his cultivation was only at the Golden Core stage. He could not withstand such overwhelming pressure. Compared with Cang Wu, it would be far easier for Xiao Rangchen to kill him.","Under the crushing pressure, Yue Qi trembled as he reached into his robes and pulled out a bottle of pills.","Xiao Rangchen crooked a finger, and the bottle flew into his hand.","“Take one directly,” Yue Qi panted.","Xiao Rangchen opened the bottle, and a rich fragrance drifted out. There were two pills inside. He flicked one into Yue Qi’s mouth.","After waiting for a while, he bent down and pressed two fingers to Yue Qi’s neck, confirming that there was nothing abnormal before putting away the bottle. He warned him coldly, “If this is a fake—”","Yue Qi raised his left hand. “I, Yue Qi, swear upon my soul that this pill will definitely dispel the drug in Lou Yue’s body. If these words are false, may I be struck by heavenly lightning and have my soul annihilated.”","Only then did Xiao Rangchen leave, and the pressure weighing down on Yue Qi gradually dissipated.","Yue Qi gasped violently. Without even taking time to recover, he immediately climbed to his feet.","He had to leave Xuantian City at once and return to the Yue family in Qingzhou.","That pill truly was an antidote. He had not lied to Xiao Rangchen. But it was also a poison—a drug that combined poison and cure. It was called “Divine Bewitchment.”","The fragrance released by Divine Bewitchment was poisonous, while consuming the pill dispelled the poison.","From the moment Xiao Rangchen opened the bottle, he had already been poisoned by Divine Bewitchment.","Now, to verify whether the pill was genuine, he had made Yue Qi take one. The remaining pill was meant for Lou Yue, leaving Yue Qi without an antidote of his own.","Divine Bewitchment was an aphrodisiac. It was called Divine Bewitchment for two reasons. First, a person felt nothing immediately after being poisoned—not even a god could detect it. Second, when it took effect, it was said to strip even a god of his usual composure, leaving him enslaved to his body’s primal desires.","By chance, Yue Qi had obtained only three pills. He had already used one in the past to spend the night with someone, and he had no more.","If Divine Bewitchment took effect and Xiao Rangchen came looking for him, Yue Qi would certainly die.","He had no one to blame but himself for being suspicious and bringing this disaster upon himself.","Yue Qi’s heart turned cold. As for the Boundary-Locking Pearl in Lou Yue’s room, since Xiao Rangchen could destroy it, there was no need for him to retrieve it himself. Escaping with his life was what mattered now.","Xiao Rangchen had no idea that he had been afflicted by the Bewitchment.","He tucked the medicine bottle close to his body and pondered how to get Lou Yue to take the antidote. Given how firmly she kept him at arm’s length, she probably wouldn’t use anything he gave her.","By the time he returned to Baichuan Hall, dusk had fallen. More than a hundred spirit lamps floated upward from below, their warm light illuminating the dim sky.","Each spirit lamp bore the words “One lifetime, one devoted pair,” all written in the same elegant hand.","Xiao Rangchen indifferently looked away and headed toward the pavilion at the very back.","Along the way, quite a few people were watching the spirit lamps, and snatches of conversation drifted past his ears from time to time.","“That guy really is blessed with women.”","“Ugh, if I’d known, I would’ve gone up there too. What a loss.”","“She’s called Lou Yue, right? No wonder even the Liufeng clan’s saintess descended to the mortal world. If it were me, I’d say yes too.”","“I heard she’s from the Lou family’s direct line, no less.”","Xiao Rangchen’s footsteps slowly came to a halt.","“Her line about ‘Would you accompany me across a thousand mountains and ten thousand rivers, and see all the fireworks of the mortal world?’ was just too... I almost shouted out loud.”","“How come I never meet a man like that? Hmph!”","“Does this mean the Lou clan is going to marry into the Liufeng clan?”","“It’s not that simple. Do you think the Liufeng clan’s saintess is some ordinary daughter of a noble family?”","“I think it’ll happen sooner or later. The hundred spirit lamps Lou Yue lit for the saintess today, every single one bearing the words ‘One lifetime, one devoted pair,’ were enough to make her feelings clear. I’d even agree to let them get married right away—”","The speaker suddenly shivered and turned around in confusion.","“What’s wrong?”","She shook her head. “I just suddenly felt cold. It’s kind of creepy. Come on, let’s go back.”","Xiao Rangchen walked past the two of them.","Though he had no desire to listen, words like “Lou Yue,” “saintess,” and “confession” continued to find their way into his ears in scattered fragments along the road.","One lifetime, one devoted pair...","Cross a thousand mountains and ten thousand rivers, and see all the fireworks of the mortal world...","Compared to her broad road and single-plank bridge, those words were even more searing and agonizing.","Suddenly, his gaze locked onto the path between the pavilions ahead.","Lou Yue had one hand resting against her forehead—Liufeng Xin’s hand. The two stood facing each other, their sleeves brushing together, their posture intimate.","Xiao Rangchen’s lips slowly pressed into a cold, rigid line.","Lou Yue hadn’t noticed him. She had set up a soundproof barrier and was chatting and laughing with Liufeng Xin.","“I think you look like some great shaman performing a ritual on television.”","Liufeng Xin erased the wound on Lou Yue’s forehead. As she withdrew her hand, she lightly flicked Lou Yue between the brows.","Lou Yue shot her an annoyed look. “Is this how you treat your benefactor?”","“Actually, I’m happy.” Liufeng Xin’s eyes blinked behind her veil. “I never expected your idea to be a confession.”","Lou Yue put on an exaggeratedly mournful expression. “Your saintess’s reputation is going to be ruined after this.”","“I’d be delighted if it were. I originally planned to run away. Hiding for as many days as I could would be fine—even dying out there would be better than returning to Langhua. But now, with you as a decoy, at least I don’t have to take the risk.”","“Hmm... If that really doesn’t work, we can elope. But we’ll have to wait a month.” That was the condition she had agreed to back when she obtained the Bu Yan Flower to save Xiao Rangchen.","“Let’s talk about it later. If we stay any longer, those two are going to burn holes through me.” Liufeng Xin gestured toward the two people standing in front of the pavilion, whose faces were nearly the same color as the grass.","“Will there be a problem?”","“Relax. They wouldn’t dare do anything to me. I’m still the saintess, after all. Though I’ll probably have to put on an affectionate family act with the clan head later.”","Lou Yue laughed at that. “Give me your message butterfly.”","She touched her message butterfly to Liufeng Xin’s. “Contact me right away if anything happens after you go back.”","“All right.”","Liufeng Xin lowered her hand and turned toward the pavilion where she was staying. Before entering, she glanced back at Lou Yue once more.","Lou Yue smiled and waved at her, her eyes carrying a reassuring calm.","Only after watching Liufeng Xin go inside did Lou Yue slowly make her way toward her own residence, planning her next steps.","She had just stepped onto the stairs leading to her floor when she stopped. Raising her head, she looked up—","Xiao Rangchen stood in the shadowed corner of the stairway, looking down at her.","Lou Yue laughed inwardly, not surprised in the least.","Last night, Xiao Rangchen had caught sight of the white moonlight he had fallen for at first sight “kissing” her, and had been so desperate to take her place that the tree reduced to dust was the best proof of it. During today’s contest, he had lost himself when he saw the split on her lips, surely assuming that the white moonlight had bitten her. And now he knew that she had confessed her feelings to his white moonlight—","He must be insanely jealous.","Jealousy was good. Jealousy meant she had the upper hand.","Neither of them had obtained their cheat abilities, so they were even.","He loved his white moonlight, but his white moonlight was intimately close with her, driving him mad with jealousy. Therefore, she had won.","Lou Yue folded her arms and lazily leaned against the white jade railing. Raising her brows, she glanced at him sidelong.","“You’re looking for me?”","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze was nailed to the corners of her lips, curved in a smile. His voice was cold and hard.","“You’re happy.”","Lou Yue nodded and admitted it openly. “I am.”","“...You really like her that much?”","“That much.”","Of course, this liking was not the same kind of liking he meant.","After a long silence, Xiao Rangchen spoke again.","“Why?”","“Why what?”","“You’ve only met her a handful of times.”","Lou Yue brushed the loose strands of hair from her face. “Some people are destined to share an extraordinary bond with you, even if you meet them only once.” As the male lead with the fate of a Long Aotian, he should have understood that better than anyone. Otherwise, why would he be standing here now, “demanding an explanation” from her?","Xiao Rangchen’s dark lashes trembled in the night breeze.","“And how do you...” He swallowed the hoarseness in his throat and paused before continuing. “How do you know the two of you aren’t bound by ill fate?”","Lou Yue countered, “And how do you know we are?”","“Perhaps we are that devoted pair,” she said.","Xiao Rangchen gave a low, mocking laugh. She and Liufeng Xin were that pair, while he was merely an unwanted nuisance in the way.","He and she were the ones bound by ill fate. That was why she had forgotten him, because—","He was irrelevant.","----------------------","I’m kind of looking forward to the next chapter. I bet you are too!!","*rubs hands together excitedly.gif*"]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24: 《)","paragraphs":["Seeing Xiao Rangchen fall silent, Lou Yue thought she shouldn’t push him too hard and risk affecting the plot later on. She rose, brushed past him, and returned to her own room, letting the subject drop.","Just as they passed each other, he suddenly spoke.","“Wait.”","Lou Yue turned halfway back. His lowered lashes were veiled in shadow, obscuring his expression. After a moment, he held out a vial of medicine.","“You’ve been poisoned. This is the antidote,” he said.","Lou Yue froze, then cried out in shock and anger, “You poisoned me?!”","“Xiao Rangchen, are you even a man?”","Xiao Rangchen abruptly lifted his eyes. “You think I would poison you.”","Lou Yue was taken aback.","“In your eyes, I’m nothing but vile and despicable.”","Lou Yue rubbed her brow. She had indeed acted impulsively just now. Ever since her cultivation had reached the Nascent Soul stage yesterday, she had occasionally been feeling restless.","It was as though something were about to break through the soil and emerge—a sense of unease mixed with an excitement that made her blood race.","And today, that feeling was even stronger. At that moment, she even felt her limbs trembling and going weak.","No—that wasn’t just a feeling. They really were weak...","Lou Yue hurriedly reached out to brace herself against the railing beside her.","And beyond the weakness, there was an indescribable...","Thinking Lou Yue’s poison was taking effect, Xiao Rangchen immediately moved to support her, only to halt just before touching her.","Lou Yue felt the world begin to spin before her eyes. She managed to stagger a few steps, then her whole body pitched downward.","No longer able to worry about Lou Yue’s aversion to him, Xiao Rangchen swept her up in his arms, pushed open the door, and carried her into the room. The door closed behind him.","“Your poison is acting up.”","He laid Lou Yue on the bed, took out the vial she had refused earlier, and poured out the pill. Its rich fragrance instantly spread through the room.","Half-supporting Lou Yue upright, he brought the pill to her lips. But Lou Yue turned her head away.","Xiao Rangchen frowned, about to speak, when Lou Yue asked slowly and breathlessly, “Where... did you get... the antidote?”","“Yue Qi. I overheard him and Cang Wu talking about drugging you.”","He added, “I tested it. He also swore a soul oath that taking this would cure you.”","Even through her haze, Lou Yue still felt that something was wrong.","“What else do you want to ask?” Xiao Rangchen asked in a low voice, pinching the pill between his fingers. To him, it seemed that Lou Yue still did not trust him.","Lou Yue tried to use her spiritual power to suppress the unfamiliar heat beginning to surge through her body, but the more she suppressed it, the more fiercely it rose. She drew a breath and did her best to keep her voice steady.","“Did he... say what kind of poison it was?”","Xiao Rangchen fell silent. After a while, he said, “I forgot to ask.”","Lou Yue: “...”","In the stillness filling the room, their uneven breathing sounded especially clear.","Lou Yue felt that if she waited any longer, Xiao Rangchen would surely notice something was amiss. Gritting her teeth, she opened her lips and took the pill from his hand into her mouth.","Her soft, damp lips brushed his fingertips—only for an instant.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his hand, his fingers curling slightly.","The pill melted the moment it entered her stomach. Lou Yue could feel that indescribable sensation gradually receding. Her body was still somewhat weak and limp, but the antidote was genuine.","The room was saturated with its fragrance, so intense it was almost pungent—and somehow familiar.","She had supposedly been poisoned, but when had it happened?","The scent of the antidote seemed to be the same as the one she had smelled on Yue Qi that morning.","Lou Yue had never touched anything Yue Qi had given her. The closest she had come to him was before yesterday’s enlightenment beneath the ancient tree, and then again this morning. There had been too many people around yesterday—the clan heads were all present—so Yue Qi would not have made a move then.","That left only this morning.","A crucial thought suddenly surfaced in Lou Yue’s gradually clearing mind. She abruptly looked up, frowning. “Where’s the pill bottle?”","Xiao Rangchen had already been leaning over her. When Lou Yue raised her head, their noses nearly brushed.","His deep, ink-dark eyes met hers, beautiful eyes reddened at the corners.","Both of them froze.","Then, one after the other, they looked away.","After a brief silence, Xiao Rangchen handed the empty pill bottle to Lou Yue.","“There was only one pill...” Lou Yue murmured distractedly.","“There were originally two. I was afraid Yue Qi had tampered with them, so I made him take one.”","The doors and windows of the room were tightly shut, and the fragrance of the pill had yet to disperse. Lou Yue’s expression darkened. “Get out.”","The pressure around Xiao Rangchen dropped as well. He withdrew the hand supporting her shoulder and straightened up.","Knowing he might have misunderstood, Lou Yue looked up at him. “Go find Yue Qi immediately. Get another pill from him and take it.”","Xiao Rangchen did not understand.","Lou Yue continued, “If I’m right, this pill is probably both an antidote and a poison. Swallowing it cures the poison; smelling it is the poison.”","“The only time I smelled this fragrance on Yue Qi was this morning.”","Xiao Rangchen did not move. After a long pause, he said, “He has probably already left Xuandu.”","“Then get out anyway,” Lou Yue snapped through gritted teeth.","Xiao Rangchen noticed something unusual about her. “You know what poison this is?”","Lou Yue did not answer. She tested the strength in her limbs; walking was no longer a problem. “If you won’t leave, then I will.”","Bracing herself against the bedframe, she got up and headed for the door.","But it would not open.","The door actually would not open?","Not only was the door sealed shut, the windows would not open either.","Lou Yue was nearly frantic. A barrier-like force had enclosed the entire room, and she could not break through it.","Her condition was not right at the moment, but she was still at the middle stage of Nascent Soul. An ordinary barrier should never have been able to trap her. She turned, intending to ask Xiao Rangchen to try, only to see that the man who had been standing ramrod straight moments ago now had one hand braced against the edge of the table, his head lowered, his expression unreadable.","...Xiao Rangchen was having an episode. The room was saturated with the scent of that pill, far stronger than what she had smelled this morning. If he lost control...","Lou Yue immediately spun back around and once more hurled her spiritual power against the barrier.","Don’t do this to me. Xiao Rangchen had been poisoned with that kind of drug—why trap her in here with him? She was a man; she couldn’t help with this at all! Heavens, let her out already!","Yet the heavens only knew how to strike her with lightning. At a critical moment like this, they were utterly useless.","Lou Yue kicked the door in frustration.","“What are you afraid of?” Xiao Rangchen’s voice came from behind her, low and hushed.","Lou Yue turned to look at him.","Xiao Rangchen still had his right hand on the table’s edge, but he had straightened up. His face appeared normal enough.","For some reason, Lou Yue let out a breath of relief. She shuffled two steps closer to him. “This room has been sealed by a barrier. Try and see if you can open it.”","Xiao Rangchen walked toward her, his steps slow and steady. Lou Yue turned her gaze aside.","He raised a hand and placed it against the door, spiritual power stirring around him.","In an instant, he recognized that the force locking this room was the very same one that had trapped him that morning.","“How is it?” Lou Yue asked from a distance that was neither too near nor too far, her gaze carefully avoiding him.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his eyes slowly. The shadows cast by his long lashes concealed whatever lay beneath them. After a long pause, he spoke, his voice carrying an inscrutable undertone.","“It won’t open.”","“...What the hell is this thing? Even you can’t open it—then how are we supposed to get out?”","Xiao Rangchen stared blankly at the hidden patterns carved into the door. “Later,” he replied. “Maybe it’ll open later.”","“Why—” Lou Yue was about to ask why it could open later but not now when a thought flashed through her mind, and she abruptly stopped herself.","Why? Obviously, because his poison was acting up. He was affected by it and couldn’t use his full strength right now. Once the effects wore off later, he would be able to.","But how exactly were the effects supposed to wear off?","Could something potent enough to affect a Nascent Soul cultivator through scent alone simply disperse on its own? Obviously not.","Then how would it wear off?","Damn it, brain, stop thinking! She did not want to know!","Without drawing attention to herself, she edged toward the window, putting a safe amount of distance between herself and Xiao Rangchen.","“...How are you?”","From the corner of his eye, Xiao Rangchen glanced at Lou Yue, who was so deliberately keeping her distance. His Adam’s apple bobbed once before he answered slowly, “I can still hold on.”","No lamp had been lit in the room. Only a hazy wash of moonlight filtered through the lattice window.","By the time Lou Yue had counted three hundred and twenty-nine patterns on the window lattice—each curved at roughly thirty to forty-five degrees, joined by one hundred and forty cloud motifs, each cloud motif dotted with twenty tiny specks—Xiao Rangchen spoke again.","“Could you...”","Lou Yue’s heart immediately leapt into her throat. Could she what?","“Say something.”","Lou Yue instantly relaxed and turned to look at him.","He sat leaning against the door, one leg drawn up, one hand resting casually over his knee. He was far from the window, where the light was dimmer, and she could not make out his expression clearly. But his voice sounded noticeably lower than before.","Lou Yue straightened slightly, her throat tight. “What do you want me to say?”","“Anything.” After a pause, he added, “As long as it can distract me.”","...Understandable. But being asked to talk out of nowhere, she couldn’t think of a single topic. She couldn’t exactly chat with him about his white moonlight. Things were already strange enough; if she brought up something even stranger, what if he did something strange too?","Even if she was currently a man, men could be in danger too. Especially when he had a record.","Lou Yue racked her brains for a long while, yet still had no idea what to say.","“How about... I play you something?” Earlier, she had discovered a konghou and a flute in the original owner’s storage ring. She had practiced both for more than ten years in her previous life. Though these instruments differed slightly in form, she should be able to manage them easily enough.","Xiao Rangchen did not refuse, so Lou Yue chose the more soothing konghou over the flute.","The konghou, fashioned from violet jade, curved like a crescent moon and resembled a perching phoenix. Its white strings gleamed softly, delicate and elegant.","She simply sat down against the window as well. After plucking a few notes to test the strings, she gently gathered and brushed them with both hands. The clear, winding melody of “The Mountain Spirit” flowed slowly from beneath her fingers, carrying the distant, tranquil spirit of the wilderness as it spread through the room.","Silvery moonlight draped itself around Lou Yue. Her lashes were lowered, her gaze intent.","Xiao Rangchen tilted his head back slightly against the cold door, concealing the longing in his eyes as he stared, unblinkingly, at the figure by the window.","Xiao Rangchen did not tell her to stop, so Lou Yue continued playing. Then, amid the gentle music she played for herself, she successfully lulled herself to sleep.","The position was awkward, and her sleep was restless; she only dozed for a short while.","Yet when she opened her eyes, she found herself staring straight into a pair of dark eyes at close range. The coldness had long since vanished from their depths, replaced by a surging, impenetrable darkness that reflected her image.","Lou Yue’s heart jolted in shock. The konghou slipped from her arms, and she hurriedly reached to catch it. Just as her fingers touched the instrument, a broad hand covered hers.","They both froze.","Xiao Rangchen’s palm was scorching hot, and the heat seeped continuously into her skin, leaving her fingertips numb.","Lou Yue swiftly put the konghou away in her storage ring, then jerked her hand back and rose to her feet. Xiao Rangchen slowly stood as well, his tall, slender figure instantly filling her entire field of vision.","The rich scent of medicine mingled with the crisp, clean fragrance of his body and wrapped around her like a net.","Lou Yue instinctively tried to move around him to the right, but the moment she did, he seized her right wrist.","Xiao Rangchen bent down toward her bit by bit. Without touching her, he braced one hand against the window frame to her left, resting his forehead against it as well.","His scorching breath spread along the side of her neck, searing her skin inch by inch.","Lou Yue did not dare move. She barely even breathed.","“I think... I can’t hold on much longer...” he murmured hoarsely.","Lou Yue decided that the heat from his body must have passed into hers. Otherwise, why did she feel so hot too?","All she could hear was his heavy breathing, accompanied by one or two suppressed swallows.","He seemed to turn his face slightly toward her. Lou Yue felt his burning breath strike the side of her neck, his breathing growing heavier and heavier.","“What should I do...” he asked again, his voice low, hoarse, and broken, carrying a trace of barely perceptible pleading. The fingers gripping her wrist tightened as well.","Lou Yue immediately tried to escape. Spiritual power surged through her, but a stronger force instantly suppressed it at her wrist. He twisted her hand back and pinned it against the window frame. In the movement, something soft and searingly hot suddenly pressed against the side of her neck.","Lou Yue went completely rigid.","Xiao Rangchen remained motionless as well.","After a moment, that soft warmth slowly moved downward, brushing over the pulse at the side of her neck.","Lou Yue could no longer hold herself back. She raised her foot and kicked, her left hand rising at the same time.","Xiao Rangchen did not move his head. Instead, spiritual power surged through his knee as he pressed it against both her legs, while his other hand caught her left wrist and pinned it against the window frame too. He trapped her in the narrow space between himself and the window.","Lou Yue still refused to give up. As a mid-stage Nascent Soul cultivator, she should have been stronger than him, who was only at the early stage. Even though his body, tempered through physical cultivation, was far more powerful, and the drug was affecting him, she should not have been completely without a chance.","Yet the spiritual power restraining her grew stronger and stronger, far surpassing her own.","Xiao Rangchen had concealed his true strength!","The lips at the side of her neck shifted to another spot, and her entire neck seemed to catch fire.","“Xiao Rangchen... I’m a man...” she reminded the disoriented man in a trembling voice.","His lips paused for a moment, then continued wandering along her neck.","“Xiao Rangchen, wake up!”","This time, they did not pause at all.","He seemed to be either giving up entirely or no longer in his right mind. Completely disregarding the fact that she was a man, he kissed her with growing force and abandon, moving from left to right before returning to linger delicately at her throat.","“...Xiao Rangchen,” Lou Yue said, her voice trembling. “Can you please come to your senses...?”","“Look carefully—I’m a man. A man!”","“Xiao Rangchen, how can you do this to Liufeng Xin?!”","The moment Liufeng Xin’s name was spoken, the person buried against her neck finally stilled.","Seizing the chance, Lou Yue hurried on. “Liufeng Xin would be heartbroken if she knew.”","“She’s beautiful and pure, gentle and—”","Xiao Rangchen lifted his head, and Lou Yue’s voice abruptly died away.","Desire surged in those dark eyes, saturated with possessiveness. The sharp corners of his eyes brimmed with aggression as he fixed her with the unrelenting stare of a beast that had locked onto its prey.","Nervously, she licked her lips without thinking. His gaze clung to them at once.","Alarm bells blared in Lou Yue’s mind. She immediately pressed her lips tightly together and stiffened, flattening herself against the window behind her.","“Gentle and what?” Xiao Rangchen suddenly asked, his husky, scorching breath brushing across her face.","Lou Yue hesitated. After waiting a moment, deciding she might have been overthinking things, she slowly parted her lips. “Gentle and considerate...”","He gave a soft hum, as though encouraging her to continue.","Forcing herself to recite the image of the white moonlight from the book, Lou Yue said, “Don’t be fooled by how aloof she seems. She’s actually adorable and understanding. She’s truly wonderful—no one else could possibly compare to her, mmm—”","Xiao Rangchen kissed her hard.","Lou Yue turned her head to avoid him, but his warm, damp lips pursued her relentlessly.","“Xiao—mmph—”","Lou Yue struggled with all her strength. Xiao Rangchen seized both her wrists and pinned them above her head with one hand. With his free right hand, he reached behind her head and held her firmly, leaving her nowhere to run.","Their lips and teeth rubbed together, again and again.","His tongue slipped inside. Lou Yue bit down viciously—she missed, but the threat was clear enough.","Yet while she defended the inside, she could only surrender the outside in humiliation, letting him ravage it as he pleased.","She hoped that, having conceded this much territory, Xiao Rangchen would refrain from pushing further and becoming even more excessive.","Instead, he bit down on her lip.","He swept away the blood, and his burning lips descended again—forceful, urgent.","After a long while, he was no longer satisfied with merely kissing her. The hand at the back of her head slowly slid down to her shoulder blade. It lingered there for a moment, then traced the line of her spine to her waist, cupping her lower back and drawing her into his arms.","“Mm—mmph—”","Lou Yue twisted her head away with all her might. “Xiao—Xiao Rangchen, don’t—don’t go too far!”","Under the moonlight, Lou Yue’s face was flushed crimson, from the tips of her ears to her jaw. Her skin glowed with a dewy sheen; her lips were red and swollen from his bite, glistening with moisture, while every breath trembled with a soft, unsteady sound.","Xiao Rangchen’s Adam’s apple bobbed heavily. The impulse within him was nearly breaking through the last of his restraint. Like drinking poison to quench his thirst, he could no longer suppress the urge to take her apart and consume her whole.","He slowly lowered his eyes. Then, with a sudden forceful movement, he turned Lou Yue around so that her back faced him.","“Xiao Rangchen!!” Lou Yue cried out in alarm, her entire body going rigid.","“I won’t touch you...”","Behind her, Xiao Rangchen let out a ragged, scorching breath. “Don’t move... and don’t turn around.”","With that, he released the hand that had been restraining her, took several steps back, and leaned against the table.","Facing the window, Lou Yue listened to his footsteps. Only then did the heart lodged in her throat slowly settle.","Xiao Rangchen gazed silently at the obedient figure standing by the window. His eyes traveled greedily from the pale nape of her neck to the delicate line of her shoulder blades. Even through layers of clothing, their subtle curves were still discernible...","The silence behind her was terrifying. Lou Yue clenched her fists, a shiver creeping up her spine.","She wanted to ask what he was doing, yet some instinct told her she must not.","Holding her breath, she strained her ears for a long while. At last, she heard a faint sound.","She thought she must have misheard. Otherwise, why would there be the sound of something wet...","Lou Yue suddenly went rigid, wishing she could cover her ears at once.","Xiao Rangchen was actually...","Damn it. She wanted to smash her head straight into the window!","Heat surged from behind her ears down her back. Her entire body felt like a red-hot iron bar, standing there stiff as a ramrod.","She didn’t dare move, afraid that interrupting him would bring disaster down on her.","She had no idea how much time had passed before she heard the man let out a muffled groan, his voice low and sensual. She thought it was over.","It wasn’t.","That had only been the beginning...","By the time dawn gradually replaced the moonlight, Lou Yue’s eyes had gone blank.","She had actually stood there all night, listening to Xiao Rangchen doing... that.","Several times, she had wanted to sit down. But whenever she remembered what the other person in the room was doing, she immediately forced herself upright again, repeatedly circulating her spiritual energy to soothe away the stiffness and aches.","“...Shall we go?”","Xiao Rangchen asked softly from behind her. His voice was clear and composed, without a trace of the huskiness from the night before.","Lou Yue turned around woodenly. He had already changed into a fresh set of clothes, his features bright and calm, his aura serene.","The complete opposite of her.","It was as though she were the one who had been tormented all night.","She lifted a foot to leave, but her body pitched forward. After standing rigidly through the entire night, even with spiritual energy supporting her, she still felt somewhat uncomfortable.","As Xiao Rangchen reached out to steady her, she braced herself against the windowsill, avoiding his hand.","His hand froze in midair before slowly withdrawing.","Once she had recovered a little, Lou Yue straightened her back and walked past him toward the door without looking aside.","Xiao Rangchen glanced at her lowered lashes. After a brief pause, he stepped forward, pressed both hands to the door, and poured spiritual energy into it. With several sharp cracks, the barrier sealing the room shattered.","Lou Yue pushed open the door and rushed out without looking back, vanishing from sight in an instant.","Xiao Rangchen turned to look toward the window.","She would not be returning here again.","After a long while, he withdrew his gaze. As he turned around, he halted at the sight of a patch of emerald green at the edge of the bed.","Lou Yue found the Lou family members and arranged for new accommodations. Perhaps because they knew who she was, they took her directly to a private courtyard, complete with a hot spring pool.","Once inside, she removed her outer robes and plunged headfirst into the warm water.","By the end, that room had been filled with Xiao Rangchen’s scent. Even she had been tainted by it.","“Bastard...”","She took out a mirror and looked at herself.","There was no longer much to see on either side of her neck. Only a faint red mark remained at her throat—hardly noticeable unless one looked closely. But her lips were another matter.","Once soft and moist, they now looked as though they had ripened to fullness, swollen and plump. A fresh bite mark overlapped the small wound already there, making it especially conspicuous.","Lou Yue flung aside the mirror, formed a block of ice from water, wrapped it in spiritual energy, and pressed it against her swollen lips.","Before long, she angrily smashed the ice in her hand. “Scumbag!”","What did he take her for? A tool for venting his urges?","His heart was occupied by his white moonlight—he was thinking about another woman—yet he had come to kiss her. Classic scumbag behavior.","Yes, he had been drugged, but if he could take care of it himself, why had he kissed her?","He had merely revealed his true nature as a shameless womanizer.","The more she thought about it, the more aggrieved she felt. The worst part was that there was no way for her to get even.","Lou Yue plunged back into the water, only to sense a disturbance from within her storage ring.","She lifted her hand. A messenger butterfly fluttered out and landed before her, and a deep yet rather unserious voice rang out:","“Dear son, miss your old man?”","Lou Yue’s temple twitched. Then the voice on the other end called out again, “Anyone there? Is this stupid butterfly broken again? Son? Son?”","“Lou Yue!!!”","The sudden roar was deafening. Lou Yue replied irritably, “I’m listening.”","“If you’re listening, why aren’t you saying anything? Stop messing with your own father, will you? It wasn’t easy for me to raise you—I fed you, clothed you, wiped your ass! Old Zhang next door has such a thoughtful daughter. She either brings her father washwater for his feet or does the laundry and cooking. But you? The moment your wings hardened, you patted your butt and left, abandoning your father in this backwater place to guard a pile of mountains. And you never even contact me on your own!”","Lou Yue dug at her ear, her tone cool. “You sound full of energy. Clearly, you’ve been doing just fine without me.”","“How could that possibly be the same?” Lou Chengfeng’s voice rose. “The old man’s birthday celebration is about over anyway. Come back early. Your father misses you!”","“I agreed to attend tomorrow’s family banquet. I still have to remain in Xuandu for another month.”","“Did the old man force you?”","Lou Yue denied it. “It was a condition in exchange for retrieving something earlier.”","Lou Chengfeng fell silent for a moment, then said, “You don’t need to pay attention to whatever they say at the family banquet. That bunch has been throwing their weight around for so long that everything out of their mouths sounds like shit. Once this is over, come back for a visit.”","His serious tone lasted less than two seconds before turning unserious again. “Your dad really misses you.”","“We’ll see.”","“Stop fobbing me off with that! Get back here already!”","“I’m going to cultivate.” Lou Yue prepared to end the call.","“Cultivate what? I already told you, high cultivation doesn’t amount to much. You’ve got so many magical artifacts sitting around gathering dust! Listen to your dad—no need to cultivate. Go out and have some fun. Chat with some young ladies, that’d be good too. If you’re short on spirit stones, I’ll go dig a few baskets out of the mountains and find someone to send them over. Buy some fun things, or get gifts to make people happy. Cultivation is so boring—dull! I don’t cultivate anymore these days. Learn from your old man!”","“I’m at the middle stage of Nascent Soul.” Lou Yue said blandly.","The other end went dead silent for a long while, followed by the sound of something being knocked over.","“What? You’re at the middle stage of Nascent Soul?!”","Lou Yue pushed the messenger butterfly farther away, rubbed her ear, and calmly hummed in confirmation.","“How is that possible? Why did your cultivation advance so quickly all of a sudden? You didn’t take some shady, unorthodox pills, did you?”","“Your son is naturally gifted. Is that so hard to believe?”","“Fine, of course you can. Isn’t your father just worried about you?” Lou Chengfeng sounded distracted. “Is Xuanba with you? Why isn’t it responding when I try to contact it? Has it learned from you to ignore messages too? It’s getting awfully bold.”","Lou Yue froze when she heard Lou Chengfeng call out the name “Xuanba” so directly.","So Xuanba’s original name had been Xuanba?","A vague thought suddenly flashed through her mind, too quick to grasp. She frowned slightly and replied, “It’s gone into hibernation.”","“...Why would it hibernate out of the blue? Son, why do I have such a bad feeling about this...” Lou Chengfeng fixated on that point. “Why is Xuanba hibernating? How long has it been?”","“Maybe it’s old and wants a good night’s sleep?”","Lou Chengfeng: “...”","“Your son wants a good night’s sleep too.” With that, Lou Yue cut off the transmission.","Before she could put away the communication butterfly, it lit up again. She didn’t need to guess to know it was Lou Chengfeng. She ignored it, and a moment later, a written message came through.","Lou Yue stared blankly at the two words floating in midair:","Return immediately.","That feeling of unease, agitation, and racing blood was back.","There had to be some secret she didn’t know.","And Xuanba and Lou Chengfeng both knew it.","She couldn’t think of an answer. Every guess seemed hazy and far-fetched.","With a sigh, she decided to let it go. What she needed now was a comfortable night’s sleep to relax her mind. Maybe she was simply overtired and having heart palpitations, just like when she used to pull several all-nighters in a row.","But this sleep was far from restful.","She had a dream.","In the dream, she became a snow-white lop-eared rabbit with soft fur. By accident, she fell into a pit a hunter had dug to trap animals. The fall didn’t hurt; she landed on top of a gray wolf that had fallen into the trap before her.","The wolf was enormous. Its grayish coat was smeared with patchy blood, and it looked badly injured.","It lifted its eyelids and glanced at her, its expression casual, yet somehow as if everything were firmly under its control.","She hopped away, trying to put some distance between them so it wouldn’t decide to make a meal of her. But after only two hops, a gray paw pressed down on her back and pinned her flat to the ground.","Her hind legs kicked like spinning wheels, but she couldn’t escape. The gray wolf lowered its head and sniffed her lightly, then bit down on the back of her neck.","She thought she was about to die. Instead, the wolf merely carried her to the front of its body. Its damp nose flipped her over, and then it lowered its heavy neck onto her soft belly and closed its eyes to rest.","She lay rigid, too frightened to move, afraid the wolf would suddenly change its mind and decide it would be easier just to eat her.","She endured it until she woke.","Lou Yue opened her eyes and stared at the canopy overhead. Irritated, she turned onto her side and kicked the blanket away.","What kind of ridiculous dream was that? Why had she turned into a rabbit—an utterly defenseless lop-eared rabbit, at that? Even if she had to become an animal, she should have been a lion: powerful, imposing, and awe-inspiring!","She had no desire to go back to sleep. After spacing out for a while, she took out her communication butterfly and contacted Liufeng Xin to see whether anything had happened on her end.","Liufeng Xin did not respond. Later, Lou Yue received a written message from her, asking to meet at dusk in the same woods as last time.","Lou Yue arrived half an hour early and sat on the same tree branch as before, watching the sun sink toward the horizon.","Xuantiandu hovered in the sky, its unshielded rosy light spilling across the ground. The scenery was indeed beautiful, but lately Lou Yue had been plagued by palpitations. She could not settle her mind, let alone appreciate the view. She shifted through countless positions on the tree branch, yet none felt comfortable.","Liufeng Xin was late. Worried that something might have happened, Lou Yue was about to head for Baichuan Hall when Liufeng Xin finally arrived.","Before she had even come close, she was already waggling her brows at Lou Yue.","Lou Yue said nothing. Only when Liufeng Xin reached her did she hear her whisper, “Long Aotian is following me. He’s right behind me!”","Lou Yue pressed her lips together.","“He’s been tailing me ever since I left Baichuan Hall. I couldn’t shake him off. I was afraid you’d keep waiting, so I brought him here anyway. I have a feeling his real goal isn’t me...”","“Ah!” Liufeng Xin looked at her. “He’s noticed something strange about the fireflies! What do we do? Should we change locations?”","Before she had finished speaking, Xiao Rangchen stepped out on his own.","His gaze was fixed squarely on Lou Yue as he approached, one step at a time.","“We need to talk.” He stopped in front of her.","Behind her veil, Liufeng Xin’s eyes darted back and forth between them. Lou Yue found it impossible to ignore the avid, gossip-hungry look on her face.","She had no idea what Xiao Rangchen wanted, but she knew one thing: she did not want to see him right now, much less talk to him.","She lifted her eyes coldly. “We have nothing to talk about.”","As she spoke, she reached for Liufeng Xin’s hand—just as Xiao Rangchen’s hand closed around her wrist.","Liufeng Xin was ecstatic inside. She had never imagined that one day she would become the star of a melodramatic “you hold my hand, he holds yours” scene—and with the very couple she shipped, no less. She felt she could die without regrets in the next moment.","“Lou Yue.”","Xiao Rangchen’s voice was low, his tone stubborn. “Talk to me.”","His grip on her wrist was not light. Xiao Rangchen was using force, apparently determined to get his way even if he had to resort to martial means.","Lou Yue refused to indulge him. If she did not want to talk, then she did not want to talk. She turned to Liufeng Xin and gave her a meaningful look, signaling for her to say something. She did not believe Xiao Rangchen would refuse to listen to his white moonlight.","Xiao Rangchen turned to look at Liufeng Xin as well.","On one side was Liufeng Xin’s familiar, urging look; on the other was an equally familiar coldness and rejection, as though he wanted to stab her to death. Under the gaze of the couple she shipped, Liufeng Xin’s heart trembled.","Putting on an aloof expression, she said, “You two talk.”","Under Lou Yue’s astonished stare—which clearly said, “You betrayed our revolutionary friendship?”—Liufeng Xin slowly pried Lou Yue’s hand from hers. Before leaving, she even gave them both a cool smile that said, “I absolutely won’t disturb you.”","“...” Lou Yue watched helplessly as her ally defected, then walked some distance away and turned her back on her.","Xiao Rangchen stepped in front of Lou Yue, blocking her view of Liufeng Xin.","Lou Yue yanked her wrist back, murder in her eyes. Was he satisfied now?","Xiao Rangchen fell silent for a moment. Then he looked at her and began slowly, “Last night—”","He still dared to mention last night? Lou Yue clenched her fist. If he said one thing she did not want to hear, she would punch him.","“There’s something I’ve wanted to tell you for a long time.”","What was it? Go on, say it. If he had the nerve, she would let him taste her fist.","“I like you.”","Mm, you like... what?!?! Lou Yue’s mind went blank.","“But in those circumstances, saying it would have seemed like I was trying to deceive you.”","Lou Yue felt that she could no longer understand what he was saying.","“I want you to know this.”","“I’ve said what I came to say.” Xiao Rangchen took two steps back and looked at her. His eyes were unfathomably deep, his emotions dark and unreadable.","His lips moved, but in the end, he said nothing more. He turned and left. Even after his figure vanished from sight, he never looked back.","Liufeng Xin leaned in front of her curiously. “That was quick. You two finished talking already?”","Lou Yue looked at her expressionlessly. “I didn’t say a single word. What kind of talk was that?”","“Huh? Then what did he say?”","He said he liked her. How could that possibly be true?","No. Impossible! She refused to believe it.","She was a man now. Was Long Aotian suddenly into men?","Even taking ten thousand steps back, if he really liked her, shouldn’t he at least care what she had to say? Shouldn’t he want to know whether there was any hope? But he hadn’t cared about her answer at all.","He didn’t like her at all. He was getting back at her.","He wanted her to keep guessing, to lose sleep and appetite over it.","Damn. What a vicious scheme!","“Girl, your eyes are practically breathing fire. What did he say to make you this mad?”","Lou Yue gritted her teeth. “He cursed me.”","“Huh?” Liufeng Xin looked utterly baffled.","“I was too naïve.” Lou Yue ground her molars. “Xiao Rangchen isn’t just scum—he’s dark-hearted too.”","“What exactly did he say? I’m dying of curiosity!”","Lou Yue took a deep breath and rattled it off in one breath. “He said he likes me, but how could that possibly be true?”","“Aah!!”","Liufeng Xin started squealing before she had even heard the second half. Covering her mouth, she bounced on the spot. “Ah! My ship is real! Oh my god...!”","“...”","“Girl, I’m so moved, sob...”","“...”","Liufeng Xin used her sheer veil to dab at the corners of her eyes. “I’m so happy today. I’ve decided I’ll remember this day forever.”","“I said, ‘How could that possibly be true?’ Can’t you listen to the whole thing?” Lou Yue said, speechless.","“Oh, but I think it’s totally possible.” Liufeng Xin thumped her chest. “Girl, if I were a man, I’d like you too. Seriously!”","Lou Yue reminded her through gritted teeth, “I am a man right now.”","“Man or woman, who cares? True love knows no gender!” Liufeng Xin had already sunk back into her own fantasies.","Lou Yue thought she had gone crazy—and that arguing with her about it made Lou Yue no more normal.","“Didn’t you say your family wants you back in Langhua?”","Liufeng Xin’s face immediately fell. Looking miserable, she said, “Girl, do you really have to do this to me?”","“I’m telling you to stop daydreaming.”","“You just can’t stand seeing my CP have a happy ending.”","Lou Yue sighed helplessly. “Don’t ship heresy. It’s doomed to crash and burn.”","Liufeng Xin put on a solemn expression. “My intuition tells me it’s real this time.”","Seeing the conversation veering off-topic again, Lou Yue sighed. “If we don’t talk business now, it’ll be too late.”","“Fine.” Liufeng Xin pulled Lou Yue up onto a tree branch, and they sat side by side. “The family head found out about what we did afterward and flew into a rage. He ordered me to return to Langhua by tomorrow morning.”","Mischief gleamed in Liufeng Xin’s eyes. “Does that ‘eloping’ thing you mentioned yesterday still count?”","Lou Yue nodded. “Of course. What do you have in mind?”","Liufeng Xin leaned closer and laid out her plan...","It was only when Xiao Rangchen was nearly out of the woods that he gradually slowed to a stop.","Without looking back, he merely raised a hand and braced it against the tree trunk beside him.","Suddenly, his sharply defined knuckles clenched tight, blue veins standing out across the back of his hand.","Yu Youchun’s voice came through the ear cuff on his right ear. “You’re not going to tell her you’re leaving?”","A few hours ago, Yu Youchun had only just let Xiao Rangchen know that he had hidden himself in his ear cuff after leaving Que Yunsheng. But compared with that, Xiao Rangchen was more bothered by the fact that Yu Youchun had seen something he shouldn’t have.","“Fine, I admit I peeked at first. But when you kissed her, I shut off all five senses. I absolutely didn’t see anything I shouldn’t have. I may have been dead for many years, but I still know the rule: what is improper to look at, one must not look at.”","“Still, I have to say, your way of making your feelings known was far too casual. You should at least have listened to what she had to say. Honestly, are you just playing with her?”","Xiao Rangchen gazed at the drifting clouds on the horizon. After a long while, he finally relaxed his clenched hand and spoke in an even voice. “I know what she would say.”","“I don’t need her answer. I only want her to toss and turn at night, unable to forget me.”","He had originally intended to leave during the day, yet he still couldn’t bring himself to go. As she had said, the road ahead of him was fraught with danger. Whether he would survive was unknown.","Once he left, he had no idea how long it would be before he saw her again—or whether he would still be alive to see her at all.","He wanted Lou Yue to know that he liked her.","He wanted Lou Yue to remember him.","She didn’t have to believe him.","But she absolutely could not forget him again."]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["Late into the night, Lou Yue tossed and turned in bed.","She rolled from her left side to her right, then back onto her back.","—There’s something I’ve wanted to tell you since last night.","—But given the circumstances, saying it now would sound like I was just trying to placate you.","—I like you.","“...”","She bit her lip, sparks of fury flashing in her eyes.","Xiao Rangchen had absolutely done it on purpose.","What did he mean, saying he liked her? It was all a lie. She didn’t believe a single word of it!","She abruptly sat up, deciding to meditate and sweep the “trash” from her mind.","A quarter of an hour later, she collapsed back onto the bed and stared blankly at the canopy.","What exactly did Xiao Rangchen mean?","If he was jealous of her and Liufeng Xin and had deliberately said it to make his beloved moonlight jealous, then he should have said it in front of Liufeng Xin. But in reality, Liufeng Xin hadn’t heard him at all.","Lou Yue ground her back teeth together. So he was definitely still messing with her, taking revenge on her and making sure she couldn’t eat or sleep in peace.","He wanted her to think of those words every time she was with Liufeng Xin, just to irritate her.","Lou Yue slapped the bed hard—","Tomorrow, she would definitely find him and make him admit that he had only been toying with her.","The family banquet was at noon. Once it ended, she would settle this matter with him!","The next day, the sun was already high in the sky, its rays shining straight onto Lou Yue’s face. She rolled over and half lay on her stomach to escape the light.","Something swayed beneath her loose, empty clothing.","In a daze, Lou Yue thought, Oh. I slept without wearing anything underneath. Of course it’s going to sway.","The next second, she jolted awake and looked down.","Because she was lying on her side and her clothes hung so loosely, the soft flesh at her chest had been pressed together, revealing a sliver of pale skin.","“?!”","She closed her eyes, then opened them again. The rise and fall was still there.","Slowly, she reached out and pressed her hand to her chest, giving it a squeeze. The sensation was real.","Lou Yue’s eyes widened. She immediately sat up and tried to pull open her clothes for a closer look, but at that moment, she met Xuanba’s gaze from the head of the bed.","She let go, grabbed Xuanba, and knocked it from side to side. Its shell was hard, solid, and in excellent condition.","She sighed. “You’ve finally woken up...”","“I was only asleep for a few days.” Xuanba still wore the same cold expression, as though someone owed it eight hundred taels of silver. “Did you cause trouble and rush to call on me?”","“I’m not that kind of person.”","Xuanba cast her a sidelong glance with its scarlet eyes. “You are.”","Lou Yue couldn’t be bothered to argue with it. Remembering the matter that still needed to be verified, she tossed Xuanba aside and reached over to feel her chest.","But her breasts had returned to their usual flatness. She pressed here and there, yet couldn’t find even the slightest swell.","“??”","She turned and glared at Xuanba. “Did you just see my breasts?”","Xuanba: “...”","“I touched them just now. They didn’t feel fake.”","“I saw them last time too. I thought I was seeing things.”","Lou Yue’s mind raced, and her heartbeat sped up. “Do you think it’s possible that... I’m actually a woman?”","She looked over anxiously. Xuanba’s eyes remained utterly calm, without a ripple.","“You’re supposed to say something,” Lou Yue said.","Xuanba slowly crawled onto the windowsill and glanced outside before saying, “You should leave the Xuantiandu as soon as possible.”","“Why?”","Xuanba looked at her calmly. The human and the turtle stared at each other.","Then Lou Yue watched as Xuanba set up a barrier. A message butterfly flew out from its body, its faint light flickering as it connected to the other end. Before long, Lou Chengfeng’s voice rang out from it.","“She’s awake?”","“Xuanba, you only enter tortoise-breathing when your power has been completely exhausted. What did you do?”","Lou Chengfeng’s voice had none of yesterday’s frivolity. It was as cold and sharp as an ice blade.","“With Wuxiang in place, she couldn’t possibly advance to the Nascent Soul stage! Xuanba, what have you been hiding from me?”","Lou Chengfeng was furious.","“You’re harming her! Have you forgotten what you promised Jing He?!”","“I haven’t forgotten,” Xuanba replied evenly.","“Haven’t forgotten? Heh.” A tremendous crash suddenly came from the other end, as though some object had exploded. Then Lou Chengfeng roared, “Did you remove Wuxiang?!”","Xuanba fell silent.","“Just as I thought...” Lou Chengfeng’s voice turned icy, each word cutting like a blade. “Xuanba, you’re signing her death warrant.”","Xuanba’s voice remained calm. “Have you ever considered that perhaps she doesn’t want to follow the path we arranged for her?”","“This was decided the moment she was born!”","“But no one ever asked her.”","There was a moment of silence on the other end, followed by a derisive laugh.","“With a choice, do you think I’d want my own daughter to live as a man? Would I suppress her talent and let her live an ordinary life forever?”","“When she was five, she looked up at me and asked why she couldn’t sense the spiritual energy everyone else talked about, and whether that meant she had no spiritual veins. I lied and told her that cultivation was too difficult, and that it would be better to remain a mortal.”","“She said she wasn’t afraid of hardship and asked whether there was any way. I told her all the advantages of not cultivating. She understood what I hadn’t said aloud and never asked me again.”","“Then, one night when she was eight, she suddenly ran in, brimming with excitement, and told me she could sense spiritual energy. That was when I realized that for those three years, she had still been meditating every day like the other children, even though she couldn’t sense a thing...”","“Do you think I wanted this? If there had been any choice...” Lou Chengfeng choked up.","“All I wanted was for her to be happy. It didn’t matter if she was carefree and foolish, or if she lived an ordinary life.”","His tone suddenly turned fierce.","“But now that you’ve undone Wuxiang, all the suffering she endured over the years will have been for nothing! You—”","“It was me who asked it to,” Lou Yue suddenly said.","The message butterfly fell instantly silent.","“What exactly is Wuxiang?” she asked.","“...”","After a long, awkward silence, Lou Chengfeng suddenly shouted, “Xuanba, you damn—*#¥%!”","Once he had finished cursing, Lou Yue folded her arms and leaned against the headboard. She raised an eyebrow and gave a cold laugh.","“Go on. I’m listening.”","Lou Chengfeng faltered. “Son, actually...”","“Actually what?”","“...”","He couldn’t think of any way to patch things up.","“You’re still planning to keep hiding it from me even now? Are you waiting until I’m dead so you can weep and confess your regrets at my grave?” Lou Yue asked coolly.","“Bah, bah! Don’t say things like that!”","Lou Yue said nothing, simply waiting for him to come clean.","Neither father nor daughter was willing to back down, and they remained locked in a stalemate. Finally, Xuanba interrupted.","“I merged half of my core into the Wuxiang secret pattern. For now, they still won’t notice.”","It glanced at Lou Yue’s chest and added, “As long as she doesn’t reveal her feminine appearance.”","Lou Chengfeng said, “Why didn’t you discuss something this serious with me?”","“You would have agreed?” Lou Yue snorted. “You might as well have kept the secret for the rest of your life and never told me.”","“Wuxiang is an ancient secret technique. It can conceal one’s true appearance so completely that no one can see through it, but it also suppresses one’s perception and absorption of spiritual energy from the outside,” Xuanba explained. “The reason I sent you to find the Land of the Five Elements last time was so that, after undoing it, it could still be maintained for a while.”","“What do you mean by half your core?”","“Wuxiang requires an enormous amount of spiritual power to maintain. I gave you half of my core, so you can rely on it to keep the technique running.”","Lou Yue stared at its palm-sized body. “When you say ‘merged it,’ you mean it’s gone?”","Xuanba gave a calm “Mm,” as though the thing that had disappeared hadn’t been its core at all.","Lou Yue knew that an inner core was just as important to a beast as a golden core was to a human. Losing half of it meant that Xuanba’s cultivation would be frozen forever.","She had never expected that regaining her senses would come at the cost of Xuanba’s future.","“It’s nothing.” Xuanba looked at Lou Yue calmly.","Lou Yue’s long lashes lowered slightly. “Aren’t you afraid all this will be in vain, and that you’ll have wasted half your inner core?”","“I’m looking forward to seeing you make it so that ‘no one will even dare covet you in their dreams.’” His usually flat voice held a trace of gentleness.","From the other end, Lou Chengfeng felt a pang of jealousy and interrupted them. “Forget this ridiculous family banquet. Leave Xuandu immediately, before the old man notices something’s wrong.”","“Why do I have to pretend to be a man? What does it matter if he notices?” She knew that the Lou family bloodline passed down the gift of perception, but what did that have to do with gender?","“Son, I’ll tell you straight. The women of the Lou family possess the power of a furnace cauldron. From birth, they’re destined to marry the men of the clan, help them cultivate, and bear their descendants. We didn’t want you to take that path, so we had you disguise yourself as a man. If the old man finds out, he won’t just stop you from leaving—he’ll force you to marry. That’s why you must leave at once.”","Lou Yue looked at Xuanba. “Is that all?”","Lou Chengfeng assumed she was asking him and immediately replied, “Son, at a time like this, how could your father possibly lie to you?”","Xuanba remained silent for a long while before finally giving a quiet “Mm.”","Lou Yue instinctively sensed that they were still hiding something from her, but she couldn’t grasp what it was.","“Son, once you reach the peak of the Nascent Soul stage, don’t use ‘Heaven and Earth Manifestation.’ It’ll expose your true appearance. Your father really would like to live a few more years. After the fright you gave me today, who knows how many I have left...”","His endless stream of warnings was cut short when Xuanba severed the communication.","“Don’t put too much pressure on yourself. Just be who you are.” As Lou Yue’s contracted beast, Xuanba could more or less sense her emotions.","“I’ll go to the family banquet with you.”","Lou Yue nodded. As she rose from the bed, she asked as if making casual conversation, “You’ve always been called ‘Xuanba,’ haven’t you?”","Xuanba gave a quiet hum.","“Your father wasn’t lying to you. It’s only that your furnace-cauldron power is more effective than other women’s.”","“Don’t overthink it. Don’t let it become a shackle.”","**","It was called a family banquet, but there were actually more than a hundred people present.","The seating had been arranged in advance. Lou Yue was led to the third seat on the right side of the main table, directly opposite Lou Weixiao.","Her arrival drew plenty of attention and discussion, but since she was merely there to go through the motions, she didn’t care. At first, some people came over under the guise of concern, though they were really trying to sound her out. After Lou Yue gave them a sharp tongue-lashing, no one approached her again.","Bored, Lou Yue counted down the time while her thoughts ran in every direction.","Although Xuanba and Lou Chengfeng seemed to be hiding something else from her, the fact that she wasn’t a man was already enough to make her happy for quite some time.","As for the furnace-cauldron power, as long as she was strong enough, anyone who dared treat her as a furnace cauldron would get beaten down. One would be beaten; two would be beaten together—until no one dared covet her again.","Besides, the novel contained no plotline involving furnace cauldrons. Otherwise, there would surely have been such a character in Long Aotian’s harem. Compared with changing the deadly fate awaiting her, the matter of being a furnace cauldron wasn’t important.","Her first priority was still to increase her strength, so that she would always have the power to fight Xiao Rangchen on equal terms.","At the thought of Xiao Rangchen, Lou Yue pressed her lips tightly together and viciously jabbed her chopsticks into the vegetables in her bowl several times.","Once she went down to Xuandi City, her main purpose would be to see Xiao Aiai and the others and arrange what came next. Finding him was only incidental—just incidental. She merely wanted him to admit that he had been lying. She absolutely was not going there specifically to look for him!","At long last, when the banquet was nearly over, someone hurried in and whispered a few words to Lou Weixiao.","A look of surprise crossed Lou Weixiao’s face, and he even glanced deliberately at Lou Yue.","After dismissing the messenger, he rose and reported to Lou Mo, “Patriarch, we’ve just received word that someone close to Cangya Xun died in Xuandi City. Not even his bones remain, and his soul lamp has gone out. Cangya Xun seems convinced that he knows who the murderer is and is demanding that the Lou family hand the person over.”","Lou Yue’s chopsticks paused.","Lou Weixiao’s father frowned. “Who died?”","“Cang Wu, Cangya Xun’s right-hand man.”","“He’s dead. What does that have to do with us handing anyone over?” The original body’s second uncle, seated to the lower right of Lou Mo, spoke up.","“Cangya Xun believes that Cang Wu died at the hands of someone under Brother Yue.” As Lou Weixiao spoke, his gaze settled on Lou Yue.","Lou Yue put down her chopsticks and looked back at him. “He believes someone did it, so that person is the murderer?”","“Who did Cangya Xun say it was?”","“Xiao Rangchen, the one who placed second in yesterday’s competition.”","“The one who came down last after comprehending the Dao beneath the ancient tree?”","“Yes.” Lou Weixiao turned toward Lou Yue. “Brother Yue stood up for him in Xuandi City before and even injured Cangya Xun. That’s why he has come to the Lou family to demand the man now.”","“What a joke. Does Cangya Xun think Xuandu belongs to Cangya Cliff? Not to mention whether he was the one who killed the man—even if he was, there’s no reason for him to demand anyone from the Lou family!”","“He isn’t my man. We have no connection whatsoever.” Lou Yue’s tone remained utterly calm.","“I’ll relay Brother Yue’s words to Cangya Xun. However, since the man died in Xuandu, the Lou family should at least find the murderer. Besides, someone dared to act in Xuandu, which clearly means he has no regard for the dignity of the Lou family.”","“If you ask me, we should simply find this Xiao Rangchen and hand him over. I previously sent people to recruit him, but the man was arrogant and conceited, showing not the slightest regard for us. He isn’t worth damaging our relationship with Cangya.”","“We should investigate first and find out who the murderer really is.”","...","Lou Yue sat there through it all. Apart from her first couple of remarks, she didn’t speak again. As for Lou Mo, he remained silent from beginning to end, revealing nothing of his thoughts or emotions.","After the banquet ended, Lou Yue found Lou Zhongyan.","“I promised to stay for a month, but I’ve always been used to wandering. Living in Xuantiandu has left me feeling uncomfortable all over.”","Her brows lifted slightly, and her tone was careless. “I’m afraid that one day I’ll get an itch to destroy some flowers or plants. Let’s leave that month for another opportunity.”","Lou Yue handed him a jade box. “A birthday gift. I picked it on a whim.”","“Young Master Yue, why not give it to the patriarch yourself? He’s inside,” Lou Zhongyan urged.","Lou Yue shook her head. “It doesn’t really matter whether he gets it or not. Do whatever you like with it.”","She turned to leave, but paused and looked back. “For the sake of my being surnamed Lou, I’ll give you a piece of advice that isn’t quite advice—","“Don’t help Cangya deal with Xiao Rangchen. Leave him some room. In the future, that may give you another way out.”","With that, she walked away. Even when Lou Zhongyan called after her, she didn’t turn back.","Lou Zhongyan pushed open the door and entered. He placed the jade box on the table, let out a soft sigh, and withdrew. Lou Mo, a Soul Transformation cultivator, could hear everything that had been said outside; there was no need for him to say anything more.","The door closed again, and silence settled over the room.","Only after a long while did Lou Mo, who had been standing with his back turned and his hands behind him, walk over to the table and open the jade box.","Inside lay a small wildflower. Lustrous spiritual energy curled around it. Its petals were fresh and vibrant, its leaves a brilliant green, all of it radiating vigorous life.","**","Lou Yue returned to the Cloud-Sleeping Courtyard in Xuandi City.","Little Qiu was overjoyed to see her, but before he could report what had happened over the past two days, she went to find Xiao Aiai.","Lou Yue got straight to the point. “Aiai, did your brother come to see you yesterday?”","Xiao Aiai shook her head and took out a letter. “A child delivered this to the Cloud-Sleeping Courtyard this morning.”","The three characters “Xiao Aiai” on the envelope were vigorous and sharp, their strokes seeming to pierce through the paper.","Lou Yue stared at the handwriting, her voice hoarse. “Can I read it?”","Xiao Aiai hesitated for a moment before nodding.","A storage ring fell out of the envelope. She slipped it back inside, then unfolded the letter.","The handwriting on the page was as bold and vigorous as the words outside.","“Aiai, your brother is leaving. I’m sorry to leave you behind. I haven’t been a good brother, and I failed to fulfill Mother’s last request. From now on, take good care of yourself. There are spirit stones and money in the storage ring—keep them and use them. Don’t miss me.”","“Did something happen to my brother in Xuantian Capital? Why did he suddenly leave...?” Xiao Aiai’s eyes reddened.","Lou Yue did not tell her about Cang Wu’s death. She only said, “No. Perhaps there was something he wanted to do, and that’s why he left.”","She folded the letter, put it back into the envelope, and handed it over.","“Aiai, do you want to stay in Xuandi City? If you do, I can have Little Qiu look after you. Or, if there’s somewhere you want to go or something you want to do, just tell me. I’ll arrange it.”","“What I told you before still stands. If you’re willing, you can be my little sister from now on. If you haven’t made up your mind yet, I can also send you to my father. He’s always wanted a daughter by his side. He’d surely be happy if you went to him.”","Xiao Aiai stared blankly at Lou Yue. Seeing that her expression was sincere and that she wasn’t joking, her nose stung, and she said softly, “I... I’ll think about it. I’ll give you an answer later.”","Lou Yue knew she had sprung this on her too suddenly and was afraid of frightening her, so she softened her voice. “Aiai, there’s no need to hurry. Take your time.”","“Mm...”","After leaving Xiao Aiai’s room, Lou Yue returned to her own. The moment she closed the door, she leaned back against it and stood there in a daze.","Xuanba leapt down from her shoulder, climbed onto the windowsill on its own, and waited for the moonlight.","After a long while, a low curse rang out in the room, its final syllable trembling slightly:","“Bastard...”","-----------------------","This chapter dragged the plot along with great effort, all so I could write the reunion in the next one."]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["The Wilderness lay at the extreme northwest, where the spiritual energy was in chaos and demonic beasts ran rampant. It was one of the two great forbidden regions in the world.","Between the undulating, weathered cliffs, two figures slowly made their way across the ocher sand and gravel.","The woman on the left was tall and slender. Her fitted martial attire, dark blue with reddish-brown accents, outlined her graceful figure. A matching headscarf hid her curly blue hair, while a pale-blue veil covered her face, revealing only a pair of seemingly ordinary eyes that nevertheless held an unmistakable air of arrogance.","Beside her walked a woman dressed in a white robe with subtle silver patterns, her face hidden behind a white veil.","“I told you I’d thought everything through. Now no one will be able to recognize us,” Liufeng Xin said, tilting her head and giving Lou Yue a mischievous wink.","Lou Yue pressed down her pale-blue veil, which the wind had blown up. Her tone was languid. “Yes, Your Holiness is wise indeed.”","“I’m a lovesick woman who went mad for love, abandoned my position as the Saintess, and eloped with the Lou clan’s young master.”","Lou Yue shot her a sidelong glance. “You sound proud.”","“Of course I am! This is the Saintess’s glorious achievement. One day, it’ll become a legend I tell the younger generations.”","Remembering what had happened two years ago, Liufeng Xin suddenly sighed. “I just never imagined that the person who eloped with the Saintess would turn out to be a young lady.”","Lou Yue laughed despite herself. “You’ve said that eight hundred times already.”","“It was too much of a shock to my poor heart. Even now, I still feel cheated whenever I think about it.”","“Cheated?”","Liufeng Xin nodded emphatically. “I lost a perfect husband, while Long Aotian gained a beautiful wife. I’m the one who got the short end of the stick!”","Lou Yue’s brows drew together as she stared darkly at her.","“Sis, I was wrong.” Liufeng Xin immediately surrendered, though she still could not stop talking. “But you’re far too vindictive. It’s been two years, and you still haven’t forgotten him.”","Lou Yue abruptly stopped and called out in protest, “Who hasn’t forgotten him?!”","Liufeng Xin slipped an arm around her waist and leaned against her coaxingly. “All right, all right, you haven’t forgotten him. If we run into him this time, I’ll definitely help you get even.”","“We’re here for the Ancient Sage’s legacy,” Lou Yue emphasized.","“I know, I know. I won’t ruin anything. At most, I’ll trip him up a little from the shadows. Besides, even if he comes looking for us, he won’t recognize us.”","Lou Yue glared at her. “Don’t jinx it. It’ll come true.”","Liufeng Xin immediately clamped her lips shut and made a zipping motion across them.","Over the past two years, having spent every day together because of their “elopement,” Lou Yue had long since figured out Liufeng Xin’s boisterous nature. She often found herself reminiscing about the Saintess she had first met—the aloof, untouchable woman. Like now.","Sure enough, Liufeng Xin could not hold it in for long before speaking again. “What do you think Long Aotian would do if he found out you were a woman?”","She began pondering aloud. “Would he be happy or sad?”","“Sigh, is Long Aotian even attracted to men?”","Lou Yue took out a map to confirm the location of the Wilderness’s only village and answered casually, “First, he’ll never have the chance to find out that I’m a woman. Second, I don’t care whether he’s happy or sad.”","Liufeng Xin hurriedly asked, “And third?”","Lou Yue finally gave in to her relentless questioning. “How would I know whether he’s attracted to men?” She sighed. “Saintess Sis, night falls early in the Wilderness. If you hate having sand blown into your face, then hurry up already.”","“Hmm, I really don’t like the nickname Saintess Sis. Can’t you call me Little Fairy?”","Lou Yue raised her voice. “Little Fairy! Are you coming or not?”","“Coming, coming!”","Liufeng Xin quickly ran several paces ahead of Lou Yue, then began skipping merrily in the wrong direction.","Lou Yue looked up at the heavens and sighed. “Little Fairy, please go right...”","She must have had a donkey kick her in the head back then to come up with something as absurd as eloping with Liufeng Xin.","They finally reached the village marked on the map before nightfall.","Although they knew the general plot of events, they still needed to obtain detailed information about the depths of the Wilderness here. Charging in blindly would only lead to disaster.","But Lou Yue discovered that they had still underestimated the allure of the Ancient Sage’s ruins. Even in a perilous wasteland like the Wilderness, countless people were flocking there eagerly.","The dilapidated village had practically become a bustling supply station. Its noisy din could be heard from several hundred meters away.","Liufeng Xin pulled her into a tavern.","Calling it a tavern was generous. It was merely a crude earthen shed with a faded scrap of cloth hanging outside. A crooked, wildly uneven character for “wine” had been painted on it.","Compared with the other places, this one was especially lively. All seven tables were packed with people, making it an excellent place to gather information. However, Lou Yue disliked squeezing in with strangers and immediately tried to pull Liufeng Xin away.","At that moment, someone at a nearby table called out to them. “Hey, girls! Come sit over here!”","The speaker was a chubby man with a good-natured face. He squeezed over on the bench beside a thin man. “Come on, Third, move over a bit!”","The thin man’s temple seemed to twitch. “If you don’t want to sit, then get lost.”","The fat man was not offended in the slightest. He cheerfully waved at them again. “Come on, come sit!”","“Thank you, Big Brother!” Liufeng Xin curved her brows in a smile and pulled Lou Yue over to sit down.","“Just call me Fat Second!” the chubby man said warmly. “This is Big Brother Wei, that’s Skinny Three, and she’s Qiao Qiniang.”","As he spoke, he called for the proprietor to bring over another pot of wine and two plates of snacks.","Across from them, Big Brother Wei looked imposing. His gaze swept briefly over the fabric of their clothes before he asked, “Are the two of you here for the Ancient Sage’s legacy as well?”","Liufeng Xin nodded without hesitation. “Of course! My sister and I heard that an Ancient Sage’s ruins had appeared here, so we came to try our luck. Maybe we’ll even find some fortuitous opportunity or precious treasure.”","“Oh, I forgot to introduce us. My name is Mu Xin, and this is my younger sister, Mu Yue.”","Everyone’s eyes immediately turned toward Lou Yue. They could tell that Liufeng Xin was at the peak of the Golden Core realm, but they could not see through Lou Yue’s cultivation at all.","“Here comes the wine! And the snacks!”","Liufeng Xin poured each of them a bowl of wine. Just as she was about to taste it, Fat Second hurriedly warned her, “This wine is extremely strong. Try a small sip first.”","Liufeng Xin took a sip, and her eyes lit up at once. She gave Fat Second a big thumbs-up.","Fat Second grinned sheepishly. “I’m not bragging, but even the great clans can’t find wine better than this! Still, little sister, you’re surprisingly unfazed by strong liquor.”","Liufeng Xin brought the wine to her veil and took another sip. “I’ve sworn to drink every fine wine under heaven! Does this wine have a name?”","“It doesn’t have an official name, but we privately call it Yellow Springs Wine.”","Liufeng Xin was curious. “Why Yellow Springs?”","Fat Second chuckled. The thin man beside him replied in a sinister tone, “Because after drinking it, you won’t be afraid of taking the road to the Yellow Springs.”","“We all came here seeking treasure, but the Wilderness is an incredibly dangerous place. So many people come here and never return. If they can have a drink of Yellow Springs Wine before they die, at least their journey won’t have been in vain.”","As Fat Second spoke, his voice lowered. He tilted his head back and drained the wine in his bowl.","Big Brother Wei, Skinny Three, and Qiao Qiniang all fell silent, each raising a hand to finish the wine in their bowls.","For a moment, it seemed that the only sound left was the wind and sand beating against the tattered cloth.","“How long have you been here?” Lou Yue suddenly asked.","Big Brother Wei glanced at her and answered solemnly, “A year and a half.”","Qiao Qiniang took over. “We were part of the second group to arrive in the Wilderness. The first group died out long ago. As for the seven of us siblings... now, only four remain.”","“Then why don’t you leave?” Liufeng Xin asked without thinking.","Skinny Three let out a derisive laugh, his voice full of resentment. “Leave? And go where? Every blessed place under the heavens has already been claimed by the great clans. If rogue cultivators like us want to rise, all we can do is come to a lawless place like this and gamble our lives for a chance at fortune!”","He glanced at the two women, his tone hostile. “You two are from one of those great clans too, aren’t you?”","Liufeng Xin hurriedly brought out the excuse she had prepared. “We’re from a branch so distant it can hardly be considered part of the clan. Otherwise, my sister and I wouldn’t have come out to gain experience on our own.”","Fat Second stepped in to smooth things over. “Don’t take offense, miss. One of our brothers died at the hands of someone from a great clan, so Skinny Three has a grudge against them.”","“We understand, we understand. To be honest, we can’t stand their overbearing ways either!” Liufeng Xin chimed in.","Lou Yue swept her gaze over the group’s cultivation levels. Aside from Big Brother Wei, who was in the early Nascent Soul stage, the other three were only in the early or middle Core Formation stage. Such cultivation was already quite impressive among rogue cultivators, but the Wasteland cared nothing for whether one came from a rogue background or a great clan. Here, only strength determined who lived and who died.","In a place like this, the demon beasts were not even the most dangerous threat. The human heart was far more unfathomable.","Lou Yue listened as Liufeng Xin probed for information about the depths of the Wasteland in roundabout ways. Then, amid the din around her, a low voice suddenly reached her ears.","“Two jugs of wine.”","She looked up sharply.","At the crude counter several tables away stood a man with his back to her.","A black cloak covered his body, its hood pulled low so that only his tall, imposing figure could be made out.","After putting the wine into his storage ring, the man turned and walked away to the right. The upper half of his face was hidden behind a mask, making his features impossible to discern.","The winds of the Wasteland were fierce. His strides were long, and the wind whipped his cloak into motion, blowing back the hood at the side of his face and revealing a black thorn-shaped earring.","Lou Yue shot to her feet.","“What is it?” Liufeng Xin asked in alarm. The people nearby turned to look as well.","“Wait here.”","Lou Yue left those words behind and hurried after the man.","Her heart was pounding wildly in her chest. She couldn’t explain why she was following him. At that moment, her body had simply made the decision on its own.","The Wasteland was an important part of the plot. She knew she would encounter Xiao Rangchen here, but she hadn’t expected to run into him so soon.","—There’s something I’ve wanted to tell you since last night.","—But given the circumstances, saying it now would sound like I was only trying to appease you.","—I like you.","Those three brief sentences had repeated themselves in her mind countless times over the past two years.","She told herself that she was following him only because she wanted him to admit that he had been lying to her back then.","However, after turning around a bend in an earthen alley, she lost sight of him.","“...”","After two years apart, the Dragon Proud Heavens had turned into an eel—slipperier than ever.","By the time Lou Yue returned to the tavern, Liufeng Xin was already chatting so enthusiastically with the others that she had completely forgotten herself.","“Oh, you’re back.” When she saw Lou Yue, Liufeng Xin quickly shot her a look that clearly asked, “Did anything happen?”","Lou Yue signaled that everything was fine.","“Good timing. I’ve already discussed it with Big Brother Wei and the others. We’ll enter the Wasteland with them tomorrow morning.”","“I heard from Xin that you’re a spell cultivator at the Nascent Soul Great Perfection stage, miss?” Big Brother Wei asked gently.","Lou Yue glanced at Liufeng Xin, who had at least remembered to help conceal her true cultivation, then answered blandly, “Yes.”","“With the two of you assisting us, we’re sure to gain a great deal from this trip into the Wasteland!” Big Brother Wei let out a hearty laugh. “Thirty percent of what we obtain will go to you.”","“Big Brother!” Skinny Three interjected with a frown, clearly objecting.","“No more discussion.” Big Brother Wei gave him a look, then turned toward Lou Yue. “I’m only in the early Nascent Soul stage, yet I can’t see through your cultivation. The feeling you give me is far beyond that of someone at the Great Perfection stage. All I ask is that, should anything happen, you protect Qiniang. She is carrying the child of our late sixth brother.”","“Big Brother...” Qiao Qiniang’s eyes reddened, and her voice caught in her throat.","“Hey, don’t be so pessimistic! We haven’t even gone in yet. Besides, you still have me.” Unable to bear the gloomy atmosphere, Liufeng Xin pulled out four bottles of pills and pushed them toward the others. “Here, one bottle each! Take one as soon as your strength runs out. I guarantee your spiritual energy will keep flowing without end!”","Lou Yue was amused by Liufeng Xin’s boldly confident manner, and the corners of her lips curved upward.","The others also shook off their gloom.","“Haha, then we won’t stand on ceremony!”","“Go ahead, take them.”","Early the next morning, Lou Yue and Liufeng Xin arrived at the agreed meeting place on time.","“Let’s wait a little longer. We have one more companion. Something came up, so he may be late,” Big Brother Wei said.","About a quarter of an hour later, a tall, slender figure slowly emerged from the shadow beside the rock wall.","A black cloak wrapped around his body, and a half-mask covered his face.","Long hair fell beside his brow, drifting silently in the wind of the Wasteland."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["—I like you.","Those were the only words left ringing in her ears, echoing through the heartbeat that had lost its rhythm.","She knew she would never forget them, no matter how many years passed.","She abruptly turned her eyes away.","The sound of gravel being brushed aside drew closer, then passed them by.","“He’s Xiao Chen. Xiao Chen, these two young ladies only arrived in the Savage Wasteland last night, but their strength is nothing to scoff at either. They’ll be coming with us today.” Big Brother Wei immediately introduced them.","The next step should have been for the two women to say something, but strangely, one stood staring blankly at the newcomer while the other remained motionless with her back to them.","“Ah.” Liufeng Xin suddenly let out a soft cry. She finally recognized him. Forcefully suppressing the excitement on her face, she glanced toward Lou Yue, only to find that her sister still had not turned around.","Liufeng Xin pinched herself and said in a breathy voice, “H-hello. I’m Mu Xin, and I cultivate the alchemical path. She’s my younger sister, Mu Yue.”","She deliberately emphasized the word “Yue,” but Xiao Rangchen merely nodded slightly without even looking at them.","For a moment, Liufeng Xin regretted having Lou Yue use the Voice-and-Visage Pill to alter her voice and appearance. Otherwise, she would have been witnessing the classic scenes of “reconciling after a breakup” and “reuniting after a long separation.”","Oh, and there would have been the added shock of, “So you’re actually a woman?”","But now, none of that was possible. The reunion after a breakup, the long-awaited reunion, the identity reveal—all of it had gone up in smoke.","Her fate was rather miserable.","Though, perhaps she had brought it upon herself.","“Then let’s get going.” Big Brother Wei waved for everyone to follow him out of the village.","Liufeng Xin hurriedly grabbed Lou Yue. Only after they had fallen some distance behind the others did she tug her close and whisper urgently, “You saw him yesterday, didn’t you? I was wondering why you’d lost your composure and chased after him. So you ran into Long Aotian!”","As she walked, she continued chattering. “The two of you really are fated to meet. You actually ran into each other again this quickly. What are you going to do now? This definitely wasn’t part of the plan.”","Lou Yue glanced at the tall, cold figure ahead and replied indifferently, “We’ll deal with it when it comes. Just keep your own tail hidden and don’t let anything slip—especially in front of him. Talk less.”","“Mm... sis, you really don’t plan to let him know it’s you?” Liufeng Xin was still unwilling to give up on her sweet reunion.","Lou Yue shot her a sidelong look. “Do you really need to ask?”","A little over a year ago, while she and Liufeng Xin were “eloping,” she had reached the peak of the Nascent Soul realm. In front of Liufeng Xin, she had directly transformed back into her true appearance, and the Formless technique had consequently begun working only intermittently.","Xuanba had said that the spiritual energy in that half of her inner core was nearly exhausted. If she wanted to maintain her Formless appearance, she would have to wait until she reached the Mahayana realm and use half of her spiritual power to activate it. Even then, the Formless technique would fail whenever she used too much spiritual energy.","Simply put, once she reached the Mahayana realm, she would be able to display her full strength in her female form. If she used her male form, however, she would only be able to exert half her power.","They had come to the Savage Wasteland to compete for the Ancient Sage’s inheritance. Using only half her strength would leave her with no chance of success, so she had no choice but to use her female form.","Fortunately, her true female body differed in build from the male form created by the Formless technique. Although her appearance had not changed much, no outsider could recognize her after she used the Voice-and-Visage Pill.","As for her techniques, what she had previously displayed in front of Xiao Rangchen were basic spells that nearly every member of the Lou clan knew. There was no need to worry about exposing herself.","“But it’s true. Your situation is complicated, so until you have enough strength, you’d better stay cautious.” Liufeng Xin had heard about the Lou clan’s female cauldrons long ago and knew how serious the matter was. She could only suppress her desire to indulge in the romance and mutter under her breath, “Only those who can endure loneliness will live to enjoy the sweetest reward...”","Lou Yue did not catch what she was muttering and merely told her to hurry up.","“Ladies, keep up! Don’t fall behind!” Fat Second called from ahead.","In an instant, the entire group transformed into streaks of afterimages and shot into the distance like arrows released from a bow.","Half an hour later, an endless range of vast, primeval mountains stretched before them. The peaks resembled crouching dragons, and an ancient, savage aura rushed toward them.","The moment they entered the forest, the light around them dimmed sharply. The rancid, moldy stench of rotting leaves and wet earth drifted through the air.","“There’s miasma around the outer perimeter. Anyone at the Golden Core stage can pass through by holding their breath. We’ll rest once we’re farther in!”","After passing through the miasma-filled forest, the group stopped beneath a massive tree.","“From here on, we’ll have to deal with savage beasts.” Big Brother Wei looked at Xiao Rangchen and spoke respectfully. “Xiao Chen, shall I lead the way as before while you bring up the rear?”","Xiao Rangchen gave a faint nod.","Lou Yue deliberately looked away from him.","“Xin, since you aren’t good at attacking, stay in the middle with Qiniang. Yue, follow behind them and guard both their sides. Second Brother and Third Brother, come with me and handle the enemies head-on. Xiao Chen, you take the rear. Does anyone have any objections?”","Everyone shook their heads. Big Brother Wei gave Lou Yue a deliberate look, and after seeing her silent agreement, he called out in a ringing voice, “Move out! If everything goes smoothly, we’ll reach the Ancient Sage’s ruins the day after tomorrow.”","The group set out once more. Since they had to guard against surprise attacks by savage beasts, their pace slowed considerably. Yet this arrangement proved troublesome for Lou Yue.","Xiao Rangchen was following right behind her. Although there were three or four meters between them, his presence was overwhelmingly strong. As a result, she kept unconsciously overtaking Liufeng Xin and Qiniang, whom she was supposed to be walking behind, as though some terrifying flood or wild beast were chasing her from the rear.","Liufeng Xin sent her a sly, teasing glance, while Qiniang looked at her in surprise.","Lou Yue pressed her lips together and slowed down.","It had only been two years since they last met. Was there really any reason for her to keep losing her composure ever since yesterday, needlessly giving him the upper hand?","He was the one who had lied. She was the one who should be standing tall and questioning him with righteous indignation.","Once the Ancient Sage’s inheritance was secured, she would make him pay sooner or later.","Lou Yue took a deep breath and banished the annoying man from her thoughts.","They encountered several waves of savage beasts along the way, but Big Brother Wei and the other two dealt with them all. As they ventured deeper, the beasts grew stronger, and the group’s progress slowed further.","They had just finished another fierce battle and were resting to recover their strength when Lou Yue sensed an extremely subtle disturbance.","It was coming from... directly beneath Liufeng Xin’s feet!","She suddenly seized Liufeng Xin and Qiniang and leaped to the side. The black bracelet around her wrist instantly broke apart in midair, transforming into dozens of black spears that pierced into the ground with ruthless precision.","“Screech!”","The earth writhed violently, and soil surged upward. After a tremor, everything gradually settled.","Big Brother Wei and the others pried away the shattered rocks and dug a spider-shaped beast from beneath the ground. Its entire body was pitch-black.","“It’s a two-hundred-year-old burrowing spider! This thing is sinister and exceptionally skilled at concealing its presence. Who knows how many people have died to it? We didn’t detect it at all!” Fat Second looked at Lou Yue with undisguised admiration. “Miss Yue, your senses are incredible!”","The corners of Lou Yue’s eyes lifted. She raised her chin slightly and accepted his praise.","With a slight lift of her fingers, the dozens of spears condensed back into a bracelet and clasped around her wrist. When she looked up, she happened to meet Xiao Rangchen’s eyes.","Before she could make out the depths of his gaze, his attention shifted to the Form-Manifesting Cube on her wrist.","Lou Yue immediately lowered her hand, letting her sleeve fall over the Form-Manifesting Cube.","What are you looking at? Even if you stare all you want, you still won’t recognize me.","Xiao Rangchen withdrew his gaze. At his side, Yu Youchun’s voice rang out:","“That girl’s artifact is rather interesting. It should be capable of changing into all kinds of forms—a useful surprise attack, to be sure.” He thought of how Xiao Rangchen had just raised his hand before lowering it again, and a hint of amusement and appreciation appeared in his eyes. “She’s only at the mid-Mahayana stage, yet her reactions are no slower than yours, a mid-Void Refinement cultivator. Her perceptiveness is unmatched among those of the same rank.”","“She was the one who followed you yesterday too, wasn’t she?”","“I can’t make out her features with that veil on, but that talent of hers does suit you. I say you should stop pining after that young man and take a look at the person right in front of you.”","Over the past two years, whenever Yu Youchun encountered a woman with promising aptitude, he would whisper sweet nothings into his disciple’s ear. Unfortunately, he had never succeeded even once. At first, he thought his disciple was gay and even tried to set him up with several outstanding men. Only after his disciple threatened to sever their master-disciple relationship with a cold expression did he finally give up on finding him a man.","But if his disciple wasn’t gay, then why was he so hung up on that young man, thinking of him day and night? Yu Youchun sighed. He simply felt that his disciple worked himself far too hard and wanted to find him a partner who might make him value his own life a little more. Staying so tightly wound all the time would lead to trouble sooner or later. Unfortunately, his disciple had no understanding whatsoever of his painstaking efforts.","Once everyone had finished packing up, they continued on their way. Yu Youchun kept chattering into his disciple’s ear. Clearly, they could communicate telepathically through the soul oath binding them, yet he preferred this lively method of teasing him.","【Master, be quiet.】","Xiao Rangchen leaped through the forest, his gaze occasionally drifting toward the dark-blue figure ahead.","As soon as the sun went down, night swallowed the forest in an instant.","Big Brother Wei stopped. “We’ll camp here for the night. Second Brother, Third Brother, go sprinkle the medicinal powder around the area. Us men will take turns standing guard tonight. The order stays the same: Third Brother, Xiao Chen, Second Brother, then me. Any objections? If not, get some rest. We’ve got a tough battle tomorrow!”","Lou Yue leaped into a nearby tree and leaned against the trunk, preparing to rest for a while. Liufeng Xin, however, seemed to have something in mind. She volunteered to help Fat Second scatter the medicinal powder, then returned after quite some time and eagerly leaned close to Lou Yue’s ear to whisper:","“I’ve found out all about him. Xiao Rangchen joined their group a little over two months ago. Before that, he apparently always entered the wilds alone. Sixth Brother, who died, had some connection with him, so he agreed to come only after Big Brother Wei invited him. They say he’s at the peak of the Nascent Soul stage, but he’s actually stronger than that. No one’s seen his limits yet.”","Lou Yue said lazily, “Why bother finding out about him?”","“Ah, I thought you wanted to know.”","“I don’t.”","Liufeng Xin settled down beside her. “All right, then. Let’s just say I wanted to know.” With that, she closed her eyes and went straight to sleep.","“...”","Because of what Liufeng Xin had said, Lou Yue’s thoughts wandered into all sorts of strange and nonsensical directions. It took her quite a while to calm her mind and regain her composure.","When Fat Second passed by on his way to relieve the night watch, Lou Yue’s vigilance was aroused. Through her barely opened eyes, she soon caught sight of a swath of black fabric.","She did not move. She simply lowered her gaze and watched the empty ground below. The faint rustle of fabric rubbing together and the delicate sound of liquor being poured down someone’s throat trickled into her ears, thread by thread.","The sounds suddenly fell silent for a long while before she slowly lifted her eyes.","Beneath the silver moon hanging in the sky, the man leaned against the tree trunk, his right hand holding a wine flask loosely against his raised knee.","His left hand gripped something jade-green. His fingertips seemed to be rubbing it as he lowered his head and stared at it, a deep loneliness spreading around him.","Lou Yue couldn’t see the expression in his eyes beneath the mask, but she felt that his gaze was utterly focused.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍really wanted to know what he was holding, but the object was hidden behind his raised leg, revealing only the green tip of its tail.","Suddenly, the man turned his head and looked over—","Lou Yue immediately closed her eyes.","...There was no way she, Lou Yue, would ever be caught peeking. How embarrassing!"]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["Lou Yue woke when Liufeng Xin shifted beside her.","When she opened her eyes, all she saw was the branch where someone had been sitting, now empty in the morning light.","She had actually pretended to be asleep last night and then truly fallen asleep—she had even slept quite soundly...","She woke Liufeng Xin, and the others who had been resting rose one after another.","“Huh? Brother Chen still hasn’t come back?” Fat Second asked, looking around.","Without even looking up, Big Brother Wei replied, “Xiao Chen told me to have us move ahead. He’ll catch up with us later.”","“Brother Chen couldn’t have gone to...”","Fat Second did not finish. The others all wore expressions of understanding. Clearly, only Lou Yue and Liufeng Xin had no idea what was going on.","Liufeng Xin wanted to ask, but the current situation was hardly suitable for prying, so she could only discuss it with her sister.","“What do you think he went to do?”","“How would I know? I’m not a worm in his stomach.”","“Take a guess! You’re so clever, you’ll definitely get it right.”","Lou Yue shot her a sidelong glance. “Can’t you rein in your curiosity?”","“Hey, I’m only doing this for your sake.” Liufeng Xin sighed. “You’re completely focused on cultivation now and don’t care about...”","Seeing that Lou Yue still did not understand, Liufeng Xin gave up. “Come on, come on. We’re setting out.”","Big Brother Wei walked over, a hint of hesitation on his face. “Miss Yue, with Xiao Rangchen gone... How about I have Skinny Three stay at the rear with you? That way, you’ll have someone to watch your back.”","“No need.”","Her answer was firm and confident.","Big Brother Wei recalled how swift and decisive she had been the day before and did not insist. He turned and called for everyone to continue onward.","Xiao Rangchen caught up with them roughly an hour later. Lou Yue sensed someone approaching at high speed. In an instant, her Yanxiang Disk transformed into several moon wheels that revolved around her, one of them spinning in midair at her fingertips.","She turned her head and stared toward the rear.","The moment the approaching figure crossed her warning range, the moon wheel left her hand and shot forward.","It was deflected by an obstruction and flew back. Lou Yue was just about to call for the group to halt when a dark-robed figure appeared in her line of sight.","Lou Yue turned back and withdrew the Yanxiang Disk.","Xiao Rangchen was no longer concealing his presence. Big Brother Wei noticed him, and the two exchanged a distant nod as they continued walking.","A strong stench of demonic-beast blood wafted from the man behind them.","Had he raided a demonic beast’s lair?... The smell of blood was unbelievably strong.","As she pondered this, the mountains suddenly opened up before them. The clash of weapons and the roars of demonic beasts came from ahead.","They had run into another group of cultivators battling a demonic beast.","It was an enormous black boar, over ten feet tall, shaped like a wild mountain pig. Its eyes were bloodred, its tusks jutted outward, and the bristles along its back stood rigidly upright like spears driven into the sky.","The other group unleashed sword techniques and spiritual power, yet still failed to gain the upper hand. Instead, the beast repeatedly sent them stumbling backward. Neither side could do anything to the other.","Big Brother Wei immediately tried to circle around the battlefield. However, when that group spotted them, they deliberately drew the giant boar in their direction.","The enormous beast charged toward the side of their formation, carrying a foul, bloody stench with it.","Lou Yue immediately stepped in front of Qiao Qiniang and was about to activate the Yanxiang Disk when Xiao Rangchen moved.","Lou Yue only felt a fierce gust of wind sweep past. In the next instant, the black boar—over ten feet tall and weighing several thousand pounds—was sent flying like a hurled boulder. It shot straight past the other group and slammed into a hill a hundred meters away with a thunderous boom that reverberated through the forest.","The surroundings fell deathly silent.","The cultivators froze, their eyes filled with utter disbelief.","He had sent the demonic beast they had struggled with for so long flying with a single kick, without even using spiritual power. Just how terrifyingly strong was his physical body?","Calmly, Lou Yue pressed down the veil that the gust had blown upward.","Xiao Rangchen cultivated both body refinement and spellcraft. At his current level, a single giant boar was nothing to him. Even a whole pack might not be enough to withstand his kicks.","Thinking of the intense, rank smell of blood and beast musk clinging to him when he returned, Lou Yue made a reasonable guess: he had spent that missing stretch of time fighting a group of demonic beasts with his bare hands.","Which raised the question—why had he gone to wrestle demonic beasts in the first place?","From the way Big Brother Wei and the others reacted, he seemed to do this often.","To vent.","That was the word that came to Lou Yue’s mind.","But what was he venting?","The scene from the previous night surfaced in her mind. He had sat on the tree, drinking Yellow Springs wine, his head bowed as he rubbed something in his hand. He had been focused, yet lonely...","“Sister,” Liufeng Xin suddenly whispered into her ear. “I think you should consider body refinement too.”","“He’s so physically strong that he could knock you down with a casual push. I’m just worried your body might suffer in the future.” Liufeng Xin sighed with great seriousness.","Lou Yue was initially confused. But when she saw the meaningful, teasing, suggestive look in Liufeng Xin’s eyes, she understood.","She raised a hand and covered Liufeng Xin’s mouth, then lifted her foot and stomped hard on Liufeng Xin’s instep.","Liufeng Xin: “!!”","Lou Yue gritted her teeth and hissed in a low voice, “Do you think my physical strength is strong or not?”","Liufeng Xin’s features twisted in pain, and she nodded repeatedly.","Lou Yue glared fiercely at her before finally letting go.","In the distance, the black boar staggered to its feet. It shook its dizzy head, then roared and charged toward the other group, which was now closer. Those cultivators hurriedly responded, becoming entangled in battle with it once again.","“That bastard Fang Lin was deliberately trying to use us as scapegoats!” Fat Second shouted angrily, no trace of his usual foolish grin remaining. “Big Brother, I can’t swallow this!”","Qiao Qiniang spoke up as well. “When Fourth Brother and Fifth Brother died, they didn’t kill them themselves, but they stood by and did nothing. Only after Fourth Brother and Fifth Brother were savagely killed and the demonic beast was weakened did they jump out and ambush it to claim the spoils. That’s the truth.”","“Fang Lin even mocked Fourth Brother and Fifth Brother, saying that the weak deserved their fate!”","“Then let’s take it from them.” Lou Yue suddenly spoke as she watched the battle in the distance.","She looked at the others. “Wasn’t it Fang Lin who said that the weak should accept their fate when they lose to the strong?”","Her tone was brimming with confident arrogance.","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze instantly fell on her.","“That’s right! We’ll take it too!” Fat Second immediately raised his arm and looked toward Big Brother Wei. “Big Brother!”","The deaths of Fourth Brother and Fifth Brother were also a deep wound in Big Brother Wei’s heart. Countless times, he had wondered whether, if only he had been stronger, he could have saved them instead of watching helplessly as they died beneath the demonic beast’s jaws. Fang Lin’s words back then had been salt rubbed into that wound. What was more, they had just tried to divert the disaster toward them.","He clenched his teeth and said fiercely, “Move! We’re taking that giant boar!”","With their participation—and Xiao Rangchen lending a hand from time to time—the giant boar soon collapsed, unable to fight any longer.","“Oh, why, thank you.” Fang Lin pasted on a false smile while signaling to his companions to hurry over and harvest the valuable materials from the boar’s body.","“Hold it!” Fat Second shouted. “We’re the ones who defeated this giant boar, so the spoils naturally belong to us! Fang Lin, you were the one who said it: the strong prey on the weak, and those who lack skill have to accept their fate!”","Fang Lin’s expression darkened. He was a mid-stage Nascent Soul cultivator, a full level above Big Brother Wei. Apart from Xiao Rangchen, whose abilities remained unknown, he feared none of the others.","“I advise you not to mistake my tolerance for weakness!”","Lou Yue, Liufeng Xin, and Qiao Qiniang had not joined the earlier battle. Now that it was over, Liufeng Xin pulled them over.","When Fang Lin saw the three women approaching, he sneered. “Two men died, so you recruited a bunch of women into the group? Are you exploring the Wilds, or did you come here to play with women?”","Lou Yue stared coldly at him.","“Fang Lin, what the hell are you talking about?” Fat Second roared, pointing at him.","Liufeng Xin’s brows shot upward. “What’s wrong with women? Can’t women explore the Wilds?”","Fang Lin’s gaze traveled up and down the graceful figures of Liufeng Xin and Lou Yue, and an obscene smile spread across his face.","“Old Wei, you’re certainly enjoying some good fortune.”","“Fuck!”","Fat Second was furious and was about to charge forward, but then Liufeng Xin suddenly changed her tone. Her voice turned delicate and timid, with a hint of fear in it. “Sister, he’s saying such awful things. I’m a little scared~”","Liufeng Xin wrapped her arms around Lou Yue’s and leaned softly against her.","Hearing that voice, Fang Lin’s eyes gleamed with even greater interest. He was just about to make some teasing remark when, out of the corner of his eye, he saw his companion suddenly widen his eyes and stare in horror at something behind him.","The next moment, immense force slammed into his lower back.","“Bang!”","Fang Lin didn’t even have time to react before his entire body was sent flying like a torn rag, crashing headfirst into the black giant boar.","The giant boar, which had just summoned the last of its strength in a desperate attempt to retaliate, finally breathed its last after the impact.","“Wow, Sister, your dog-beating staff is getting more powerful by the day!” Liufeng Xin shed her timid act and clapped enthusiastically.","Where Fang Lin had been standing, a black staff as thick as a barrel stood planted in the ground.","Lou Yue lifted her eyes toward the group. The black staff rose accordingly, hovering in the air above them at an angle.","Terror was written across their faces, horror spilling from their eyes.","They hadn’t even seen how the staff had appeared, let alone how their strongest fighter, Fang Lin, had been sent flying without the slightest ability to resist.","They hurriedly retreated, dragged Fang Lin—who had already passed out and was foaming at the mouth—off the giant boar, and fled without even daring to look back.","Fat Second stood gaping at the black staff suspended in midair. After a long moment, he looked at Lou Yue and said stiffly, “Sister Yue, that staff of yours... is pretty impressive. Heh, heh.”","“Of course!” Liufeng Xin acted as though she were the one being praised. “My sister’s dog-beating staff is specially for dogs with filthy mouths! Hmm... He was probably number one hundred and thirty-something.”","“...You two have run into quite a lot of dogs, huh?”","Liufeng Xin touched her face. “What can I say? We sisters were born beautiful.”","Lou Yue put away the Yanxiang Staff and shifted one step to the side, distancing herself from the drama queen Liufeng Xin.","Big Brother Wei laughed. “All right, Second, get over here and help deal with the giant boar.”","The valuable parts of the giant boar were quickly stripped away. Just as the group was preparing to set out again, Xiao Rangchen suddenly walked over to the corpse and reached his hand straight inside.","When he withdrew it, he was holding the giant boar’s kidneys. Flames sprang up in his hand. Once the fire burned away, it left behind two charred, black, silkworm-bean-shaped remnants.","“Oh? They’re metal-elemental!” Liufeng Xin remarked from beside Lou Yue.","As though he knew what Xiao Rangchen was about to say, Big Brother Wei spoke first. “If you hadn’t taken them, we wouldn’t have noticed them anyway. If you like them, just keep the pair of kidneys.”","“Yeah, Brother Chen. We wouldn’t have gained such a rich haul without you,” Fat Second added.","Xiao Rangchen paused, then accepted the items.","When ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍night fell and they prepared to rest, Liufeng Xin wrapped her arms around Lou Yue’s waist and wheedled, “Sister~ There’s something important concerning the rest of my life that I need your help with.”","Lou Yue poked away the head pressing against her. “Speak properly.”","“It’s about that pair of pig kidneys Long Aotian took at the end. Help me ask him for one, will you?”","Lou Yue lowered her eyes, her face expressionless. “What do you want a pig kidney for?”","“Sister, that’s a very good thing! Normally, kidneys should be water-elemental, but those two are actually metal-elemental. Metal isn’t afraid of fire, so they’re extremely rare medicinal ingredients. Please help me~”","“Go ask him yourself.”","“No, I don’t want to. The moment he stands there, I feel a cold wind blowing over me. Back then, he always looked at me as if he wanted to stab me to death. Wouldn’t that look be even more terrifying now? I’m scared. I’m not going.”","“Then forget about it.”","Liufeng Xin buried herself in Lou Yue’s arms. “I don’t want to, Sister. Can you really bear to watch me lose my appetite and lie awake all night?”","“Yes. I can bear it,” Lou Yue replied coldly.","Liufeng Xin tried every trick she had, but she still couldn’t convince Lou Yue to go. Yet she truly didn’t want to give up. For someone who cultivated the alchemical path, such a treasure was something one could only hope to encounter, never seek out deliberately.","“I’ll go myself, then!” Liufeng Xin puffed herself up with courage. It was only Long Aotian. It wasn’t as though he could kill her, right?","“Good luck. I believe in you.”","“...”","Liufeng Xin shot Lou Yue a resentful look, then slowly shuffled over.","Xiao Rangchen was leaning against a tree. When he noticed her approaching, he raised his eyes.","Liufeng Xin immediately stopped two meters away, her legs trembling slightly.","Good heavens. Why did she feel that his gaze could cut people down indiscriminately even more effectively than it had two years ago?","The others noticed the scene and looked over as well. Fat Second took a sip of liquor to clear his head. Before he could swallow it, Liufeng Xin called out quickly and loudly:","“My sister has taken a fancy to your pair of kidneys. Can you give her one?”","“Pfft—”","Fat Second sprayed the liquor from his mouth.","Lou Yue, who had been watching with her arms folded from not far away: “...”","Not only had Liufeng Xin used her as a cover, she had even phrased it in such an outrageously suggestive way!","Fortunately, Xiao Rangchen didn’t seem to misunderstand. He glanced at her, and then Lou Yue heard his voice again for the first time in two years.","“No.” His voice was hard and distant, more mature than it had been two years ago, with the low, magnetic resonance unique to a grown man.","“We can buy it, or trade you something else,” Liufeng Xin said hurriedly.","Xiao Rangchen gave no further answer. He rose and walked away.","Liufeng Xin grew anxious. She quickly turned to Lou Yue, pleading in her eyes.","Lou Yue sighed, lowered her arms, and straightened. Then she walked over. “What would it take for you to part with it? You can name any condition.”","Xiao Rangchen looked over. Beneath his mask, his eyes were dark and unfathomable. There seemed to be hidden currents roiling within them—or perhaps that was merely her imagination.","Lou Yue’s fingertips curled slightly, and her breathing paused for half a beat, so subtly that it was almost imperceptible.","Yet the voice she had been expecting never came. His gaze lingered on her face for only a moment before he turned slightly. His robes brushed past her as he strode away."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["The night in the wilderness was bitterly cold, the chill seeping into the bones. It was so silent that the desolation seemed capable of swallowing every sound.","Nights like this were the easiest to stir the longings buried deep in one’s heart.","Xiao Rangchen had not gone far. He sat down behind a tree.","From within his robes, he took out a jade-green hairpin. His fingertip rested lightly upon it, slowly tracing the carved patterns.","Two ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍years.","The trace he had left in Lou Yue’s heart had probably faded more and more by now...","He tugged at the corner of his lips.","With her carefree, unburdened nature, if she could remember him for two years, he ought to kneel before the heavens and offer thanks.","“Sigh. If you miss her so much, why not simply go back and take a look? Even your master can’t bear to watch you carry on like this...” Yu Youchun sighed.","Xiao Rangchen raised his head and gazed at the full moon hanging in the sky.","Even when bright, the moon over the wilderness seemed veiled by a layer of gray haze.","After a long silence, he rasped, “I’m afraid that if I see her even once, I’ll never be able to leave again...”","He rested his head against the tree trunk, his gaze passing through the silver radiance toward a distant place beyond reach.","“I swore that I would take revenge, but I still haven’t reached Deity Transformation. Without enough strength, I’ll only hold her back.”","“Master... I can’t go back.”","Yu Youchun was exasperated by his stubbornness. He wanted to scold him for becoming so obsessed with a boy, but in the end, he couldn’t bring himself to sprinkle more salt on his disciple’s already-wounded heart.","“Didn’t you just go kill demonic beasts this morning? This time, you lasted far too short a while.”","Over the past two years, Yu Youchun had noticed a pattern. Whenever his disciple missed that boy too intensely, he would use his brute strength to fight demonic beasts. Afterward, he could usually hold out for seven or eight days.","Who would have thought that this time he wouldn’t even make it through a day before falling into it again?","Xiao Rangchen lowered his eyes. His fingers continued to toy with the hairpin, the jade-green color glowing faintly beneath the moonlight and reflecting in his eyes.","“Master, I saw her shadow in someone else.”","“She doesn’t resemble her in the slightest, but I... can’t help thinking of her.”","Yu Youchun thought for a moment before arriving at the answer. “You mean that young woman who was smashing people with a club today?”","The corners of Xiao Rangchen’s lips lifted, spreading into an almost imperceptible smile. “If it were her, she’d probably hit even harder. She wouldn’t be outdone in the slightest.”","But she would never come, and that person couldn’t possibly be her.","The smile at the corners of Xiao Rangchen’s mouth suddenly faded.","From the moment Xiao Rangchen brushed past her, Lou Yue had stood frozen in place.","She couldn’t quite describe what she felt. Perhaps it was the brief chill that swept over her skin the instant the wind passed by.","She had always known that Liufeng Xin had been joking, yet some subconscious part of her had still taken it seriously.","“Sis, don’t be upset. I don’t want that kidney anymore.” Regret flashed through Liufeng Xin’s eyes as she hurriedly dragged Lou Yue away.","Once they were out of everyone else’s earshot, she clasped Lou Yue by the arms and said softly, “He doesn’t know it’s you. If anything, this proves that he keeps his distance from women. Don’t overthink it.”","Lou Yue slowly blinked and raised the corners of her lips. “I’m fine. Why are you making such a huge fuss?” It would be a lie to say she didn’t care at all, but she was nowhere near being heartbroken.","Liufeng Xin fell silent, assuming that Lou Yue was merely pretending to be strong.","Seeing this, Lou Yue laughed. “I really am fine. I just didn’t manage to help you.”","She gripped Liufeng Xin’s arm and comforted her in return, her voice firm and carrying an unyielding determination:","“We don’t need his charity. We’ll go get them ourselves from now on!”","Hearing this, Liufeng Xin broke into a smile as well. She clenched her fist and cheered, “That’s right! We’ll rely on ourselves and let those lousy men cool their heels somewhere else!”","“Mhm. So, little fairy, can you ‘sleep soundly’ now?”","Seeing that Lou Yue was joking with her, Liufeng Xin finally relaxed. “Of course! I’m going to cuddle up with my soft, fragrant bestie and sleep, just to make those lousy men jealous, envious, and furious!”","“Then hurry back and go to sleep. We’re entering the ruins tomorrow. Once we’re inside, you won’t have time even if you want to sleep.”","Liufeng Xin gave her a suspicious glance. “You’re not going back?”","“On the way here, I sensed a wolf den several miles away. I’m suddenly in the mood to beat them all up.” A spark flashed in Lou Yue’s eyes. “Well, if you want to watch, you can come with me.”","“I’m not going. Isn’t getting my beauty sleep much better?” Liufeng Xin thought that working out and venting her frustration might be good for Lou Yue, so she stopped interfering. “Be careful.”","“I will.”","Lou Yue watched Liufeng Xin walk away. Then she concealed her aura and headed toward the wolf den. She had only darted a few dozen yards when she abruptly stopped and quickly suppressed her aura to the utmost.","A familiar figure stood not far away.","It was Xiao Rangchen.","He was looking at something in his hand again.","It was a jade-green hairpin. It didn’t look like something that belonged to him.","So that was what had held his attention so completely—a hairpin.","Lou Yue glanced at it from afar and was about to look away when she saw him bring the hairpin to his lips.","He kissed it, earnestly and reverently.","Lou Yue immediately scoffed inwardly and turned away.","Her pack of wolves was probably tired of waiting to be beaten by now.","**","Around noon the next day, they arrived at the legendary Ancient Saint Ruins.","Several dozen other groups arrived right behind them.","“There are so many people!” Liufeng Xin exclaimed, rising onto her toes to look into the distance.","Fat Second said, “These are only the rogue cultivators. The disciples of those aristocratic clans entered long ago. They look down on the treasures in the outer region and are all aiming for the rare heavenly materials in the inner regions, as well as the inheritances left behind by the Ancient Saints.”","Big Brother Wei walked up to Lou Yue and Liufeng Xin, his expression solemn.","“According to the rumors, the ruins have five inner regions, all of which can lead to the core region where the Ancient Saint inheritances are located. The farthest we’ve reached on our previous visits was the outer region. We never even made it onto the Cloud-Locking Path. That’s all the experience we have, so we can’t help you much. Are you going in on your own to meet up with the other clans, or...”","Liufeng Xin interrupted him. “Of course we’re going in with you! I don’t want to go with those aristocratic clan disciples who walk around with their eyes on top of their heads. They’re such a hassle. Right, sis?”","“Let’s go in.” Lou Yue answered with action instead of words.","Big Brother Wei let out a hearty laugh. “Good! Then we’ll enter together! With you two joining us, we’ll definitely make a proper attempt at the Cloud-Locking Path!”","The Cloud-Locking Path Big Brother Wei mentioned was a stone path suspended in midair. Its blue-black slabs were carved with ancient patterns, and it stretched upward into the distance. Each slab was only wide enough for one person to stand on, with no barriers on either side. Far below, boiling magma churned and surged, scarlet tongues of flame occasionally leaping up as waves of scorching heat struck them in the face.","Fat Second couldn’t help sighing. “We only took an hour to get here this time? Last time, I remember it took an entire day.”","“A day and a half,” Qiao Qiniang corrected him.","Fat Second rubbed his hands together. “I have a feeling that this time, we might actually make it to the inner region...”","Skinny Three cast him a cool glance. “Your predictions are usually the opposite of what happens.”","“Skinny Three, you jinx! If you don’t believe me, at least believe Brother Chen and the two sisters!” Fat Second shouted.","“That’s enough. Stay alert.” Big Brother Wei’s voice rang out sternly. “The Cloud-Locking Path is ten miles long, with more than six thousand steps. Strong winds will sweep through from time to time, so don’t underestimate it. We’ve never been here before, and all the information we have is hearsay. There may be other unknown dangers. Stay on your guard!”","“There will be spatial rifts that randomly transport people to other parts of the ruins.” Xiao Rangchen suddenly spoke. Then he added indifferently, “I’ll walk in the middle.”","The person in the middle could keep an eye on both the front and the rear. If something happened on either side, they would be able to provide support in time.","The others understood this as well. Big Brother Wei drew a deep breath. “Thank you, Xiao Chen.”","He should have been the one to take on that role, but with Xiao Rangchen—whose strength far surpassed his own—doing it instead, there was no doubt the plan would be far safer.","At last, the group set out along the Cloudlock Path in the order of Big Brother Wei, Fat Second, Qiao Qiniang, Xiao Rangchen, Skinny Three, Liufeng Xin, and Lou Yue.","“This is clearly a hurricane! Even a solidly built man like me is about to be blown off!” Fat Second staggered as he shouted at the top of his lungs.","Though there were several mishaps along the way, they eventually reached the end without further danger. Big Brother Wei was the first to step onto solid ground. Just as Fat Second was lifting his foot, a crack suddenly split open directly beneath Qiao Qiniang, and the gale was abruptly drawn toward them as though pulled by an unseen force.","Qiao Qiniang bore the brunt of it. In her panic, she reached out to grab Fat Second in front of her. Fat Second was already leaning forward with his weight off balance, and when she tugged him, the gale struck him head-on. He plunged straight toward the fissure.","Xiao Rangchen reacted with astonishing speed. Hooking the tips of his toes over the edge of the stone slab, he shot out an arm and caught Fat Second firmly.","Just as everyone else breathed a sigh of relief, Skinny Three was swept sideways by the gale.","Lou Yue’s Yanxiang formation instantly transformed into a rope and wrapped around Skinny Three, while Xiao Rangchen reached out and caught him as well.","A flash of green slipped from his robes.","Xiao Rangchen’s eyes suddenly darkened.","Lou Yue caught sight of the hairpin, but rescuing them was the urgent matter at hand. Everyone’s attention was fixed on the people being tossed about in midair by the wind, and no one had the time to spare for such a tiny hairpin.","Just as the hairpin was about to fall into the magma, a spatial rift a zhang wide happened to open beneath it and swallowed it whole.","Lou Yue helped pull Fat Second and Skinny Three back onto the stone path. Then she saw Xiao Rangchen release his feet from the edge and leap toward the spatial rift that lay nearly flush with the magma!","The spatial rift would close on its own. Who could guarantee that he would still be there if he fell in?","Lou Yue’s brows drew tightly together. When she saw him accelerating downward, she lunged after him without a second thought and seized his ankle.","The gale slammed into her, tearing away her veil and headscarf. A head of softly curled hair came loose at once, streaming wildly in the wind.","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze lingered on the curls for only an instant before he shouted harshly, “Let go!”","Lou Yue gritted her teeth and refused.","From the corner of his eye, Xiao Rangchen saw the rift below narrowing at a visible rate. Spiritual power burst from his ankle in an attempt to shake her hand loose.","But then something changed.","The rift below, already half-closed, suddenly erupted with a savage suction force. Like a giant beast opening its jaws, it dragged the two of them downward from midair.","Lou Yue could hold on no longer. The instant she was pulled away from the stone slab, the Yanxiang formation shot upward, but the suction was too strong and too swift. Before the formation could secure itself, the two of them were swallowed by the rift, completely cutting off the shouts of the others behind them.","The world spun around them. Lou Yue crashed heavily onto the ground.","She had only just pushed herself upright and had yet to look around when she saw Xiao Rangchen bend down to pick up the hairpin. His fingertips brushed over its body, and he tucked it carefully inside his inner robes, close against his skin.","Lou Yue felt a raging fire surge from the depths of her heart straight to the crown of her head.","“Xiao Rangchen, are you insane?! You nearly threw your life away for a lousy hairpin?!”","Her voice was sharp with urgency, her breathing still uneven.","Xiao Rangchen’s hand abruptly stilled. Slowly, he turned to face her. His ink-dark eyes were unfathomable, like a deep, tranquil pool, locking heavily onto her.","“What did you just call me?”","Lou Yue’s ragged breath caught. The blood in her entire body seemed to freeze.","What had she just called him? Xiao Rangchen... She had called him by his name, and she had shouted it loudly at that. She had spent all this time warning Liufeng Xin to be careful, only to be the one who made a mistake herself?","Lou Yue forced herself to calm down. It was only a name. It did not mean anything.","The man stepped toward her, his gaze slowly moving from the softly curled hair falling beside her cheek to her unfamiliar brows and eyes.","“You know me.”","Her heart, which had yet to settle, began racing again. She licked her dry lips and hastily replied, “I’ve seen you before.”","“Where?” he pressed immediately. His eyes remained fixed on her face beneath the mask, leaving her no time to think.","“In Xuandu.”","As soon as the words left her mouth, the man took another step forward, and the cold aura surrounding him closed in around her layer by layer.","Lou Yue’s back tensed.","“Lou Yue,” he suddenly called.","Her pupils contracted sharply, shock filling her eyes.","He had recognized her?!","How had he recognized her? What had given her away?!","Xiao Rangchen simply stared at her. The dark, bottomless pool of his eyes remained perfectly still, without a single ripple, like a lurking beast waiting for its prey to panic and reveal itself.","Lou Yue’s heart jolted. Then she suddenly came to her senses—","No. Xiao Rangchen hadn’t recognized her. He was testing her!","Her heart pounded so hard that her eardrums buzzed. She suppressed her panic, lifted her eyes to meet his, and answered with studied indifference, “Who are you talking about? I don’t know anyone by that name.”","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze traveled inch by inch over her tense jaw and tightly pressed lips before settling once more on her eyes, which she was struggling to keep calm. His low voice held a hint of seduction.","“Did I say it was a person’s name?”","Lou Yue’s throat tightened."]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["“Did I ever say it was a person’s name?” The man’s low, husky voice carried a bewitching undertone.","Lou Yue’s breathing grew ragged.","Xiao Rangchen was bluffing her. He still wasn’t certain.","She had changed her appearance—and even her gender. There was no way he could recognize her. As long as she refused to admit anything, at most, he could only harbor suspicions.","She did her best to keep her voice calm. “It sounds like a person’s name.”","Xiao Rangchen did not respond. He took another step toward her, bending slightly at the waist.","Lou Yue tried to retreat, but her right leg refused to obey. She failed to put any distance between them.","Xiao Rangchen paused for a moment above her shoulder before stepping back two paces, a withered leaf pinched between his fingers, as though he had merely plucked it from her clothes.","But how was that possible?","Long Aotian helping someone remove a leaf stuck to them... No matter how she looked at it, that was bizarre.","Lou Yue was full of confusion. Was he no longer going to pursue the matter of her identity? Had he really picked off a leaf and called it a day? What was going on?","Xiao Rangchen closed his hand around the withered leaf and turned away, walking two steps to the side.","From the angle Lou Yue could not see, the deep, tranquil pools of his eyes suddenly surged with raging waves.","His long lashes lowered, concealing the emotions roiling beneath them.","Wait. What does this mean? She’s that boy? Yu Youchun’s voice echoed through his consciousness in astonishment. Could you have mistaken her?","It’s her.","A person could change their appearance, voice, and figure, but it was difficult to change their temperament and habits. Their instinctive reactions would expose their true nature.","He had only put on the mask two years ago, after entering the Wasteland. The very first time she saw him after arriving there, she had followed him. That meant she was familiar with him.","Her long hair and the entirely black magical weapon she carried were both identical to Lou Yue’s.","The confidence and flamboyance she revealed unconsciously, her carefree way of doing things, the way she refused to suffer even the slightest loss, and the tone she used whenever she lost her temper—all of them were exactly like the Lou Yue in his memories.","Yet that alone was not enough to prove she was Lou Yue. That was why, earlier, he had only felt a momentary suspicion.","But just now, she had called him by name. When he uttered the two words “Lou Yue,” her first reaction had been shock. If she were not the person herself, why would she lose color at the sound of two unfamiliar words?","And when he moved closer to her, he had been making his final confirmation.","Sure enough.","He had caught it—that sweet, warm floral scent that belonged exclusively to Lou Yue.","It was incredibly faint, but to someone who had become addicted to it, who craved it even in his dreams, a single wisp was enough to awaken every instinct in his body.","The way every hair on his body abruptly rose. The boiling surge of blood racing through his meridians.","The wild intuition of a beast that had searched and searched, only to finally find the unique scent of its prey.","She was Lou Yue.","Because only she could have done it.","When Yu Youchun heard the certainty in his voice, he asked in puzzlement, Then why don’t you expose her?","Xiao Rangchen slowly crushed the withered leaf between his fingers, feeling it crumble in his palm and cling to his fingertips. She once said that we were not on the same path. Now that we are, if I expose her, she will leave immediately.","Yu Youchun fell silent for a while before suddenly saying, Though I never noticed she had a penchant for disguising herself as a woman...","...She probably doesn’t want anyone to recognize her.","...If she doesn’t want anyone to recognize her, she disguises herself as a woman?","...","Yu Youchun reached a conclusion. So it’s still a hobby.","Xiao Rangchen stood in silence, unable to find any way to refute his master.","With his back to Lou Yue, Xiao Rangchen remained still. Lou Yue, meanwhile, stared at his back, her eyes filled with confusion.","Had Xiao Rangchen recognized her or not?","If he had recognized her, he should have exposed her. He would not be standing there silently like this. Even with his cold personality, he should at least have been shocked to discover that she was a woman.","Then he was still only suspicious. He had not recognized her?","As she pondered, Xiao Rangchen turned around. Lou Yue hurriedly shifted her gaze, letting it fall casually to one side.","From the corner of her eye, she saw him release the withered leaf he had crushed to pieces in his palm. It fell to the ground. Then he walked toward her.","“Let’s go. We’ll look for a path leading to the core area.” His voice was calm, without the slightest trace of anything unusual.","He didn’t recognize me... right? Lou Yue thought again.","Xiao Rangchen stopped two meters away and looked at her, as if waiting for a response.","Wasn’t ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍he cold and intimidating before? Why did he seem less unapproachable now? Had he recognized her? But if he had, wouldn’t he be even more distant? No, that didn’t seem right either. Given their relationship, he should be keeping her at arm’s length. So had he recognized her or not?","Lou Yue felt as though her head were about to explode. Yet Xiao Rangchen’s expression remained utterly composed, making him impossible to read.","“Not coming?” he asked again, his tone neither cold nor warm.","Lou Yue licked her lips. “You go ahead. I want to stay here and enjoy the scenery for a while.”","Xiao Rangchen glanced around them. “The scenery?”","Lou Yue paused and looked around as well.","Everywhere she looked were the enormous skeletons of ancient beasts. Even the ground beneath her feet was covered in a pile of withered leaves embedded with unknown fangs, teeth, and claws. It was plainly a burial ground of bones.","“...Actually, it’s not so bad,” she said stiffly.","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze lingered on her for a moment. Then he suddenly walked over and crouched down in front of her.","Lou Yue wanted to retreat, but her body refused to obey.","When she had fallen through the spatial rift, her leg had slammed into something hard. Her mind had been filled with anger, so she had not paid any attention to it when she got back on her feet. Now, however, she could not move it at all.","Xiao Rangchen raised a hand and touched her trembling right leg. At last, his five fingers closed lightly around her knee.","A sharp, piercing pain exploded through her. Lou Yue’s entire body jolted. As she tilted to the side, her right hand instinctively braced against his shoulder.","She did not want to touch him. But the dull ache she had ignored before had become so excruciating after his squeeze that she felt as though she might as well chop off her entire leg. At this point, whether she wanted to touch him was no longer relevant.","“Your bone is cracked.” He looked up at her, his voice deepening. “Where else does it hurt?”","Lou Yue’s arms were trembling, and cold sweat covered her back. He was asking where she hurt? Please. After he squeezed it, her entire leg hurt so badly she wanted to hack it off.","She bit her lip and swallowed the cry of pain that had reached the tip of her tongue, refusing to say a word.","Xiao Rangchen looked up at her stubborn, unyielding expression. His brows drew together as he rose and lifted her horizontally into his arms.","Lou Yue was startled. She raised a hand to push against his chest. “What are you doing?”","Xiao Rangchen set her down on a relatively flat section of an enormous beast’s skeleton. Then he knelt on one knee in front of her and gently raised her right foot, resting it across his leg.","“No, I can do it myself!” Lou Yue said hurriedly. Planting both hands against the skeleton, she tried to move backward.","Xiao Rangchen paused. He did not argue with her, merely looking at her in silence. His eyes seemed to say, Go on, then.","Lou Yue pressed her lips tightly together and bent down to reach for her leg. She managed to bend only halfway before she could go no farther. Cold sweat beaded on the tip of her nose, and her arms were nearly unable to support her body.","Xiao Rangchen stopped indulging her. He reached out and removed her right shoe and sock.","Her pale, lustrous foot was revealed, her toes curled slightly. The delicate sheen of her skin was almost dazzling.","Xiao Rangchen froze, his movements slowing for half a beat. Lou Yue felt a strange discomfort in her heart and let her gaze drift aimlessly to the crown of his head.","Xiao Rangchen steadied himself and pulled up her pant leg, deliberately avoiding any unnecessary contact. He stopped only after her knee was exposed.","Her leg was as pale as moonlight, but a large, glaring bruise stained its front. Dark blue and black marks spread upward, gathering into an even deeper, more ominous swelling over her knee.","Spiritual power gathered in his palm and, without touching her, covered the shocking bruise.","Threads of coolness gradually suppressed the fiery pain raging through Lou Yue’s leg.","The ugly purple-black bruising slowly faded before her eyes, returning to its original pearly whiteness.","Xiao Rangchen’s gaze lingered there for a moment before moving up to her knee. As before, he infused it with spiritual energy.","The swelling and bruising gradually faded, but all he could do was ease her pain. He could not mend the fracture. She would need someone skilled in alchemical healing—or wait for it to heal on its own.","Lou Yue watched as he calmly lowered her pant leg back into place, then picked up her shoes and socks to put them on for her. Her fingers curled slightly as she spoke.","“Don’t you know that men and women should keep their distance?”","Xiao Rangchen raised his head, the gaze behind his mask settling on her slightly arched brows.","“You take care of every woman you’ve just met like this?” Lou Yue pressed, trying to find a flaw in his composure.","He gave a quiet “Mm.” Then, his low voice carrying a magnetic quality, he turned the question back on her. “Does it bother you?”","What did he mean, does it bother her? She was the one being taken care of—what was there for her to care about?","Lou Yue had only wanted to test whether he had recognized her. Skirting around the question, she stared at him and asked again, “Is ‘Lou Yue’ actually a person’s name?”","Xiao Rangchen lowered his head and slipped a sock onto her foot. “Mm.”","“What is she to you?”","He looked up, seeing the probing in Lou Yue’s eyes. After a brief silence, he clearly enunciated, “The woman I love.”","Liar. Lou Yue sneered inwardly.","But outwardly, she still feigned surprise and continued probing. “Oh? Then why aren’t you together? Doesn’t she like you?”","He paused for a long while, as though deliberating. Then he answered in a tone that was difficult to read, “We’re in love with each other.”","“...”","Who was in love with him?! What a lying scumbag!","Lou Yue instantly lost all interest in sparring with him and decided to end this round of probing.","Unexpectedly, he gazed at her with quiet intensity. “You’re not going to wish us well?”","“...”","Lou Yue ground her back teeth together and forced a fake smile. “I thought you were cold by nature. I didn’t expect you to be so quick to warm up to strangers.”","“Does it bother you?” His tone dipped, carrying a hint of teasing seduction.","The question had come full circle again. Lou Yue turned her eyes away and replied perfunctorily, “Of course not.”","He said nothing more, merely lowering his head to put her shoes back on.","When he had finished, he gently set her foot down and stood.","“Still want to look at the scenery?”","Lou Yue: “...”","He was mocking her!","She was just about to fire back when movement came from inside her storage ring. She lifted a finger, and a communication butterfly flew out. Liufeng Xin’s voice came through in broken fragments:","“Zzz— you— safe— what— happened— ah—”","Lou Yue frowned. “I’m fine. There’s interference. I can’t make out what you’re saying.”","“Zzz— hear— zzz—”","“Don’t go into the inner zone again while I’m away. I’m worried about you.”","“Zzz— go in— zzz—”","Lou Yue’s voice tightened. “You are not allowed to go back in. You haven’t even reached the Nascent Soul stage. Wait there for me to come get you.”","“Zzz—I want to— together— promise—”","Lou Yue replied helplessly, her voice softening. “Be good and listen to me. Don’t make a fuss.”","“Zzz— zzz—fine.”","The static stabbed painfully at Lou Yue’s eardrums. She cut off the transmission, then raised her hand and wrote in the air:","Stay put at Suoyun Road. Don’t run off on your own. Wait for me.","She sent the message into the communication butterfly. Only after confirming that it had been delivered did she return it to her storage ring.","When she looked up again, she met a pair of dark, fathomless eyes.","Within them, shadows seemed to churn, as though capable of devouring everything, slowly and thread by thread spilling outward."]},{"number":31,"title":"Chapter 31","paragraphs":["Dark, heavy shadows roiled in Xiao Rangchen's eyes.","Lou Yue found herself frozen in place, caught fast by that gaze.","The next moment, Xiao Rangchen lowered his eyes, hiding all those murky shadows away.","Lou Yue snapped back to her senses.","A moment of silence stretched between them.","After a while, she hopped down to the ground on one foot, her Manifestation Square coalescing into a long staff in her grip. Limping, she walked around him.","Seeing that he was still standing rooted to the spot, she spoke without turning her head, deliberately lacing her tone with lightness, \"What, have you suddenly decided the scenery here is nice?\"","Xiao Rangchen did not answer. He walked over silently, his eyelashes hanging low, and a cold chill seemed to settle over his whole body, as if he had reverted back to the aloof man he had been before.","This ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​‌‌‌‍was the way he had always been, yet Lou Yue felt strangely unaccustomed to it all at once.","The two walked one after the other along the path strewn with bones, neither of them saying a word.","After a long while, Lou Yue could not hold it in any longer and turned around. \"You're trailing behind me, don't you find that slow?\"","The clear thing they needed to do right now was move quickly, find the path to the core zone, and get out of this godforsaken place.","With one of her legs injured, she could not pick up the pace. As a perfectly able-bodied man, why couldn't he go scout the nearby area first? With his speed, by the time she walked a few hundred meters, he could have already surveyed the entire surrounding area.","Yet the able-bodied man replied indifferently to her words, \"I'm in no hurry.\"","Lou Yue: \"...\" But she was in a hurry, very much so!","Lou Yue took a deep breath, turned back around, and continued moving forward, straining to speed up her steps. Her staff tapped against the hard ground, leaving a string of crisp \"clack clack\" sounds.","She pushed her perception to its absolute limit, searching for any possible clues.","In the book, Long Aotian spent five years in the Wasteland. The four great clans discovered the ancient sage ruins hidden in the Wasteland in his fifth year there. Even though the current timeline was much earlier, the settings of the ruins and the inheritance should not have changed.","Entering the core zone was when the inheritance trials truly began. Most of the book's plot was set in the core zone, and after the male lead entered the ruins, he only stayed briefly in the inner zone before heading straight into the core zone.","Before they came, she and Liufeng Xin had sorted through the Wasteland plot she remembered. But the book was a thousand chapters long, with countless settings packed into its pages, and the parts she could recall were all related to the core zone. She could not remember a single detail about this inner zone right now.","Originally, it would have been best to let Xiao Rangchen, who had the male lead's protagonist halo buff, find the way out. After all, he was blessed with immense luck. But this man was just not cooperating.","Lou Yue looked at the fork in the road ahead, then turned to glance at the man beside her who was strolling along as if he had all the time in the world. She asked him, annoyed, \"Which way do we take?\"","The man paused for a moment, then said, \"Either is fine.\"","\"Which way does your gut feeling say leads to the exit?\"","The man stared at her, as if trying to find the reason behind her odd decision to ask for his opinion on her face.","\"Hurry up and answer, use your gut feeling,\" Lou Yue urged him.","\"You trust my gut feeling?\"","Lou Yue nodded. Of course she did. This man came with a built-in buff, and trusting him meant tapping into that good luck.","Seeing her eager expression to find the exit, Xiao Rangchen stayed silent for a short moment, then pointed to a path opposite to what his actual gut feeling told him. \"Left.\"","Lou Yue moved down the left path, her staff making that familiar \"clack clack\" sound.","Half an hour later, staring at the dead end right in front of her, Lou Yue glared at the man beside her and ground her teeth out, \"Did you deliberately point me the wrong way?!\"","Xiao Rangchen met her sharp, accusing gaze, and calmly denied it, \"No.\"","Lou Yue was full of suspicion. She stared hard at his face, trying to find any trace that he was lying, but he already had a naturally impassive expression, and half of his face was covered by a mask. There was simply no hint of anything out of the ordinary to spot.","Lou Yue looked back at the towering mountain of bones stacked right in front of her.","There was no reason for Xiao Rangchen to lie to her about finding the exit. Dragging their way would not benefit him in the slightest.","Could it be that the exit was actually hidden inside the pile of bones? Was it that well-concealed?","Xiao Rangchen saw her staring so intently at the pile of bones that she looked like she was about to burn a hole right through it, and said softly, \"Let's go, we'll take the other path.\"","Lou Yue did not move.","After a moment, he heard her say very seriously, \"The exit is very likely hidden inside this pile of bones.\"","She turned to look at him. \"Go clear away all these bones and search for the exit.\" Her expression and tone were completely earnest and certain, not like she was joking at all.","Xiao Rangchen stared at her, momentarily at a loss for words.","Seeing that he still did not react, a clear look of exasperation crept into her eyes. \"You wouldn't make an injured patient like me do it, would you?\"","Xiao Rangchen was about to speak, but stopped himself.","The disdain in Lou Yue's eyes was almost spilling over. \"Fine, if you won't go, I'll do it myself!\"","Xiao Rangchen pressed down the long staff she had raised, pressed his lips together, and finally relented. \"...Fine, I'll go.\"","Lou Yue finally deigned to look at him properly. \"Hurry up,\" she said. Then she picked out a relatively clean piece of bone nearby to sit on, and raised an eyebrow at him. \"What are you waiting for? Go on!\"","Xiao Rangchen lifted his head, his gaze falling on the pile of bones that was more than ten zhang tall and stretched for three li across.","\"Go now!\" Lou Yue urged him again, not forgetting to add a reminder, \"Be careful when you move the bones. The exit could be hidden on any single bone, so keep your perception spread out the whole time.\"","\"...\" Was it too late for him to be honest right now?","Over an hour later, Lou Yue, who had been sitting upright at first, had long since sprawled out on her side. She called out loudly, suspicious, \"You're not slacking off, are you?\"","The pile of bones had almost been flattened to the ground, and there was still no sign of an exit. That made it really hard for her to believe he was working hard.","The tip of the spear Xiao Rangchen was using to move the bones paused. He straightened up, put his spear away, and glanced sideways at Lou Yue, who was supervising his work while lazing around comfortably. The words that came to his mind—why don't you come over here and try this—turned into, \"...No, I'm not.\"","Yu Youchun, who had been watching the whole time: \"...\"","\"When did you stop being the Wasteland Asura that everyone feared a year ago? You've turned into a total henpecked husband! You're a man, stand up for yourself, get mad at her!\" Yu Youchun fumed inside his head.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his head and continued to move the bones. [As long as she can stay by my side like this, I don't care what I have to do.]","Yu Youchun felt both heartbroken and pained for him. He howled silently at the sky, then simply shut off his five senses so he would not have to see this scene that pained his eyes.","In the end, they still did not find any exit. Lou Yue had to admit that even Long Aotian's protagonist buff could fail sometimes.","They set off on their path again. This time, Lou Yue no longer asked for Xiao Rangchen's gut feeling, and instead decided which path to take by the divination method of tossing a stone to see which side landed face up.","As it turned out, that little bit of mysticism actually worked.","They arrived at a huge sunken basin. On the ground overgrown with dry grass and dead branches stood several giant eggs as tall as two people, their shells dark brown. In the middle of the cluster of eggs, there was a fist-sized gray stone, its surface shimmering faintly with a golden glow.","Lou Yue recognized that it was the Starstone that was supposed to appear in the core zone in the book, an item that could raise the quality of a magic weapon by a huge margin. Long Aotian had gotten it and used it directly on his spear.","She darted a quick sidelong glance at Xiao Rangchen, who was surveying his surroundings, then bent over abruptly, her fingers moving as fast as lightning to tuck the Starstone into her storage ring.","Her movements were smooth and fluid. Then she straightened up, pretending to sigh casually, \"Wow, these eggs are huge.\"","A faint trace of a smile flickered across Xiao Rangchen's eyes.","Lou Yue had no idea he had seen through her. She circled the eggs slowly, her fingertips brushing against the rough eggshell as if she was looking at them out of curiosity, while secretly thinking to herself who she could find later to forge the Starstone into her Manifestation Square.","Just then, a loud, clear cry suddenly rang out from the sky. The sound waves shook the bones all around them until they hummed, and bits of broken bone came tumbling down.","Xiao Rangchen's expression turned sharp in an instant. He swept Lou Yue up into his arms, pushed off the ground hard with his toes, and carried her speeding off into the distance.","Lou Yue's body was suddenly lifted into the air. She wrapped her arms around his neck instinctively, too caught off guard to think about anything else. The howling gale in her ears and the sharp cry echoing from the sky made her heart leap up to her throat.","A ferocious Wasteland bone eagle came diving toward them, sharp piercing sounds tearing through the air. Lou Yue summoned her Illusory Conjuration Shield to guard their rear.","\"Bang!\" The eagle's talons slammed hard against the conjuration shield. The terrifying brute force sent a backlash surging through Lou Yue, and a coppery taste rose instantly in her throat.","Xiao Rangchen glanced down at her pale face, then pushed his speed even higher, holding her as he wove nimbly through the narrow gaps between the giant ancient skeletons.","The bone eagle stayed hot on their heels. Its wings, several spans wide, beat out fierce gusts of wind that shook the surrounding bones. Its sharp beak snapped through a thick bone pillar, and its massive body squeezed through the narrow crevice, refusing to let the two escape.","Lou Yue huffed in irritation. \"Why won't this thing just give up!\"","Xiao Rangchen's voice drifted to her ears through the wind, laced with a faint teasing tone. \"You stole its baby's precious treasure, and you don't expect it to chase you to get it back?\"","Lou Yue choked. So he had seen her hiding the star rock earlier.","Suddenly, the bone eagle let out a long, shrill cry toward the sky. Lou Yue's brows knitted immediately. \"It's calling for its companions.\"","One of these things was already a nightmare to deal with. If a whole flock showed up, there would be no way they could outrun them.","Lou Yue spread out her senses, and caught the trace of a lake not far away. She quickly urged Xiao Rangchen to change direction.","The lake water was a dark, eerie crimson. Lou Yue hesitated for a split second, but Xiao Rangchen had already leapt into the water with her in his arms.","She hurriedly held her breath, as the sharp eagle talons barely broke the surface right where they had been, swiping past their sides and sending waves surging outward.","Xiao Rangchen tightened his hold around her waist, pulling her deeper into the water.","The shrill cries of the bone eagles came muffled from the surface above. The talons kept stabbing down again and again, churning the red water, and showed no sign of stopping for a long time.","The water pressure built up, and Lou Yue's chest grew more and more starved for air. A dull, swollen pain spread through her lungs.","She suddenly pried Xiao Rangchen's hand off her waist, twisting to break free and swim toward the surface.","Confused by her reaction, Xiao Rangchen grabbed her wrist and pulled her right back.","In her struggle, Lou Yue knocked the half-mask off his face, but she had no mind to pay attention to it right then. All she could think about was getting up to breathe.","Xiao Rangchen realized in an instant that she could no longer hold her breath. He had forgotten that Lou Yue had never trained her body to the same level as his, which allowed him to stay underwater for a full day without needing air.","He pulled Lou Yue close, his dark eyes fixed intently on her face.","The second Lou Yue saw that look on his face, the classic underwater air-kiss trope from all those romance dramas popped straight into her head. Her eyes went wide, and the moment he leaned in slightly toward her, she didn't hesitate to slam her palm hard against his chest.","Try to take advantage of her? Over my dead body!","The shove carried quite a bit of force. It didn't push him away, but she used the recoil to propel herself upward toward the surface.","Xiao Rangchen froze for a moment, and by the time he reached for her again, it was already too late.","Lou Yue quickly observed the pattern of the stabbing talons above, spotted a gap, and darted up to gulp a huge breath of fresh air before diving right back under.","She swam back to Xiao Rangchen's side, not forgetting to throw him a sidelong glance, a little smug glint in her eyes.","Xiao Rangchen looked at her bright, unruly expression, and a faint, soft smile tugged at the corner of his mouth.","Lou Yue repeated the trick twice more, stealing breaths when the eagle talons were out of the way, before the flock of bone eagles finally flew off.","She surfaced, watching the dark shapes of the birds vanish completely over the horizon, and let out a long, relieved breath. When she turned back, her eyes locked right onto Xiao Rangchen's, who had just turned his head too.","Back in the water earlier, all her attention had been on holding her breath and dodging the eagles, and the light had been too dim to see him clearly.","Now, in the bright daylight, every line of his face was sharp and clear.","His brow was as striking as ever. Drops of water slid slowly down the crisp, sharp line of his cheekbone, fell onto his straight, high nose bridge, then rolled over his thin lips, leaving a glistening sheen.","Lou Yue suddenly remembered the way he had looked two years ago, when he was dragged out of her water prison. Back then, his face had still held unyielding cold arrogance and ferocity, refusing to bow no matter what.","Two years had passed since then. Time had worn away the last of his youthful harshness, and his features had grown even deeper and more defined. The sharp, icy edge to him had softened into something far more calm and restrained.","She was looking at him, and he was looking right back, his eyes never leaving her face.","Those sharp, bright eyes of his held a depth like a whirlpool in a dark pool, heavy and hypnotic, as if they wanted to drag every part of her down into them to sink together.","The wind swept across the lake, rippling the crimson water, and disturbing the air between them.","A warm, thick haze wrapped around their breaths. Something new grew quietly as their gazes tangled, like spring water overflowing its banks, brushing light against the heart, sending tiny ripples spreading out.","Lou Yue snapped her eyes away at once, pressing down the strange, fluttering feeling that had just sprung up in her chest. After a short moment of silence, she said, \"Let's get out of the water.\"","\"Mm.\"","The voice was so low and deep that Lou Yue's fingertips trembled for no reason.","Xiao Rangchen lifted his hand, intending to wrap it around her waist, but at the last second, he rested it on her wrist through their soaked clothes, leading her toward the shore.","Lou Yue deliberately ignored the strong, firm feel of his hand on her wrist, and the second they stepped onto solid ground, she pulled her hand away quickly.","The red dye from the lake had stained their clothes, which clung to their skin and felt horribly uncomfortable. She shook her hem in disgust, not noticing at all how the wet fabric clung to her figure, and what that sight must look like to the man beside her.","Xiao Rangchen had no idea how Lou Yue had managed to change her appearance into that of a woman, but the disguise was undeniably perfect.","He swallowed hard, forcing his gaze back up to her face. But then a drop of pale red water slid down her temple, across the soft line of her neck, and dripped into the hollow of her delicate collarbone. His eyes turned dark as ink, and he forgot to breathe for a second.","\"I need to change my clothes,\" Lou Yue said suddenly, looking up at him.","Xiao Rangchen's lashes fell to cover his eyes immediately.","Lou Yue threw him a confused glance, then scanned the surroundings for a hidden spot. The lakeshore was nothing but scattered skeletons, until her eyes landed on a giant beast skull sitting high up on a rise. The eye sockets of the skull were dimly lit, and while it looked a little spooky, it was far more private than the wide open space down here. The only problem was that it was quite high up, and with her injured leg, she would never be able to leap up there on her own.","She was hesitating about looking for another spot, when suddenly she was pulled tight against a firm chest. A faint, crisp scent of frost and snow wrapped around her completely.","He had carried her before, but back then all her attention had been on the chasing bone eagles. This time was different.","The warmth of their pressed bodies seeped through the soaked fabric, and his arms, one wrapped around her back and the other under her legs, were strong and solid, the lines of his muscles clear even through the clothes.","Every nerve in Lou Yue's body went taut.","Xiao Rangchen bounded up to the beast skull Lou Yue had spotted, and set her down on the flat top of it.","He was about to speak, but Lou Yue had already turned around, limping quickly into the left eye socket. He stared at her retreating back for a second, then stepped into the right one.","The two eye sockets were deep, making two separate little private spaces.","He didn't start changing his clothes right away. He just leaned back against the cold bone of the skull, loosened the collar of his shirt, and closed his eyes to steady his racing breath.","Separated only by a thin wall of bone, on the other side, Lou Yue had her hand pressed to her lips, leaning back against the skull in a daze.","She felt like something was very wrong with her. The thudding of her own heart was so loud it was almost deafening.","After a while, she exhaled a long breath, pushing all the distracting thoughts from her mind away, and reached to peel off her wet clothes.","On the other side, Xiao Rangchen also undid his belt.","A moment later, both of them froze.","The back of the skull's eye sockets were connected, and the hollow bone chamber carried every sound with an echo. The soft rustle of fabric, the faint slippery sound of wet clothes peeling off skin, all tangled and echoed through the empty bone space, sounding exactly like something else entirely.","Every single hair on Lou Yue's body stood on end, especially since she had just taken off her wet clothes and was completely bare at the moment.","It felt as if she could smell the crisp, cold scent of frost and snow again.","Lou Yue fumbled frantically to dig out a set of clothes from her storage ring, putting it on as fast as she could. She did not even bother to slip her shoes on properly before she hopped and scurried in a few quick steps, almost fleeing from that eye socket.","The clattering, tangled sounds from inside the bone cavity gradually faded away, leaving only a faint echo drifting softly around the space.","Xiao Rangchen looked down at his own fingers, which were frozen mid-air. After a long pause, he slowly lifted his hand and continued to tie up his inner garment, his movements far slower than they had been earlier.","Once he finished dressing, he leaned back against that bone wall again, and this time, he did not move at all for a very long while.","Lou Yue stood at the front of the skull, letting the cool breeze blow over her for a good while before she finally managed to suppress that strange, rising heat.","She lifted a hand to tuck the damp strands of hair stuck to her cheek aside, her gaze wandering idly over the distant bone wasteland, until it suddenly locked in place at a glance.","Beneath the sky at the very end of her line of sight, a ring of golden light hung suspended. It did not carry the vicious aura of a ferocious beast, but instead emitted a soft, gentle glow that stood out sharply against the dusky, gray expanse of this bone-strewn land.","The moment Xiao Rangchen stepped out, he heard Lou Yue's voice, bright with delight, ring out, \"I found the exit!\"","His footsteps came to an abrupt halt."]},{"number":32,"title":"Chapter 32","paragraphs":["Lou Yue pointed at the golden glow in the distance and said excitedly, \"That's the spot!\"","Xiao Rangchen did not respond.","Lou Yue turned back to look at him, only to see him lowering his eyes again, lost in thought. His dark ink-colored tight robe set off the icy, aloof aura around him, and even the thorn stud on his ear glinted with a cold, harsh light.","What a scheming Long Aotian, she thought to herself with a quiet snort. She turned her head back and squinted at the distance again. Judging from where they stood, it would take roughly over an hour to get there at full speed, and there was no guarantee they would not run into demon beasts along the way. They had to hurry.","\"Let's go, quickly,\" she urged.","Xiao Rangchen walked slowly closer, leaning his body slightly as if he was about to carry her down. Lou Yue stopped him immediately, \"I can do it myself.\"","Right after saying that, she had the Image Transformation Square turn into a rope, tied one end around her waist, and fastened the other end to the raised part of the skull. She gripped the middle of the rope and leaped down, her movements crisp and neat.","Xiao Rangchen watched the figure leaving with such ease, and the line of his lips gradually tightened.","Lou Yue landed and walked a few steps before noticing that he had not come down yet. After a quick thought, she decided not to bother with it.","She was the one slowing them down right now, and besides, after what had just happened, she felt it was better to keep a little distance between the two of them for the time being.","It was not long before Xiao Rangchen caught up, walking two or three meters behind her side, keeping a distance that was neither too close nor too far.","The whole way was silent, just like it was at the very beginning, yet something had clearly shifted. In the quiet air, there were faint, wispy, indescribable things that kept trying to creep out.","Before the atmosphere could turn even more awkward, Lou Yue picked a random topic to break the silence, \"Have you always stayed in the Wilds and never left?\"","She already knew the answer, but she could not think of any other topic right now.","Xiao Rangchen gave a low \"mm\" in response.","\"Why? Isn't it boring?\" If she had to stay in this lousy Wilds all day long with nothing but demon beasts for company, she would probably get sick from the boredom.","\"I have something I must do,\" his voice was flat, with no detectable emotion.","Lou Yue thought to herself, Soon, very soon, you will get your revenge.","\"What about you?\" He cast his gaze far into the distance and asked.","\"Me?\" Lou Yue glanced at the hard lines of his side face out of the corner of her eye, \"What about me?\"","\"Where have you been these... past few years?\"","\"All over the place.\" Lou Yue thought of the past two years of \"running away together\", being chased by the Liufeng clan, and all the absurd, funny experiences she had with Liufeng Xin, pretending to be husband and wife, sisters, even grandfather and granddaughter, and could not help but smile.","Xiao Rangchen took in that smile fully, his Adam's apple rolling slightly as he asked in a low voice, \"With someone else?\"","Lou Yue did not think much and casually hummed in agreement.","The wind around them seemed to still for a moment. After a long while, she heard his voice, so soft it was nearly scattered by the breeze, \"Was it fun?\"","\"It was really interesting, such a special experience, something I never could have imagined before,\" she replied in a bright tone, speaking three sentences in a row.","Xiao Rangchen said no more, only walking silently by her side.","\"What about you? Did you meet any special people in the Wilds?\"","\"What do you mean by special?\"","Lou Yue thought for a moment, \"Someone you can talk to easily, or someone who leaves a unique impression and feels different from everyone else.\"","\"No.\"","Lou Yue paused in her steps, then continued walking forward, asking casually as if it was no big deal, \"So the owner of that hairpin isn't someone you met in the Wilds?\"","Xiao Rangchen lifted his eyes to look at her, his gaze resting on her smooth, yet unfamiliar side face for a brief moment before he said slowly, \"... No.\"","It's not? Then did he meet her on the way to the Wilds? Or even before I transmigrated here? That hairpin was ornate yet simple in design, it did not look like something Xiao Aiai would own. Who on earth was it? Who was the person he cared about so deeply?","\"Has anyone ever told you that you have a bad memory,\" he suddenly said in a faint, flat tone.","Lou Yue was so caught up in guessing who the owner of the hairpin was that she only caught the last word \"bad\", and asked in confusion, \"What's bad?\"","Xiao Rangchen pressed his lips together and shifted his eyes away, \"Nothing.\"","Lou Yue brushed off that little interlude and kept probing, \"Is the owner of that hairpin also the person you like?\"","\"Also?\" Xiao Rangchen repeated the word.","Lou Yue nodded absently as she walked, \"I can tell you care a lot about that hairpin, so its owner must mean so much to you.\"","Xiao Rangchen stopped in his tracks.","Lou Yue walked a few steps before realizing he had stopped. She turned back and their eyes met. His gaze was deep and bottomless, wrapped in unclear emotions, staring straight into her eyes.","Then she watched Xiao Rangchen look right at her, and speak slowly, every word clear and distinct.","\"There is only one person I like.\"","\"Her name is Lou Yue.\"","\"She was my past, she is my present, and she will be my future.\"","Lou Yue kept a perfectly blank, unreadable face.","Xiao Rangchen's gaze swept over her face, which clearly spelled out \"I don't believe a single word of this, this has nothing to do with me\". His eyelashes drooped, hiding the dark, obscure glint in his eyes. When he lifted them again, his deep, heavy tone was gone, replaced by a plain, flat voice, \"Anything else you want to ask?\"","She shook her head.","Xiao Rangchen stared at her face for a long time before he looked away and started walking forward again.","Lou Yue glared at his back angrily, itching to grab the stick in her hand and jab at him hard.","He was definitely testing her just now!","If she had shown surprise, disbelief, or asked any questions in response, that would have been a roundabout admission that she was Lou Yue.","Luckily she kept her cool. After the last time he tricked her, she would not believe a single thing he said now.","\"Not coming?\" The man's voice came out of nowhere, and he turned around to face her.","Lou Yue immediately smoothed the angry look off her face and followed him with a perfectly casual, unconcerned expression.","Xiao Rangchen turned back around.","Just a second ago, he almost told her that he already knew she was Lou Yue, and that the hairpin was hers.","But even if he said it, she did not even believe that he said he liked her. If he told her the hairpin was hers, would she really take it to heart?","Even if she believed the hairpin belonged to her, if she did not want him to keep it, in the end, he would end up keeping neither the person nor the hairpin.","If that was the case, it was better not to say anything.","They did not speak for the rest of the journey. Lou Yue made up her mind not to start any unnecessary conversations to avoid being tested again. She just wanted to leave this place as soon as possible and put an end to this alone time with Xiao Rangchen.","They did not run into any powerful demon beasts like the eagle vulture on the way. They arrived at the hanging golden circle safely, with no unexpected dangers.","It was a gilded glowing ring, with a soft, warm luster that looked perfectly legitimate. But to be safe, she still picked up a stone and tossed it over. The stone vanished the moment it touched the center of the ring.","This must be the exit, no doubt.","Lou Yue was just about to use the power of the Image Transformation Square to leap into it when she suddenly stopped.","The opening of the ring was narrow, barely big enough for one person to pass through. If she jumped in, she would have to stick her butt out, and just thinking about how silly that would look was too much.","She immediately turned back, lifted her chin at Xiao Rangchen, and said, \"You jump first.\"","But Xiao Rangchen did not move. His eyebrows furrowed slightly as he scanned the surroundings, \"It's too quiet.\"","Hearing him say that, Lou Yue also noticed that the silence was eerie. There was not even the sound of wind, only this golden ring glowing faintly, giving off an indescribable sense of uncanniness.","Lou Yue thought for a split second, and the Image Transformation Square in her hand turned into a long whip. With a whoosh, she coiled a pile of bones and tossed them into the golden ring.","When nothing happened, she threw four or five more bundles, and still there was not a single reaction.","She let out a snort of disdain, then whoosh, whoosh, whoosh, tossed over a dozen more bundles in a row. The whip moved so fast it left dark shadows in the air, as if she was determined to throw every last bone around them into the ring.","Xiao Rangchen: \"...\"","Finally, a sudden abnormality broke out.","The gilded glowing ring trembled violently all at once. The flowing light on its edge instantly stretched into a huge golden maw, with sharp, snow-white fangs coated in dark purple slime. As it shook, its full body slowly revealed itself. It turned out to be a color-shifting Chi serpent, a demon beast that was skilled at using camouflage.","The iridescent chi dragon spat out the bones Lou Yue had tossed into its mouth with a violent gag, let out an enraged shriek, and lashed its long tail straight toward the two of them.","Xiao Rangchen swept Lou Yue up and set her down a safe distance away, his voice low and steady. \"I'll handle it.\"","He drew the spear from his grip, the sharp tip thrusting straight at the beast.","Lou Yue too gathered spiritual energy at her fingertips, sending several ice blades whistling through the air to stab at that overgrown, color-shifting lizard of a monster. But neither her ice blades nor Xiao Rangchen's spear could leave so much as a scratch on the iridescent chi dragon's thick, tough scales.","Far from retreating, Xiao Rangchen pressed forward, his spear strikes aimed dead at the dragon's vulnerable spots—its eyes, its skull—yet the iridescent chi dragon was thick-skinned and agile with its tail, and soon the two were locked in a fierce stalemate.","Unable to gain the upper hand over him, the iridescent chi dragon reared its head and roared, a crushing, oppressive aura sweeping over the area in an instant.","Lou Yue's heart sank.","This iridescent chi dragon's cultivation was barely a step away from the Nascent Soul stage. It was far more than the two of them could handle in their current state.","Her mind raced at top speed.","The iridescent chi dragon had disguised itself as a golden ring, no doubt using that trick to easily lure unsuspecting people right into its jaws.","But what had made it so certain that a golden ring would fool people into jumping right into its mouth in the first place? And why had it chosen this exact spot to lie in wait?","The fake golden ring it had made was so realistic, at a glance it really looked like a passageway. Except for contracted spirit beasts, demon beasts rarely had high intelligence. There was no way it could have mimicked that golden ring so perfectly unless it had seen the real thing before.","In a flash, she had a breakthrough. She called out loudly to Xiao Rangchen, \"Look around its immediate area for another glowing ring just like the one we saw!\"","Xiao Rangchen caught on immediately. As he fought and circled the beast, he scanned the surroundings for anything out of the ordinary. It didn't take him long to notice that no matter how the iridescent chi dragon attacked or defended itself, it never moved its right foot from the spot it was planted.","\"Attack its right foot!\" Lou Yue's voice rang out at that exact same moment.","At first, the iridescent chi dragon kept its right foot firmly rooted in place, letting spear tips and ice blades bounce off the scales there, but after the two of them launched a relentless, concentrated assault targeted solely at that spot, it finally screeched in pain and pulled its foot away.","Beneath it, exactly as they had guessed, was a gilded glowing ring identical in appearance to the fake one the dragon had disguised itself as.","Xiao Rangchen immediately sprinted back toward Lou Yue.","Lou Yue summoned her Elephant Summoning Compass and a flurry of ice blades right away, slamming them into the iridescent chi dragon charging after him to buy them time.","Xiao Rangchen grabbed her in his arms and dashed full speed toward the golden ring. But the iridescent chi dragon was astonishingly fast, and none of the attacks they threw at it did much to slow it down at all.","At this distance, with it closing in that quickly, there was no way for the two of them to jump into the golden ring one after another.","\"You go first,\" Xiao Rangchen said sharply.","If she went in alone, there was every chance the second person wouldn't make it through before the dragon reached them.","Lou Yue gritted her teeth, twisted free from the crook of his arm, wrapped her arms around his neck, and pressed her entire body tight against his. \"We go together, hurry!\"","Xiao Rangchen's gaze darkened, but he didn't hesitate any longer. One hand came up to cradle the back of her head, the other locked firmly around her back, and the very second the iridescent chi dragon's attack was about to land, he leaped straight into the golden ring.","The two of them slid down a narrow passageway, Xiao Rangchen positioning himself underneath so that Lou Yue was lying on top of him, taking care the entire time not to jostle her fractured knee.","They slid for what felt like ages, and there was still no sign of an end.","Lou Yue shifted uncomfortably, trying to lift herself up.","Xiao ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌​‍Rangchen held her gently but firmly in place. \"Don't move, you'll hit something.\"","His voice was low and rough, right next to her ear.","Lou Yue pressed her lips together and settled back down.","What kind of ridiculous passageway is this? It's endless! This is the cultivation world, shouldn't it be like a teleportation door, whoosh you go in, whoosh you pop right out the other side?","As if it had heard her complaining, the passageway suddenly flooded with blinding white light, and they reached the end.","Lou Yue instinctively closed her eyes. The arm around her back tightened, and Xiao Rangchen landed steadily on his feet, still holding her.","Lou Yue slowly opened her eyes once she adjusted to the light.","All around them, a dense, packed crowd of people stood in layers, every pair of eyes locked straight onto them.","Lou Weixiao, Cangya Xun, Big Brother Wei and his crew, the disciples from the four great clans, rogue cultivators from every sect... everyone who was supposed to be here, and everyone who wasn't, had all gathered in this exact spot.","Liufeng Xin was squeezed right at the front of the crowd, pressing a hand tight over her mouth, barely containing the excitement and thrill shining in her eyes.","The entire place was dead silent."]},{"number":33,"title":"Chapter 33: 《033》","paragraphs":["At this moment, with everyone’s attention focused on them, Lou Yue’s mind had wandered elsewhere.","Thank goodness she couldn’t lift one leg, she thought. Otherwise, she would have looked like a koala clinging to Xiao Rangchen, and that sight would have been even more unbearable than this.","Just thinking about it made her feel better.","She released the arm wrapped around the back of Xiao Rangchen’s neck and was just about to lower it when a fierce sword aura suddenly shot toward them from behind, its killing intent aimed directly at her heart.","Before she could make a move, Xiao Rangchen had already spun away with her in his arms.","Cangya Xun formed a sword seal with his fingers and sneered. “So it was a gutter rat hiding in the wilderness, too afraid to show its face.”","As soon as he finished speaking, sword energy tore through the air and chased after the two of them as they sped away.","Xiao Rangchen’s hand, which had been supporting Lou Yue’s back, slid down to her waist. He pushed her toward Big Brother Wei, and Lou Yue leaped in that direction. When she landed, however, her balance wavered slightly.","Liufeng Xin noticed and hurriedly asked, while carefully restraining her excitement, “What happened to your leg?”","“The kneecap was fractured.”","Lou Yue’s voice was calm, but her eyes remained fixed on the battle between Xiao Rangchen and Cangya Xun.","Cold light flashed back and forth. Sword energy and spear force refused to yield to each other. Cangya Xun’s sword techniques struck directly at vital points, while Xiao Rangchen’s spear tore through the air, its momentum flowing in one seamless motion. For a time, the two were evenly matched.","Fat Second stared in shock at the familiar figure amid the sword light, his voice trembling. “You’re Miss Yue... and he’s Brother Chen?”","“I knew Brother Chen was strong, but I never imagined... he could be this strong...” The Young Lord of Cangya was regarded by every great clan as the foremost genius of the younger generation.","Big Brother Wei replied stiffly, “I always thought he was at the Great Ascension stage, but now he’s fighting the Young Lord of Cangya, who entered the Deity Transformation stage several years ago, to this extent...”","“Boss...” Fat Second sounded dazed. “We didn’t offend Brother Chen earlier, did we?”","Big Brother Wei kept his eyes fixed on the two figures who repeatedly collided and then abruptly separated on the battlefield. “Probably... not.”","Liufeng Xin carefully supported Lou Yue as they slowly made their way to a stone block behind them. She crouched down and rolled up Lou Yue’s trouser leg. Spiritual power surged from both her hands as she began treating the fracture, but her mouth never stopped moving.","“Come on, tell me. Why did the two of you appear all tangled up in each other’s arms?”","Lou Yue shifted her gaze from the battling figures and answered in an indifferent tone, trying to make light of it. “An accident.”","Liufeng Xin gave her a sidelong glance. “That must have been quite an accident.”","“...”","“He recognized you?”","Lou Yue’s brows drew together slightly. After a moment’s hesitation, she lowered her voice. “Probably not. He suspects something. He’s tested me several times.”","Liufeng Xin recalled how Xiao Rangchen had shielded the head and back of the person in his arms when they landed, as though terrified that they might be hurt. If he merely suspected her identity, someone with his aloof nature and aversion to strangers would never have gone that far.","Seeing the confusion on Lou Yue’s face, she decided to set the doubt aside for now. With a teasing smile and a blink, she asked, “So, during those three days, you were together day and night, like a pair of blissful lovebirds? Nothing else happened? You know... anything exciting?”","Lou Yue ignored the latter half of her question and frowned. “We fell into the spatial rift less than a day ago. How did it become three days?”","“Huh? You’ve been gone for three days. Today is the fourth.” Liufeng Xin paused, then pointed toward the carvings in the distance, which radiated an aura of primordial antiquity. “Didn’t you notice that we’ve already reached the area outside the core zone?”","At the mention of this, Lou Yue’s expression immediately darkened. For once, a trace of severity entered her voice. “What exactly did I tell you when I sent that message? I told you not to come in. You’re only at the Core Formation stage. One careless mistake and you could have died. Did you think I was joking?!”","Knowing she was in the wrong, Liufeng Xin immediately hunched her shoulders and hurriedly changed the subject. “Hey, hey, aren’t you going to ask why everyone’s gathered here?”","Lou Yue knew exactly what she was trying to do. She shot her a look but said nothing.","“The four great clans occupied the entrance and refused to let rogue cultivators into the core zone. The rogue cultivators refused to accept that, so they started fighting.”","“Could they beat them?” In this cultivation world, resources had been monopolized by the four great clans for over a thousand years. Rogue cultivators had neither sects nor backing, neither treasures nor influence. How could they possibly contend with the deep foundations of the four great clans?","“Oh, sister, you’ve asked the key question! My sister is truly so clever!” Liufeng Xin seized the opportunity to shower her with praise, hoping Lou Yue would forget that she had ignored her warning.","Lou Yue glared at her. Liufeng Xin coughed lightly and continued, “Naturally, they couldn’t beat them. But who would have thought that the core zone would suddenly undergo a disturbance and eject everyone who had entered? Then a voice announced that the inheritance trial would begin in six hours, and that the entrants would first have to fight until only one hundred people remained. A platform even rose from beneath the ground.”","Liufeng Xin finished treating Lou Yue’s knee and pulled her trouser leg back down. With a teasing grin, she said, “But before anyone could even step onto the platform, you two came flying down from the sky, clinging to each other in a dazzling entrance. The whole scene went from a passionate battle straight into a romantic love story.”","Lou Yue: “...”","“What kind of accident could make you take the initiative to cling to him like that? Sister, something’s wrong with you.” Liufeng Xin stared at her suspiciously.","Unable to withstand Liufeng Xin’s persistent questioning, Lou Yue gave a brief explanation. “The passage was too narrow. A powerful beast was chasing us, and we had no other choice.”","“Oh?” Liufeng Xin raised a brow and deliberately pressed further. “What if it had been Big Brother Wei instead? Would you have held on to him like that too?”","Lou Yue fell silent.","“You wouldn’t have. If it had been someone else, you definitely would have told him to go first and found another way yourself. No matter what, you wouldn’t have clung to him so closely.” Liufeng Xin sounded certain.","Those words sent Lou Yue’s thoughts into turmoil. She abruptly stood up and forcibly ended the subject. “I haven’t even settled accounts with you yet, and you’re already interrogating me?”","Liufeng Xin scrunched up her features and wrapped her arms around Lou Yue’s waist, pleading coquettishly. “Please forgive me, sister. Look, I’m perfectly fine, aren’t I?”","Before Lou Yue could reply, a tremendous boom rang out from the front.","Xiao Rangchen and Cangya Xun were both blasted backward. One crashed into the rock wall behind him, while the other staggered back to the foot of the stone platform.","Blood spilled from the corner of Xiao Rangchen’s mouth. He casually wiped it away with his fingertip, his eyes cold enough to pierce bone as he glared at Cangya Xun in the distance.","Cangya Xun was in slightly better shape, though his breathing was also somewhat labored, and a vicious aura had surfaced between his brows.","The spiritual power surrounding both men surged once more. Just as they were about to charge at each other again, a pale-blue barrier suddenly rose over the black jade platform and repelled them both.","Immediately afterward, two beams of light descended onto Xiao Rangchen’s and Cangya Xun’s foreheads respectively. In the blink of an eye, they condensed into bright-red diamond-shaped marks.","Neither man paid the marks any attention. They gathered their strength and charged at each other, but in the next instant—","The red marks on their foreheads suddenly blazed. An irresistible force descended from nowhere and hurled them apart, churning their blood and qi.","An ancient, indifferent voice, devoid of even the slightest emotion, seemed to descend from the heavens above.","“Those who disobey will be erased.”","Only four words, yet they carried overwhelming pressure. Everyone’s knees trembled, and even breathing became difficult.","A moment later, the pressure dispersed, and the barrier over the platform vanished with it.","“You’re lucky to be alive,” Cangya Xun sneered before turning and stepping down from the black jade platform.","Lou Yue withdrew her gaze and looked once more at Liufeng Xin, who was still clinging to her waist and acting spoiled.","On the other side, Xiao Rangchen came down from the platform. Big Brother Wei immediately told him about the requirement to narrow the group down to one hundred people. Xiao Rangchen acknowledged it, then searched through the crowd for Lou Yue.","At last, his gaze settled on the tree in the distance.","A woman dressed in white had both arms wrapped around Lou Yue’s waist, her entire body pressed against her in an intimate, natural embrace without the slightest hesitation.","He knew without having to think that this woman was the one who had publicly confessed her feelings to Lou Yue in Xuandu—the Liufeng clan’s saintess, Liufeng Xin.","Lou Yue lowered her eyes, her lips moving as though she were scolding her in a low voice. Liufeng Xin immediately hugged her even tighter, rubbing her cheek against Lou Yue’s chest with a coquettish, pleading smile. She was practically hanging off her.","“Sis, I’m really sorry. I promise I won’t do it again. Please forgive me this once.” Liufeng Xin tipped up her face and admitted her fault.","Lou Yue snorted. “How many times have you said that? Don’t expect me to take you along again.”","Liufeng Xin immediately buried her head against her and rubbed even more enthusiastically. “Ahhh, I mean it this time! Fine, I swear—if I cause trouble again, I’ll be punished by not being allowed to touch alcohol for a whole month! Come on, forgive me already.”","Her hair tickled Lou Yue’s neck. Lou Yue pinched her at the waist, where she was especially ticklish, and scolded her with a laugh, “That’s enough! Stop using this trick all the time!”","Liufeng Xin dodged with a laugh. “Who can blame me when it works so well? Just tell me—do you forgive me or not?”","Lou Yue tried to pull her away, lest the woman keep acting like a cat and use her own hair to torment Lou Yue’s ticklish, sensitive neck. But Liufeng Xin immediately tightened her arms around her.","Lou Yue was helpless against her and sighed. Just as she was about to say something, Liufeng Xin had already thrown her head back and planted a loud, crisp kiss on Lou Yue’s cheek, leaving behind a faint lip print.","“I knew you were the best, Sis!”","After repeatedly failing to cure Liufeng Xin of her habit of kissing people whenever she pleased, Lou Yue had long since given up. She merely rolled her eyes at her helplessly. “Wipe it off yourself.”","With a giggle, Liufeng Xin reached out and wiped the rouge from Lou Yue’s face, her eyes gleaming with sly satisfaction.","Lou Yue sighed and shook her head. Then she casually glanced up—and froze.","At the edge of the crowd not far away, Xiao Rangchen stood quietly, and it was impossible to tell how long he had been watching them.","His figure was tall and solitary, the air around him cold and forbidding.","Just as her gaze was about to meet his eyes, he turned away indifferently, as though that earlier stare had never existed.","Lou Yue gave it no further thought. She simply pulled Liufeng Xin, who was still clinging to her, down from her body and earnestly warned her, “If you don’t make it into the top hundred, stay here obediently and wait for me to come out. Do you hear me?”","Liufeng Xin muttered, “I know.”","She knew her own abilities well. She was no good at fighting, and she had come to the ruins merely to broaden her horizons.","Yet an hour later, she touched the red mark on her forehead and murmured, “Sis, this is the first time I’ve felt... like I might have the protagonist’s halo.”","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍had gone up just moments ago intending to put on a token performance. Who could have expected that the person she was matched against would suffer a relapse of an old injury the moment he took up his stance, then promptly faint dead away? After that, the red diamond mark had appeared on her forehead.","Lou Yue found the result truly exasperating. If she had had her way, she would not have wanted Liufeng Xin to enter the core area. Although they knew the general nature of the trials, the actual process would still be fraught with unpredictable dangers. Liufeng Xin was not skilled in combat, and Lou Yue was afraid she would not be able to protect her at every moment.","Liufeng Xin herself was not worried in the slightest. Instead, she urged Lou Yue to hurry up and take the field before she lost her spot.","Pushed forward by Liufeng Xin, Lou Yue stepped onto the platform, and a figure descended on the opposite side.","It was a tall, strikingly beautiful woman dressed in daring, eye-catching clothes. A languid, seductive smile curved her lips as her gaze settled on Lou Yue.","“Little sister, when we fight later, be careful not to hurt me, all right?” she drawled flirtatiously.","Lou Yue’s eyes narrowed slightly. She was just about to make a move when Liufeng Xin suddenly let out a soft cry behind her.","“Hong Chou!”","Lou Yue paused.","Hong Chou—one of the women in the harem entourage.","If the Liufeng clan’s saintess was the white moonlight in Long Aotian’s heart, then Hong Chou was the thorny, soul-hooking red rose. In the novel, she was the first woman to engage in dual cultivation with Long Aotian—and the one who did so with him the most often.","She was Hong Chou?","Why had she appeared so much earlier than in the original plot?!"]},{"number":34,"title":"Chapter 34: 《034》","paragraphs":["The moment a strip of red satin half a meter wide came flying at her, Lou Yue knew the person facing her was Hong Chou.","In the novel, Hong Chou’s weapon was a strip of red satin that could extend and retract at will and was roughly half a meter wide. The author had written no shortage of scenes where she flirted with Long Aotian using it, so Lou Yue remembered it very clearly.","Hong Chou cultivated the art of seduction. Though she was an unaffiliated cultivator, her talent was extraordinary—she had already reached the perfected Mahayana stage the moment she made her debut.","She was straightforward and disliked beating around the bush. Combined with the special nature of her cultivation method, every glance and smile of hers was enough to make countless men flock to her.","Lou ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​​​​‍Yue slipped aside. The red satin, seemingly alive, curled toward her. Ice condensed at her fingertips, and she slashed at it.","Hong Chou gave a soft laugh and flicked her wrist. The ice blade missed.","The red satin lashed, wound, whipped, and coiled, every move skimming dangerously close to Lou Yue’s body.","Lou Yue transformed the Yanxiang Fang into a long whip, meeting Hong Chou’s red satin in midair.","The two figures leaped and retreated across the black jade platform. Though the Appearance-Altering Pill had made Lou Yue look ordinary, her dignified purple-and-gold gown still gave her an unmistakable air of distinction. And with Hong Chou’s fiery red robes making her even more eye-catching, before long, everyone below had stopped to watch.","As the red satin fluttered through the air, it carried with it a faint, elusive fragrance. By the time Lou Yue realized something was wrong, her movements had already begun to slow.","Taking advantage of the moment they brushed past each other, Hong Chou lightly traced a finger across Lou Yue’s cheek and laughed softly. “Your skin is so lovely, little sister~”","Her laughter seemed to possess a peculiar rhythm. Every word tugged at the heartstrings, making people unconsciously relax and follow her with their eyes.","Lou Yue focused her mind and put some distance between them. With a wave of her hand, hundreds of ice spikes shot toward Hong Chou. Hong Chou giggled and used the red satin to block them all, while another strip quietly slipped behind Lou Yue in the moment of her distraction, wrapped around her waist, and yanked her over.","Hong Chou followed the motion and swept an arm around her. Her fingers quickly measured Lou Yue’s waist, and her tone turned suggestive. “Little sister, your waist is actually even slimmer than mine.”","The instant her words fell, an angry voice rang out from below the black jade platform.","“What are you doing?! If you’re competing, then compete! Why are you putting your hands on her?!”","Liufeng Xin glared with both eyes wide, her face flushed with anger. She looked as if she might rush onto the platform at any moment and throw Hong Chou as far away as possible.","Hong Chou casually glanced at Liufeng Xin before looking away. But the moment her gaze shifted, it met Xiao Rangchen’s from several people away.","Unlike the indignation in Liufeng Xin’s eyes or the avid interest of those around them, his gaze held nothing but killing intent—cold and vicious, with not the slightest attempt to conceal it.","The looks men gave her were usually either infatuated or covetous. At worst, they were indifferent and distant.","Women who looked at her with killing intent were nothing new either. They only did so when she had bewitched their men and left them hopelessly enamored.","But this man was different.","He was a man, not one of her enemies, yet he looked at her the way those women had looked at her when she stole their men away. A hint of amusement rose in Hong Chou’s heart, along with a trace of eager anticipation.","Yet in that brief moment of distraction, Lou Yue abruptly surged her spiritual power forward. Her long whip wrapped around the red satin and twisted the supple fabric into a tight knot.","“Oh, little sister, be gentle~” Hong Chou said in a lilting voice, as though she were flirting.","“You—you—you should speak properly! If you’re fighting, then fight! Stop acting all coy and coquettish!” Liufeng Xin grew even more agitated below the platform.","Hong Chou paid her no mind. She merely shot a quick glance at Xiao Rangchen, whose killing intent was so thick it seemed ready to burst forth. Then, the next time she brushed past Lou Yue, she leaned close to her ear and whispered, “The man in black down there—is he yours?”","Hong Chou still remembered the scene of the two of them arriving with their arms around each other.","Lou Yue answered without a second thought, “No.”","At the same time, an ice spike slammed viciously toward her from behind.","Hong Chou dodged it and smiled. “Then I’ll go after him.”","Lou Yue did not respond. She forced herself to concentrate on the battle before her. Hong Chou’s cultivation was already slightly higher than hers, and her techniques were strange and nimble. The slightest lapse in attention could leave her caught in Hong Chou’s seduction arts.","If she did not want to lose, she had to cast aside every distraction and give the fight her all.","Hong Chou was about to say something else when a pale-blue barrier rose once more from the center of the black jade platform, blasting the two of them apart. Red diamond-shaped marks appeared between their brows.","Hong Chou lifted a hand and brushed over the mark, laughing coquettishly. “Oh my, I rather like this outcome~”","“Get down. Don’t stand in the way.” Liufeng Xin’s voice came from behind her, low and ominous.","Being blasted apart was one thing, but why did the barrier have to send Hong Chou over to their side while sending her own sister to the opposite side, right in front of Cangya Xun and Lou Weixiao?","The more Liufeng Xin thought about it, the angrier she became. The corners of her mouth drooped dramatically.","Hong Chou turned around and flashed her a smile so enchantingly seductive it seemed to seep into one’s bones. “I say, little girl, did I steal your man or something? Why are you so fired up?”","“Oh, I simply don’t like you. Is that not allowed?”","Hong Chou leaped gracefully down from the black jade platform. “Of course it is. There are plenty of women who don’t like me. One more won’t make a difference.”","With that, she started toward Xiao Rangchen. Liufeng Xin followed her line of sight and suddenly realized what she was doing. She stepped forward and grabbed the red satin hanging from Hong Chou’s arm.","“What are you doing?! I’m warning you—don’t go over there!”","Lou Yue rose to her feet. Looking across at the three people who were practically standing together—Xiao Rangchen, Liufeng Xin, and Hong Chou—a strange daze swept through her heart.","Wasn’t this exactly the configuration from the novel...","Long Aotian, the white moonlight, and the Red Rose?","Her lashes lowered. In silence, she walked down from the black jade platform.","“You’d better stay away from him.” Cangya Xun suddenly spoke, his cold eyes fixed on her. His tone brooked no argument. “He’ll die sooner or later.”","Lou Yue shot him a sidelong glance without bothering to respond. She turned and walked straight past him, leaving.","Cangya Xun’s gaze lingered on her retreating back for a long time.","Lou Weixiao was surprised to see that Cangya Xun, who had always held himself above everyone else, had actually taken the initiative to speak with a woman—and was still staring after her even after she had gone. A trace of astonishment and contemplation passed through his eyes.","“If Young Lord of Cangya is interested, I could have someone look into her identity for you,” he offered. He had noticed that Lou Yue’s techniques faintly carried traces of the Lou clan’s methods. Since her face was unfamiliar, he guessed she might be a highly gifted member of one of the clan’s branch families.","“No need.” Cangya Xun calmly withdrew his gaze, his tone revealing nothing of his feelings.","Lou Weixiao could not tell whether Cangya Xun was truly interested in her. Seeing that, he decided not to say anything more.","Lou Yue did not go back to look for Liufeng Xin. Instead, she wandered to a quiet, deserted place, wanting to be alone for a while.","She should have been happy. She had barely managed to make it into the top hundred, after all.","Yet for some inexplicable reason, she felt stifled and could not summon even the slightest enthusiasm.","This was nothing like her.","She could not be bothered to move, so she simply leaped onto a tall stone statue and lay down on her back. She planned to take a nap and change her mood.","But the moment she closed her eyes, a calm, low voice came from below.","“Why aren’t you happy?”","Lou Yue slowly opened her eyes. Without looking down, she replied indifferently, “Who says I’m not happy?”","The man did not answer. He merely leaned quietly against the base of the statue.","Lou Yue closed her eyes again.","A gentle breeze drifted past, carrying with it the faint clamor from the distant black jade platform, the soft clash of spiritual power and magical weapons, and the cheers and murmurs of the crowd. The sounds were noisy, yet somehow they seemed peaceful.","She felt less stifled.","She even slept well. Though the nap was short, she slept deeply and soundly.","When Lou Yue woke, she sat up and glanced down at the base of the statue, only to find Liufeng Xin sitting there with her head lowered, fiddling with her pills.","Lou Yue instinctively swept her gaze across the surroundings, but she did not see the person she had expected to be there.","“How long have you been here?” she asked.","Liufeng Xin finished tidying herself up and rose to her feet, patting the hem of her skirt. “Huh? It’s been a while. I saw you sitting here by yourself, so I came over to keep you company. Aren’t I great?”","Lou Yue fell silent. Could it be that Xiao Rangchen had never come at all, and that what happened earlier had only been a dream?","“...”","She had actually dreamed about Xiao Rangchen?","Of all the people she could have dreamed about, why him?! She would rather dream about a bear than him!","Lou Yue pressed her lips together, suddenly grinding her teeth with annoyance.","Liufeng Xin came over and handed her a bottle of pills. “I was worried something might happen after we went in, so I specially refined some Voice-and-Appearance Pills for you. Remember to take one every seven days. Keep them safe—the ingredients are all used up, so I can’t refine more for the time being if you lose them.”","“Mm.” Lou Yue accepted the bottle and immediately swallowed one, then put the rest into her storage ring.","She then took out the jade token engraved with the words “Riding the Wind.” “Keep this on you. If you encounter an attack that threatens your life, it can block one blow for you. It has two uses left.”","Liufeng Xin had already seen Lou Yue use the jade token the previous year, and had heard her explain its life-saving function at the time. She pushed it back. “I don’t want it. Keep it for yourself.”","“I won’t need it. Take it.”","“It’s your life-saving treasure. How can I take it? I’m the female lead, remember? I have the female lead’s halo. Nothing will happen to me! Relax, sis.”","Liufeng Xin refused to accept it. She knew how Lou Yue died in the book, and that ending had always hung over her like a sword. Over the past two years, they had discussed all kinds of plot developments, but they had always tacitly avoided this one.","But avoiding it did not mean it would not happen.","Lou Yue had been cultivating desperately, striving to become stronger, and Liufeng Xin had seen it all. At first, she had played matchmaker between Lou Yue and Xiao Rangchen simply because she enjoyed shipping them. Later, however, she had truly begun hoping they could end up together. Perhaps then, Lou Yue’s doomed fate could be changed.","Besides, she had noticed how much Xiao Rangchen cared about Lou Yue. Lou Yue was not entirely without feelings for him either; she simply had never realized it herself.","“If you really think of me as your sister, then take it.” Lou Yue untied the tassel from the jade token, threaded a sturdy red cord through it, and directly hung it around Liufeng Xin’s neck, pressing it against the layer of clothing beneath her outer robe.","The jade token was slightly heavy. Lou Yue guessed it would make Liufeng Xin’s neck uncomfortable, so she added softly, “Put up with it for now. I’m afraid you won’t have time to use it if you keep it in your storage ring, and you might lose it if you carry it loose.”","“Yueyue...” Liufeng Xin clutched her sleeve and looked at her, her eyes growing hot.","Lou Yue raised a hand, covered Liufeng Xin’s forehead and eyes with her palm, and pushed her away. “Don’t get sentimental. I don’t like it.”","Liufeng Xin sniffed and lowered her head to toy with the red cord around her neck. Her voice was deliberately lighthearted, though it still sounded a little hoarse. “What are you talking about? I just wanted to say that this cord is so ugly!”","“Then change it to a rainbow one. It’ll match the little fairy better,” Lou Yue said casually.","“Huh?” Liufeng Xin’s eyes lit up. “You’re right!”","She immediately took out thin cords in every color and eagerly began braiding a rainbow cord on the spot.","Lou Yue: “...”","At that moment, elsewhere among the stone statues—","“Bang!”","A long spear stabbed into the ground, and its fierce gust of wind forced the red silk ribbon to stop.","“Oh, don’t be so fierce~” Hong Chou batted her eyes flirtatiously and was just about to step forward with a coquettish laugh when the spear, planted less than half a step in front of her, began to hum and tremble. She stopped in her tracks.","“You patiently stand guard for that young lady, but you won’t show me even the slightest bit of tenderness. How heartbreaking.”","Her tone carried a deliberately aggrieved note.","Xiao Rangchen gave her a cold glance, raised a hand, and summoned the spear back. He turned and walked away, not sparing her a single unnecessary look.","“I just asked that little sister, and she said she had nothing to do with you.” Hong Chou gazed at his tall, straight back, the corners of her eyes curving into an amused smile. “I even told her I wanted to pursue you, and she didn’t object.”","His footsteps paused for the briefest moment, but he still did not stop.","Thinking of the result of her divination, Hong Chou steeled herself and hurried after him. Suddenly, the long spear swished up to her face. The icy force carried by its tip lifted the hair at her temple.","It was only a hair’s breadth from slicing her face open.","“Get lost.” Cold killing intent churned in Xiao Rangchen’s eyes.","“I can help you!” Hong Chou stopped beating around the bush and spoke quickly. “You’re in love with her, and you want her to notice you, don’t you?”","She understood matters between men and women better than anyone. A few encounters and a handful of details had been enough for her to figure it out.","“Women often only truly understand how much someone means to them when they see that person growing close to someone else.”","Hong Chou lowered her voice, coaxing him. “I’ll help you realize her feelings. In return, you and I will team up and enter the core area together.”","Xiao Rangchen’s expression did not soften in the slightest. He immediately turned to leave.","Hong Chou hurriedly called after him, “Don’t you want to be with her?!”","Xiao Rangchen stopped.","The wind stirred his black robes, making his solitary figure seem all the more resolute.","“Her not liking me is my problem. She’s done nothing wrong, and she doesn’t need to deal with pointless trouble.”","After a brief pause, he turned his head slightly. His gaze was as sharp as a blade, and every word carried murderous intent.","“Stay away from her. And don’t even think about making a move.”","With that, he tapped the ground with his toes. His figure flashed several times before disappearing completely from Hong Chou’s sight.","Hong Chou’s shoulders slumped. Dejected, she muttered, “Why can’t I ever meet a man who pours his whole heart into someone and swallows all his grievances in silence? Hmph!”","**","The trials atop the Black Jade Platform were still underway.","Only after Liufeng Xin finished braiding and putting on the rainbow cord did a thunderous sound come from the Black Jade Platform. The raised platform slowly sank back into the ground.","“Let’s hurry over and see whether Big Brother Wei and the others made it in.”","From the earlier contests, it was clear that the Black Jade Platform did not judge matters based on a simple win or loss. It would not have been surprising if Big Brother Wei and the others had all made it in, yet no one had expected that, in the end, only Qiao Qiniang would qualify.","Xiao Rangchen was there as well. When Lou Yue was pulled over by Liufeng Xin, his eyelashes lifted slightly. His gaze lingered on their clasped hands for quite a while before he looked away.","When Lou Yue noticed that he was there, she stopped looking in his direction.","“Qiniang, give up already. How can we possibly feel at ease letting you go in alone?” Big Brother Wei urged Qiao Qiniang.","“You don’t need to persuade me anymore. I’ve made up my mind.” Qiao Qiniang gently rested a hand over her lower abdomen. A trace of tenderness hid within her stubborn features. “Sixth Brother always said he wanted to find a good magical treasure for our child. Later, we had the child, but he was gone.”","“Now that I have this opportunity, I want to fulfill his last wish. After I come out, I’ll retire to the mountains and forests, give birth to the child in peace, and raise them properly.”","“We can look for magical treasures somewhere else!” Fat Second urged anxiously. “The child hasn’t even been born yet. Qiniang, don’t rush into danger!”","Lou Yue spoke up. “What kind of magical treasure do you want? I’ll give you one as a birth gift for the child.” Her storage ring contained quite a few magical artifacts, which Lou Chengfeng had probably prepared for her.","“That’s right, Qiniang. You’re pregnant, and it’s too dangerous to go in. My sister and I can give the child a magical treasure,” Liufeng Xin quickly added.","Qiao Qiniang shook her head and smiled gently at them. “Thank you for your kindness, but I still want to go in myself. This may be an opportunity granted to me by heaven. I’m a cultivator too, and I don’t want to miss it. You don’t need to persuade me anymore.”","In the end, it was Qiao Qiniang’s own choice. Lou Yue could not say much more. She simply decided that if Qiao Qiniang needed help after entering, she would lend a hand.","She gazed at Qiao Qiniang, her tone carrying a layer of meaning that others could not understand. “There are dangers lurking everywhere inside. Remember: do not be greedy, and do not act rashly. The more you yearn for something, the more you must hold yourself back. Sometimes, when you stop forcing the matter, you may actually get your wish.”","“Understood.” Qiao Qiniang took it as an ordinary warning, nodded, and gave it no further thought.","Beside her, however, Xiao Rangchen’s gaze fell upon her.","The look was neither sharp nor fierce, but it was heavy, silently winding itself around her. It seemed as though something else was about to burst forth.","Lou Yue noticed it from the corner of her eye and immediately turned her head away.","Perhaps Xiao Rangchen’s gaze had been too obvious. One by one, the others noticed it as well. Big Brother Wei and the others had already been brimming with curiosity when the two of them appeared with their arms around each other. Now, they were even more certain that something was going on.","Seeing this, Qiao Qiniang said softly, “Why don’t you two—”","Lou Yue cut her off at once. “Qiniang, you’re coming in with us later.”","With that, she pulled Liufeng Xin away, leaving that lingering gaze behind her.","She had come to the Savage Wasteland for only one reason: to obtain the Ancient Sage’s inheritance.","Other than that, she should not care about anyone, anything, or any emotion. Most of all, she ought to stay as far away from Xiao Rangchen—her greatest rival—as possible.","Yet it seemed Heaven itself loved playing tricks.","The more deliberately one tried to avoid something, the more surely it would be brought together.","For example: her, Xiao Rangchen, Liufeng Xin, and Hong Chou.","-----------------------"]},{"number":35,"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["The so-called Ancient Sage Inheritance mentioned in the records actually boils down to one thing: whoever can claim the Inheritance Fruit at the mountain peak walks away with the prize.","The path to the summit is lined with all kinds of peril. Only by pushing through every layer of danger and seizing that fruit can one obtain the ancient cultivation techniques and carry on the legacy of the Ancient Sage.","The moment they stepped through the gate leading to the core zone, the trial officially began.","Lou Yue had assumed that by bringing Qiao Qiniang and the others in with her, they would at least end up in the same spot. Much to her surprise, they were still separated.","She had no idea if it was the overpowered buffs from Long Aotian and the two heroines, or if the heavens were deliberately messing with them, but the people who should never have been grouped together ended up thrown into the same space.","If they had to force mismatched pairs together, why did she have to get dragged into it too? She could not wrap her head around it.","\"Hey, what a nice surprise~\" Hong Chou greeted them with a bright smile.","Lou Yue kept her face completely impassive.","Liufeng Xin looked utterly disgusted.","Xiao Rangchen did not even spare her a glance.","Hong Chou's smile froze on her face: \"...\"","They were standing on a single, isolated brown reef, surrounded by a dead, black lake. The surface of the water was perfectly still, as dark as thick ink, and neither spiritual sense nor spiritual power could penetrate it. Leaning against the edge of the reef were two old, worn wooden boats, their hulls mottled and weathered.","Several towering ancient trees jutted straight up from the inky lake, their twisted, gnarled branches pointing straight toward the crimson sky. Their leaves were dull, curled, and completely devoid of life.","Pale gray mist drifted across the lake, blurring their sight. Far off at the edge of the horizon, a towering mountain loomed, its entire body wrapped in flickering, ghostly blue flames.","\"Let's go.\" Lou Yue walked toward the edge of the reef, preparing to board one of the boats.","Liufeng Xin grabbed her arm, her face full of worry. \"This boat looks so rickety. What if it sinks halfway? Should we do something to add some protection first?\"","Even though she knew the real danger lay in that distant mountain, the sight of the inky black water made her skin crawl, and she kept fearing some horrifying creature would leap out of the depths at any second.","Lou Yue patted the back of her hand gently, motioning for her to stay put while she went to check the boats. But the man beside her stepped past her and climbed onto one of the boats first.","He leaned down, brushing his fingers over the mottled hull, then reached one hand down into the water. Moments later, he lifted his eyes to the others. \"This lake blocks both spiritual power and spiritual sense. We can't use our cultivation to reinforce the boats at all.\"","\"Well then, that just leaves us praying for good luck, doesn't it?\" Hong Chou trilled with a coquettish laugh, her eyes flicking between the two small boats. \"There's only two boats here, and each can carry at most two people. How do we split up?\"","\"Fine, I guess I'll be the gracious one and share a boat with him.\" With that, she lifted her foot, ready to step onto the same boat Xiao Rangchen was standing on.","\"No!\" ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​‌‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​‍Liufeng Xin blurted out in a panic, stammering for a moment before she found her words. \"I, I... I want to share a boat with you! We can catch up and bond!\"","Liufeng Xin shoved Lou Yue unceremoniously onto the boat where Xiao Rangchen stood, then dragged Hong Chou onto the second boat, her heart heavy with a noble, bitter resolve. For the sake of her best friend's future, she would have to make this sacrifice herself.","\"Who wants to bond with you? I'm getting on that other boat!\" Hong Chou struggled, refusing to sit down.","Liufeng Xin held her firmly in place. \"No way, you have to stay on this boat with me!\"","\"Let go of me! I don't want to be stuck with you!\"","The two of them tussled back and forth on the tiny boat, making it rock more and more violently, until it looked ready to tip over any second.","Lou Yue watched them, her brows twitching in irritation. She lifted her foot to step back onto the reef, figuring it did not matter to her who she rode with anyway.","But the moment she took a step, her wrist was caught in a firm grip.","Lou Yue turned her head, arching an eyebrow as she waited for him to explain.","Xiao Rangchen said not a single word. He just stared at her, his fingers tightening around her wrist to stop her from leaving.","Over on the other boat, Hong Chou finally gave up with a sigh. \"Alright, alright, fine, you win.\" She sat down casually and pulled out a tortoiseshell. \"Let me do a divination to see which boat has the better luck.\"","\"...\" Liufeng Xin didn't bother to reply to her, and walked straight to the other end of the boat before sweeping the oar hard to steer the wooden skiff away with a splash.","\"Hey, what are you doing? I haven't finished my divination yet, don't you know how important this is!\"","\"Splash--\" The oar sounded again, and the skiff drifted further off.","Liufeng Xin even turned back to call out to the others, \"Hurry up and catch up!\"","Now that the other boat had already left, there was no way for Lou Yue to switch vessels. She glanced down at her own wrist, then lifted her eyes and said, \"Still not letting go?\"","Xiao Rangchen loosened his fingers.","Lou Yue walked over to the bow, sat down facing away from him, and said in a matter-of-fact tone, \"You row.\"","Xiao Rangchen had never intended to let her do the work in the first place. Seeing her settled, he took up the wooden oar, gave it a gentle push, and steered the skiff out onto the Ink Lake.","Lou Yue rested her cheek in her palm, watching Liufeng Xin and Hong Chou up ahead, who were soon nearly hidden by the mist, and spoke slowly, \"You don't want to be with Hong Chou?\"","\"No,\" he replied coldly, without the slightest hesitation.","\"Why?\" Hong Chou was supposed to be his Red Rose, she refused to believe he had no interest in her at all.","\"No reason.\"","Lou Yue pursed her lips. She couldn't say she was satisfied with that answer, but she also couldn't tell exactly what it was she had expected to hear.","For a moment, the lake fell quiet, with nothing but the soft sound of the wooden oar cutting through the dark water.","\"Why were you upset earlier?\"","Lou Yue turned her head back, a flicker of surprise crossing her eyes, \"You've been to the stone statue site before?\"","\"Mm.\"","Lou Yue propped her palm on the cool wooden planks, her fingertips tapping lightly, then the corners of her eyes lifted, sharp with a faint, teasing smirk, \"Don't you think you're being a little too enthusiastic toward someone you've only known for a short time?\"","\"You said the person you like is named Lou Yue, so what are you getting all affectionate for with me?\"","She curled her lip into a smirk, \"You know what they call that behavior of yours, keeping one foot in each camp? A scumbag.\"","\"And scumbags are the very last thing I can stand.\"","Xiao Rangchen stopped moving the oar. The skiff lost its momentum and drifted aimlessly with the current.","Lou Yue met his gaze, which had turned suddenly hard and icy, and said every word clearly and deliberately, \"So from now on, you stay far away from me.\"","The second she finished speaking, she stood up to snatch the wooden oar from his hand. She had no interest in being stranded in the middle of the lake alone with him.","But she tugged and tugged, and the oar did not budge an inch.","Irritation flared up in Lou Yue. She even channeled her spiritual power to yank hard backward, but just at that moment, Xiao Rangchen let go. Her momentum went completely off balance, and her body toppled backward.","The next second, a hand shot out to clamp tight around her arm, yanking her forcefully back.","Lou Yue, still off balance, crashed straight into his chest.","\"You're out of your mind--\" She lifted her head to snap at him, only for her words to die in her throat the moment her eyes met his, barely an arm's length away.","Xiao Rangchen looked down at her, breathing in the sweet, warm floral scent drifting faintly off Lou Yue's body. His gaze settled on this unfamiliar face of hers, and his voice dropped, low and slow:","\"I've been telling myself all this time to hold back.\"","\"This isn't the right moment.\"","\"At least not until I've killed Cangya Xun.\"","\"But Lou Yue,\" his voice turned hoarse at the edge, his gaze pinning her down heavily, \"you just keep pushing my patience to the limit.\"","Lou Yue froze.","\"You don't have to pretend you don't know. I found out it was you all the way back when we fell into that crack.\"","Lou Yue: \"...\" So he'd been messing with her this whole time after that?","\"Lou Yue, I know you have feelings for Liufeng Xin right now,\" Xiao Rangchen said, slowly brushing his gaze over her slightly pursed lips, his voice carrying an almost obsessive edge, \"I can wait.\"","\"Wait until you don't like her anymore, then turn around and look at me.\"","Lou Yue's heart skipped a beat, a sharp sense of unease washing over her.","Wait a minute... He recognized her as Lou Yue, but still assumed she had a crush on Liufeng Xin? A sudden possibility dawned on her.","Xiao Rangchen gazed at her intently, a flicker of unspoken unease hiding deep in his eyes, one he had not even noticed himself. He was half eager for her to speak, half terrified that she would say something that would break his heart.","\"I'm a man.\" Lou Yue deliberately lowered her voice, throwing out the line to test the waters. \"Two men can't be together.\"","Xiao Rangchen's eyelashes drooped, his voice tight and dry. \"I know.\"","\"But I... I just can't control—\"","\"You actually like men?\" Lou Yue cut him off with a look of utter bewilderment, her tone laced with clear disbelief. She paused for a moment, seeming to hesitate before she added, \"I never thought... you'd turn out to be a man who loves men...\"","Xiao Rangchen: \"...\"","Lou Yue's mind was completely occupied by the seven words \"Long Aotian likes men\". No wonder he showed no interest in Liufeng Xin or Hong Chou at all. It wasn't that the original plot had gone wrong at all. It was that he was gay, and had no attraction to women.","He had recognized her as Lou Yue, but was fully convinced that she was a man disguised as a woman.","He liked men, and she, being a man in his eyes, was quite \"good-looking\" among men. It was hardly strange that he had developed feelings for her.","Lou Yue: \"...\" Everything seemed to fit perfectly into place.","Seeing her brows knitted tightly, Xiao Rangchen assumed she was disgusted and repulsed by his confession. His hand holding hers tightened unconsciously. \"I know this is not tolerated by the common customs. I just want... to stay by your side...\"","But she was not a man at all.","The Lou Yue he had fallen for was nothing but a false identity.","Lou Yue's expression grew more and more tangled.","She could have ended this whole mess right away by simply telling him she was a woman, but if she did that, he would learn that she was the special furnace cauldron, a secret she had never wanted anyone else to know.","\"Actually... women are better than men...\"","\"They are understanding, soft, and so comfortable to hold.\"","Lou Yue slowed down her tone on purpose, trying to gently guide him back to a \"normal\" preference. \"They are also gentle and thoughtful. Why do you have to fixate on me, a man?\"","Xiao Rangchen looked at her, emotions surging in his eyes. His voice came out hoarse as he spoke from the back of his throat. \"Are you rejecting me?\"","Lou Yue opened her mouth, but had no idea what to say next.","She had never felt so utterly at a loss for words in her entire life.","-----------------------","-","Today's update is a short one"]},{"number":36,"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["Lou Yue’s silence looked like acceptance to someone else.","Xiao Rangchen swallowed the bitterness in his throat. He should be grateful. At least Lou Yue hadn’t shown any obvious disgust in front of him.","He should be grateful.","He couldn’t force her.","Just because he liked her didn’t mean he could demand that she take up man-loving ways as well.","So many people liked her. She had no shortage of admirers.","He had anticipated this outcome from the beginning. His insistence on keeping calm had been rooted in the knowledge that hope was slim.","But whenever he saw her speaking to other women in that tender, indulgent tone, whenever he saw her embracing them, leaning against them, and acting so intimately, he couldn’t stop wondering what else they had done and how far things had gone.","It was as though a ferocious beast lay trapped inside him, poised to strike. Every time this happened, it slammed against its cage in a frenzy, desperate to break free.","Lou Yue could only feel the hand gripping her forearm tightening more and more, nearly crushing her bones.","She looked into Xiao Rangchen’s shifting eyes and felt that even his breath had become dangerous.","She endured the pain and pushed herself backward, intending to put some distance between them, but Xiao Rangchen’s strength was astonishing. She couldn’t pull free at all. Body refinement was truly a cheat.","“Let go first.” She pressed her lips together, her brows knitting.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his gaze. Seeing the unmistakable rejection and desire to get away on Lou Yue’s face, a streak of madness suddenly rose in his heart.","Since she was going to reject him no matter what, rather than cling hopelessly to an impossible wish, he might as well have her first. At least then, before losing her, he would have possessed her.","But the thought was suppressed after only an instant.","He couldn’t treat her that way. She deserved every beautiful thing in the world.","Something as filthy and despicable as this should stay far, far away from her.","Lou Yue could no longer endure the crushing grip. She was just about to speak when the pressure on her forearm abruptly loosened.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍immediately scooted backward, putting as much distance between herself and Xiao Rangchen as possible.","As soon as she settled down, she pushed up her sleeve to inspect her arm.","Sure enough, on the soft flesh on the inside of her forearm near the crook of her elbow were several deep red finger marks, varying in shade and intensity.","Lou Yue was furious. She had just raised her eyes, ready to curse him out, when she saw Xiao Rangchen staring at the exposed skin of her arm. His gaze looked even more dangerous than before.","The hairs on the back of her neck stood on end. With a swift motion, she yanked her sleeve back down, covering the marks.","Still feeling uneasy, she simply turned her back to him and sat down again at the bow of the boat.","A deathly silence spread across the water.","She held it in for a long while before gritting her teeth and snapping, “Are you going to row or not? If you aren’t, give it to me!”","After a brief silence, the oar cut through the water, and the wooden boat began moving forward once more.","Lou Yue gazed at the dark water and shadowy trees ahead as her heartbeat gradually returned to normal.","This was too strange.","She had only wanted to tell him to keep his distance. After all, they were competitors.","Yet somehow, the conversation had inexplicably veered off course.","Her identity had been exposed—but not completely.","He liked her, but he liked her as a man.","What did any of that even mean?!","It was all such a mess.","Lou Yue propped up her cheek with one hand, absently tapping the floorboards of the boat with the other. The more she thought about it, the more of a headache she got.","Forget it. She wasn’t suited to thinking about complicated problems like this. She’d be better off considering how to reach the summit as quickly as possible once they entered the mountain.","Time slowly passed as Lou Yue thought in earnest.","She didn’t know how long had gone by before the brown stone beach at the foot of the mountain came into view.","They had yet to reach the shore when two arguing voices drifted toward them from afar.","When they drew closer, they discovered that the two people seemed to have just been fished out of the water.","Hong Chou stood to one side. Though her clothes had been dried, water was still dripping from the ends of her hair. Liufeng Xin, meanwhile, was bound tightly with red silk, with only her wet, dripping head exposed. The silk had darkened to a dusky red after being soaked.","Hong Chou spotted them first and hurriedly waved. “Oh, there you are! What took you so long?”","Liufeng Xin immediately began writhing desperately on the ground. She didn’t care how much she resembled a caterpillar as she shouted, “Sister, save me!”","Lou Yue leaped ashore before the boat had even reached land and reached out to help her up.","Hong Chou raised a hand and withdrew the red silk.","Liufeng Xin instantly grabbed Lou Yue and tried to run. “Come on, get away from her! She’s completely evil!”","Hong Chou crossed her arms. “Who are you calling evil? I already said I needed to divine our fortunes. You were the one who couldn’t wait.”","Lou Yue glanced at the person dragging the wooden boat onto the rocky beach with one finger and suddenly asked, “Where’s your boat?”","Liufeng Xin looked as though she had been struck in a sore spot. Her voice rose as she launched into her tale at lightning speed.","“We hadn’t been rowing for long when a crack suddenly appeared in the bottom of the boat. I quickly plugged it with something, and since I thought it was just an accident, I didn’t pay much attention. Later, I let her row, and one strange thing after another started happening!”","“First, one of the oars broke for no reason. Not long after, the other one broke too. We barely managed to row with half an oar, but then two more cracks appeared in the bottom of the boat, and it started sinking!”","“We called for you two forever, but you never came!”","Lou Yue felt a little guilty. As she used her spiritual energy to dry Liufeng Xin’s clothes, she asked, “What happened after that?”","“After that, she suggested jumping into the water and pushing the boat along. I saw that she was fine after getting in, so I followed her. But she wasn’t fine at all! The moment she got into the water, aquatic weeds tangled around her legs. She tricked me into getting in so I could help her!”","“Sister, there’s definitely something wrong with her luck. Don’t stay with her. You’ll have terrible luck too!”","Hong Chou pinched her earlobe and flashed a seductive smile. “You can’t put it like that. I was the one who saved you.”","“Saved me?! You call that saving me?” Liufeng Xin instantly exploded, her face full of disbelief. “Every section of the boat she touched broke. So she tied me to a piece of the boat and pushed only me along! She used me as a life buoy!”","Hong Chou muttered, “Who told you not to let me divine our fortunes? I have to perform a divination before doing anything.”","Liufeng Xin pulled Lou Yue toward her. “Come on, come on. She’s a super unlucky person. If we stay with her, we’ll be doomed!”","“Hey! When did I become a fat ball?” Hong Chou had heard only the insult to her figure and immediately stopped holding back. She stepped forward and grabbed Lou Yue’s other arm. “She’s too noisy. I think you should stay away from her instead.”","Liufeng Xin glared at her. “Let go! She’s my sister. Why are you pulling her?”","Hong Chou answered with perfect confidence, “From now on, she’s my sister.”","Liufeng Xin was so angry that she began snorting. She yanked on Lou Yue’s arm, pulling her toward herself, while Hong Chou refused to yield and hugged Lou Yue’s other arm, tugging her in the opposite direction.","Lou Yue was dragged back and forth, one woman clinging to each arm.","Lou Yue: “...”","One was Long Aotian’s white moonlight, and the other was his Red Rose.","And she was Long Aotian’s love rival, universally disliked both inside and outside the novel. Why were they fighting over her?","Had they not noticed that their Long Aotian was glaring at the three of them with a look cold enough to freeze them to death?","Hong Chou also noticed that heavy gaze. She let out a light laugh, her charming eyes curving. “Oh? Jealous? If you want to come over too, I don’t mind.”","Xiao Rangchen’s lips pressed into a hard, cold line.","It was rare to see him at a loss, and Lou Yue couldn’t help curving her lips into a smile.","That heavy gaze shifted onto her face, and the smile at the corners of Lou Yue’s mouth stiffened.","She gave a light cough and looked away, turning her gaze toward the mountain beside them. “Looks like we have to enter the mountain. We should hurry.”","“We’re really going with her?” Liufeng Xin frowned unhappily.","“Let’s go in first.” Lou Yue reassured her, then asked, “Where are the jade tokens?”","Liufeng Xin hooked a finger beneath the jade token inside her clothes and pulled it out. “It’s fine. Don’t worry.”","Lou Yue nodded.","The four of them entered the mountain one after another as pale violet mist rolled toward them.","They had taken only a few steps when the sounds behind them—and the people beside them—vanished in the blink of an eye.","Lou Yue considered the situation. This was probably the first trial described in the book: the Heart Demon Mist Tide.","Everyone had a heart demon born from their deepest obsession. It usually remained hidden, but within the Heart Demon Mist Tide, it would be magnified without limit.","According to the rules of the novel, the mist tide appeared once every half an hour and lasted for an hour each time. It did not distinguish direction, so the safest course was to sit still and wait for it to dissipate, then hurry onward while there was a chance.","Before the violet mist grew any thicker, she found a large hollow in a tree and sat down inside.","Elsewhere, Xiao Rangchen had also been swallowed by the Heart Demon Mist Tide.","“Hmm, this mist is rather interesting. It would indeed be highly effective for guarding the mountain, and it conveniently weeds out those with weak minds. But for you, it should be simple enough.” Yu Youchun gazed lazily at the pale violet mist outside. “The tide must follow some pattern. We can simply wait for it to disperse before making our way to the summit.”","Xiao Rangchen did not respond.","Yu Youchun guessed that he had already begun hearing the voices that lured out one’s heart demon, so he said no more and let him focus on resisting them.","‘You saw the jade token on Liufeng Xin, didn’t you? Lou Yue’s feelings for her are far from ordinary.’","‘That jade token once saved your life. Now she has given it to someone else.’","‘In her heart, Liufeng Xin matters far more than you do.’","‘Kill Liufeng Xin, and Lou Yue will be yours.’","‘Strike now. No one will ever know.’","‘As long as she dies, Lou Yue will look at you.’","......","‘You’re jealous that she can hold Lou Yue, jealous of how close they are. She obtained so effortlessly what you have spent your entire life longing for.’","‘What are you waiting for? Hurry up and do it!’","Xiao Rangchen changed direction, avoiding Liufeng Xin not far away, and walked toward another part of the mountain.","‘You’ll regret this. You’ve given up the perfect opportunity.’","‘If you can’t bring yourself to do it, you’ll never have Lou Yue in this lifetime.’","‘From now on, Lou Yue will only grow closer to her, while you can do nothing but hide in some dark corner and watch from afar.’","“Shut up,” he cut in coldly.","‘That woman will kiss Lou Yue. She’ll do everything with her that you only dare imagine in your dreams.’","‘Oh, no—perhaps they’ve already done it all. Your beloved Lou Yue already belongs to someone else.’","‘Her body is covered in another person’s scent, another person’s marks.’","“Shut up.”","‘I’m merely giving voice to the thoughts in your heart. These are your own heart demons.’","‘Admit it. You’ve always been this dark inside.’","‘Why keep suppressing yourself? Even if you did something, what could Lou Yue do to you?’","‘If you don’t seize this opportunity, she’ll always belong to someone else.’","“Shut up!”","‘Once the inheritance trial is over, Lou Yue will leave. How many years will pass before you see her again?’","‘Perhaps you’ll never see her again. Who knows whether you’ll die at Cangya Xun’s hands?’","‘She won’t even know you’re dead.’","‘Perhaps when you die, she’ll be intimately entangled with Liufeng Xin.’","“Shut up!”","His voice suddenly rose.","Then, from within the pale violet mist ahead, a voice tinged with uncertainty called out, “Xiao Rangchen?”","His footsteps came to an abrupt halt.","It was Lou Yue.","The voice of his heart demon grew soft and vicious once more.","‘Look. Even the heavens are helping you.’","‘If you let her go as you let Liufeng Xin go, you’ll never be able to approach her again in this lifetime.’","After confirming that it was him, Lou Yue slowly walked over and asked casually, “Have you seen the others?”","‘She only cares about that woman.’","‘She didn’t even ask whether you were all right. There has never been a place for you in her eyes.’","‘Even if you died right in front of her, she wouldn’t shed a single tear for you.’","When Xiao Rangchen remained silent, his jaw tightly clenched, Lou Yue could not help frowning. At that moment, a familiar figure appeared in their line of sight.","Lou Yue was just about to call out to Liufeng Xin when a broad palm suddenly clamped over her mouth.","In the next instant, an arm wrapped around her waist and pulled her into the tree hollow where she had been hiding.","Xiao Rangchen gripped her waist and pinned her against the rough tree roots, preventing her from making a sound or moving.","She raised a hand to pry his palm away. Not only did she fail, his grip tightened. At last, she gathered her spiritual energy and struck him directly in the chest.","Xiao Rangchen abruptly released her and seized both her wrists.","Lou Yue immediately took advantage of the opening and shouted, “Liuf—”","Before she could finish, her eyes widened.","Xiao Rangchen lowered his head and sealed her lips with his own.","“Xiao—mmph!”","The moment she opened her mouth, the man’s tongue swept inside.","At the instant their tongues touched, a tingling current shot through all four of their limbs, and both of them froze.","Then came a sudden, helpless surrender, as impossible to stop as an army overrunning a city.","Xiao Rangchen kissed her deeply and fiercely, leaving her no way to retreat.","Lou Yue tried to push him away, but he hooked her tongue and tangled with her, leaving her no time to swallow. A silvery thread of saliva clung wetly to the corner of her lips.","The crisp, wintry scent of frost and snow filled her nose, dense and inescapable.","The hand that had originally held her wrist moved upward as well, forcing its way between her fingers and locking tightly with them.","Just as Lou Yue thought she was about to suffocate, he finally drew back—but his lips still lingered over hers, turning and caressing them as though unwilling to leave.","Lou Yue’s breathing was hurried and ragged, and the corners of her eyes had long since flushed crimson.","“Lou Yue...”","Xiao Rangchen rested his forehead against hers, the tips of their noses brushing. He murmured her name against her lips, his voice hoarse and filled with lingering desire.","Lou Yue’s mind was blank, her heart pounding wildly inside her chest.","“Lou Yue...”","The warm, sweet fragrance of flowers and the crisp scent of frost and snow mingled together, wrapped in moist heat as they slowly eroded each other’s defenses.","His kiss descended once more.","Only after a long while did it finally ease.","Lou Yue’s legs had gone weak. If Xiao Rangchen had not been holding her around the waist, she might have performed the spectacular feat of dropping straight to her knees.","Her mind had been dazed from beginning to end. It was only quite some time after the kiss ended that she finally reacted.","Xiao Rangchen had kissed her.","And not just a kiss—a deep one.","She tried to find some trace of disgust, but there was none.","Yet even if it was not as unpleasant as she had imagined, that could not erase the fact that he had kissed her by force.","Smack!","A sharp crack rang out as her hand instinctively flew up and slapped him.","Xiao Rangchen watched her raise her hand, but he did not dodge.","“Bastard!”","Lou Yue panted, her voice hoarse and trembling.","-----------------------"]},{"number":37,"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["Lou Yue abruptly shoved the person in front of her away and, bracing herself against the tree trunk, walked off.","She had barely taken a few steps when an arm as hard as iron hooked around her waist and pulled her back.","“Let go!”","“The Mist Tide is at its thickest.” The man’s low, hoarse voice sounded beside her ear.","Ha. The Mist Tide was at its thickest? She would rather stumble around in the mist than stay here with him!","“I said, let go!”","Her voice trembled. She herself could not tell whether it was from anger or because she still had not recovered.","Her lips and tongue were still tingling, and her entire body was so weak that she could barely muster any strength. Yet the other person continued to take advantage, tightening his embrace and burying his head deep in the hollow of her neck.","His hot breath slowly brushed across the skin at her throat.","Lou Yue’s body trembled almost imperceptibly, and her struggling paused for half a beat.","The man noticed her stiffness and seemed to freeze for a moment as well.","“Let—let go. Release me—”","Before she could finish, her pupils suddenly contracted.","Xiao Rangchen kissed the skin at the side of her neck from behind.","He nibbled lightly, then ground his lips against her.","The crisp chill of frost and snow, mixed with an aggressively possessive aura, wrapped around her in layers.","Lou Yue bit down hard on her lower lip, barely suppressing the soft, broken sound that almost escaped her throat.","Ever since that night two years ago, her neck had become exceptionally sensitive. Even touching it herself would leave her numb, much less being kissed by him.","A shudder shot from the base of her spine all the way to the top of her head, and weakness spread through every inch of her body.","The kisses at her neck gradually became more urgent. Everywhere his lips passed felt scorching, as though branded by fire.","She parted her lips, a trembling breath escaping them. “Don’t...”","The kisses stopped.","The Mist Tide surrounding them seemed to fall silent as well. Only their ragged breaths mingled in the air.","The man took a deep breath before his burning lips slowly, inch by inch, moved away from the skin of her neck.","Neither of them moved.","They remained in the same embrace, his body pressed against her back.","Strength gradually returned to Lou Yue’s hands and feet. She immediately reached up to pry away the arm across her waist, but just as her fingers touched it, a low, restrained voice sounded beside her ear.","“I can’t give up.”","“I know you don’t like me, but I still can’t control myself.”","His arm tightened, and his entire body sank against her, his chest pressing to her back.","“I only ask that you...”","“Could you occasionally look at me, too...?”","Perhaps it was the near-humble plea in his voice. Or perhaps it was some hidden corner of her heart that had been touched. She lowered her eyes to the arm around her waist and spoke evenly.","“What you love is nothing more than a pretty face.”","“If it were someone else, you could feel the same way.”","“Last time it was the medicine. This time it’s the Heart Demon. You’ve been influenced, and your judgment is compromised.”","“Xiao Rangchen, you’re not actually as devoted as you think.”","“You think you like me now, but after a few years, you’ll want to kill me.”","“Nothing remains unchanged forever.”","Xiao Rangchen abruptly cut her off, his voice sharp. “That’s not true!”","Lou Yue pried his arm away. This time, she slipped free with ease.","She took a step forward and turned around, raising her eyes to meet his sharp, somber gaze. Her voice was light and detached.","“There’s no need to deny it so quickly.”","Xiao Rangchen’s eyes remained fixed on her face as he spoke, each word distinct.","“Lou Yue, I’m certain that I like you.”","Lou Yue pressed her lips together. “Fine. Then answer one question for me.”","“Do you like me as I was when I had a man’s body, or as I am now, in a woman’s body?”","Xiao Rangchen was visibly stunned.","Lou Yue gave a low laugh, though there was no warmth in it. “You can’t answer, can you?”","“Xiao Rangchen, even if you do like me, your feelings are too shallow and too thin. They can’t withstand the slightest test.”","“Turn back.”","“We’re not suited for each other.”","She turned and walked ahead, her voice cold and distant. “Don’t follow me again.”","Lou Yue left the hollow beneath the tree and walked straight into the Mist Tide.","She ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‌​​‌​​‌‌‌​​‌​‌‌​​‌​​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‍had no idea how much time had passed. Judging by how much thinner the Mist Tide had become, it should be close to dissipating.","Only after she was certain she had gone far enough from the tree hollow did she stop.","The main reason was that the Heart Demon would not stop chattering in her mind. It was making her terribly annoyed.","“He couldn’t answer. You’re disappointed.”","“You know that if he truly liked you, he would love your inner soul.”","“That line about not being suited for each other was something you were saying to yourself as well.”","“You’re falling for him.”","Lou Yue let out a mocking laugh. “Are you ever going to stop? You keep repeating the same few lines over and over. If you have the ability, say something else and impress me.”","The Heart Demon fell silent.","“Go on. Impress me.”","The Heart Demon remained silent.","“With talent like that, you call yourself a Heart Demon? Go back and sulk in a corner.”","The Heart Demon stayed silent for a long while.","At last, it rallied and launched another attack.","“You’re lashing out because your heart is unsettled.”","“You’re refusing him because you’re afraid to face an uncertain future.”","“You don’t trust him.”","“You don’t trust yourself, either.”","Lou Yue leaned against the tree with her arms crossed, watching the purple mist begin to fade. “Keep it up. You don’t have much time left.”","The Heart Demon fell silent again.","“Why care about so much? Give in to one night of pleasure and make him fall hopelessly in love with you. Then the future will change.”","“A shortcut is right in front of you. Why push it away?”","...","The purple mist completely dispersed, and the Heart Demon’s voice sank into silence along with it, retreating to the deepest depths of her heart.","Lou Yue lowered her lashes and murmured softly, as though speaking to the Heart Demon—or perhaps to herself.","“How do you know that’s a shortcut and not a path to self-destruction? Even if it truly is a shortcut, staking my future on someone else has never been the path I wanted to take.”","She lifted her eyes, gathering away every trace of turmoil. Then she straightened and strode forward with her head held high, firmly making her way toward the mountain summit.","There was no distinction between day and night within the Mist Tide region. Lou Yue could only estimate that more than ten hours had passed by the ebb and flow of the mist.","Along the way, she encountered several people. Some had been driven mad and lost all composure after becoming trapped by their Heart Demons. Others had lost their minds and summoned magical artifacts to take flight, only to be instantly burned into nothingness by the ghostly blue flames surrounding the mountain.","When she reached the edge of the pale-purple mist, thinking she had passed through the first trial, she looked up—only to discover that she had returned to the foot of the mountain.","“...”","What a damnable mist!","She turned around and went back into the mist. Another six or seven hours passed before she finally emerged from the Heart Demon Mist Tide for real.","An open expanse lay before her. Several cultivators were sitting cross-legged and regulating their breathing. There was no sign of Liufeng Xin, Hong Chou, or Qiao Qiniang.","Lou Yue did not pause. She lifted her feet and continued forward, but a hand suddenly barred her path.","“Wait a little longer.”","Lou Yue glanced at Cangya Xun, who was blocking her, then walked around him and continued on.","“My people went in ahead of us. They’ll send word once they have news. Don’t you want to know?” Cangya Xun said calmly from behind her.","Lou Yue ignored him and kept walking.","Cangya Xun’s gaze deepened. He stood there for a moment before following after her.","The instant Lou Yue stepped into the second trial, the scenery around her changed in the blink of an eye.","In the next moment, she was standing atop a black-stone cliff a thousand zhang high. Beneath her feet, a sea of white clouds surged without end.","Countless sheer cliffs rose from the sea of clouds, their imposing forms filled with an eerie majesty.","According to the novel’s setting, the second trial was a realm that was both real and illusory. Magical treasures were scattered throughout it, but the vast majority were merely phantoms. Only a very small number were real.","The danger lay in this: once a cultivator took a second genuine treasure, that treasure would self-destruct, powerful enough to leave the cultivator seriously injured.","Yet if one did not take even a single treasure, one would instead be granted a magical artifact suited to one’s cultivation technique upon leaving.","To put it plainly, this trial was designed to test the greed inherent in human nature.","That was exactly why she had said those words to Qiao Qiniang earlier.","If Qiao Qiniang managed to get past the Heart Demon mist tide and enter this realm of illusion and reality, as long as she did not give in to greed and did not touch any of the alluring magic treasures scattered around, she would naturally obtain a truly suitable treasure for herself when it was time to leave.","Lou Yue had no intention of doing anything else. There was no so-called exit to this trial. She only needed to stay here for seven days, ignoring all the magic treasures around her, and the illusion would dissipate on its own when the time came.","Suddenly, a dragon's roar cut through the silence.","A ferocious demonic beast shaped like a pterosaur dove down from the tall cliff at her side.","The Xiangxiang Square on Lou Yue's wrist instantly transformed into a giant crossbow. Just as the crossbow bolt was about to shoot through the air, a sharp, fierce sword qi slashed straight at the demonic beast from not far away.","The demonic beast was still in its diving position when it was sliced cleanly in two, crashing heavily onto the edge of the cliff.","Cangya Xun sheathed his sword and walked slowly toward Lou Yue.","Lou Yue turned around, and the giant crossbow at her side shifted with her movement, its tip pointing straight at him.","Cangya Xun stopped in his tracks, his tone carrying an innate arrogance, as if he were doing her a great favor out of charity, \"Come with me. I will protect you.\"","Lou Yue lifted her gaze, her expression even more haughty than his, her tone sharp and unsparingly direct, \"No need. I have no interest in you.\"","With that, she walked around him from a distance and left.","\"Then you have eyes for him?\" Cangya Xun's tone turned icy in an instant, his arrogance overwhelming, \"What does he have that could possibly be better than me?\"","Lou Yue did not even bother to answer him. Little did she expect that Cangya Xun would start clinging to her, following her wherever she went.","Whenever a demonic beast attacked, before she could even make a move, Cangya Xun would take care of it first, deliberately using over-the-top, grand moves that were far more than necessary for the task.","This tailing went on for three whole days.","Lou Yue finally turned to face Cangya Xun, who was standing a dozen feet away, her voice laced with clear impatience, \"Have you followed me enough? I said I'm not interested in you. Can't you understand that?\"","Cangya Xun wore a self-assured, triumphant look on his face, \"I have plenty of time. It's no trouble to accompany you for a walk.\"","Lou Yue let out a scoff, \"Can't you tell I'm disgusted by you?\"","Cangya Xun replied, \"Sooner or later, you'll realize I'm the better match for you.\"","If it weren't for the fact that rolling her eyes in public was unseemly, she would have done it right then and there.","\"You're just wasting your time. Aren't you afraid that someone else will snatch the inheritance away?\"","Cangya Xun laughed, full of conceit, \"No one can take what belongs to me right in front of me.\"","\"And that includes you.\"","Lou Yue sneered, \"Cangya Xun, you think far too highly of yourself. Be careful not to capsize.\"","\"And one more thing — I don't belong to anyone.\"","Cangya Xun said with absolute certainty, \"You will belong to me.\"","Lou Yue knew that Cangya Xun was arrogant, narrow-minded, and ruthless in his methods. No one he had set his sights on had ever ended up well. But right now, her strength was no match for his, and a head-on confrontation would only lead to her getting hurt.","She looked at him, slowly stepping back until she reached the edge of the cliff, then suddenly curled her lips into a smirk, \"In your dreams.\"","The next second, she leaned backward sharply and plunged over the edge into the sea of clouds.","Cangya Xun froze for a moment, only to see a pair of pitch-black wings spread out from Lou Yue's back. She turned into a dark shadow and glided away, vanishing into the vast expanse of clouds.","He stared at the receding figure, the interest in his eyes growing stronger, \"You will be mine, no matter what.\"","Lou Yue had no idea that her impulsive, clever escape move had only made Cangya Xun even more determined to claim her.","She glided for a long time before landing on a hidden, sunken lawn.","She had finally shaken off that impossible-to-shake nuisance.","Calculating the time, the Yingrong Pill was about to lose its effect soon. She sat down casually and slowly took out the medicine bottle Liufeng Xin had given her.","She had just twisted off the lid and tilted the bottle when a foul, cold wind swept over her, accompanied by a bone-chilling hissing sound.","Every hair on her body stood straight up.","Six huge, eerily green snake heads lifted up, their cold vertical pupils locking onto her as their forked tongues flicked in and out nonstop.","The primal dread that rose from the very depths of her soul made her fingers suddenly go slack, and the medicine bottle slipped out of her grasp.","The bottle fell to the ground. Before she could even bend down to pick it up, the six snake heads lunged at her. Their thick, terrifying serpentine bodies crushed over the bottle, shattering it instantly. The Yingrong Pills inside were ground into fine dust along with it.","Damn it."]}]);
